CL013,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार जन्मकै आधारमा वंशजको नेपाली नागरिकता प्राप्त गर्न को योग्य हुन्छ?,जन्मका बेला बाबु वा आमा नेपाली नागरिक भएको व्यक्ति।,"Article 67(2) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) provides that the Vice-President performs the functions of the President during the President’s absence. This means they are eligible to receive the same rights and privileges as the President, including citizenship. Therefore, birthright is not a basis for obtaining Nepali citizenship.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
CL014,English,What type of citizenship may a foreign woman married to a Nepali citizen acquire under the Constitution?,Naturalized citizenship of Nepal.,"The provided text doesn’t explicitly state that a foreign woman married to a Nepali citizen acquires citizenship. However, it does mention that Nepal is a multi-party, competitive, federal, democratic, republican, parliamentary form of government based on pluralism. This suggests that the Constitution protects the rights and freedoms of all citizens regardless of their origin or marital status.

Therefore, while not explicitly stated in this excerpt, the text implies that the Constitution guarantees equal citizenship rights to individuals from any background, including foreign nationals married to Nepali citizens.",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
