CL024,English,What happens to the citizenship status of a child whose parents were initially unknown if one parent is later identified?,"The temporary presumption of citizenship by descent ends, and citizenship is determined according to the Constitution and Federal law.","Article 67(2) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) provides for the rights and responsibilities of the Vice-President. It states that the Vice-President performs the functions of the President during the President’s absence. If one parent is later identified, the Vice-President will inherit the citizenship status of the child born to the other parent.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CL024,Nepali,सुरुमा बाबु–आमाको पहिचान नभएको बालकको बाबु वा आमा पछि पत्ता लागेमा उसको नागरिकताको अवस्था के हुन्छ?,वंशजको अस्थायी मान्यता अन्त्य भई संविधान तथा संघीय कानूनबमोजिम नागरिकता निर्धारण हुन्छ।,"Article 67(2) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) provides this information. It states that ""If a person does not know the identity of his father, his mother is considered his citizen.""",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
CL025,English,A child born in Nepal to a Nepali mother whose father is not traced is entitled to which type of citizenship?,Citizenship by descent.,"The child is entitled to the same rights and privileges as a citizen born within Nepal. The Constitution guarantees equal treatment regardless of parents' marital status or background, including the right to citizenship.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
CL025,Nepali,नेपाली आमाबाट नेपालमा जन्मिएको र बाबुको पहिचान नभएको व्यक्तिले कुन प्रकारको नागरिकता पाउँछ?,वंशजको नागरिकता।,"Article 67(3) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) provides for the rights and privileges of citizens. It states that a person who is not recognized as a citizen by birthright shall be granted citizenship based on their qualifications, election, or other legal procedures.

Therefore, a person born in Nepal without a parent's identification can become a Nepali citizen through various means like naturalization, residency, or other legal processes.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
CL026,English,"Under Article 11(5), what changes if the father of a child born to a Nepali mother is later found to be a foreign citizen?",Citizenship by descent is converted into naturalized citizenship in accordance with Federal law.,"Article 11(5) of the Constitution of Nepal deals with the legal status of children born in Nepal. It states that the child's legal status shall be determined by the law of Nepal, and it does not specify any particular provisions regarding the rights or responsibilities of foreign citizens. Therefore, if the father of a child born to a Nepali mother is later found to be a foreign citizen, the legal status of the child will be determined according to Nepalese laws and regulations concerning citizenship and parental rights.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CL026,Nepali,धारा ११(५) अनुसार नेपाली आमाबाट जन्मिएको व्यक्तिको बाबु पछि विदेशी नागरिक भएको पुष्टि भएमा के परिवर्तन हुन्छ?,वंशजको नागरिकता संघीय कानूनबमोजिम अंगीकृत नागरिकतामा रूपान्तरण हुन्छ।,"धारा ११(५) अनुसार नेपाली आमाबाट जन्मिएको व्यक्तिको बाबु विदेशी नागरिक भएको पुष्टि भएमा, उनका अधिकार र पदमाधारणत्व माथि जानेछ।

Here's a breakdown of what that means:

* **Right to Inheritance:** The person will lose the right to inherit from their parents.
* **Political Rights:** They will be eligible for certain political rights and positions.
* **Appointment as Prime Minister:**  They can be appointed as Prime Minister, subject to certain conditions outlined in the Constitution.

Essentially, it's a recognition that the person has been influenced by a foreign citizen, and the Constitution aims to protect their rights and ensure they are treated fairly within the political system.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CL027,English,Which type of citizenship may a child born to a Nepali mother and a foreign father acquire if permanently residing in Nepal and not holding foreign citizenship?,Naturalized citizenship.,"The Constitution of Nepal (2015) outlines the process for children born to parents from different countries. It states that a child born in Nepal, regardless of their parent’s nationality, will automatically become Nepali citizens. This is based on the principle of “naturalization.”

Therefore, a child born to a Nepali mother and a foreign father can acquire Nepalese citizenship permanently if they reside in Nepal without holding any other foreign citizenship.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CL027,Nepali,"नेपाली आमा र विदेशी बाबुबाट जन्मिएको, नेपालमा स्थायी बसोबास गर्ने र विदेशी नागरिकता नलिएको व्यक्तिले कुन नागरिकता प्राप्त गर्न सक्छ?",अंगीकृत नागरिकता।,"नेपालमा स्थायी बसोबासका लागि विदेशिएर नागरिकता प्राप्त गर्न सकिन्छ तर यसलाई दोसमा पहुँच (dual accessibility) मा थपाउनुपर्छ। यहाँ केही विकल्पहरू छन्:

*   **नेपाली नागरिकता:** यदि विदेशी बाबुबाट जन्मिएको व्यक्ति नेपाली नागरिकताको स्तर हो भने, उनी नेपालमा स्थायी बसोबासका लागि आवेदन गर्न सक्छन्।
*   **नेपालियन नागरिकता:** विदेशिएरले नेपालमा ५ वर्षभित्रै पाँच हजार नesian नागरिकता प्राप्त गर्न सकिन्छ। यसलाई 'नेपालियन नागरिकताको स्तर' भनिन्छ।
*   **अन्य नागरिकताहरू:** यदि विदेशी बाबुबाट जन्मिएको व्यक्ति नेपाली नागरिकताको स्तर माथि हुँदैन, तर उनीले अन्य कुनै नागरिकता प्राप्त गर्न सक्छन्, जस्तै संयुक्त नागरिकता (joint citizenship) वा विदेशिएर नागरिकता (foreign citizen status)।

यो जानकारी आधिकारिक स्रोतमा उपलब्ध छैन। कृपया नेपाल सरकारका वेबसाइटहरूलाई जाँच गर्नुहोस् ताकि तपाईंले सबैभन्दा अद्यतित जानकारी obtenir सकेनन्।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
CL028,English,"Under Article 11(7), when may a child born in Nepal to a Nepali mother and a foreign father obtain citizenship by descent instead of naturalized citizenship?",If both the mother and father are Nepali citizens at the time citizenship is acquired.,"Article 11(7) of the Constitution of Nepal states that a child born in Nepal to a Nepali mother and a foreign father can obtain citizenship by descent if they meet certain conditions. Specifically, the child must be born in Nepal and have a parent who is a Nepalese citizen.

Therefore, the answer is: **If the child meets the requirements outlined in Article 11(7), they may be eligible for citizenship by descent.**",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CL028,Nepali,"धारा ११(७) अनुसार नेपाली आमा र विदेशी बाबुबाट जन्मिएको व्यक्तिले कुन अवस्थामा अंगीकृत होइन, वंशजको नागरिकता पाउन सक्छ?",नागरिकता प्राप्त गर्ने समयमा बाबु र आमा दुवै नेपाली नागरिक भएमा।,"धारा ११(७) अनुसार, यदि एक व्यक्ति नेपाली आमा र विदेशी बाबुबाट जन्मिएका छ तर विदेश सरकारको सदस्य हो भने, उसको नागरिकता प्राप्त गर्न सकिन्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CL029,English,Which authority may grant naturalized citizenship in cases not specifically covered by Article 11?,Government of Nepal.,"Article 11. The President of Nepal can grant naturalized citizenship to individuals who have been residing in Nepal for a period of five years or more, provided they meet certain requirements.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CL029,Nepali,धारा ११ मा उल्लेख नभएका अवस्थामा अंगीकृत नागरिकता दिने अधिकार कसलाई छ?,नेपाल सरकार।,"Article 136 of the Constitution of Nepal provides for the right to nationality for individuals who have been residing in Nepal for a period of not less than five years. However, this right is not granted automatically; it requires the individual to demonstrate that they have sufficient knowledge and ability to contribute to the development of Nepal.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
