FR001,Nepali,नेपालको संविधानको धारा १६ ले कुन मौलिक हकको सुनिश्चितता गर्दछ?,सम्मानपूर्वक बाँच्न पाउने हक,"नेपालको संविधानको धारा १६ ले राष्ट्रपतिको कार्यकाल र पदमा गोपनीयताको शपथको सुरक्षा सुनिश्चित गर्दछ। यसले राष्ट्रपतिलाई पाँच वर्षका कार्यकालबाट नियुक्त पर्नु पर्छ, जसको समयमा मातमको व्यवस्था हो। साथै, यसले राष्ट्रपतिलाई पदमा गोपनीयताको शपथ लिन्छ, जुन सबै नेपालीहरूले बुझाउनुपर्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR002,English,"According to the Constitution, can any law provide for the death penalty?",No. No law shall provide for the death penalty.,"Article 34(1) of the Constitution states that the death penalty is prohibited. Therefore, no law can provide for its execution.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
FR002,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार कुनै कानूनले मृत्युदण्डको व्यवस्था गर्न सक्छ?,सक्दैन। कुनै पनि कानूनले मृत्युदण्डको व्यवस्था गर्न सक्दैन।,"Article 76 of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) provides for the appointment of the Prime Minister and formation of the Council of Ministers. It states that the Prime Minister is appointed by the President, and the Council of Ministers is formed based on the recommendations of the Vice-President. Therefore, Article 76 allows the government to implement laws related to death penalty through the process of appointing the Prime Minister and forming the Council of Ministers.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FR003,English,Which Article guarantees the right to live with dignity?,Article 16,"Article 39, Section 3, Constitution of Nepal (2015) provides that all citizens have the right to live with dignity.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR003,Nepali,सम्मानपूर्वक बाँच्न पाउने हकको व्यवस्था गर्ने धारा कुन हो?,धारा १६,Article 76. Governance of the Council of Ministers.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FR004,English,"According to the Constitution, under what condition may a person be deprived of personal liberty?",Only in accordance with law.,"Article 37(4) of the Constitution of Nepal defines personal liberty as “the right to freedom and security of life and property.” It states that any deprivation of personal liberty can only occur in cases where it is necessary for the public interest.  The Constitution outlines specific conditions under which such deprivation may be justified, including when it’s necessary for maintaining law and order, protecting national security, or preventing grave dangers to society.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR004,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार कुन अवस्थामा कुनै व्यक्तिलाई व्यक्तिगत स्वतन्त्रताबाट वञ्चित गर्न सकिन्छ?,केवल कानूनबमोजिम।,"Article 76,धारा ७६,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,

The Constitution states that a person can be subjected to personal freedom and deprivation of liberty only if they have committed a serious offense.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FR005,English,How many specific freedoms are guaranteed to every citizen under Article 17(2)?,Six freedoms,"Article 17(2) guarantees every citizen the right to freedom of expression, freedom of opinion and belief, freedom of association, and freedom of peaceful assembly.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FR005,Nepali,धारा १७(२) अन्तर्गत प्रत्येक नागरिकलाई कति वटा स्वतन्त्रताहरू सुनिश्चित गरिएको छ?,छ वटा स्वतन्त्रता,"The Constitution of Nepal (2015) provides for the following freedoms to all citizens:

*   Freedom of speech
*   Freedom of assembly
*   Freedom of religion
*   Right to privacy
*   Right to education
*   Right to a fair trial
*   Right to vote
*   Right to participate in political life",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FR006,English,Which constitutional freedom allows citizens to form political parties?,Freedom to form political parties,"Article 69,धारा ६९,Constitution of Nepal (2015) provides that the Vice-President performs the functions of the President during the President’s absence.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FR006,Nepali,नागरिकलाई राजनीतिक दल गठन गर्न दिने संवैधानिक स्वतन्त्रता कुन हो?,राजनीतिक दल गठन गर्ने स्वतन्त्रता,"Article 76,धारा ७६,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,The Constitution grants the Prime Minister the power to form the Council of Ministers.,Political parties can be formed by the President, but the President cannot form the Council of Ministers without the consent of the Parliament.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FR007,English,"Which freedom protects peaceful assembly, and which freedom protects the formation of unions and associations?",Freedom to assemble peaceably and without arms; Freedom to form unions and associations.,Article 19 and Article 36.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FR007,Nepali,"कुन स्वतन्त्रताले शान्तिपूर्ण भेला हुन पाउने अधिकार सुनिश्चित गर्छ, र कुन स्वतन्त्रताले संघ तथा संस्था गठन गर्न पाउने अधिकार सुनिश्चित गर्छ?",हतियारविहीन शान्तिपूर्ण भेला हुने स्वतन्त्रता; संघ तथा संस्था गठन गर्ने स्वतन्त्रता।,"Article 67(1).,Art. 67(1),Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,The independent body is responsible for organizing and conducting peaceful meetings.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FR008,English,"According to the Constitution, can the freedom of opinion and expression be reasonably restricted by law?",Yes. Reasonable restrictions may be imposed by law under the circumstances specified in the Constitution.,"Article 37(1) of the Constitution guarantees freedom of opinion and expression. However, this right is not absolute and can be limited by law when it harms others or public order. The Constitution does not explicitly define what constitutes a “reasonable restriction.” It relies on balancing these rights with other fundamental principles like national security, public safety, protection of honor, integrity, and the rights and freedoms of others.

Therefore, while freedom of opinion and expression is protected, the extent to which it can be reasonably restricted by law depends on the specific circumstances and the legal justification for such restriction. It’s a complex area that requires careful consideration within the context of the Constitution.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR008,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार विचार तथा अभिव्यक्तिको स्वतन्त्रतामा कानूनद्वारा मनासिब प्रतिबन्ध लगाउन सकिन्छ?,सकिन्छ। संविधानमा उल्लेखित अवस्थाहरूमा कानूनद्वारा मनासिब प्रतिबन्ध लगाउन सकिन्छ।,"Article 67(2) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) provides for the rights of the Vice-President to express their views and make recommendations. It states that the Vice-President shall perform the functions of the President during the President's absence, and they have the right to express their opinions and suggestions. Therefore, it is permissible for the Constitution to impose restrictions on the Vice-President’s freedom of expression.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FR009,English,"According to the Constitution, are all citizens equal before the law?",Yes. All citizens are equal before the law.,"Yes, according to the Constitution of Nepal (2015), Article 70 states that ""All citizens must be treated equally before the law.""",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR009,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार सबै नागरिक कानूनको दृष्टिमा समान छन्?,हुन्। सबै नागरिक कानूनको दृष्टिमा समान छन्।,"Article 69. ,Art. 68(a),Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,

The Constitution guarantees that all citizens are equal before the law.,धारा ६९।,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://law commission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FR010,English,Name any four grounds on which discrimination is prohibited under Article 18(2).,"Any four of the following: origin, religion, race, caste, tribe, sex, physical condition, health condition, marital status, pregnancy, economic condition, language, region, ideology, or similar grounds.","According to Article 18(2) of the Constitution of Nepal, discrimination is prohibited on the following grounds:

1.  **Race:** Discrimination based on race or ethnicity.
2.  **Religion:** Discrimination based on religious beliefs or practices.
3.  **Sex:** Discrimination based on gender.
4.  **Social Class/Cast:** Discrimination based on social class or caste.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR010,Nepali,धारा १८(२) अनुसार भेदभाव गर्न नहुने कुनै चार आधारहरूको नाम लेख्नुहोस्।,"निम्नमध्ये कुनै चार: उत्पत्ति, धर्म, जात, जाति, लिङ्ग, शारीरिक अवस्था, स्वास्थ्य अवस्था, वैवाहिक स्थिति, गर्भावस्था, आर्थिक अवस्था, भाषा, क्षेत्र, विचार वा यस्तै अन्य आधार।","धारा १८(२) अनुसार भेदभाव गर्न नहुने कुनै चार आधारहरू हुदैः

1.  **वंश:** जाति, थर, जन्मस्थान आदिमा भेदभाव गर्न गर्नुहोस्।
2.  **लिंग:** पुरुष, महिला, ट्रांसमान, आदिमा भेदभाव गर्न गर्नुहोस्।
3.  **धार्मिक:** कुनै खास आस्थाको व्यक्तिलाई धर्मी मान्ने प्रयास गर्न गर्नुहोस्।
4.  **सामाजिक वर्ग:** आर्थिक पृष्ठभूमि, सामाजिक समूह, या अन्य सामाजिक स्तरमा भेदभाव गर्न गर्नुहोस्।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR011,English,Which fundamental right protects the freedom of communication in Nepal?,Right to Communication,"Article 69, Section 3, Constitution of Nepal (2015) provides that the Vice-President performs the functions of the President during the President’s absence. This ensures a degree of continuity and allows for the President to remain accessible while the Vice-President handles duties.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FR011,Nepali,नेपालमा सञ्चारको स्वतन्त्रताको संरक्षण गर्ने मौलिक हक कुन हो?,सञ्चारसम्बन्धी हक,"The Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that the right to freedom of expression and information is a fundamental human right. It further clarifies that this right is essential for democratic governance, public participation, and accountability.  Specifically, it's enshrined in Article 19(1)(f).",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FR012,English,Which Article guarantees the Right to Communication?,Article 19,Article 69.,Correct,Not a strict error,False
FR012,Nepali,सञ्चारसम्बन्धी हकको व्यवस्था गर्ने धारा कुन हो?,धारा १९,"Article 76.,धारा ७६,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR013,English,"According to the Constitution, can newspapers or other media be closed merely because they published or broadcast news?",No. Newspapers and other communication media cannot be closed merely for publishing or broadcasting news.,"Article 67(2) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that “The government may close newspapers and other media outlets only when they publish or broadcast news that threatens national security, public order, or peace.”

Therefore, the answer is **yes**, newspapers and other media can be closed if they publish or broadcast news that threatens these things.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR013,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार समाचार प्रकाशित वा प्रसारण गरेको आधारमा मात्र पत्रपत्रिका वा सञ्चारमाध्यम बन्द गर्न पाइन्छ?,पाइँदैन। समाचार प्रकाशित वा प्रसारण गरेको आधारमा मात्र सञ्चारमाध्यम बन्द गर्न पाइँदैन।,"उत्तर: नहीं।

कारण: संविधान में यह स्पष्ट रूप से कहा गया है कि सरकार के पास कुछ भी करने की अनुमति नहीं दी गई है, जिसमें पत्रकार या मीडिया को बंद करना शामिल है। समाचार प्रकाशित और प्रसारण करने का अधिकार सरकार द्वारा नियंत्रित किया जाता है, लेकिन इस तरह के किसी भी कार्य को शुरू करने से पहले सरकार को सूचित करना होगा।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR014,English,"According to the Constitution, what right does every person have when arrested?",The right to be informed of the grounds for arrest.,"Article 68, Section 2, of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) guarantees every person a right to be informed of the charges against them and to have legal counsel.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR014,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार पक्राउ परेका प्रत्येक व्यक्तिलाई कुन अधिकार सुनिश्चित गरिएको छ?,पक्राउको कारणबारे जानकारी पाउने अधिकार।,"The Constitution of Nepal (2015) guarantees that every person arrested shall be entitled to the following rights:

*   **Right to a fair trial:** The accused has the right to a fair and impartial trial.
*   **Presumption of innocence:** The presumption of innocence applies to all individuals, including those who have been arrested.
*   **Legal representation:**  The accused has the right to legal counsel.
*   **Freedom from torture and cruel treatment:** The Constitution guarantees freedom from physical or psychological torture and cruel treatment.
*   **Right to be heard:** The accused has the right to be heard in their case.
*   **Protection against arbitrary detention:** The Constitution protects individuals from arbitrary detention without due process of law.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FR015,English,Which Article guarantees the Rights relating to Justice?,Article 20,Article 69.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR015,Nepali,न्यायसम्बन्धी हकको व्यवस्था गर्ने धारा कुन हो?,धारा २०,"Article 76.धारा ७६.Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR016,English,"According to the Constitution, what right does an accused person have regarding legal representation?",The right to consult and be defended by a legal practitioner of their choice.,"Article 76, Section 3, of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that “The accused has the right to be represented by a lawyer.”",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR016,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार अभियुक्तलाई कानुनी प्रतिनिधित्व सम्बन्धी कुन अधिकार प्राप्त छ?,आफ्नो रोजाइको कानून व्यवसायीसँग परामर्श गर्न तथा प्रतिरक्षा गराउन पाउने अधिकार।,"Article 76, Section 3, Constitution of Nepal (2015), https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,

The Constitution grants the Vice-President the authority to form the Council of Ministers.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FR017,English,"According to the Constitution, what information is a victim of crime entitled to receive?",Information about the investigation and proceedings of the case.,"The Constitution states that victims of crime are entitled to receive “protection and assistance” from the State. It doesn’t specify exactly *what* assistance they receive, but it does outline the general principle – providing protection and assistance.  More specifically, it says ""the State shall provide such protection and assistance as deemed necessary by the Government.""

Therefore, a victim of crime is entitled to receive **protection and assistance** from the State.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR017,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार अपराधपीडितले कुन जानकारी प्राप्त गर्ने अधिकार राख्छ?,अनुसन्धान तथा मुद्दाको कारबाही सम्बन्धी जानकारी।,"Article 76,धारा ७६,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,The victim has the right to obtain information regarding the crime committed against them.,संविधानअनुसार अपराधपीडितलेCrime विरुद्ध उनको सामना गरिएको जानकारी प्राप्त गर्ने अधिकार राख्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR018,English,Which Article guarantees the Rights of Victims of Crime?,Article 21,"Article 83,धारा ८३,Constitution of Nepal (2015) provides for the rights of victims of crime.,Art. 83,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR018,Nepali,अपराधपीडितको हकको व्यवस्था गर्ने धारा कुन हो?,धारा २१,"Article 76.,धारा ७६,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR019,English,"According to the Constitution, what treatment is prohibited while a person is in custody?","Torture and cruel, inhuman or degrading treatment.","Article 76, Section 3, Constitution of Nepal (2015), https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,

The Constitution prohibits the treatment of a person in custody with “any form of abuse or cruel treatment.”",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR019,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार हिरासतमा रहेको व्यक्तिलाई कस्तो व्यवहार गर्न निषेध गरिएको छ?,"यातना तथा क्रूर, अमानवीय वा अपमानजनक व्यवहार।",The Constitution of Nepal (2015) provides that the President shall not allow the Vice-President to be held in custody.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FR020,English,"According to the Constitution, which Article protects victims of crime, and which Article protects persons against torture while in custody?","Article 21 protects victims of crime, while Article 22 protects persons against torture in custody.","Article 67.धारा ७६.,धारा ७७.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FR020,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार कुन धाराले अपराधपीडितको हक सुनिश्चित गर्छ र कुन धाराले हिरासतमा यातनाविरुद्धको हक सुनिश्चित गर्छ?,धारा २१ ले अपराधपीडितको हक सुनिश्चित गर्छ भने धारा २२ ले हिरासतमा यातनाविरुद्धको हक सुनिश्चित गर्छ।,"संविधानअनुसार, अपराधपीडितको हक सुनिश्चित गर्ने धारा लेख ७६ मा रहेको छ। तर, हिरासतमा यातनाविरुद्धको हक सुनिश्चित गर्ने धारा लेख ६८ मा रहेको छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
FR021,English,Which constitutional right protects a person against preventive detention except as provided by law?,Right against Preventive Detention,"Article 68, Section 2, Constitution of Nepal (2015) provides protection against preventive detention.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR021,Nepali,कानूनबमोजिम बाहेक प्रतिरोधात्मक नजरबन्दबाट व्यक्तिलाई संरक्षण गर्ने संवैधानिक हक कुन हो?,प्रतिरोधात्मक नजरबन्दविरुद्धको हक,"संविधानअनुसार राष्ट्रपतिको अनुपस्थितिमा राष्ट्रपतिको कार्य कसले सम्पादन गर्छ?,Through the Vice-President.,उपराष्ट्रपति।,Article 67(2) provides that the Vice-President performs the functions of the President during the President's absence. ,Art. 67(2),Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,
PR014,Constitution & Law,Vice-President,Fact Retrieval,Easy,""According to the Constitution, what is the role of the Vice-President during the President's absence?"",The President.,The Vice-President।,The Vice-President performs the functions of the President during the President’s absence. ,Art. 67(2),Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,
PR015,Constitution & Law,Vice-President,Comparison,Medium,""According to the Constitution, what is the role of the Vice-President during the President’s absence?"",""The President resigns to the Vice-president, while the Vice-president resigns to the President."",President र उपराष्ट्रपतिले एकमेतका रूपमा अलग काम गर्छन्।,Compares Articles 65(a) and 68(a).,""Arts. 65(a), 68(a)"",Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,
PR016,Constitution & Law,Vice-President,Entity Identification,Medium,""According to the Constitution, what is the role of the Vice-president during the President’s absence?"",The previous office becomes vacant automatically.,The previous office स्वतः रिक्त हुन्छ।,Article 67(3).,Art. 67(3),Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,
PR017,Constitution & Law,Representation,Definition,Medium,""According to the Constitution, what is the role of the Vice-president during the President’s absence?"",They must represent different sex or different community.,फरक लिङ्ग वा फरक समुदायको प्रतिनिधित्व सुनिश्चित हुनुपर्छ।,Article 70 requires representation of different sex or community. ,Art. 70,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,
