FR022,English,Which practice is prohibited under Article 24 of the Constitution?,Untouchability and discrimination,Article 24 of the Constitution prohibits the practice of “promoting or encouraging the dissemination of false information.”,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FR022,Nepali,संविधानको धारा २४ अनुसार कुन प्रथालाई निषेध गरिएको छ?,छुवाछुत तथा भेदभाव,Article 24 provides that any practice which is contrary to the constitution shall be prohibited.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FR023,English,"According to the Constitution, does every citizen have the right to acquire, own, sell and otherwise dispose of property?","Yes, subject to law.","Article 69.,धारा ६९,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,

The Constitution guarantees that every citizen has the right to acquire, own, sell and otherwise dispose of property.,Art. 69,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://law commission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FR023,Nepali,"संविधानअनुसार प्रत्येक नागरिकलाई सम्पत्ति आर्जन, स्वामित्व, बिक्री तथा अन्य रूपमा उपयोग वा हस्तान्तरण गर्ने हक छ?","छ, कानूनबमोजिम।","Article 67(3) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) provides for the rights of citizens to acquire, possess, transfer, and use property. It states that citizens have the right to acquire property through various means, including inheritance, purchase, sale, etc.

Here's a breakdown:

*   **Article 67(3):** This article outlines the rights of citizens regarding property ownership and transfers.
*   It ensures that individuals can legally own and control their assets.
*   The Constitution guarantees fundamental rights related to property, including the right to acquire, possess, transfer, and use property.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FR024,English,"According to the Constitution, what does the right to freedom of religion primarily guarantee?","The freedom to profess, practice and protect one's religion according to one's faith.","The right to freedom of religion primarily guarantees the right to practice and maintain religious beliefs and practices without interference from the government. It encompasses the fundamental rights related to religious expression, worship, and participation in religious activities.  Specifically, it ensures the ability to freely choose one's faith or lack thereof, as well as the protection against discrimination based on religious belief.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR024,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार धर्मसम्बन्धी स्वतन्त्रताको हकले मुख्य रूपमा के सुनिश्चित गर्छ?,"आफ्नो आस्थाअनुसार धर्म मान्ने, अभ्यास गर्ने तथा संरक्षण गर्ने स्वतन्त्रता।",The Constitution of Nepal (2015) ensures the rights of religious freedom to the main extent.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FR025,English,Which Article guarantees the Right to Information?,Article 27,"Article 18. ,Art. 18, Constitution of Nepal (2015)",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR025,Nepali,सूचनाको हक सुनिश्चित गर्ने धारा कुन हो?,धारा २७,"Article 76.धारा ७६.,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://law commission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR026,English,"Which fundamental right protects the privacy of a person's residence, property, documents, data, correspondence and personal information?",Right to Privacy,"Article 36.,Art. 36, Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FR026,Nepali,"व्यक्तिको घर, सम्पत्ति, कागजात, तथ्याङ्क, पत्राचार तथा व्यक्तिगत जानकारीको गोपनीयताको संरक्षण गर्ने मौलिक हक कुन हो?",गोपनीयताको हक,"संविधानअनुसार राष्ट्रपतिको अनुपस्थितिमा राष्ट्रपतिको कार्य कसले सम्पादन गर्छ?,Through the Prime Minister.,प्रधानमन्त्रीमार्फत।,Article 67. ,Art. 67,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FR027,English,Which level of law determines punishment for acts prohibited under the Right against Exploitation?,Federal law,Article 67(2) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015).,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FR027,Nepali,शोषणविरुद्धको हक अन्तर्गत निषेध गरिएका कार्यको सजाय कुन तहको कानूनले निर्धारण गर्छ?,संघीय कानून,"The Constitution of Nepal (2015) provides for the punishment for offenses against the President, Vice-President, and other officials. It states that the punishment will be determined by the Council of Ministers based on the recommendations of the Vice-President. Therefore, the constitution does not provide a specific penalty for such offenses.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FR028,English,"Which constitutional right protects a clean environment, and which protects access to health services?","Article 30 protects the right to a clean environment, while Article 35 protects the right relating to health.","The Constitution of Nepal does not explicitly define specific rights related to environmental protection or healthcare access. However, the Constitution outlines fundamental rights and freedoms that indirectly influence these areas. Here’s a breakdown based on relevant provisions:

*   **Environmental Protection:** The Constitution guarantees the right to a healthy environment and the right to enjoy it. This is enshrined in Article 36(1).
*   **Access to Health Services:** The Constitution ensures access to healthcare for all citizens, including the rights to life, health, and dignity. It’s found in Article 25.

Therefore, while not explicitly stated, **Article 36(1) guarantees a healthy environment**, and **Article 25 ensures access to healthcare.**",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR028,Nepali,कुन संवैधानिक हकले स्वच्छ वातावरणको संरक्षण गर्छ र कुन हकले स्वास्थ्य सेवामा पहुँच सुनिश्चित गर्छ?,धारा ३० ले स्वच्छ वातावरणको हक सुनिश्चित गर्छ भने धारा ३५ ले स्वास्थ्यसम्बन्धी हक सुनिश्चित गर्छ।,"Article 67(2) provides that the Vice-President performs the functions of the President during the President's absence. This ensures a clean environment while the President is absent. Article 68(a) provides that the President submits a resignation to the Vice-President, ensuring continuity in leadership.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FR029,English,"According to the Constitution, which two groups are guaranteed both free education and compulsory basic education?",All citizens at the basic level.,Article 70 provides that separate offices shall exist for the President and the Vice-President.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FR029,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार निःशुल्क शिक्षा तथा अनिवार्य आधारभूत शिक्षा दुवैको सुनिश्चितता कुन समूहका लागि गरिएको छ?,आधारभूत तहका सबै नागरिकका लागि।,Article 69 provides that the Constitution ensures free education and compulsory basic education for all.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FR030,English,"According to the Constitution, which two fundamental rights together balance citizens' access to public information and protection of personal information?",The Right to Information and the Right to Privacy.,Article 76(3) and Article 77.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FR030,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार सार्वजनिक सूचनामा पहुँच र व्यक्तिगत जानकारीको संरक्षणबीच सन्तुलन कायम गर्ने दुई मौलिक हक कुन-कुन हुन्?,सूचनाको हक र गोपनीयताको हक।,"संविधानअनुसार सार्वजनिक सूचनामा पहुँच र व्यक्तिगत माहितीको संरक्षण बीच सन्तुलन कायम गर्ने दुवै मौलिक अधिकार खाली निम्न अनुसार छन्:

1.  **सहिष्णुता (Freedom of Information):** जनताले सरकारी जानकारी प्राप्त गर्न पाउँदा, त्यसलाई सुरक्षित राख्ने अधिकार।
2.  **व्यक्तिगत डेटा सुरक्षा (Personal Data Protection):** व्यक्तिगत माहितीको रक्षा र गोपनीयता बनाएर राखनका अधिकार।
3.  **जानकारीको पहुँचमा अधिकार (Right to Access Information):** सरकारले सार्वजनिक रूपमै जानकारी प्रदान गर्दा, जनताले त्यसलाई जान्ने अधिकार।
4.  **व्यक्तिगत जानकारीको खुलासा नथमेल्न काँसोस अधिकार (Right to Not Reveal Personal Information):** व्यक्तिगत माहितीको खुलासा गर्नबाट बचाउँदै, त्यसलाई प्रकट नगर्ने अधिकार।

यो तीनौका अधिकार सरकारले सार्वजनिक सूचनामा पहुँच र व्यक्तिगत जानकारीको संरक्षण बीच सन्तुलन कायम गर्ने तरिका प्रदान गर्दछन्।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
FR031,English,"Which constitutional right guarantees every community the right to preserve and promote its language, script, culture, cultural civilization and heritage?",Right to Language and Culture,"Article 67, Section 3, Constitution of Nepal (2015), https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,Article 67 states that every community has the right to preserve and promote its language, script, culture, cultural civilization and heritage.,https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,",Correct,Not a strict error,False
FR031,Nepali,"प्रत्येक समुदायलाई आफ्नो भाषा, लिपि, संस्कृति, सांस्कृतिक सभ्यता तथा सम्पदाको संरक्षण र प्रवर्द्धन गर्ने हक सुनिश्चित गर्ने संवैधानिक हक कुन हो?",भाषा तथा संस्कृतिसम्बन्धी हक,"संविधानअनुसार राष्ट्रपतिको अनुपस्थितिमा राष्ट्रपतिको कार्य कसले सम्पादन गर्छ?,Through the Prime Minister.,प्रधानमन्त्रीमार्फत।,Article 67(2).,Art. 67(2),Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,PR011,Constitution & Law,Vice-President,Fact Retrieval,Easy,""According to the Constitution, which Article provides that the Vice-President performs the functions of the President during the President's absence?"",Article 69.,धारा ६९।,Article 69 states that these provisions are the same as those applicable to the President.,Art. 69,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,PR012,Constitution & Law,Vice-President,Constitutional Provision,Easy,""Which Article provides that the Vice-president performs the functions of the President during the President's absence?"",Article 67(2).,धारा ६७।,Article 67(2),Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,PR013,Constitution & Law,Vice-President,Fact Retrieval,Easy,""According to the Constitution, which Article provides that the Vice-president performs the functions of the President during the President's absence?"",Article 69.,धारा ६९।,Article 69 states that these provisions are the same as those applicable to the President.,Art. 69,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,PR014,Constitution & Law,Vice-President,Comparison,Medium,""According to the Constitution, to whom does the Vice-president submit a written resignation?,The President.,The Vice-president submits a written resignation to the President."",The President resigns to the Vice-president, while the Vice-president resigns to the President."",The President resigns to the Vice-president, while the Vice-president resigns to the President।,Compares Articles 65(a) and 68(a).,""Arts. 65(a), 68(a)"",Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,PR015,Constitution & Law,Vice-President,Entity Identification,Medium,""According to the Constitution, before whom does the President take the oath of office and secrecy?"",The Chief Justice.,The President takes the oath of office and secrecy before the Chief Justice.,The Chief Justice.,The President takes the oath of office and secrecy before the Chief Justice।,Article 71.,Art. 71,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,PR016,Constitution & Law,Vice-President,Fact Retrieval,Easy,""According to the Constitution, before whom does the Vice-president take the oath of office and secrecy?"",The President.,The Vice-president takes the oath of office and secrecy before the President."",The President takes the oath of office and secrecy before the President।,PR017,Constitution & Law,Representation,Definition,Medium,""According to the Constitution, what principle must be ensured when electing the President and the Vice-President?"",They must represent different sex or different community.,They must represent different sex or different community.,Article 70 requires representation of different sex or community.,Art. 70,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,PR018,Constitution & Law,Vice-President,Multi-hop Factual,Hard,""According to the Constitution, if a person holding a political office filled by election, nomination or appointment is appointed as the Vice-president, what happens to that office?"",""The previous office becomes vacant automatically.,The previous office becomes vacant automatically।,Article 67(3).,Art. 67(3),Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,PR019,Constitution & Law,Vice-President,Fact Retrieval,Easy,""According to the Constitution, before whom does the Vice-president take the oath of office and secrecy?"",The President.,The Vice-president takes the oath of office and secrecy before the President."",The President takes the oath of office and secrecy before the President।,FE001,Constitution & Law,Federal Executive,Fact Retrieval,Easy,""According to the Constitution, in whose name are all Federal executive functions performed?,The Council of Ministers.,The Council of Ministers performs all federal executive functions.,The Council of Ministers.,The Council of Ministers performs all federal executive functions।,FE002,Constitution & Law,Prime Minister,Constitutional Provision,Easy,Which Article provides for the constitution of the Council of Ministers??,Article 76.,धारा ७६।,Article 76 governs the appointment of the Prime Minister and formation of the Council of Ministers.,Art. 76,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,PR013,Constitution & Law,Vice-President,Fact Retrieval,Easy,""According to the Constitution, in whose name are all Federal executive functions performed?,The Council of Ministers.,The Council of Ministers performs all federal executive functions.,The Council of Ministers.,The Council of Ministers performs all federal executive functions।,FE004,Constitution & Law,Vice-President,Comparison,Medium,""According to the Constitution, before whom does the Vice-president submit a written resignation?,The President.,The Vice-president submits a written resignation to the President."",The President resigns to the Vice-president, while the Vice-president resigns to the President।,Compares Articles 65(a) and 68(a).,""Arts. 65(a), 68(a)"",Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,PR015,Constitution & Law,Vice-President,Entity Identification,Medium,""According to the Constitution, before whom does the President take the oath of office and secrecy?,The Chief Justice.,The President takes the oath of office and secrecy before the Chief Justice."",The Chief Justice.,The President takes the oath of office and secrecy before the Chief Justice।,",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR032,English,"According to the Constitution, who has the right to employment?",Every citizen,"Article 76, Section 3, Constitution of Nepal (2015) provides that the Prime Minister is appointed by the Council of Ministers and is responsible for the employment of officials.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FR032,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार रोजगारीको हक कसलाई प्राप्त छ?,प्रत्येक नागरिक,"Article 83 of the Constitution of Nepal provides for the rights and responsibilities of employees. It states that employees have certain rights, including the right to fair wages, working conditions, and protection against unfair dismissal. They also have responsibilities such as fulfilling their duties and maintaining a safe workplace.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FR033,English,"According to the Constitution, what does the Right to Labour guarantee to every worker?","The right to appropriate remuneration, facilities and social security, and the right to form and join trade unions in accordance with law.",Article 83 of the Constitution guarantees every worker the right to labour.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FR033,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार श्रमसम्बन्धी हकले प्रत्येक श्रमिकलाई के सुनिश्चित गर्दछ?,"उपयुक्त पारिश्रमिक, सुविधा, सामाजिक सुरक्षा तथा कानूनबमोजिम ट्रेड युनियन गठन र त्यसमा सहभागी हुने हक।","Through the Constitution, labor laws ensure that each worker receives a fair wage and benefits. It also guarantees workers' rights to safe working conditions, overtime pay, vacation time, and protection against unfair dismissal.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FR034,English,"According to the Constitution, what basic health service is guaranteed to every citizen?",Free basic health services.,"Article 49, Section 3 of the Constitution guarantees every citizen the right to healthcare.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FR034,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार प्रत्येक नागरिकलाई कुन आधारभूत स्वास्थ्य सेवा सुनिश्चित गरिएको छ?,निःशुल्क आधारभूत स्वास्थ्य सेवा।,"Through the Constitution of Nepal (2015), Article 67(2).,Art. 67(2),Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,

The Constitution guarantees a fundamental health service to every citizen.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FR035,English,Which Article guarantees the Right relating to Food?,Article 36,Article 69.,Correct,Not a strict error,False
FR035,Nepali,खाद्यसम्बन्धी हक सुनिश्चित गर्ने धारा कुन हो?,धारा ३६,"Article 76.,धारा ७६,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR036,English,"According to the Constitution, what protection does the Right to Housing provide against eviction?",No citizen shall be evicted from the housing owned or occupied by them except in accordance with law.,Article 83 of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) provides protection against eviction based on a person’s right to housing. It states that “The State shall ensure the right to housing for all citizens.”,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FR036,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार आवाससम्बन्धी हकले कसरी जबरजस्ती घरबाट हटाउन नपाइने व्यवस्था गरेको छ?,कानूनबमोजिम बाहेक कुनै पनि नागरिकलाई निजले बसोबास गरेको वा स्वामित्वमा रहेको आवासबाट बेदखल गर्न पाइँदैन।,"Article 67(2) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) provides for the procedure to remove a person from the position of President, and it states that the Vice-President shall perform the functions of the President during the President's absence. This means that the Vice-President is appointed by the President and can take over the duties of the President without being removed.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FR037,English,Which group is specifically guaranteed the right to safe motherhood and reproductive health under the Constitution?,Women,"Article 76, Section 3, Constitution of Nepal (2015), https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FR037,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार सुरक्षित मातृत्व तथा प्रजनन स्वास्थ्यको हक विशेष रूपमा कसलाई सुनिश्चित गरिएको छ?,महिला,"Through the Constitution, the Government of Nepal is responsible for ensuring the safety and reproductive health of women and children. Specifically, Article 67(2) states that the Vice-President performs the functions of the President during the President’s absence. This includes ensuring the safety and reproductive health of women and children.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FR038,English,"According to the Constitution, every child has the right to what type of identity?",Name and birth registration,Every child has the right to a unique identification number.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
