FR039,English,"Which constitutional Article guarantees the rights of women, and which Article guarantees the rights of children?","Article 38 guarantees the rights of women, while Article 39 guarantees the rights of children.","Article 69 provides that the qualifications, election procedure, and term of office of the Vice-President shall be the same as those of the President.  It also states that the Constitution ensures the rights of women. Article 70 provides for the establishment of separate offices for the President and Vice-President.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FR039,Nepali,कुन धाराले महिलाको हक सुनिश्चित गर्छ र कुन धाराले बालबालिकाको हक सुनिश्चित गर्छ?,धारा ३८ ले महिलाको हक सुनिश्चित गर्छ भने धारा ३९ ले बालबालिकाको हक सुनिश्चित गर्छ।,Article 69 provides that the Vice-President performs the functions of the President during the President's absence.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FR040,English,"According to the Constitution, which Article guarantees the right to constitutional remedies for the enforcement of fundamental rights, and which Article sets out the fundamental duties of citizens?","Article 46 guarantees the right to constitutional remedies, while Article 48 sets out the fundamental duties of citizens.",Article 67.धारा ७६.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FR040,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार मौलिक हकको कार्यान्वयनका लागि संवैधानिक उपचारको हक कुन धाराले सुनिश्चित गर्छ र नागरिकका कर्तव्य कुन धारामा उल्लेख गरिएको छ?,धारा ४६ ले संवैधानिक उपचारको हक सुनिश्चित गर्छ भने धारा ४८ मा नागरिकका कर्तव्य उल्लेख गरिएको छ।,"Article 77.धारा ७७, Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,The constitutional provisions must be implemented effectively and efficiently.,संविधानअनुसार मौलिक हक कार्यान्वयनको लागि संवैधानिक उपचारले सुनिश्चित गर्छ कि नागरिकका कर्तव्य कुन धारामा उल्लेख गरिएको छ?",Correct,Not a strict error,False
DP001,English,"According to the Constitution, what are the directive principles, policies and obligations intended to serve as?",Guiding principles for the governance of the State.,"The Constitution states that the Directive Principles, Policies, and Obligations intended to serve as are to ensure social justice, equality, and development. It further clarifies that these provisions should be implemented in a way that promotes the welfare of all citizens.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DP001,Nepali,"संविधानअनुसार निर्देशक सिद्धान्त, नीति तथा दायित्वहरू केका लागि मार्गदर्शक हुन्?",राज्य सञ्चालनका मार्गदर्शक सिद्धान्त।,"संविधानअनुसार निर्देशक सिद्धान्त, नीति तथा दायित्वहरू कार्यान्वयनको लागि मार्गदर्शन र तरिकाहरूको रूपमा कार्य गर्छन्। यो संविधानले सरकारलाई धर्मी निर्णय गर्न र सार्वजनिक नीतिकाहरूलाई सही दिशानिर्देशित गराउन मद्दत गर्दछ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DP002,English,"Which Article states that the directive principles, policies and obligations are guiding principles for the governance of the State?",Article 49,"Article 76.,धारा ७६, Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DP002,Nepali,"निर्देशक सिद्धान्त, नीति तथा दायित्व राज्य सञ्चालनका मार्गदर्शक सिद्धान्त हुन् भन्ने व्यवस्था कुन धाराले गरेको छ?",धारा ४९,"Article 76.,धारा ७६, Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DP003,English,"According to the Constitution, what is the political objective of the State?","To establish a public welfare system of governance based on justice, the rule of law, fundamental rights, human rights, gender equality, proportional inclusion, participation and social justice.",The Constitution states that the political objective of the state is to represent different sex or different community.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DP003,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार राज्यको राजनीतिक उद्देश्य के हो?,"न्याय, कानूनी शासन, मौलिक हक, मानव अधिकार, लैङ्गिक समानता, समानुपातिक समावेशिता, सहभागिता तथा सामाजिक न्यायमा आधारित जनकल्याणकारी शासन प्रणाली स्थापना गर्नु।","Article 74 provides that the purpose of the state is to ensure political stability and harmony through a multi-party, competitive, federal, democratic, republican, parliamentary form of government based on pluralism.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DP004,English,"According to the Constitution, what type of economy is the State directed to develop?",A socialism-oriented independent and prosperous economy.,"A multi-party, competitive, federal, democratic, republican, parliamentary form of government based on pluralism.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DP004,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार राज्यले कस्तो अर्थतन्त्र विकास गर्ने उद्देश्य राखेको छ?,समाजवादउन्मुख स्वतन्त्र तथा समृद्ध अर्थतन्त्र।,"The Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that the State has the objective of developing the economy through sustainable and inclusive growth. It emphasizes a balanced approach, aiming for economic development while ensuring social equity and environmental protection.  Specifically, it mentions:

*   **Sustainable Development:** Economic growth must be environmentally sound and not deplete natural resources.
*   **Inclusive Growth:** The benefits of economic progress should be shared across all segments of society (including marginalized groups).
*   **Promoting Social Equity:** Policies should address poverty reduction, improve access to education and healthcare, and ensure fair distribution of wealth.

Essentially, the Constitution calls for an economy that is both prosperous and just.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
DP005,English,"Which objective relates to establishing a public welfare system of governance, and which relates to developing a socialism-oriented economy?","The political objective relates to public welfare governance, while the economic objective relates to developing a socialism-oriented economy.","Article 76 provides for the constitution of the Council of Ministers, while Article 66(2) discusses the functions of the President during his absence. Therefore, the answer is **Article 76**.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DP005,Nepali,जनकल्याणकारी शासन प्रणाली स्थापना गर्ने उद्देश्य कुन हो र समाजवादउन्मुख अर्थतन्त्र विकास गर्ने उद्देश्य कुन हो?,राजनीतिक उद्देश्य जनकल्याणकारी शासनसँग सम्बन्धित छ भने आर्थिक उद्देश्य समाजवादउन्मुख अर्थतन्त्रसँग सम्बन्धित छ।,"The Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that the objective of establishing a welfare state is to promote जनकल्याणकारी शासन प्रणाली। This means it aims to create a system where all citizens benefit from government policies and programs.

Furthermore, the constitution also outlines the objectives for socialistic economic development:

*   **Promoting Social Justice:** The Constitution emphasizes reducing inequality and promoting fairness in society through measures like progressive taxation and social safety nets.
*   **Investing in Human Capital:** It aims to improve education, healthcare, and other essential services to enhance human potential and opportunity.
*   **Strengthening the Economy:**  The constitution encourages a socialist economic model that prioritizes public investment, worker empowerment, and sustainable development.

In essence, it's about creating a society where everyone has opportunities for a better life through government intervention and social programs.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
DP006,English,"According to the Constitution, what is the first policy relating to national unity and national security?","To protect the freedom, sovereignty, territorial integrity and independence of Nepal while keeping national unity intact.","Article 76.,धारा ७६,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DP006,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार राष्ट्रिय एकता तथा राष्ट्रिय सुरक्षासम्बन्धी पहिलो नीति के हो?,"राष्ट्रिय एकतालाई अक्षुण्ण राख्दै नेपालको स्वतन्त्रता, सार्वभौमसत्ता, भौगोलिक अखण्डता तथा स्वतन्त्रताको संरक्षण गर्नु।","Article 67(1).,Art. 67(1),Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,National Unity and National Security",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DP007,English,"According to the Constitution, which three security organizations are specifically mentioned in the national security policy?","Nepal Army, Nepal Police and Armed Police Force Nepal.","The Constitution mentions the following three security organizations in the national security policy:

1.  Police Force
2.  Army
3.  Intelligence Services (also known as the National Security Bureau)

Let me know if you’d like a more detailed explanation of each organization's role!",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DP007,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार राष्ट्रिय सुरक्षा नीतिमा विशेष रूपमा उल्लेख गरिएका तीन सुरक्षा निकाय कुन-कुन हुन्?,"नेपाली सेना, नेपाल प्रहरी र सशस्त्र प्रहरी बल नेपाल।","संविधानअनुसार राष्ट्रिय सुरक्षा नीतिमा विशेष रूपतया उल्लेख गरिएका तीन सुरक्षा निकाय खाली पठाए गेले आहेत. ते खालीलप्रमाणे:

1.  सुरक्षा छत्र会
2.  सुरक्षा नेपाल
3.  सुरक्षा त्रिकोण",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DP008,English,"According to the Constitution, which principle guides the relationship between the Federal Units in the system of governance?",Cooperative federalism.,"A multi-party, competitive, federal, democratic, republican, parliamentary form of government based on pluralism.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DP008,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार शासन प्रणालीमा संघीय एकाइहरूबीचको सम्बन्ध कुन सिद्धान्तद्वारा निर्देशित हुन्छ?,सहकारी संघीयता।,"Article 74 of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) provides for the relationship between the Federal Executive and the Regional Governments. It states that the Council of Ministers is responsible for issuing general directives and regulating the governance of Nepal.  The Constitution also emphasizes the importance of maintaining a balance between the federal system and regional governments, ensuring their autonomy and mutual cooperation.

Therefore, the connection between the Federal Executive and Regional Governments is guided by the principles of **mutual cooperation and balance** as outlined in Article 74.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
DP009,English,"According to the Constitution, what principle should be incorporated into the system of governance on the basis of local autonomy and decentralization?",The principle of proportional participation.,The Constitution emphasizes representing different sex or community when electing the President and Vice-President. It also requires Nepal government to provide necessary employees and other arrangements for the functioning of the offices of the President and Vice-President.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DP009,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार स्थानीय स्वायत्तता र विकेन्द्रीकरणका आधारमा शासन प्रणालीमा कुन सिद्धान्त समावेश गरिनुपर्छ?,समानुपातिक सहभागिताको सिद्धान्त।,"संविधानअनुसार स्थानीय स्वायत्तता र विकेन्द्रीकरणका आधारमा शासन प्रणालीमा निम्न सिद्धान्तहरू समावेश गरिनुपर्छन्:

*   **संसदीय व्यवस्था:** संविधानले स्थानीय सरकारलाई संसदको अधीनमा काम गर्न दिन्छ, जसले यसलाई शक्तिशाली बनाउँदैन।
*   **बहुमतवाद:** स्थानीय स्वराज्यहरूको सहभागिता सुनिश्चित गर्छ ताकि सबै आवाजहरू पहिचान गरिन्छ।
*   **सहिष्णुता:** विभिन्न प्रकारका स्थानीय स्वायत्तताहरूलाई स्वीकार्छ र समावेश गर्छ।
*   **सामुदायिक अधिकार:** स्थानीयहरले आफ्नो समुदायको विकासमा सहभागी भएर योगदान गर्न पाउँछन्।
*   **सशयता:** स्थानीय सरकारहरूको क्षमता, स्रोत, तरिका, और प्रभावको स्तर समान बनाउनुपर्छ।

यी सिद्धान्तहरू समावेश गरेर, संविधानले स्थानीय स्वराज्यहरूको स्वायत्ततालाई बलस्त पार्छ र विकेंद्रीकरणलाई कम गर्छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
DP010,English,"According to the Constitution, what is the primary objective of Nepal's international relations?","To enhance the dignity of the nation in the world community while safeguarding Nepal's freedom, sovereignty, territorial integrity, independence and national interest.","The Constitution outlines that Nepal’s primary objective of its international relations is to promote peace and stability in the region. It emphasizes diplomacy, cooperation with neighboring countries, and upholding international law.  Specifically, it states that Nepal aims to be a responsible member of the global community while safeguarding its sovereignty and national interests.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DP010,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार नेपालको अन्तर्राष्ट्रिय सम्बन्धको मुख्य उद्देश्य के हो?,"नेपालको स्वतन्त्रता, सार्वभौमसत्ता, भौगोलिक अखण्डता, स्वतन्त्रता तथा राष्ट्रिय हितको संरक्षण गर्दै विश्व समुदायमा राष्ट्रको प्रतिष्ठा अभिवृद्धि गर्नु।","Through the President., राष्ट्रपतिको पर्दा।,Article 67(2), Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,

The main objective of international relations according to the constitution is to be performed by the President.,Art. 67(2), Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://law commission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DP011,English,"According to the Constitution, what should remain intact while protecting Nepal's freedom, sovereignty, territorial integrity and independence?",National unity.,"The Constitution of Nepal (2015) outlines several principles that are crucial for maintaining these fundamental aspects. Here’s a breakdown of what remains intact while protecting Nepal’s freedoms, sovereignty, territorial integrity, and independence, as outlined in the constitution:

*   **Freedom:** The Constitution guarantees fundamental rights and freedoms to all citizens, including freedom of speech, religion, assembly, and association.
*   **Sovereignty:**  The Constitution affirms Nepal's sovereign right to self-determination and its ability to govern itself without external interference. It emphasizes the importance of national identity and cultural heritage.
*   **Territorial Integrity:** The constitution establishes a clear demarcation of Nepal’s territory, recognizing its unique geographical boundaries and emphasizing its sovereignty over its land and resources.
*   **Independence:**  The Constitution guarantees Nepal's independence from foreign control and ensures that it maintains the ability to pursue its own interests without undue influence or interference from other nations.

Essentially, the constitution establishes a framework where these principles are protected through legal mechanisms, constitutional provisions, and the protection of fundamental rights.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DP011,Nepali,"संविधानअनुसार नेपालको स्वतन्त्रता, सार्वभौमसत्ता, भौगोलिक अखण्डता तथा स्वतन्त्रताको संरक्षण गर्दा केलाई अक्षुण्ण राख्नुपर्छ?",राष्ट्रिय एकता।,"संविधानअनुसार नेपालको स्वतन्त्रता, सार्वभौमसत्ता, भौगोलिक अखण्डता तथा स्वतन्त्रताको संरक्षण गर्दा, राष्ट्रले निम्न उपाय अपनाउनुपर्ने छ:

*   **आत्मनिर्भर विकास:** देशका अर्थव्यवस्थालाई आत्मनिर्भर बनाउने प्रयासमा ध्यान செலுத்தुपर्नु र विदेशीDependence कम गर्नुपर्छ।
*   **सुरक्षाबन्द:** नेपालको सुरक्षा भटभानीलाई तत्काल समाधान गरुपनासाथ, सीमावर्ती क्षेत्रहरू सुरक्षित राख्ने उपायय अपनाउनुपनासाथै जाँच गरनी पर्छ।
*   **आख़ण्डताको संरक्षण:** नेपालका भूभाग र प्राकृतिक सौदेहरूको रक्षा गर्नुपर्छ।
*   **सशक्त राज्य:** राष्ट्रको शक्तिलाई बलस्त राख्नुपर्नु र जनताको भल्तीमा अधिकार दिने व्यवस्था गर्नुपनासाथ, भ्रष्टाचारलाई हटाउनुपनासाथ जाँच गरनी पर्छ।
*   **आचारसंहिता:** नेपालका समाजमा नैतिकता, आचारसंहितासहित जझिसनुपर्छ।

यो सबै उपायहरूले नेपालको स्वतन्त्रता, सार्वभौमसत्ता, भौगोलिक अखण्डता र स्वतन्त्रताको संरक्षणलाई सुरक्षित राख्नेछन्।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
DP012,English,"According to the Constitution, which three dimensions of diversity are specifically mentioned in promoting national unity among communities?","Religion, language and culture.",Article 70 provides that it shall provide the necessary employees and other arrangements required for the functioning of the offices of the President and the Vice-President.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
DP012,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार समुदायहरूबीच राष्ट्रिय एकता प्रवर्द्धन गर्दा कुन तीन प्रकारका विविधतालाई विशेष रूपमा उल्लेख गरिएको छ?,"धर्म, भाषा र संस्कृति।","Article 76,धारा ७६, Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,

The article states that the Council of Ministers is formed to promote national unity. It also mentions that diversity should be celebrated and respected.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
DP013,English,"According to the Constitution, what kind of security system should the State develop to maintain law and order?",A national security system.,"Article 76, Section 3, Constitution of Nepal (2015), https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,

The Constitution outlines the responsibilities of the government in maintaining law and order. It states that the State should develop a security system to maintain law and order.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DP013,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार कानून र व्यवस्था कायम गर्न राज्यले कस्तो सुरक्षा प्रणाली विकास गर्नुपर्छ?,राष्ट्रिय सुरक्षा प्रणाली।,"Through the Constitution, the State must develop a security system to safeguard its interests and ensure stability. This is outlined in Article 76 of the Constitution of Nepal (2015). It states that the State shall develop a security system to safeguard its interests and ensure stability.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
DP014,English,"According to the Constitution, what is meant by good governance in the context of public administration?","Public administration that is fair, competent, impartial, transparent, corruption-free, accountable and participatory while ensuring equal and easy access to public services.","Article 76,धारा ७६,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,Good governance in the context of public administration refers to practices and principles that ensure accountability, transparency, efficiency, effectiveness, and responsiveness to citizens' needs.,बेठीकठा प्रशासनको सन्दर्भमा सार्वजनिक प्रशासनका लागिpraktices र Principes जो सुरक्षित गराउनुसको आवश्यकता हो।,",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DP014,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार सार्वजनिक प्रशासनको सन्दर्भमा सुशासन भन्नाले के जनाउँछ?,"समान तथा सहज सार्वजनिक सेवा पहुँच सुनिश्चित गर्दै निष्पक्ष, सक्षम, पारदर्शी, भ्रष्टाचारमुक्त, उत्तरदायी तथा सहभागितामूलक सार्वजनिक प्रशासन।","संविधानअनुसार सार्वजनिक प्रशासनको सन्दर्भमा सुशासन भनेको राष्ट्रपति द्वारा दिएको निर्णय र आदेश अनुसार सरकारले काम गर्ने तरिका हो। यसमा, सरकारी अधिकारीहरूले आफ्नो कार्यमा नैतिकता र कानूनलाई ध्यानपूर्वक पालन गर्नुपर्छ। सार्वजनिक प्रशासनले जनताका हितलाई प्राथमिकता दिने गरी चलाउनुपर्छ, त्यसैगरूमधील समस्या समाधान गरिनेदेखछ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DP015,English,Which Article contains the State Policies relating to the political and governance system?,Article 51(b).,Article 76.धारा ७६.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DP015,Nepali,राजनीतिक तथा शासन प्रणालीसम्बन्धी राज्यका नीतिहरू कुन धारामा उल्लेख छन्?,धारा ५१(ख)।,"Article 76.,धारा ७६,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DP016,English,"According to the Constitution, international treaties and agreements to which Nepal is a party should be what?",They should be implemented.,"The Constitution states that Nepal is a party to the following international treaties and agreements:

*   **United Nations Convention on the Law of Treaties (UNOC)**
*   **International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights (ICCPR)**
*   **International Covenant on Economic, Social and Cultural Rights (ICESCR)**
*   **The Vienna Convention on Diplomatic Relations**
*   **The Treaty on International Organization (TIO)**

You can find the full list in Article 67 of the Constitution.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
DP016,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार नेपाल पक्ष भएका अन्तर्राष्ट्रिय सन्धि तथा सम्झौताहरूलाई के गर्नुपर्छ?,कार्यान्वयन गर्नुपर्छ।,"संविधानअनुसार नेपाल पक्ष भएका अन्तर्राष्ट्रीय सन्धि तथा सम्झौताहरूलाई, नेपालको हितलाई सुरक्षित राख्दै, निम्न कार्यहरू गर्नुपर्छ:

*   **नेपालको नाममा महत्त्वपूर्ण भूमिका निर्वाह:** नेपालको अर्थशास्त्र, सामाजिक व्यवस्था, सुरक्षा र स्थिरतालाई सुरक्षित राख्ने काम गर्इनु पर्छ।
*   **स्थानीयकृत मुद्दाहरूको सम्मान:** स्थानीय सरकारका निर्णयहरू, कानून, र सम्झौताहरूलाईRespect गर्नुपर्छ।
*   **नेपालको नाममा सहभागिता:** नेपालले अन्तर्राष्ट्रिय सन्धि तथा सम्झौताहरूमा सहभागी भएर, नेपालको हितलाई सुरक्षित राख्ने भूमिका निर्वाह गर्इनु पर्छ।
*   **संसदीय प्रक्रियामा भागपाड:** नेपालका संसदमा सक्रिय रूपमा योगदान दिने हुनु पर्छ।
*   **आगामी नीतिहरूको योजना:** नेपालको भविष्यको विकास र स्थिरता सुनिश्चित गर्न, आगामी नीतिहरूलाई योजना बनाएर कार्यान्वयन गर्नुपर्छ।

यो तरतव्यले नेपालको सुरक्षा र हितलाई सुरक्षित राख्ने काम गर्इन्छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
DP017,English,"According to the Constitution, which policy promotes studies and research for protecting cultural heritage, and which policy focuses on the development of arts, literature and music?","Article 51(c)(2) promotes studies and research for cultural heritage, while Article 51(c)(4) focuses on arts, literature and music.","Article 76.,धारा ७६,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DP017,Nepali,"संविधानअनुसार कुन नीतिले सांस्कृतिक सम्पदाको संरक्षणका लागि अध्ययन तथा अनुसन्धानलाई प्रवर्द्धन गर्छ र कुन नीतिले कला, साहित्य तथा संगीतको विकासमा जोड दिन्छ?","धारा ५१(ग)(२) ले सांस्कृतिक सम्पदाको अध्ययन तथा अनुसन्धानलाई प्रवर्द्धन गर्छ भने धारा ५१(ग)(४) ले कला, साहित्य तथा संगीतको विकासमा जोड दिन्छ।","संविधानअनुसार, सांस्कृतिक सम्पदाको संरक्षणका लागि अध्ययन तथा अनुसन्धानलाई प्रवर्द्धन गर्ने नीति Article 77.,धारा ७७, Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,, कला, साहित्य, संगीतको विकासमा जोड दिन्छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
DP018,English,"According to the Constitution, which three sectors are expected to contribute to enhancing the national economy through partnership?","Public, private and cooperative sectors.","Article 76 provides for the constitution of the Council of Ministers. It states that the appointment of the Prime Minister and formation of the Council of Ministers shall be the same as those of the President. Therefore, three sectors are expected to contribute to enhancing the national economy through partnership based on this provision.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DP018,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार साझेदारीमार्फत राष्ट्रिय अर्थतन्त्रलाई सुदृढ बनाउन कुन तीन क्षेत्रको सहभागिता अपेक्षित छ?,"सार्वजनिक, निजी तथा सहकारी क्षेत्र।","Article 67(2) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that the Vice-President performs the functions of the President during the President's absence. Therefore, three sectors should participate through partnership to strengthen the national economy. The answer is:

*   **Agriculture**
*   **Industry**
*   **Trade and Commerce**",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
DP019,English,"According to the Constitution, what two measures are emphasized to make the national economy competitive while protecting consumers' interests?","Maintaining trade fairness and discipline, and eliminating black marketing, monopoly, artificial scarcity and restrictions on competition.","Article 76, Section 3, Constitution of Nepal (2015) emphasizes that the Council of Ministers should ensure a balance between economic competitiveness and consumer protection.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DP019,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार उपभोक्ताको हित संरक्षण गर्दै राष्ट्रिय अर्थतन्त्रलाई प्रतिस्पर्धी बनाउन कुन दुई उपायमा जोड दिइएको छ?,"व्यापारमा निष्पक्षता र अनुशासन कायम गर्ने तथा कालोबजारी, एकाधिकार, कृत्रिम अभाव र प्रतिस्पर्धा सीमित गर्ने गतिविधिको अन्त्य गर्ने।","संविधानअनुसार उपभोक्ताको हित संरक्षण गर्दै राष्ट्रिय अर्थतन्त्रलाई प्रतिस्पर्धी बनाउन दोसौ उपायहरू हुन्:

1.  **कठोर नियमन (Strict Regulations):** सरकारले प्रतिस्पर्धात्मक उद्योगहरूको लागि कठोर নিয়মन तोड्नी पर्छ। यसले धेरै ठूलो कम्पनीहरूलाई कमजोर गराउँदै, नयाँ कम्पनीहरूलाई विकास गर्न मद्दत गर्दछ।
2.  **सशक्त श्रम कानन (Strong Labor Laws):** कर्मचारी र व्यवसायी व्यक्तिहरूको अधिकार सुरक्षित गर्न सधानुको नियमन 시행 गर्नु पर्छ। यसले प्रतिस्पर्धात्मकतामा सुधार ल्याउन र उद्योगहरूको विकासलाई प्रोत्साहन दिन्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DP020,English,"According to the Constitution, for what types of investment should foreign capital and technology be encouraged?","Import substitution, export promotion and infrastructure development, in consonance with the national interest.","Article 76, Section 3, Constitution of Nepal (2015), https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,

The article states that foreign capital and technology should be encouraged for investment purposes.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DP020,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार विदेशी पूँजी तथा प्रविधिगत लगानी मुख्यतया कस्ता क्षेत्रमा प्रोत्साहित गरिनुपर्छ?,"राष्ट्रिय हितअनुकूल आयात प्रतिस्थापन, निर्यात प्रवर्द्धन तथा पूर्वाधार विकासका क्षेत्रमा।","संविधानअनुसार विदेशी पूँगरी पत्राचार तथा प्रविधिगत लगानी मुख्यतया निम्न क्षेत्रमा प्रोत्साहन दिने व्यवस्था गरिएको छ:

*   **प्रौधन र विकास:** विदेशी पूँगरी लगनकाले देशको आर्थिक विकासलाई गति प्रदान गर्छ।
*   **रोजगार सृष्टिको माध्यम:** विदेशी पूँगरी लगनले स्थानीय स्तर पर रोजगारी निर्माण गर्न मद्दत गर्दछ।
*   **तकनीकी हस्तांतरण:** विदेशी पूँगरी लगनबाट नेपालमा नयाली टेक्नोロジーको प्रयोग बढाइन्छ ।
*   **आर्थिक स्थिरता:** विदेशी पूँगरी लगानीलाई प्रोत्साहन दिने तरिकाले देशको आर्थिक स्थिरता सुनिश्चित हुन्छ।
*   **पर्यटन र पर्यटन्यता:** विदेशी पूँगरी लगानीले पर्यटक आकर्षित गर्छ, जसले नेपालमा पर्यटन्यता कोठोटि बढाइन्छ।

यस अनुसार, संविधानले विदेशी पूँगरी पत्राचार तथा प्रविधिगत लगानीलाई यी क्षेत्रहरूमा प्रोत्साहन दिने व्यवस्था गरेको छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DP021,English,"According to the Constitution, what existing land ownership system should scientific land reforms end?",Dual land ownership.,"The Constitution states that scientific land reforms should end “the existing system of land ownership.” However, it doesn’t specify *which* system. The text simply indicates a need for reform.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DP021,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार वैज्ञानिक भूमि सुधारले कुन विद्यमान भूमि स्वामित्व प्रणालीको अन्त्य गर्नुपर्छ?,दोहोरो भूमि स्वामित्व।,"संविधानअनुसार वैज्ञानिक भूमि सुधारले कुन विद्यमान भूमि स्वामित्व प्रणालीको अन्त्य गर्नुपर्छ?,Through the Constitution, scientific land reform must end the existing system of land ownership.",Question repetition / non-answer,Question repetition / non-answer,True
DP022,English,"According to the Constitution, what are the two primary objectives of land-use policies in agriculture?","To increase agricultural production and productivity, and to promote commercialization, industrialization, diversification and modernization of agriculture.",The Constitution states that the objective of land-use policies in agriculture is to ensure sustainable agricultural development and protect the environment. It further mentions that these policies should promote economic growth while safeguarding natural resources and biodiversity.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DP022,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार कृषिमा भूमि उपयोग नीतिका दुई प्रमुख उद्देश्य के हुन्?,"कृषि उत्पादन तथा उत्पादकत्व वृद्धि गर्नु तथा कृषिको व्यावसायीकरण, औद्योगिकीकरण, विविधीकरण र आधुनिकीकरणलाई प्रवर्द्धन गर्नु।","Article 67(2) of the Constitution of Nepal provides that the Council of Ministers is responsible for the implementation of land use policies according to the provisions of the Land Use Plan.

Here's a breakdown of the two key objectives:

1.  **Implementation of Land Use Plans:** The government must adhere to and implement the Land Use Plan, which outlines specific guidelines for land use across different regions.
2.  **Sustainable Development:** The Council of Ministers is tasked with ensuring that land use practices are sustainable and environmentally sound, promoting long-term ecological health.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
DP023,English,"According to the Constitution, to what should farmers be provided easy access?","Agricultural inputs, agricultural products at fair prices, and markets.",Article 76 provides that the Council of Ministers shall provide farmers with easy access.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DP023,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार किसानलाई कुन कुरामा सहज पहुँच उपलब्ध गराइनुपर्छ?,"कृषि सामग्री, उचित मूल्यमा कृषि उत्पादन तथा बजार।","The Constitution of Nepal (2015) provides for the provision of easy access to land and resources to farmers. Specifically, it states that ""the State shall ensure the ease of access to land and resources for farmers.""",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
DP024,English,Which Article contains the State Policies relating to Development?,Article 51(f).,Article 76.धारा ७६.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DP024,Nepali,विकाससम्बन्धी राज्यका नीतिहरू कुन धारामा उल्लेख छन्?,धारा ५१(च)।,"The development-related policies of the state are mentioned in Article 76, Section 76, Constitution of Nepal (2015).",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DP025,English,"According to the Constitution, what type of physical infrastructure should the State develop?","Balanced, environment-friendly, quality and sustainable physical infrastructure.","The Constitution states that the State shall develop physical infrastructure. However, it doesn’t specify a particular type. The text says “the State shall develop physical infrastructure.”",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DP025,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार राज्यले कस्तो प्रकारको भौतिक पूर्वाधार विकास गर्नुपर्छ?,"सन्तुलित, वातावरणमैत्री, गुणस्तरीय तथा दिगो भौतिक पूर्वाधार।","Through the Constitution of Nepal (2015), Article 76(2) states that the State shall develop physical infrastructure and resources for the benefit of all citizens. It further specifies that the development should be undertaken in a sustainable manner, considering environmental protection and social equity.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
DP026,English,"According to the Constitution, what two actions should the State take to strengthen information technology for national development?","Develop and expand information technology according to national needs, and make optimum use of information technology in national development.","Article 76, Section 3, Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,It governs the appointment of the Prime Minister and formation of the Council of Ministers.,Art. 76, Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://law commission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DP026,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार राष्ट्रिय विकासका लागि सूचना प्रविधिलाई सुदृढ बनाउन राज्यले कुन दुई कार्य गर्नुपर्छ?,राष्ट्रिय आवश्यकताअनुसार सूचना प्रविधिको विकास तथा विस्तार गर्ने र राष्ट्रिय विकासमा यसको अधिकतम उपयोग गर्ने।,"The Constitution states that the state should strengthen information methods for national development. It requires the state to undertake two actions. These are:

1.  **Establish a system of information dissemination:** The state must establish a system for disseminating information effectively and widely across the country.
2.  **Promote transparency and accountability:** The state needs to promote transparency in decision-making processes and ensure accountability in the use of resources related to national development initiatives.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
DP027,English,"According to the Constitution, which information system should be developed to manage citizens' information in an integrated manner?",An integrated national identity management information system.,"Article 76.,धारा ७६,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DP027,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार नागरिकको विवरण एकीकृत रूपमा व्यवस्थापन गर्न कुन सूचना प्रणाली विकास गर्नुपर्छ?,एकीकृत राष्ट्रिय परिचय व्यवस्थापन सूचना प्रणाली।,The Constitution of Nepal (2015) requires the development of an integrated information system for managing citizen details.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DP028,English,"According to the Constitution, which principle gives priority and preferential rights to local communities in the distribution of benefits from natural resources?",Priority and preferential rights of local communities.,"Article 76, Section 3, Constitution of Nepal (2015), https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DP028,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार प्राकृतिक स्रोतबाट प्राप्त लाभको वितरणमा स्थानीय समुदायलाई प्राथमिकता र अग्राधिकार दिने सिद्धान्त कुन हो?,स्थानीय समुदायको प्राथमिकता तथा अग्राधिकार।,"Article 67(2).,Art. 67(2),Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,
