FE004,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार संघीय कार्यकारी कार्यहरू कसको नाममा सम्पादन गरिन्छ?,नेपाल सरकारको नाममा।,"The Vice-President performs the functions of the President during the President’s absence., उपराष्ट्रपतिको कार्य राष्ट्रपतिसमक्ष कसमार्फत प्रस्तुत गरिने अध्यक्षका अनुपस्थितिकालमा राष्ट्रपतिको कार्य सम्पाद गर्छ।",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FE005,English,Which Article provides for the constitution of the Council of Ministers?,Article 76.,Article 76.धारा ७६.,Correct,Not a strict error,False
FE005,Nepali,मन्त्रिपरिषद्को गठनसम्बन्धी व्यवस्था कुन धारामा गरिएको छ?,धारा ७६।,"Article 76.,धारा ७६,Constitution of Nepal (2015),https://lawcommission.gov.np/en/?cat=152,Constitution,,,,",Correct,Not a strict error,False
FE006,English,"According to the Constitution, whom does the President appoint as Prime Minister when a single parliamentary party commands a majority in the House of Representatives?",The leader of the parliamentary party commanding the majority in the House of Representatives.,"The Constitution doesn’t explicitly state who the President appoints as Prime Minister. However, it states that the President is responsible for appointing the members of the House of Representatives. The Constitution outlines the process for electing members of the House of Representatives, which includes a vote by the members themselves. Therefore, the President appoints the Prime Minister based on the outcome of this election.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE006,Nepali,प्रतिनिधिसभामा कुनै एक संसदीय दलको स्पष्ट बहुमत भएमा संविधानअनुसार राष्ट्रपतिले कसलाई प्रधानमन्त्री नियुक्त गर्छन्?,प्रतिनिधिसभामा बहुमत प्राप्त संसदीय दलको नेता।,"Article 181 of the Constitution of Nepal defines the process for appointing the Prime Minister. According to this article, the President appoints the Prime Minister if and only if a parliamentary party (sanchalaya) has a clear majority in the House of Representatives (प्रदेश सभा)।

In essence, Article 181 states that the President can appoint the Prime Minister if there is a majority vote within the State Assembly.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FE007,English,"According to the Constitution, if no political party has a majority in the House of Representatives, who may be appointed Prime Minister?",A member of the House of Representatives who can command a majority with the support of two or more parties.,"The Constitution doesn’t explicitly state how the Prime Minister is chosen when there isn't a clear majority. However, it states that the Prime Minister is appointed by the President of Nepal based on the recommendations of the National Assembly (State Legislature). The article focuses on the process for electing members and not the appointment mechanism itself.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FE007,Nepali,प्रतिनिधिसभामा कुनै दलको स्पष्ट बहुमत नभएमा संविधानअनुसार प्रधानमन्त्री कसलाई नियुक्त गर्न सकिन्छ?,दुई वा दुईभन्दा बढी दलको समर्थनबाट बहुमत प्राप्त गर्न सक्ने प्रतिनिधिसभाको सदस्य।,Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FE008,English,"According to the Constitution, who appoints the Prime Minister, and on whose recommendation is the Council of Ministers constituted?","The President appoints the Prime Minister, and the Council of Ministers is constituted on the recommendation of the Prime Minister.",The Constitution states that the Prime Minister is appointed by the King. The Council of Ministers is constituted on the recommendation of the Prime Minister.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE008,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार प्रधानमन्त्री कसले नियुक्त गर्छन् र मन्त्रिपरिषद् कसको सिफारिसमा गठन हुन्छ?,राष्ट्रपतिले प्रधानमन्त्री नियुक्त गर्छन् र प्रधानमन्त्रीको सिफारिसमा मन्त्रिपरिषद् गठन हुन्छ।,"संविधानअनुसार प्रधानमन्त्रीConstitutional Bench of the Supreme Court द्वारा नियुक्त गर्छन। मन्त्रिपरिषद् (Majlis Committee) सिफारিসका आधारमा गठन हुन्छ।

Explanation:
Article 181 states that the Prime Minister is appointed by the Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court. The Council of Ministers (Ministry) is formed based on their recommendations.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE009,English,"According to the Constitution, what is the maximum number of Ministers that may comprise the Council of Ministers, including the Prime Minister?",Twenty-five Ministers.,"The provided text doesn’t explicitly state a limit on the number of ministers in the Council of Ministers. It focuses primarily on the composition and election processes within the State Assembly. Therefore, I cannot answer this question based solely on the given information.",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
FE009,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार प्रधानमन्त्रीसहित मन्त्रिपरिषद्मा बढीमा कति जना मन्त्री रहन सक्छन्?,बढीमा २५ जना मन्त्री।,"Article 181, Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that the Council of Ministers and the Draft Parliament Assembly (SPA) can have a maximum of 7 members in the draft parliament assembly.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FE010,English,"According to the Constitution, to whom are the Prime Minister and Ministers collectively responsible?",The Federal Parliament.,"The Constitution outlines the responsibilities of the Prime Minister and ministers collectively. They are collectively responsible for the administration of the state. Specifically, they are accountable to the people through elections. The constitution states that “the Prime Minister and ministers are collectively responsible for the administration of the State.”",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FE010,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार प्रधानमन्त्री तथा मन्त्रीहरू सामूहिक रूपमा कसप्रति उत्तरदायी हुन्छन्?,संघीय संसद्।,The Prime Minister and Ministers are collectively accountable to the Constitution of Nepal.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FE011,English,"According to the Constitution, to whom does the Prime Minister submit a written resignation?",The President.,The Constitution states that the Prime Minister submits a written resignation to the Speaker of Parliament.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE011,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार प्रधानमन्त्रीले आफ्नो लिखित राजीनामा कसलाई बुझाउँछन्?,राष्ट्रपति।,"The Constitution doesn’t specify how the Prime Minister submits their resignation. It states that they can submit their resignation in writing to the President of Nepal. However, it does not outline any specific procedure for this submission.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FE012,English,"According to the Constitution, to whom does a Minister submit a written resignation?",The Prime Minister.,Article 181 of the Constitution of Nepal states that a Minister submits a written resignation to the Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE012,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार मन्त्रीले आफ्नो लिखित राजीनामा कसलाई बुझाउँछन्?,प्रधानमन्त्री।,"The Constitution doesn't explicitly state how a minister must resign. However, it does provide for the possibility of resignation through a written declaration. The text states that ""the Minister may resign by writing."" This implies that the Minister is obligated to submit their resignation in writing.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FE013,English,"According to the Constitution, what happens to the Council of Ministers if the office of the Prime Minister becomes vacant?",The same Council of Ministers continues to function until a new Council of Ministers is constituted.,"Article 181 of the Constitution of Nepal states that “The Council of Ministers shall be unicameral and called the State Assembly. Art. 175, Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

Therefore, if the office of the Prime Minister becomes vacant, the Council of Ministers is unicameral and called the State Assembly.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE013,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार प्रधानमन्त्रीको पद रिक्त भएमा मन्त्रिपरिषद्को के हुन्छ?,नयाँ मन्त्रिपरिषद् गठन नभएसम्म सोही मन्त्रिपरिषद्ले कार्य सञ्चालन गरिरहन्छ।,"यदि संविधानअनुसार प्रधानमन्त्रीको पद रिक्त भएमा मन्त्रिपरिषद्को कति भागमा हट्नेछ?, संविधानअनुसार प्रधानमन्त्रीको पद रिक्त भएमा मन्त्रिपरिषद्को पाँच भाग हट्नेछ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE014,English,"According to the Constitution, if the Prime Minister dies, who acts as the Prime Minister until a new Prime Minister is appointed?",The senior-most Minister.,"The Constitution states that “if the Prime Minister dies, the Deputy Prime Minister shall assume the duties of the Prime Minister.”",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE014,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार प्रधानमन्त्रीको मृत्यु भएमा नयाँ प्रधानमन्त्री नियुक्त नभएसम्म कार्यवाहक प्रधानमन्त्रीको रूपमा कसले काम गर्छ?,वरिष्ठतम मन्त्री।,"कार्यवाहक प्रधान मंत्री के तौर पर, संविधान द्वारा स्पष्ट नहीं कहा गया है कि यदि संसोधनअधिकार (executive power) प्राप्त करने के लिए प्रधानमन्त्री की मृत्यु हो जाती है तो वह कितने समय तक कार्यवाहक प्रधान मंत्री बने रह सकते हैं। हालाँकि, संविधान में यह प्रावधान है कि कार्यवाहक प्रधानमंत्री को एक निश्चित अवधि के लिए नियुक्त किया जाएगा और उसे उस पद पर काम करना होगा जब तक कि संसोधन प्रक्रिया पूरी न हो जाए।",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FE015,English,Which Article allows a person who is not a member of the Federal Parliament to be appointed as a Minister?,Article 78.,Article 181,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
