FE019,English,"According to the Constitution, is a person who was defeated in the election to the current House of Representatives eligible to be appointed as a Minister during the term of that House?",No. A person defeated in the election to the current House of Representatives is not eligible to be appointed as a Minister during that House's term.,No. Article 181 of the Constitution states that a person who was defeated in an election to the State Assembly is not eligible for appointment as a Minister during the term of that House.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE019,Nepali,वर्तमान प्रतिनिधिसभाको निर्वाचनमा पराजित भएको व्यक्ति सोही प्रतिनिधिसभाको कार्यकालमा मन्त्री नियुक्त हुन योग्य हुन्छ?,हुँदैन। वर्तमान प्रतिनिधिसभाको निर्वाचनमा पराजित व्यक्ति सोही प्रतिनिधिसभाको कार्यकालभर मन्त्री नियुक्त हुन योग्य हुँदैन।,"उत्तर:
उत्तर: सदस्यले मन्त्री नियुक्त हुन योग्य हुँ, यदि उनका निर्वाचनमा पराजित भन्यो।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE020,English,"According to the Constitution, by what type of law are the remuneration and other facilities of the Prime Minister and Ministers provided?",A Federal Act.,"Article 177(1) of the Constitution defines “office of profit” as a position, other than an elected or nominated political position, for which remuneration or economic benefit is paid from a government fund. Therefore, the remuneration and facilities of the Prime Minister and Ministers are provided under Article 177(1).",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FE020,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार प्रधानमन्त्री तथा मन्त्रीहरूको पारिश्रमिक तथा अन्य सुविधा कुन प्रकारको कानुनद्वारा निर्धारण गरिन्छ?,संघीय ऐन।,"Article 181 of the Constitution of Nepal, 2015, defines how the Prime Minister and Ministers receive their allowances and other benefits. It states that this determination is made by the Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FE021,English,"According to the Constitution, before whom does the Prime Minister take the oath of office and secrecy?",The President.,The Constitution states that the Prime Minister takes an oath of office and secrecy before the Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE021,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार प्रधानमन्त्रीले पद तथा गोपनीयताको शपथ कसको समक्ष लिन्छन्?,राष्ट्रपति।,संविधानअनुसार प्रधानमन्त्रीले पद तथा गोपनीयताको शपथ सर्वोच्च अदालतका समक्ष लिन्छन्।,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE022,English,"According to the Constitution, before whom do Ministers of State and Assistant Ministers take the oath of office and secrecy?",The Prime Minister.,The Constitution states that ministers of state and assistant ministers must take an oath of office and secrecy before the Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FE022,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार राज्यमन्त्री तथा सहायक मन्त्रीहरूले पद तथा गोपनीयताको शपथ कसको समक्ष लिन्छन्?,प्रधानमन्त्री।,The State Assembly Article 179 states that every member of the State Assembly or its committees must take an oath before first participation.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FE023,English,"According to the Constitution, who administers the oath of office to the Prime Minister, and who administers the oath to Ministers of State and Assistant Ministers?","The President administers the oath to the Prime Minister, while the Prime Minister administers the oath to Ministers of State and Assistant Ministers.","Article 179, Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that “The oath of office is administered by the Speaker of the House of Representatives.”  This means the Speaker administers the oath to the Prime Minister.  For ministers of state and assistant ministers, the oath is also administered by the Speaker.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
FE023,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार प्रधानमन्त्रीलाई पद तथा गोपनीयताको शपथ कसले गराउँछ र राज्यमन्त्री तथा सहायक मन्त्रीलाई कसले शपथ गराउँछ?,राष्ट्रपतिले प्रधानमन्त्रीलाई शपथ गराउँछन् भने प्रधानमन्त्रीले राज्यमन्त्री तथा सहायक मन्त्रीलाई शपथ गराउँछन्।,संविधानअनुसार प्रधानमन्त्रीलाई पद तथा गोपनीयताको शपथ राज्यमा नियुक्त व्यक्तिले गराईन्छ। राज्यमन्त्री तथा सहायक मन्त्रीलाई राज्य सरकारका सदस्यले शपथगिर्नुपर्छ।,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE024,English,"According to the Constitution, who must inform the President about the resolutions of the Council of Ministers?",The Prime Minister.,"Article 181, Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that “The Council of Ministers shall inform the President about the resolutions of the State Assembly.”",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FE024,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार मन्त्रिपरिषद्का निर्णयहरूको जानकारी राष्ट्रपतिलाई कसले गराउनुपर्छ?,प्रधानमन्त्री।,"संविधान अनुसार मान्त्रिपरिषद्का निर्णयहरूको माहिती राष्ट्रपतिलाई कसले गराउनुपर्छ, यसको मुख्य आधारमा तीन भागमा विभाजित हुन सक्छ। यहाँ ती ३ भागहरू बुझिन्छ:

1.  **सहमती (Appointment):** राष्ट्रपतिले मान्त्रिपरिषद्का सदस्यहरू चयन गर्नबाटै जानकारी प्राप्त गर्दछन्। राष्ट्रपतिले मान्त्रिपरिषद्का निर्णयहरूको बारेमा जानकारताको लागि, यसलाई सरकारलाई गराउनुपर्छ।

2.  **निगरानी (Monitoring):** राष्ट्रपतिले मान्त्रिपरिषद्का कार्यको निगरानी गर्न र त्यसको प्रभावशीलताको मूल्यांकन गर्नबाट जानकारी प्राप्त गर्दछन्। राष्ट्रपतिले मान्त्रिपरिषद्का निर्णयहरूमा आएको भ्रष्टाचार वा अनियमितताहरूको जाँच गर्नुपर्छ।

3.  **सुरक्षा (Protection):** राष्ट्रपतिले मान्त्रिपरिषद्का निर्णयहरूलाई सुरक्षित राख्ने तरतव्य हुन्छ, ताकि यसले राज्यको सुरक्षामा जड नहोस्। राष्ट्रपतिले मान्त्रिपरिषद्का निर्णयहरूको जानकारी सरकारलाई गराउनुपर्छ, त्यसैले पनि यसको रक्षात्मकता सुनिश्चित गर्नुपर्छ।

संक्षेप में कहें तो, राष्ट्रपतिले मान्त्रिपरिषद्का निर्णयहरूको बारेमा जानकारताको लागि, यसलाई सरकारलाई गराउनुपर्छ, तर यसको निगरानी र सुरक्षादेखि पनि जानकारी प्राप्त गर्दछन्।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE025,English,"According to the Constitution, who has the duty to inform the President about Bills to be introduced in the Federal Parliament?",The Prime Minister.,"Article 181 of the Constitution of Nepal states that “The Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court makes the final decision on whether a member of the State Assembly is disqualified.” Therefore, any member of the State Assembly must inform the President about Bills to be introduced in the Federal Parliament.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FE025,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार संघीय संसद्मा पेश गरिने विधेयकहरूको जानकारी राष्ट्रपतिलाई गराउने दायित्व कसको हुन्छ?,प्रधानमन्त्री।,Article 181 of the Constitution of Nepal states that the President of the Federal Council is responsible for approving the bill to be presented to the House of Representatives.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FE026,English,"According to the Constitution, what information regarding the country's affairs must the Prime Minister provide to the President?",The current general state of affairs of the country and matters concerning foreign relations.,"The Constitution states that the Prime Minister must provide the President with a report on the state of the nation. Specifically, Article 180(d) outlines this requirement.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FE026,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार प्रधानमन्त्रीले राष्ट्रपतिलाई देशको अवस्थासम्बन्धी कुन जानकारी दिनुपर्छ?,देशको समसामयिक सामान्य अवस्था तथा वैदेशिक सम्बन्धसम्बन्धी विषयहरू।,"Article 181, Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that the Prime Minister must inform the President about the country's situation in a written format.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FE027,English,Which Article governs the transaction of the business of the Government of Nepal?,Article 82.,Article 177.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE027,Nepali,नेपाल सरकारको कार्य सञ्चालनसम्बन्धी व्यवस्था कुन धारामा गरिएको छ?,धारा ८२।,"SL003,Constitution & Law,Composition of State Assembly,Fact Retrieval,Medium,What percentage of State Assembly members are elected through the first-past-the-post electoral system?,प्रदेश सभाका कति प्रतिशत सदस्य प्रत्यक्ष निर्वाचन प्रणालीबाट निर्वाचित हुन्छन्?,Sixty percent.,साठी प्रतिशत।,Article 176(3) provides that forty percent are elected through the proportional electoral system.,Art. 176(3),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FE028,English,"According to the Constitution, in accordance with what are the business of the Government of Nepal allocated and transacted?",In accordance with the rules approved by the Government of Nepal.,"The Constitution outlines the powers and responsibilities of the government of Nepal. According to Article 177(1) of the Constitution, the government is tasked with managing the state's finances, collecting taxes, and providing public services. It also states that the government’s business includes:

*   **Managing State Finances:** Collecting revenue through taxation, managing budgets, and ensuring financial stability.
*   **Providing Public Services:** Delivering essential services to citizens such as healthcare, education, infrastructure development, social welfare programs, and law enforcement.
*   **Maintaining Law and Order:** Ensuring public safety and security through the administration of justice and upholding laws.

Essentially, the government's activities are centered around governing Nepal effectively and ensuring its well-being.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE028,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार नेपाल सरकारको कार्य कुन आधारमा बाँडफाँट र सञ्चालन गरिन्छ?,नेपाल सरकारले स्वीकृत गरेका नियमहरू अनुसार।,संविधानअनुसार नेपाल सरकारको कार्य संविधान द्वारा निर्धारित कार्यआधारमा बाँडफाँट र सञ्चालन हुन्छ।,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE029,English,"According to the Constitution, can a court question whether the rules governing the transaction of the Government of Nepal's business have been observed?",No. No question may be raised in any court regarding whether those rules have been observed.,"Yes, according to Article 181 of the Constitution of Nepal, the Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court has the authority to question whether the rules governing the government’s business have been observed.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE029,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार नेपाल सरकारको कार्य सञ्चालनसम्बन्धी नियमहरूको पालना भएको वा नभएको विषयमा अदालतमा प्रश्न उठाउन सकिन्छ?,सकिँदैन। ती नियमहरूको पालना भएको वा नभएको विषयमा कुनै अदालतमा प्रश्न उठाउन सकिँदैन।,"हाँ। संविधानअनुसार नेपाल सरकारको कार्यसञ्चાલनसम्बन्धी नियमहरूको पालना भएको वा नभएको विषयमा अदालतमा प्रश्न उठाउन सकिन्छ।

यहाँ कारणहरू छन्:

*   **अधिकार क्षेत्र (Jurisdiction) जाँच:** संविधानले विभिन्न अधिकार क्षेत्रहरूdefined गर्दछ, जस्तै संवैधानिक इजलास, न्यायपालिका, र सरकारको अधिकार। यदि नेपाल सरकारले नियमहरूको पालनामा धर्मी रूपमा आउँछ भने, अदालतले निर्धारित गर्ने अधिकार हुन्छ।
*   **नियमहरूको अनुपाल्यता:** संविधानले सरकारी कार्यका लागि नियमहरूको पालनालाई निर्देशित गर्दछ। यदि नियमहरू अनुपाल्य योग्य नहुन् तर सरकारले उनका पालनामा परिवर्तन गर्न सक्ने अधिकार हुन्छ।
*   **संसदीय व्यवस्थाको सुरक्षा:**अदालतले सुनिश्चित गर्छ कि सरकारले कानूनको पालनामा धर्मी रूपमा आउँछ, जसले संवैधानिक व्यवस्थाको सुरक्षित保संरक्षण हो।

त्यसैността, संविधानअनुसार नेपाल सरकारको कार्यसञ्चાલनसम्बन्धी नियमहरूको पालना भएको वा नभएको विषयमा अदालतमा प्रश्न उठाउन सकिन्छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
FE030,English,"According to the Constitution, besides the resolutions of the Council of Ministers and Bills to be introduced in the Federal Parliament, name one additional category of information that the Prime Minister must provide to the President.","Either (i) other necessary information requested by the President regarding those matters, or (ii) the current general state of affairs of the country and matters concerning foreign relations.","Article 181 of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that the Prime Minister must provide information to the President on the following matters:

*   **The status of the State Assembly:** This includes details about the assembly's composition, functions, and any significant events or decisions.
*   **The implementation of laws:** The Prime Minister is responsible for ensuring that laws are effectively implemented across all regions of Nepal.
*   **Any changes to the Constitution:** Any amendments made to the Constitution must be reported to the President.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FE030,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार मन्त्रिपरिषद्का निर्णय र संघीय संसद्मा पेश गरिने विधेयकबाहेक प्रधानमन्त्रीले राष्ट्रपतिलाई उपलब्ध गराउनुपर्ने थप जानकारीमध्ये एउटा उल्लेख गर्नुहोस्।,"(१) ती विषयमा राष्ट्रपतिले मागेको अन्य आवश्यक जानकारी, वा (२) देशको समसामयिक सामान्य अवस्था तथा वैदेशिक सम्बन्धसम्बन्धी जानकारी।","SL019,Constitution & Law,Members of the Supreme Court,Fact Retrieval,Medium,What is the primary role and responsibility of the Members of the Supreme Court (मन्त्रिपरिषद्) in relation to the President of Nepal?"",""मन्त्रिपरिषद्का मुख्य भूमिका र उत्तरदायित्व कति वर्षको हुन्छ?"",To interpret laws, adjudicate disputes, and provide advisory opinions.,To interpret laws, adjudicate disputes, and provide advisory opinions."",""To interpret laws, adjudicate disputes, and provide advisory opinions."",""To interpret laws, adjudicate disputes, and provide advisory opinions."",""To interpret laws, adjudicate disputes, and provide advisory opinions."",""To interpret laws, adjudigate disputes, and provide advisory opinions."",""To interpret laws, adjudicate disputes, and provide advisory opinions."",""To interpret laws, adjudicate disputes, and provide advisory opinions."",""To interpret laws, adjudicate disputes, and provide advisory opinions."",""To interpret laws, adjudicate disputes, and provide advisory opinions."",""To interpret laws, adjudigate disputes, and provide advisory opinions."",""To interpret laws, adjudicate disputes, and provide advisory opinions."",""To interpret laws, adjudicate disputes, and provide advisory opinions."",""To interpret laws, adjudigate disputes, and provide advisory opinions."",""To interpret laws, adjudicate disputes, and provide advisory opinions."",""To interpret laws, adjudigate disputes, and provide advisory opinions."",""To interpret laws, adjudigate disputes, and provide advisory opinions."",""To interpret laws, adjudigate disputes, and provide advisory opinions."",""To interpret laws, adjudigate disputes, and provide advisory opinio