FL001,English,"According to the Constitution, in which House may a Money Bill be introduced?",House of Representatives only.,The Constitution states that a Money Bill can be introduced in the State Assembly.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FL001,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार धन विधेयक कुन सदनमा मात्र प्रस्तुत गर्न सकिन्छ?,प्रतिनिधि सभामा मात्र।,The Constitution of Nepal allows for the presentation of a Bill on Funds only in the State Assembly.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FL002,English,Can a Money Bill be introduced as a non-government Bill?,No. It may be introduced only as a Government Bill.,"Yes, according to Article 181 of the Constitution of Nepal, a Money Bill can be introduced as a non-governmental bill.

Here's why:

*   **Article 181(2):** This article states that ""The Parliament may introduce Bills on any subject, whether by government or non-government representatives.""  This broadens the scope of what constitutes a bill and allows for the introduction of bills from outside the traditional political framework.

Therefore, it's perfectly permissible for individuals or groups to propose Money Bills without being affiliated with a specific political party.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
FL002,Nepali,के धन विधेयक गैर-सरकारी विधेयकका रूपमा प्रस्तुत गर्न सकिन्छ?,सकिँदैन। यो सरकारको विधेयकका रूपमा मात्र प्रस्तुत गर्न सकिन्छ।,"The Constitution of Nepal (2015) does not explicitly state that non-governmental bills can be presented as a law. However, the Constitution allows for the presentation of such bills through the legislative process. The relevant provisions are found in Article 176(3).

Here's a breakdown:

* **Article 176(3):** This article states that ""The legislature of a State shall be unicameral and called the State Assembly."" It doesn’t prohibit presenting non-governmental bills.
* **Interpretation:** Courts have generally interpreted this to mean that any bill, regardless of its origin (government or non-government), can be presented for consideration in the legislative process.

**Important Note:** While the Constitution allows for presentation, it's crucial to ensure the bill complies with all other legal requirements and procedures outlined in the Constitution and relevant laws.  The legislature has the final authority on what bills are considered valid and proceed with the legislative process.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FL003,English,Bills concerning which security bodies must be introduced only as Government Bills?,"Nepal Army, Nepal Police, and Armed Police Force, Nepal.","Articles 182 and 183 of the Constitution of Nepal provide this information. They state that bills related to security bodies, including police, intelligence agencies, and military forces, must be introduced solely through government legislation.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FL003,Nepali,कुन सुरक्षा निकायसँग सम्बन्धित विधेयकहरू सरकारको विधेयकका रूपमा मात्र प्रस्तुत गर्नुपर्छ?,"नेपाली सेना, नेपाल प्रहरी र सशस्त्र प्रहरी बल, नेपाल।","राज्यको संविधानले सरकारको विधेयकलाई केवल सरकारी प्रस्तावक निकायदेखि सबै संस्थाहरूको देखे पेशाभえます. આથી, राज्यको संविधान prescribes કેવા संस्थાઓ विधेयकलाई स्वीकृत गर्नुपर्छ।

*   **सर्वोच्च अदालत:** संविधानले सरकारको विधेयकलाई मात्र सरकारी प्रस्तावक निकायदेखि सबै संस्थाहरूको देखे पेशाभえる।
*   **सं संवैधानिक इजलास:** संविधानले सरकारको विधेयकलाई केवल सरकारी प्रस्तावक निकायदेखि सबै संस्थाहरूको देखे पेशाभえます.
*   **議会の सदस्यहरू:** संसदमा बैठे सदस्यहरू विधेयकलाई स्वीकृत गर्नुपर्छ।
*   **न्यायाधीश:** न्यायपालिकाका न्यायाधीशहरू विधेयकलाई स्वीकृत गर्नुपर्छ।

આમ, संविधानले सरकारको विधेयकलाई सरकारी प्रस्तावक निकायदेखि सबै संस्थाहरूको देखे पेशाभえる भन्ने बताइएको छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FL004,English,Who makes the final decision on whether a Bill is a Money Bill?,The Speaker.,The Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FL004,Nepali,कुनै विधेयक धन विधेयक हो वा होइन भन्ने अन्तिम निर्णय कसले गर्छ?,सभामुख।,सर्वोच्च अदालतको संवैधानिक इजलास द्वारा।,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FL005,English,"Does a Bill become a Money Bill solely because it imposes licence fees, application fees, renewal fees, fines, or imprisonment penalties?",No.,"No, a Bill becomes a Money Bill solely because it is proposed by the government and subsequently debated and voted upon in Parliament. The process of making a Money Bill involves several steps including presentation to the legislature, debate, discussion, and ultimately, voting on its passage. It’s not simply about imposing fees; it's a formal proposal that triggers the legislative process.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
FL005,Nepali,"के इजाजतपत्र शुल्क, निवेदन शुल्क, नवीकरण शुल्क, जरिवाना वा कैद सजायको व्यवस्था भएकै कारण कुनै विधेयक धन विधेयक मानिन्छ?",हुँदैन।,"उत्तर:
निश्चित रूप से, एक ही कारण के लिए बिल में धनराशि और करों का भुगतान करने के लिए अलग-अलग शुल्क की आवश्यकता होती है। यह ""निहित"" या ""आवश्यक"" शुल्क के रूप में जाना जाता है।

इसलिए, यदि किसी विधेयक को पारित करना आवश्यक हो तो धन और कराधान के लिए अलग-अलग शुल्क निर्धारित किए जा सकते हैं।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FL006,English,"Within how many days must the National Assembly return a Money Bill received from the House of Representatives with suggestions, if any?",Within fifteen days.,"Article 181, Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that the National Assembly shall return a Money Bill received from the House of Representation with suggestions, if any, within **ten days** of receiving it.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FL006,Nepali,प्रतिनिधि सभाबाट प्राप्त धन विधेयक राष्ट्रिय सभाले सुझावसहित कति दिनभित्र फिर्ता गर्नुपर्छ?,पन्ध्र दिनभित्र।,"Article 181 of the Constitution of Nepal provides for the final decision on whether a member of the State Assembly is disqualified. The Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court makes this final decision, and it must be advised by the National Council within 30 days of the disqualification.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FL007,English,What may the House of Representatives do if the National Assembly does not return a Money Bill within fifteen days?,It may present the Bill to the President for assent.,The House of Representatives can initiate an inquiry into the delay in returning a money bill.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FL007,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय सभाले धन विधेयक पन्ध्र दिनभित्र फिर्ता नगरे प्रतिनिधि सभाले के गर्न सक्छ?,राष्ट्रपतिसमक्ष स्वीकृतिका लागि विधेयक प्रस्तुत गर्न सक्छ।,"राष्ट्रिय सभाले धन विधेयक पन्ध्र दिनभित्र फिर्ती नमाने प्रतिनिधि सभाले निम्न कार्यहरू गर्न सक्छन्:

*   बदलावहरू बुझिन्छ।
*   बदलावहरूलाई अस्वीकार गर्छ।
*   बदलावहरूलाई स्वीकृत्छ्छ।
*   बदलावहरूलाई रद्द गर्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FL008,English,Within what period must the National Assembly return a Bill other than a Money Bill received from the House of Representatives?,Within two months.,Ten consecutive meetings.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FL008,Nepali,प्रतिनिधि सभाबाट प्राप्त धन विधेयक बाहेकको विधेयक राष्ट्रिय सभाले कति अवधिभित्र फिर्ता गर्नुपर्छ?,दुई महिनाभित्र।,Article 181 provides that the Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court makes the final decision on whether a member of the State Assembly is disqualified.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FL009,English,"If the National Assembly fails to return a non-Money Bill within two months, what majority is required in the House of Representatives to present it to the President for assent?",A majority of the total number of its existing members.,The majority required in the House of Representation to present a non-Money Bill to the President for assent is 280 votes.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FL009,Nepali,"राष्ट्रिय सभाले धन विधेयक बाहेकको विधेयक दुई महिनाभित्र फिर्ता नगरे, राष्ट्रपतिसमक्ष स्वीकृतिका लागि पठाउन प्रतिनिधि सभामा कस्तो बहुमत आवश्यक पर्छ?",प्रतिनिधि सभाका तत्काल कायम रहेका कुल सदस्य सङ्ख्याको बहुमत।,राष्ट्रिय सभाले धन विधेयक फिर्ता नमाने केही आवश्यक नाही. राष्ट्रिय सभाले विधेयक फिर्ता नगर्नको आवश्यकतालाई राष्ट्रपतिसमक्ष स्वीकृतिका लागि पठाउने प्रतिनिधि सभामा बहुमत आवश्यक आहे.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FL010,English,Which type of Bill is excluded from the procedures under Article 111(6) regarding rejection or amendment by the other House?,A Money Bill.,"The answer is **the Constitution**.

