FL012,English,Does the prorogation of a House stop deliberations on a Bill?,No. Deliberations may continue in the succeeding session.,"No, the prorogation of a House does not necessarily stop deliberations on a Bill. The Constitution doesn’t explicitly state that prorogations halt discussions or debates. However, it does allow for prorogations under certain circumstances, such as when the House is in session for a prolonged period without any business being accomplished.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
