JD020,English,Can a specialized court be created for a specific individual case?,No.,"Yes, according to Article 181 of the Constitution of Nepal, a specialized court can be established for a specific individual case. The Constitution states that “The Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court shall have the power to establish specialized courts for specific cases.” This provision allows for tailored legal processes and judgments based on particular circumstances.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
