JD024,English,"A Supreme Court Judge and a High Court Judge are both 64 years old. According to the Constitution, which judge must retire first?","The High Court Judge must retire first because the retirement age is 63 years, whereas Supreme Court Judges retire at 65 years.","According to the Constitution of Nepal, the High Court Judge must retire first. The Constitution states that “The High Court Judge shall retire at the age of sixty-four.”",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
JD024,Nepali,सर्वोच्च अदालतका एक न्यायाधीश र उच्च अदालतका एक न्यायाधीश दुवै ६४ वर्षका छन्। संविधानअनुसार पहिले कसले अवकाश लिनुपर्छ?,"उच्च अदालतका न्यायाधीशले पहिले अवकाश लिनुपर्छ, किनकि उच्च अदालतको अवकाश उमेर ६३ वर्ष हो भने सर्वोच्च अदालतका न्यायाधीशको ६५ वर्ष हो।",सर्वोच्च अदालतका एक न्यायाधीश र उच्च अदालतका एक न्यायाधीश दुवै ६४ वर्षका छन्। संविधानअनुसार पहिले उच्च अदालतका एक न्यायाधीश अवकाश लिनुपर्छ।,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
JD025,English,"Although both the Supreme Court and High Courts may issue constitutional writs, which court has the final authority to interpret the Constitution?",The Supreme Court has the final authority to interpret the Constitution.,The Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court has the final authority to interpret the Constitution.,Correct,Not a strict error,False
JD025,Nepali,सर्वोच्च अदालत र उच्च अदालत दुवैले संवैधानिक रिट जारी गर्न सक्ने भए पनि संविधानको अन्तिम व्याख्या गर्ने अधिकार कुन अदालतलाई छ?,संविधानको अन्तिम व्याख्या गर्ने अधिकार सर्वोच्च अदालतलाई छ।,सर्वोच्च अदालत र उच्च अदालत दुवैले संविधानको अन्तिम व्याख्या गर्ने अधिकार सर्वोच्च अदालतलाई छ।,Correct,Not a strict error,False
JD026,English,"Are all courts and judicial bodies in Nepal subordinate to the Supreme Court? If not, what constitutional qualification applies?","Yes, except where otherwise provided by the Constitution.","No, all courts and judicial bodies in Nepal are subordinate to the Supreme Court. The Constitution of Nepal (2015) explicitly states this through Article 181, which grants the Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court the authority to review laws and regulations passed by Parliament. This ensures that the judiciary remains accountable to the highest law-making body.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
JD026,Nepali,के नेपालका सबै अदालत तथा न्यायिक निकाय सर्वोच्च अदालतअन्तर्गत हुन्छन्? यदि होइन भने संविधानले के अपवाद राखेको छ?,"हो, तर संविधानले अन्यथा व्यवस्था गरेको अवस्थामा अपवाद लागू हुन्छ।","हाँ, नेपालमा सबै अदालत तथा न्यायिक निकाय सर्वोच्च अदालतअन्तर्गत हुन्छन। संवैधानिक रूपमै यसलाई स्पष्टीकरण दिइएको छ कि कति अदालat र न्यायपालिकाका निर्णयहरू सर्वोच्च अदालतमा प्रयोग हुन्छन्।

संविधानले पाँच प्रकारका अदालत र न्यायिक निकायहरूको उल्लेख गर्यो:

1.  **सर्वोच्च न्यायालय (Supreme Court):** यो सर्वोच्च अदालत नेपालका सबै महत्वपूर्ण निर्णयहरू तय्छोल्नको लागि जिम्मेवार छ।
2.  **उच्च न्यायपालिका (High Courts):** यी अदालatहरू देशका विभिन्न क्षेत्रमा स्थानीय तहका निर्णयहरूको छान्याव गर्दछन् र उनका अनुपालन सुनिश्चित गर्दछन्।
3.  **स्थानीय न्यायपालिका (Local courts):** यी अदालतहरू जिल्ल स्तर पर निर्णयहरू तय्छोल्नको लागि जिम्मेवार छन्।
4.  **न्यायिक आदेशा जारी गर्ने निकाय (Judicial Orders Issuing Bodies):** यसमा जस्तै विभिन्न प्रकारका अदालat र न्यायिक निकाय हुन्छन्, जसले न्यायको व्यवस्थापनमा योगदान गर्दछन्।

संविधानले कतिही यो स्पष्टीकरणलाई बुझाउँछ तर यसको अर्थ हो कि नेपालका सबै अदालतहरू सर्वोच्च अदालतअन्तर्गत छन्।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
JD027,English,"Can the Supreme Court declare a law void from the beginning of its existence, or only from the date of its judgment?",It may declare the law void either ab initio or from the date of its decision.,The Supreme Court can declare a law void from the beginning of its existence. The Constitution of Nepal (2015) explicitly grants this power to the Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court. Article 181 states that the Constitutional Bench has the authority to declare laws void from the beginning of their existence.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
JD027,Nepali,"के सर्वोच्च अदालतले कुनै कानुनलाई प्रारम्भदेखि नै बदर गर्न सक्छ, वा निर्णय भएको मितिदेखि मात्र?",सर्वोच्च अदालतले कानुनलाई प्रारम्भदेखि नै वा आफ्नो निर्णय भएको मितिदेखि बदर गर्न सक्छ।,सर्वोच्च अदालतले कानुनलाई प्रारम्भदेखि नै बदर गर्न सक्छ।,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
JD028,English,Which body settles disputes regarding the disqualification of members of the Federal Parliament: the full Supreme Court or the Constitutional Bench?,The Constitutional Bench.,The Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court.,Correct,Not a strict error,False
JD028,Nepali,संघीय संसदका सदस्यको अयोग्यतासम्बन्धी विवाद सर्वोच्च अदालतको पूर्ण इजलासले टुंग्याउँछ वा संवैधानिक इजलासले?,संवैधानिक इजलास।,सर्वोच्च अदालतले संघीय संसदका सदस्यको अयोग्यतासम्बन्धी विवाद टुँग्याउनेछ।,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
JD029,English,Can a specialized court be established to hear only one specific case?,No. The Constitution expressly prohibits creating a specialized court for a specific case.,"Yes, according to Article 181 of the Constitution of Nepal, a specialized court can be established to hear only one specific case. The Constitution states that “The Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court shall have the power to hear only one specific case.”",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
JD029,Nepali,कुनै एउटा विशेष मुद्दा सुनुवाइ गर्न मात्रै विशेष अदालत स्थापना गर्न मिल्छ?,मिल्दैन। संविधानले कुनै विशेष मुद्दाका लागि मात्र विशेष अदालत गठन गर्न निषेध गरेको छ।,हाँ। तरिकाले हो कि यसको विषयवस्तु न्यायपालिकामा निर्भर छ।,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
JD030,English,Which member of the Judicial Council is nominated on the recommendation of the Nepal Bar Association?,A senior advocate or advocate with at least twenty years of experience.,The answer is **not explicitly stated in the provided text.** The text focuses primarily on constitutional provisions related to state legislatures and electoral systems. It doesn’t detail how nominations are made for judicial council members.,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
JD030,Nepali,न्याय परिषद्मा नेपाल बार एसोसिएसनको सिफारिसमा नियुक्त हुने सदस्य को हुन्?,कम्तीमा बीस वर्ष अनुभव भएका वरिष्ठ अधिवक्ता वा अधिवक्ता।,"न्याय परिषद्मा नेपाल बार एसोसिएसनको सिफारिसमा नियुक्त हुने सदस्य, बार एसोसिएटन्सका सदस्य हुन्छन।",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
JD031,English,"What proportion of vacant District Judge posts is filled through seniority, and what proportion through open competitive examination?","20% through seniority, 80% through open competitive examination (40% Judicial Service officers and 40% advocates/other eligible candidates).","According to Article 176(2) of the Constitution of Nepal, sixty percent of vacant District Judge positions are filled through seniority. Forty percent are filled through open competitive examinations.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
JD031,Nepali,जिल्ला न्यायाधीशका रिक्त पदमध्ये कति प्रतिशत वरिष्ठताका आधारमा र कति प्रतिशत खुला प्रतिस्पर्धाबाट पूर्ति गरिन्छ?,२०% वरिष्ठताका आधारमा र ८०% खुला प्रतिस्पर्धाबाट (४०% न्याय सेवा र ४०% अन्य योग्य उम्मेदवार)।,"Article 181(3) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that the final decision on whether a member of the State Assembly is disqualified shall be made by the Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court. The bench will consider both seniority and open competition.

Therefore, the answer is: **The Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court will make the final decision on whether a member of the State Assembly is disqualified.**",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
JD032,English,"After retirement, may a former Supreme Court Judge and a former High Court Judge both practice law? Compare their constitutional positions.","A retired Supreme Court Judge may not practice law, mediation, or arbitration before any office or court, whereas a retired High Court Judge may practice before the Supreme Court and other High Courts except the High Court where they served.","Based on Article 181 of the Constitution of Nepal, yes, both former Supreme Court Judges and former High Court Judges can continue to practice law after retirement. Here’s a breakdown of how this is addressed:

* **Article 181:** This article states that “The Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court shall have the power to determine whether any person, including former Supreme Court Judges and High Court Judges, may continue to practice law.”

Therefore, both individuals can continue their legal careers after retirement as long as they meet the requirements outlined in this provision.  It’s a fundamental aspect of the Constitution's structure designed to ensure continuity of judicial expertise.

**Key takeaway:** The Constitution explicitly allows for continued practice by former judges, reinforcing the importance of judicial independence and ensuring that experienced legal professionals remain available for court work.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
JD032,Nepali,अवकाशपछि पूर्व सर्वोच्च अदालतका न्यायाधीश र पूर्व उच्च अदालतका न्यायाधीश दुवैले वकालत गर्न पाउँछन्? उनीहरूको संवैधानिक व्यवस्था तुलना गर्नुहोस्।,"पूर्व सर्वोच्च अदालतका न्यायाधीशले कुनै अदालत वा निकायमा वकालत, मध्यस्थता वा मध्यनिर्णय गर्न पाउँदैनन्, तर पूर्व उच्च अदालतका न्यायाधीशले आफू कार्यरत रहेको उच्च अदालतबाहेक सर्वोच्च तथा अन्य उच्च अदालतमा वकालत गर्न सक्छन्।","तArt. 181,Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,
**Answer:**

Article 181 of the Constitution of Nepal states that ""The judges of the State Assembly may be called upon to give a legal opinion on the matter of disqualification.""  This means that both the Chief Justice of the Supreme Court and the President of the High Court can provide a legal opinion regarding whether a member of the State Assembly is disqualified.

**Comparison of the Constitutional Structure:**

Here's a comparison of how this provision relates to the structure of the State Legislature in Nepal:

* **State Assembly - Judicial Role:** The Constitution of Nepal establishes a judicial role for judges within the State Assembly. This is crucial because the assembly’s primary function is to make laws and represent the people.  The judiciary plays an important oversight role, ensuring that the legislative process adheres to constitutional principles.
* **Supreme Court & High Courts - Independent Review:** The Supreme Court and High Courts are independent bodies with significant authority in Nepal's legal system. They have the power to review decisions made by lower courts and ensure compliance with the Constitution.  Their role is to safeguard the constitutionality of laws and actions.

**Key Differences & Implications:**

* **Scope of Opinion:** The provision focuses on *legal opinions*, not a formal disqualification order. This allows for more nuanced consideration of circumstances, rather than immediate removal from office.
* **Constitutional Oversight:**  The judicial role is integral to the constitutional framework. It reinforces the principle that the legislature (State Assembly) must be accountable to the Constitution and cannot act in ways that undermine its authority.

**In essence, Article 181 provides a mechanism for the judiciary to actively oversee the legislative process within the State Assembly, ensuring it remains aligned with the constitution.**

Let me know if you'd like more detail on any specific aspect of this provision!",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
