FE077,English,Who is appointed Chief Minister when one party commands a majority in the State Assembly?,The leader of the parliamentary party commanding the majority.,"The Constitution of Nepal doesn’t explicitly state who becomes Chief Minister when one political party holds a majority. However, it outlines the process for electing the Chief Minister and emphasizes that the election should be conducted fairly and transparently. The constitution focuses on establishing a system where the winning party or coalition wins the majority vote in the Assembly.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE077,Nepali,प्रदेश सभामा कुनै दलको स्पष्ट बहुमत भएमा कसलाई मुख्यमन्त्री नियुक्त गरिन्छ?,बहुमत प्राप्त संसदीय दलको नेता।,प्रदेश सभामा कुनै दलको स्पष्ट बहुमत भएमा त्यस दलका सदस्यलाई मुख्यमन्त्री नियुक्त गरिन्छ।,Correct,Not a strict error,False
FE078,English,Who may be appointed Chief Minister if no party has a clear majority in the State Assembly?,A member who can command a majority with the support of two or more parties.,"The Constitution of Nepal doesn’t explicitly state who can become Chief Minister if there is no clear majority. However, Article 182 outlines the procedure for electing the Chief Minister. It states that the Chief Minister will be appointed by the President based on the results of the election.

