FE080,Nepali,अन्तिम निर्वाचन परिणाम घोषणा भएपछि मुख्यमन्त्री नियुक्ति प्रक्रिया कति दिनभित्र पूरा हुनुपर्छ?,पैंतीस दिनभित्र।,"Article 182, Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that the Chief Minister's appointment should be completed within 7 days of the final election results being announced.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FE081,English,What is the maximum size of the State Council of Ministers?,Twenty percent of the total number of members of the State Assembly.,The answer is 16.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FE081,Nepali,प्रदेश मन्त्रिपरिषद्को अधिकतम आकार कति हुन सक्छ?,प्रदेश सभाका कुल सदस्य संख्याको बीस प्रतिशत।,The maximum size of the State Assembly's Regional Council is 60 members.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FE082,English,"Under Article 168, what does the term ""Minister"" include?","Minister, Minister of State, and Assistant Minister.","According to Article 168 of the Constitution of Nepal, “Minister” includes individuals who are appointed by the House of Representatives (State Assembly) and hold office as ministers.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
FE082,Nepali,"धारा १६८ अनुसार ""मन्त्री"" भन्नाले कसलाई जनाउँछ?","मन्त्री, राज्यमन्त्री र सहायक मन्त्री।","धारा १६८ अनुसार ""मन्त्री"" भन्नाले राज्यका मुख्य अधिकारी हुनन्। तर, माथि नदिने अधिकारीहरूमा निम्न पर्jय छन्:

*   राज्यका प्रधान मंत्री (Prime Minister)
*   राज्यको प्रमुख प्रशासक (Chief Administrator)
*   राज्यको प्रमुख सुरक्षाकर्मी (Head of Security Officer)
*   राज्यको प्रमुख स्रोतकर्मी (Head of Source Officer)
*   राज्यको मुख्य न्यायाधीश (Supreme Judge)

अर्थात्,मन्त्री भनेर पदमा सम्भव पाउने व्यक्तिलाई राज्यका सबै आधिकारिक अधिकारीहरू मध्ये एक हुनन्।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE083,English,To whom is the State Council of Ministers collectively responsible?,The State Assembly.,"The State Council of Ministers is collectively responsible to the people of Nepal. Specifically, they are accountable to the citizens for their actions and decisions.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE083,Nepali,प्रदेश मन्त्रिपरिषद् सामूहिक रूपमा कसप्रति उत्तरदायी हुन्छ?,प्रदेश सभा।,प्रदेश मन्त्रिपरिषद् सामूहिक रूपमा Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court द्वारा निर्णयित সিদ্ধান্তले उत्तरदायी हुन्छ।,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE084,English,To whom does the Chief Minister submit a written resignation?,The Chief of State.,The answer is “to the President of the House of Representatives.”,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE084,Nepali,मुख्यमन्त्रीले लिखित राजीनामा कसलाई दिन्छन्?,प्रदेश प्रमुख।,Main Minister submits their resignation by a letter.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FE085,English,To whom does a Minister submit a written resignation?,The Chief Minister.,The answer is “to the Speaker of the State Assembly.”,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FE085,Nepali,मन्त्रीले लिखित राजीनामा कसलाई दिन्छन्?,मुख्यमन्त्री।,"मन्त्रीले लिखित राजीनामा ""संसदीय व्यवस्थाको सन्दर्भमा, मेरा मनःपर्दा अनुसार, माथि नहुँगा।"" (According to the legislative framework) भनतात।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
FE086,English,Who acts as Chief Minister if the Chief Minister dies before a new one is appointed?,The senior-most Minister.,"The Constitution of Nepal outlines procedures for appointing a replacement minister in case of the death of the current chief minister. According to Article 182, the appointment will be made by the National Council (NC) of the State Assembly. The NC will then nominate a new minister from among the members of the assembly.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE086,Nepali,नयाँ मुख्यमन्त्री नियुक्त नभएसम्म मुख्यमन्त्रीको मृत्यु भए कसले कार्यवाहक मुख्यमन्त्रीको रूपमा काम गर्छ?,सबैभन्दा वरिष्ठ मन्त्री।,"Constitutional Law, State Legislature, State Assembly, Article 182, Constitution of Nepal (2015)",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FE087,English,Within how many months must a non-member appointed as Minister become a member of the State Assembly?,Within six months.,Article 181 provides that non-members appointed as Ministers must become members of the State Assembly within ten consecutive meetings.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FE087,Nepali,प्रदेश सभाको सदस्य नभएको मन्त्री नियुक्त भएको व्यक्तिले कति महिनाभित्र प्रदेश सभा सदस्य बन्नुपर्छ?,छ महिनाभित्र।,"Through the same electoral system by which the seat was originally filled.

Art. 176(8) requires vacancies to be filled through the same electoral system.,Art. 176(8),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FE088,English,Can a person defeated in the current State Assembly election be appointed as a Minister under Article 170(1)?,No. A defeated candidate is not eligible during the term of that State Assembly.,"No., The Constitution does not explicitly state that a defeated candidate can be appointed as a minister. However, it allows for re-election or appointment based on other criteria outlined in relevant provisions of the constitution.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE088,Nepali,वर्तमान प्रदेश सभा निर्वाचनमा पराजित व्यक्ति धारा १७०(१) अन्तर्गत मन्त्री नियुक्त हुन सक्छ?,हुँदैन। त्यस्तो व्यक्ति उक्त प्रदेश सभाको कार्यकालभर मन्त्री नियुक्त हुन योग्य हुँदैन।,"उत्तर: हाँ, वर्तमान प्रदेश सभा निर्वाचनमा पराजित व्यक्ति धारा १७०(१) अन्तर्गत मन्त्री नियुक्त हुन सक्छ।

कारण: धारा १७०(१)(d) मध्ये उल्लेख छ कि ""सर्वोच्च अदालतले सदस्यको अयोग्य घोषणा र सदस्यलाई मन्त्री बनाउन निर्णय गर्छ।""",Question repetition / non-answer,Question repetition / non-answer,True
FE089,English,"Before whom do the Chief Minister and Ministers take the oath, and before whom do Ministers of State and Assistant Ministers take the oath?","The Chief Minister and Ministers take the oath before the Chief of State, while Ministers of State and Assistant Ministers take the oath before the Chief Minister.",The Chief Minister and Ministers take the oath before the Supreme Court.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE089,Nepali,मुख्यमन्त्री तथा मन्त्रीहरूले कसको समक्ष शपथ लिन्छन् र राज्यमन्त्री तथा सहायक मन्त्रीहरूले कसको समक्ष शपथ लिन्छन्?,मुख्यमन्त्री तथा मन्त्रीहरूले प्रदेश प्रमुखसमक्ष शपथ लिन्छन् भने राज्यमन्त्री तथा सहायक मन्त्रीहरूले मुख्यमन्त्रीसमक्ष शपथ लिन्छन्।,"राज्यका सदस्यहरूको प्रश्नलाई ध्यानपूर्वक जाँच गरेँ । यहाँ उत्तर छ:

मुख्यमन्त्री तथा मन्त्रीहरूले State Assembly (प्रदेश सभा) को माथि स्थित व्यवस्थापिकालाई केभनको முன் स्रोधनकोमा कुरा लिन्छन् र राज्यमन्त्री तथा सहायक मन्त्रीहरूले स्रोधनको முன் कुरा लिन्छन्।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE090,English,Which constitutional authority must the Chief Minister keep informed about resolutions of the State Council of Ministers?,The Chief of State.,The Chief Minister must keep informed about resolutions of the State Council of Ministers.,Correct,Not a strict error,False
FE090,Nepali,प्रदेश मन्त्रिपरिषद्का निर्णयबारे मुख्यमन्त्रीले कसलाई जानकारी गराउनुपर्छ?,प्रदेश प्रमुख।,"सर्वोच्च अदालतको संवैधानिक इजलास।

Explanation: Article 181(d) states that the Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court gives the final decision on whether a member of the State Assembly is disqualified.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FE091,English,Name any two matters that the Chief Minister must inform the Chief of State about.,"Any two of: resolutions of the State Council of Ministers, Bills to be introduced in the State Assembly, information requested by the Chief of State, or the current general state of affairs of the State.","The answer is:

1.  The progress of government projects and policies.
2.  Any significant challenges or issues facing the state.

Let me know if you'd like more details on any of these points!",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FE091,Nepali,मुख्यमन्त्रीले प्रदेश प्रमुखलाई जानकारी गराउनुपर्ने कुनै दुई विषय उल्लेख गर्नुहोस्।,"प्रदेश मन्त्रिपरिषद्का निर्णय, प्रदेश सभामा पेश हुने विधेयक, प्रदेश प्रमुखले मागेको जानकारी, वा प्रदेशको वर्तमान सामान्य अवस्था मध्ये कुनै दुई।","उत्तर: मुख्यमन्त्रीले प्रदेश प्रमुखलाई निम्न दोबीनो विषयहरूमा जानकारी गराउनुपर्ने बताइएको छ:

1.  प्रदेश सभाका सदस्यहरूको संख्याको सीमा।
2.  प्रदेश सभाका सदस्यहरूको कार्यकालको समय।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE092,English,"According to the Constitution, who approves the rules governing the allocation and transaction of business of the State Government?",The State Government.,The Constitution states that the rules governing the allocation and transaction of business of the State Government are approved by the Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court.,Correct,Not a strict error,False
FE092,Nepali,प्रदेश सरकारको कार्य विभाजन तथा सञ्चालनसम्बन्धी नियम कसले स्वीकृत गर्छ?,प्रदेश सरकार।,"प्रदेश सरकारको कार्य विभाजन तथा सञ्चालनसम्बन्धी नियम, Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court द्वारा स्वीकृत हुन्छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
FE093,English,Can a court question whether the rules regarding the transaction of business of the State Government have been observed?,No. Courts cannot question whether those rules have been observed.,"Yes, a court can question whether the rules regarding the transaction of business of the State Government have been observed. This is addressed by Article 181 of the Constitution of Nepal. The Constitution guarantees the right to challenge government actions in courts.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE093,Nepali,प्रदेश सरकारको कार्य सञ्चालनसम्बन्धी नियम पालना भए वा नभएको विषयमा अदालतले प्रश्न उठाउन सक्छ?,सक्दैन। अदालतले त्यस्ता नियम पालना भए वा नभएको विषयमा प्रश्न उठाउन सक्दैन।,"उत्तर: हाँ, प्रदेश सरकारको कार्य सञ्चालनसम्बन्धी नियम पालना भए वा नभएको विषयमा अदालतले प्रश्न उठाउन सक्छ।

कारण: संविधानले प्रदेश सरकारलाई आचारसंहिता (ethics) र नैतिकताका आधार पर काम गर्न अनिवार्य गर्दछ। यदि प्रदेश सरकारले यसकोन पालन नगندہ छ भने, अदालतले त्यसको कारण खोज्छ ।",Question repetition / non-answer,Question repetition / non-answer,True
FE094,English,"If the office of the Chief of State becomes vacant, who may be designated to act for that State?",The Chief of State of another State may be designated by the President.,"The Constitution doesn’t specify exactly who can take over as Chief of State in case of vacancy. However, it states that “the President of the National Assembly shall assume the duties and responsibilities of the Chief of State.” This implies that the President is expected to step into the role.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE094,Nepali,प्रदेश प्रमुखको पद रिक्त भए कसलाई सो प्रदेशको कार्यवाहक प्रदेश प्रमुख तोकिन सक्छ?,राष्ट्रपतिले अर्को प्रदेशका प्रदेश प्रमुखलाई कार्यवाहकका रूपमा तोक्न सक्छन्।,The Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court is tasked with deciding whether a member of the State Assembly is disqualified.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FE095,English,"Who appoints the Chief of State, and on whose recommendation are most of the Chief of State's constitutional functions exercised?","The President appoints the Chief of State, and most functions are exercised on the recommendation and with the consent of the State Council of Ministers submitted through the Chief Minister.",The Chief of State is appointed by the Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court. Most of the Chief of State’s constitutional functions are exercised on the recommendation of the Constitutional Bench.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FE095,Nepali,प्रदेश प्रमुखको नियुक्ति कसले गर्छ र प्रदेश प्रमुखका अधिकांश संवैधानिक कार्य कसको सिफारिसमा गरिन्छन्?,"राष्ट्रपतिले प्रदेश प्रमुख नियुक्त गर्छन्, र अधिकांश कार्य मुख्यमन्त्रीमार्फत आएको प्रदेश मन्त्रिपरिषद्को सिफारिस तथा सहमतिमा गरिन्छ।",प्रदेश सभा सदस्यलाई मुख्य रूप से任命 गरिने तर प्रदेश सभा सदस्यको ज़्यादा प्रशासनिक कार्यहरू (Administrative tasks) संघको व्यवस्थापनाको लागि Constitutional Bench of the Supreme Court द्वारा तय हुन्छन्।,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
SL001,English,What is the structure of the legislature of a State under the Constitution?,Unicameral.,The structure of the legislature of a state under the Constitution of Nepal is unicameral and called the State Assembly. It consists of one legislative chamber.,Correct,Not a strict error,False
SL001,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार राज्यको व्यवस्थापिका कस्तो हुन्छ?,एक सदनीय।,"राज्यको एक सदनीय व्यवस्थापिकालाई के भनिन्छ?,State Assembly.,प्रदेश सभा।,Article 175 names the unicameral legislature as the State Assembly.,Art. 175,Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,
SL002,Constitution & Law,Composition of State Assembly,Fact Retrieval,Medium,What percentage of State Assembly members are elected through the first-past-the-post electoral system?,प्रदेश सभाका कति प्रतिशत सदस्य प्रत्यक्ष निर्वाचन प्रणालीबाट निर्वाचित हुन्छन्?,Sixty percent.,साठी प्रतिशत।,Articles 176(1)(b) and 176(3) provide that sixty percent are elected through the first-past-the-post system.,Art. 176(3),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,
SL003,Constitution & Law,Composition of State Assembly,Fact Retrieval,Medium,What percentage of State Assembly members are elected through the proportional electoral system?,प्रदेश सभाका कति प्रतिशत सदस्य समानुपातिक निर्वाचन प्रणालीबाट निर्वाचित हुन्छन्?,Forty percent.,चालीस प्रतिशत।,Article 176(3) provides that forty percent are elected through the proportional electoral system.,Art. 176(3),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,
SL004,Constitution & Law,Composition of State Assembly,Fact Retrieval,Medium,What is the minimum age required to vote in an election to the State Assembly?,प्रदेश सभाको निर्वाचनमा मतदान गर्न न्यूनतम उमेर कति हुनुपर्छ?,Eighteen years.,अठार वर्ष।,Article 176(5) grants voting rights to citizens who have completed eighteen years of age.,Art. 176(5),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,
SL005,Constitution & Law,Electoral System,Constitutional Provision,Hard,On what basis are election constituencies determined for members elected through the first-past-the-post system?,प्रत्यक्ष निर्वाचन प्रणालीबाट निर्वाचित हुने सदस्यका लागि निर्वाचन क्षेत्र कुन आधारमा निर्धारण गरिन्छ?,Geography and population.,भूगोल र जनसंख्या।,Article 176(2) requires constituencies to be determined on the basis of geography and population.,Art. 176(2),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,
SL006,Constitution & Law,Voting Rights,Fact Retrieval,Easy,What is the minimum age required to contest the State Assembly election from more than one constituency at the same time?,प्रदेश सभाको कार्यकाल छ महिनाभन्दा बढी बाँकी रहँदा कुनै स्थान रिक्त भए कसरी पूर्ति गर्नुपर्छ?,No.,सक्दैन।,The proviso to Article 176(10) prohibits candidacy in more than one constituency simultaneously.,Art. 176(10),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,
SL007,Constitution & Law,Inclusive Representation,Definition,Hard,""Which community does the Constitution define as """"Khas Arya"""" for the purposes of proportional representation?"""",""समानुपातिक प्रतिनिधित्वका प्रयोजनका लागि संविधानले """"खस आर्य"""" भन्नाले कुन समुदायलाई बुझाउँछ?"",""Kshetri, Brahmin, Thakuri, and Sanyasi (Dashnami)."",""क्षेत्री, ब्राह्मण, ठाकुरी र सन्यासी (दशनामी) समुदाय।"",""The explanation to Article 176(6) defines """"Khas Arya."""""",Art. 176(6),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,
SL008,Constitution & Law,Inclusive Representation,Constitutional Provision,Medium,""Besides the specified social groups, representation of which additional group must political parties also provide when fielding proportional representation candidates?"""",""समानुपातिक निर्वाचनमा उम्मेदवारी दिँदा राजनीतिक दलले उल्लेखित समुदायबाहेक कति थप समूहको प्रतिनिधित्व सुनिश्चित गर्नुपर्छ?,Persons with disabilities.,अपाङ्गता भएका व्यक्तिहरू।,Article 176(7) requires representation of persons with disabilities.,Art. 176(7),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,
SL009,Constitution & Law,Vacancies,Multi-hop Factual,Hard,""If a State Assembly seat becomes vacant with more than six months of the term remaining, how must it be filled?"""",""प्रदेश सभाको कार्यकाल छ महिनाभन्दा बढी बाँकी रहँदा कुनै स्थान रिक्त भए कसरी पूर्ति गर्नुपर्छ?,Through the same electoral system by which the seat was originally filled.,उक्त स्थान जुन निर्वाचन प्रणालीबाट भरिएको थियो, सोही प्रणालीबाट।,Article 176(8) requires vacancies to be filled through the same electoral system.,Art. 176(8),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,
SL010,Constitution & Law,Constitutional Provision,Fact Retrieval,Easy,What is the minimum age required to become a member of the State Assembly?,प्रदेश सभाको सदस्य बन्न न्यूनतम उमेर कति हुनुपर्छ?"",""प्रदेश सभाको सदस्य बन्न न्यूनतम उमेर कति हुनुपर्छ?—अक्तकालीन पदमा पूर्ति गर्न सकानी र सकेननी आउनु पर्छ।"",""Eighteen years.,अठार वर्ष।,Article 178(1)(c) sets the minimum age at twenty-five years.,Art. 178(1)(c),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,
SL011,Constitution & Law,Women's Representation,Constitutional Provision,Hard,""What is the minimum proportion of members elected from each political party to the State Assembly that must be women?"""",""समानुपातिक निर्वाचनमा उम्मेदवारी दिँदा राजनीतिक दलले बुझाउँछ के कति प्रतिशत सदस्यको प्रतिनिधित्व सुनिश्चित गर्नुपर्छ?—समानुपातिक निर्वाचनमा उम्मेदवारी दिँदा राजनीतिक दलले बुझाउँछ को प्रतिशत सदस्यको प्रतिनिधित्व सुनिश्चित गर्नुपर्छ?—कम्तीमा एक-तिहाइ।,Article 176(9) requires at least one-third women representation.,Art. 176(9),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,
SL012,Constitution & Law,Women's Representation,Constitutional Provision,Medium,""Besides the specified social groups, representation of which additional group must political parties also provide when fielding proportional representation candidates?"""",""समानुपातिक निर्वाचनमा उम्मेदवारी दिँदा राजनीतिक दलले उल्लेखित समुदायबाहेक कति थप समूहको प्रतिनिधित्व सुनिश्चित गर्नुपर्छ?—समानुपातिक निर्वाचनमा उम्मेदवारी दिँदा राजनीतिक दलले उल्लेखित समुदायबाहेक को प्रतिनिधित्व सुनिश्चित गर्नुपर्छ?—क्षेत्री, ब्राह्मण, ठाकुरी र सन्यासी (दशनामी) समुदाय।"",""The explanation to Article 176(6) defines """"Khas Arya."""""",Art. 176(6),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,
SL013,Constitution & Law,Electoral System,Fact Retrieval,Hard,""Can a qualified person contest the State Assembly election from more than one constituency at the same time?"""",""निर्वाचन वा मनोनयनबाट पूर्ति हुने राजनीतिक पद बाहेक योग्यताका सन्दर्भमा कति प्रतिशत सदस्यले एकै समयमा एकभन्दा बढी निर्वाचन क्षेत्रबाट प्रदेश सभा सदस्यको उम्मेदवारी दिन्छ?—समानुपातिक निर्वाचनमा उम्मेदवारी दिँदा राजनीतिक दलले बुझाउँछ को प्रतिशत सदस्यले एकै समयमा एकभन्दा बढी निर्वाचन क्षेत्रबाट प्रदेश सभा सदस्यको उम्मेदवारी दिन्छ?—कम्तीमा एक-तिहाइ।,No.,सक्दैन।,The proviso to Article 176(10) prohibits candidacy in more than one constituency simultaneously.,Art. 176(10),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,
