SLP012,English,Who presents a Bill to the Chief of State for assent after certifying it?,The Speaker of the State Assembly.,"Article 242(3) of the Constitution of Nepal outlines the process for submitting Bills to the President for assent. The President certifies that the Bill has been approved by the House of Representatives. Therefore, the entity responsible for presenting a Bill to the Chief of State for assent is the **President**.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
