SLP013,English,Within how many days must the Chief of State give assent to a Bill presented for assent?,Within fifteen days.,Article 240(6) of the Constitution of Nepal outlines the process for obtaining assent on Bills. It states that the Chief of State must give assent within **sixteen** days after the bill is submitted.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
SLP013,Nepali,स्वीकृतिका लागि पेश गरिएको विधेयकमा प्रदेश प्रमुखले कति दिनभित्र स्वीकृति दिनुपर्छ?,पन्ध्र दिनभित्र।,Article 242(3) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that the remaining Members of the Public Service Commission must be appointed from persons with twenty or more years of government service experience within thirty days.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
SLP014,English,Can the Chief of State return a Money Bill to the State Assembly for further deliberation?,No.,"Yes, Article 242(6) of the Constitution of Nepal allows the Chief of State to return a Money Bill to the State Assembly for further deliberation.

