Article 36(1) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that “the Chief of State shall give assent to a Bill returned by the Legislature within ten days.”",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
SLP015,Nepali,प्रदेश प्रमुखले फिर्ता पठाएको विधेयक पुनः पारित भएपछि प्रदेश प्रमुखले कति दिनभित्र स्वीकृति दिनुपर्छ?,पन्ध्र दिनभित्र।,"Article 242(6) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that ""The President shall approve the proposed bill."" Therefore, theप्रदेश प्रमुखले फिर्ता पठाएको विधेयक पुनः पारित भएपछि प्रदेश प्रमुखले स्वीकृति दिनुपर्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
SLP016,English,When does a Bill become an Act?,After the Chief of State gives assent.,"The provided text doesn’t explicitly state when a bill becomes an act. It focuses on the roles and qualifications of key figures within the legal system, particularly in Nepal's Constitution and law-making process.  It mentions Article 240(4)(e) (death as a vacancy), Article 240(5) (reappointment restrictions), and Article 240(6)(a) (experience requirements).",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
