SLP017,English,Under what circumstances may the Chief of State promulgate an Ordinance?,"When the State Assembly is not in session and immediate action is necessary, on the recommendation of the State Council of Ministers.","Article 242, Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that the Chief of State can promulgate an ordinance under certain conditions. The text explicitly mentions that the Chief of State has the power to issue ordinances “in accordance with the laws and regulations.”  It doesn’t provide a detailed list of all circumstances, but it indicates that the authority is empowered to do so based on existing legal frameworks.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
SLP017,Nepali,प्रदेश प्रमुखले कुन अवस्थामा अध्यादेश जारी गर्न सक्छन्?,"प्रदेश सभा अधिवेशनमा नरहेको र तत्काल कार्य आवश्यक भएको अवस्थामा, प्रदेश मन्त्रिपरिषद्को सिफारिसमा।","Article 242(4) of the Constitution of Nepal outlines the powers of the Regional Heads to issue ordinances. They can do so under certain circumstances, including when there is a need for swift action or to address urgent issues. The specific details and conditions are outlined in the text.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
SLP018,English,What legal effect does an Ordinance have after promulgation?,It has the same force and effect as an Act.,"An ordinance has several legal effects upon its promulg, primarily revolving around its implementation and enforcement. Here’s a breakdown of the key effects:

*   **Binding Law:** Ordinances are legally binding on all individuals and entities within Nepal under their jurisdiction. This means they take precedence over other laws or regulations when there is conflict.
*   **Implementation of Government Policies:** They serve as the practical implementation of government policies, directives, and plans.  They translate broad policy goals into specific actions.
*   **Creation of Rules & Regulations:** Ordinances establish rules and regulations that govern particular aspects of life – such as business practices, public services, or social norms.
*   **Public Notice Requirement:** A crucial element is the requirement for an ordinance to be published in the Nepal Gazette (or equivalent official publication) before it comes into effect. This allows for public scrutiny and opportunity for challenge.
*   **Judicial Review Potential:**  While not always a direct outcome, ordinances can be subject to judicial review if they are deemed unconstitutional or violate fundamental rights. The courts will examine whether the ordinance is consistent with the Constitution and other laws.
*   **Authority & Responsibility:** Ordinances grant authority to government agencies and officials to implement the provisions of the ordinance. They also assign responsibility for ensuring compliance.

In essence, an ordinance transforms a policy idea into a concrete legal framework that must be followed by everyone within its scope.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
SLP018,Nepali,जारी भएपछि अध्यादेशको कानुनी प्रभाव के हुन्छ?,यसको प्रभाव ऐनसरह हुन्छ।,"AG009,Constitution & Law,Auditor General,Edge Case,Easy,What happens to the office of the Auditor General if the Auditor General dies?,महालेखा परीक्षकको मृत्यु भएमा पदको अवस्था के हुन्छ?,The office becomes vacant.,पद रिक्त हुन्छ।,Article 240(4)(e) lists death as a circumstance creating vacancy.,Art. 240(4)(e),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
SLP019,English,What happens to an Ordinance if it is not passed by the State Assembly after being tabled?,It automatically ceases to be effective.,"The ordinance will be considered inactive and will not have any legal effect. It will lapse into limbo, meaning it remains unratified.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
SLP019,Nepali,प्रदेश सभामा पेश गरिएपछि अध्यादेश पारित नभए के हुन्छ?,यो स्वतः निष्प्रभावी हुन्छ।,"प्रदेश सभामा पेश गरिएपछि अध्यादेश पारित नहुँ, यसको परिणामले एउटा नयाँ व्यवस्था बनाउनु हो। Article 241(3) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) quyidagi तथ्यहरूलाई स्पष्ट गर्दछ:

*   **अध्यादेशात्मक प्रावधानहरूको समयिक सीमा:** यदि एक अध्यादेशप्रदेश सभामा पेश गरिएकाले पारित नहुँ, तर त्यसको प्रभावकालसीमा माथि छ,$ 3 वर्षभित्रै समाप्त हुन्छ।
*   **अध्यादेशात्मक प्रावधानहरूलाई कार्यान्वयनमा राख्ने व्यवस्था:**  अध्यादेशात्मक प्रावधानहरूको कार्यान्वयनको लागि, विधायिकाले छुट्टलानी समयसीमामा संशोधन गर्नुपर्नेछ।

संक्षिप्तमा, अध्यादेश पारित नहुँ तर त्यसको प्रभावकालसीमा माथि छ,$ 3 वर्षभित्रै समाप्त हुन्छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
SLP020,English,"Unless earlier repealed or rendered ineffective, after how many days from the meeting of the State Assembly does an Ordinance automatically cease to be effective?",Sixty days.,Article 242(6) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that an Ordinance shall cease to be effective after **seven days** from its enactment.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
SLP020,Nepali,पहिले नै खारेज वा निष्प्रभावी नगरिएमा प्रदेश सभाको बैठक बसेको कति दिनपछि अध्यादेश स्वतः निष्प्रभावी हुन्छ?,साठी दिनपछि।,Article 243(1) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that an ordinance shall automatically become effective after 30 days from its date.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
SFP001,English,Under what condition may a tax be levied and collected in a State?,Only in accordance with law.,"The Constitution of Nepal outlines the powers of the government to levy taxes. According to Article 242, the state has the power to levy and collect taxes. However, this power is subject to certain conditions outlined in other provisions of the constitution. Specifically, it’s established that the state can levy taxes on:

*   **Goods:** Taxes can be levied on goods produced or traded within Nepal.
*   **Services:** Taxes can be levied on services provided by individuals and organizations within the country.
*   **Income:** The state has the power to tax income earned by citizens, legal entities, and other persons.
*   **Property:** Taxes can be imposed on property owned by individuals or entities.

It’s important to note that the specific types of taxes allowed and their rates are defined in more detail within the Constitution and related legislation.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
SFP001,Nepali,प्रदेशमा कुन अवस्थामा मात्र कर लगाउन र उठाउन सकिन्छ?,कानुन बमोजिम मात्र।,Article 242(3) of the Constitution of Nepal states that the Public Service Commission can levy taxes on individuals who have twenty or more years of government service experience. This means that the commission can tax those with sufficient experience to levy taxes.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
SFP002,English,Under what condition may a State Government raise a loan or give a guarantee?,Only as provided for in Federal law.,"Article 243, Constitution & Law, Public Finance, Medium, The State can raise a loan or give a guarantee to the private sector under certain conditions.

The text states: “The State may raise a loan or give a guarantee to the private sector for the purpose of promoting economic development and fostering investment.”

Therefore, the answer is: **To promote economic development and foster investment.**",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
SFP002,Nepali,प्रदेश सरकारले कुन अवस्थामा ऋण उठाउन वा जमानत दिन सक्छ?,संघीय कानुनमा व्यवस्था भएबमोजिम मात्र।,"प्रदेश सरकारले ऋण उठाउन वा जमानत दिन सक्ने अवस्था खालीलप्रमाणे छन्:

*   **आर्थिक स्थिति:** प्रदेश सरकारको आर्थिक स्थिति कमजोर भएमा, तिनीर्नु परेனால் ऋण उठाउनुपर्ने सम्भावना हो।
*   **सरकारी राजस्व:** प्रदेश सरकारका राजस्व कम भएગા ऋण उठाउनुपर्ने संभावना हुन्छ।
*   **कर्ज कालावधी:** प्रदेश सरकारले आफ्नो कर्जा अवधि सकरीज नहुँस्, तर जान्नु पर्छ कि तिर्नु पर्छ।
*   **आर्थिक संकट:** प्रदेश सरकारमा आर्थिक संकट आए भने, तिर्नको सम्भावना बढ्नेछ।

यो अवस्थामा, प्रदेश सरकार ऋण उठाउन र जमानत दिन सक्ने तर यो धेरै जोखिमपूर्ण हुन्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
SFP003,English,Which revenues are excluded from the State Consolidated Fund?,Revenues of trusts (Guthi).,"The Constitution of Nepal doesn’t explicitly list revenues that are excluded from the State Consolidated Fund. However, it does state that the State Consolidated Fund includes all revenues derived from the activities of the State and its agencies. Therefore, the answer would be **all revenues derived from the activities of the State and its agencies.**",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
SFP003,Nepali,प्रदेश सञ्चित कोषमा जम्मा नगरिने राजस्व कुन हो?,गुठीको राजस्व।,"प्रदेश सञ्चित कोषमा जम्मा नगरिने राजस्व, स्थानीय सरकारको राजस्व।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
SFP004,English,What is the name of the State Government Fund into which specified revenues and receipts are credited?,State Consolidated Fund.,The name of the State Government Fund is “Public Revenue Fund”.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
SFP004,Nepali,तोकिएका राजस्व तथा रकम जम्मा गरिने प्रदेश सरकारको कोषको नाम के हो?,प्रदेश सञ्चित कोष।,"The office of the Auditor General is called ""महालेखा परीक्षकको मृत्यु भएमा पदको अवस्था के हुन्छ?, महालेखा परीक्षकको मृत्यु भएमा पदको अवस्था के हुन्छ?,The office becomes vacant. ,पद रिक्त हुन्छ।,Article 240(4)(e) lists death as a circumstance creating vacancy.,Art. 240(4)(e),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
SFP005,English,"Besides revenues, what other receipts of the State Government are credited to the State Consolidated Fund?","Loans, loan repayments, and grants or loans received from the Government of Nepal.",The provided text doesn’t contain information about the receipts of the state government beyond revenue. It focuses on the appointment and qualifications of the Auditor General.,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
SFP005,Nepali,राजस्व बाहेक प्रदेश सरकारबाट प्राप्त कुन-कुन रकम प्रदेश सञ्चित कोषमा जम्मा गरिन्छ?,"ऋण, ऋण फिर्ताबाट प्राप्त रकम तथा नेपाल सरकारबाट प्राप्त अनुदान वा ऋण।",The revenue from the region government is collected by the Regional Government Office.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
SFP006,English,Can expenditure be incurred from the State Consolidated Fund or other State Government Funds without constitutional authorization?,No.,"No, expenditure cannot be incurred from the State Consolidated Fund or other State Government Funds without constitutional authorization.

Article 36 of the Constitution of Nepal outlines the sources of state revenue and establishes a clear framework for financial transactions.  Expenditure must always be authorized by the Parliament through legislation. This is enshrined in the Constitution to ensure fiscal discipline and accountability.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
SFP006,Nepali,संवैधानिक व्यवस्था बिना प्रदेश सञ्चित कोष वा अन्य प्रदेश सरकारी कोषबाट खर्च गर्न सकिन्छ?,सकिँदैन।,"नinja, न हो।

Explanation:

Article 240(7) of the Constitution of Nepal states that the Auditor General can only audit accounts of federal and state government offices and constitutional bodies. It does not grant the authority to audit other offices or bodies without the consent of the relevant authorities.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
SFP007,English,Which Act authorizes expenditure required when an Appropriation Bill is under consideration?,An Act.,"Article 241, Constitution of Nepal (2015) authorizes the government to spend money on matters related to the preparation and consideration of Appropriation Bills.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
SFP007,Nepali,विनियोजन विधेयक विचाराधीन हुँदा आवश्यक खर्च कुन ऐनले अधिकार दिन्छ?,ऐन।,"विनियोजन विधेयक विचाराधीन हुँदा, संविधानले अधिकार दिने एउटा ऐन ‘अनुदान कानून’ (Constitutional Law) हो।

यहाँ स्पष्टीकरण लिहित हूँ:

*   **अनुदान कानून:** संविधानले सरकारलाईislation प्रक्रियामा सहभागी भएर, संशोधन गर्न, नयाँ कानुनहरू बनाउन र अन्य कानूनी कार्यहरू गर्नबाटै अधिकार दिन्छ।
*   **विनियोजन विधेयक:** जब एक विधेयक प्रस्तावित हुन्छ भने, यसलाई संसदको सदन (House of Parliament) द्वारा छानन्नेछ । यदि विधेयकले संविधानको प्रावधानलाई कमजोर गराउँदै आए भने, संसदले त्यसलाई अस्वीकार गर्न पाउँदा, विधेयकमा परिवर्तनहरू ल्याउनुपर्ने अवस्था आउँछ।

त्यसैले, विधेयक तयारisdigit्ने तरतथ्यमा, संविधानले निर्णय गर्ने अधिकार दिन्छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
SFP008,English,Which Article governs matters relating to the State Contingency Fund?,Article 212.,"Article 242, Constitution of Nepal (2015) governs matters relating to the State Contingency Fund.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
