LE019,Nepali,"गाउँ सभा वा नगर सभाको सदस्य जिल्ला समन्वय समितिको प्रमुख, उपप्रमुख वा सदस्य निर्वाचित भएमा उसको पदमा के हुन्छ?",गाउँ सभा वा नगर सभाको सदस्य पद स्वतः समाप्त हुन्छ।,"AG016,Constitution & Law,Auditor General,Fact Retrieval,Medium,If the District Coordinator, Deputy Mayor, or Member of Parliament (MP) are elected to the Village Council, the Auditor General's position will be vacant. The District Coordinator, Deputy Mayor, and MP will replace the elected officials.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
LE020,English,Which government law provides for other functions of the District Assembly?,State law.,"Article 241(1) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) outlines the responsibilities of the District Assembly. It states that the District Assembly is responsible for overseeing the administration and development of local government areas, including the implementation of laws and regulations related to local governance.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
LE020,Nepali,जिल्ला सभाका अन्य कार्यहरू कुन कानुनले व्यवस्था गर्छ?,प्रदेश कानुन।,"Article 241(1) of the Constitution of Nepal lists the functions of the Districtसभा. Here's a breakdown of those functions, as outlined in Article 241(1):

*   **Legislative Function:** The Districtसभा is responsible for making laws and enacting legislation.
*   **Representation:** They represent the people of their respective districts.
*   **Local Governance:** They oversee local government activities within their districts.
*   **Monitoring:** They monitor the performance of the local government.
*   **Public Opinion:** They gather public opinion and provide feedback to the government.

Essentially, Article 241(1) defines the Districtसभा's role as a crucial component of Nepal’s democratic governance system.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
LL001,English,In which bodies is the legislative power of the Local Level vested?,Village Assembly and Municipal Assembly.,The Legislative Power of the Local Level is vested in the Municipalities and VDCs.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
LL001,Nepali,स्थानीय तहको विधायिकी शक्ति कुन निकायमा निहित हुन्छ?,गाउँ सभा र नगर सभामा।,स्थानीय तहको विधायिकी शक्ति स्थानीय तहको विधायिकी शक्ति राष्ट्रिय तहको विधायिकी शक्तिमा निहित छ।,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
LL002,English,Which Schedules contain the legislative powers of the Village Assembly and Municipal Assembly?,Schedule-8 and Schedule-9.,The relevant schedules are **Schedule 8** and **Schedule 9**.,Correct,Not a strict error,False
LL002,Nepali,गाउँ सभा र नगर सभाको विधायिकी शक्ति कुन अनुसूचीमा उल्लेख गरिएको छ?,अनुसूची–८ र अनुसूची–९।,गाउँ सभा र नगर सभाको विधायिकी शक्ति **Article 240(4)(e)** मा उल्लेख गरिएको छ।,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
LL003,English,What is the legislative body established in each Village Body called?,Village Assembly.,The Legislative Body established in each Village Body is called the Village Council.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
LL003,Nepali,प्रत्येक गाउँपालिकामा स्थापना हुने विधायिकी निकायलाई के भनिन्छ?,गाउँ सभा।,प्रत्येक गाव्यपालिकामा स्थापना हुने विधायिकी निकायलाई 'ग्रामसभा' भन्ने हो।,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
LL004,English,Who are the members of the Village Assembly?,"Chairperson, Vice-Chairperson, Ward Chairpersons, four members from each ward, and Dalit or minority members of the Village Executive.","The provided text doesn't contain information about the composition of the Village Assembly. It focuses on the Auditor General, Constitution & Law, and the Public Service Commission.",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
LL004,Nepali,गाउँ सभाका सदस्यहरू को-को हुन्छन्?,"अध्यक्ष, उपाध्यक्ष, वडा अध्यक्षहरू, प्रत्येक वडाबाट चार सदस्य र गाउँ कार्यपालिकाका दलित वा अल्पसंख्यक सदस्यहरू।","गाउँ सभाका सदस्यहरूलाई कति सदस्य हुन्छन्?

The answer is:  गाउँ सभाका सदस्यहरूलाई कति सदस्य हुन्छन्?

Article 241(1) states that the number of members in a village council is determined by the number of villagers.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
LL005,English,How many women must be represented from each ward in a Village Assembly?,At least two women.,"The provided text doesn’t contain information about the number of women representatives required per ward in a Village Assembly. It focuses on the appointment and qualifications of the Auditor General, Public Service Commission, and Constitution of Nepal.",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
LL005,Nepali,गाउँ सभामा प्रत्येक वडाबाट कति जना महिला प्रतिनिधित्व हुनुपर्छ?,कम्तीमा दुई जना महिला।,"Article 242(4) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that ""The number of women representatives in village councils shall be proportional to the proportion of women in the population of each village.""

Therefore, in a village council, there should be approximately **one woman representative per ten members** of the village. 

This is a key element of ensuring gender equality within village governance.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
LL006,English,What is the composition of a Ward Committee of a Village Body?,One Ward Chairperson and four members.,"The composition of a Ward Committee in a village body typically includes representatives from various sectors, reflecting the diverse needs and concerns within the community. Here’s a breakdown of what’s generally included:

*   **Village Elders:** These are usually respected individuals who have lived in the area for many years and possess valuable knowledge about local issues.
*   **Local Leaders/Representatives:** Individuals from the village council, religious leaders, or other influential figures can represent the community's interests.
*   **Women Representatives:** Ensuring women’s participation is crucial for equitable representation and addressing community needs.
*   **Youth Representatives:**  Young people often bring fresh perspectives and energy to the committee, ensuring the committee remains relevant and responsive to changing times.
*   **Sectoral Representatives (Depending on the Village):** Depending on the specific village's needs, representatives from sectors like agriculture, education, health, or sanitation might be included.
* **Representatives of Local Organizations:**  These could include community groups, NGOs, or other organizations that work within the village.

The exact composition can vary depending on the size and complexity of the village, but this is a general framework for ensuring a balanced and representative Ward Committee.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
LL006,Nepali,गाउँपालिकाको वडा समितिको संरचना कस्तो हुन्छ?,एक वडा अध्यक्ष र चार सदस्य।,"AG009,Constitution & Law,Auditor General,Edge Case,Easy,What happens to the structure of a village ward office?,महालेखा परीक्षकको मृत्यु भएमा पदको अवस्था के हुन्छ?,पद रिक्त हुन्छ।,Article 240(4)(e) lists death as a circumstance creating vacancy.,Art. 240(4)(e),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

AG010,Constitution & Law,Auditor General,Fact Retrieval,Easy,Is the village ward office appointed under Article 240(2) eligible for reappointment?,धारा २४०(२) बमोजिम नियुक्त महालेखा परीक्षक पुनः नियुक्तिका लागि योग्य हुन्छन्?,""No, not eligible."",""होइन, योग्य हुँदैन।"",Article 240(5) prohibits reappointment of the Auditor General appointed under clause (2).,Art. 240(5),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

AG011,Constitution & Law,Auditor General Qualification,Definition,Medium,What type of qualification is required regarding audit experience for appointment as Auditor General?,महालेखा परीक्षक नियुक्तिका लागि लेखापरीक्षण अनुभवसम्बन्धी कस्तो योग्यता आवश्यक छ?,""Twenty years of audit-related experience or equivalent specified qualification.,बीस वर्ष लेखापरीक्षणसम्बन्धी अनुभव वा तोकिएको समकक्ष योग्यता।,Article 240(6)(a) provides the experience and education requirements.,Art. 240(6)(a),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

AG012,Constitution & Law,Auditor General Qualification,Fact Retrieval,Medium,Which academic fields are mentioned for a bachelor's degree qualification for Auditor General appointment?,महालेखा परीक्षक नियुक्तिका लागि स्नातक तहको कुन-कुन विषय उल्लेख गरिएको छ?,""Management, commerce, or accounting."",""व्यवस्थापन, वाणिज्य वा लेखा।"",Article 240(6)(a) mentions these fields of bachelor’s degree.,Art. 240(6)(a),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

AG013,Constitution & Law,Auditor General Qualification,Constitutional Provision,Medium,Can a person who is a member of a political party at the time of appointment become Auditor General?,नियुक्तिको समयमा राजनीतिक दलको सदस्य रहेको व्यक्ति महालेखा परीक्षक बन्न सक्छ?,""No.,सक्दैन।,Article 240(6)(b) requires the person not to be a member of any political party at appointment.,Art. 240(6)(b),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

AG014,Constitution & Law,Auditor General Qualification,Fact Retrieval,Easy,What minimum age is required for appointment as Auditor General?,महालेखा परीक्षक नियुक्तिका लागि न्यूनतम उमेर कति आवश्यक छ?,""Forty-five years.,पैँतालीस वर्ष।,Article 240(6)(c) requires attainment of forty-five years of age.,Art. 240(6)(c),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

AG015,Constitution & Law,Auditor General Qualification,Definition,Easy,What moral requirement is specified for appointment as Auditor General?,महालेखा परीक्षक नियुक्तिका लागि कस्तो नैतिक आवश्यकता तोकिएको छ?,""High moral character.,उच्च नैतिकता चरित्र।,Article 240(6)(d) requires the person to have high moral character.,Art. 240(6)(d),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

AG016,Constitution & Law,Auditor General,Constitutional Protection,Hard,Can a person who is a member of a political party at the time of appointment become Auditor General?,एक पटक महालेखा परीक्षक नियुक्त भएको व्यक्ति अर्को सरकारी सेवामा नियुक्त हुन योग्य हुन्छ?,""No.,हुँदैन।,Article 240(6)(b) requires the person not to be a member of any political party at appointment.,Art. 240(6)(b),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

AG017,Constitution & Law,Auditor General Qualification,Exception Handling,Hard,What is the exception to the protection against disadvantageous alteration of the Auditor General's remuneration and service conditions?,महालेखा परीक्षकको सेवाका सर्तहरू प्रतिकूल परिवर्तन गर्न नपाइने व्यवस्थाको अपवाद के हो?,""Emergency declared due to extreme economic disarrays.,चरम आर्थिक अव्यवस्थाका कारण संकटकाल घोषणा भएको अवस्था।,The proviso of Article 240(7) provides this exception.,Art. 240(7),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

AG018,Constitution & Law,Auditor General,Edge Case,Medium,Is a person once appointed as Auditor General eligible for another government service?,एक पटक महालेखा परीक्षक नियुक्त भएको व्यक्ति अर्को सरकारी सेवामा नियुक्त हुन योग्य हुन्छ?,""No.,हुँदैन।,Article 240(8) restricts appointment in another government service after serving as Auditor General.,Art. 240(8),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

AG019,Constitution & Law,Auditor General Functions,Entity Identification,Easy,What authority audits the accounts of Federal and State Government Offices and constitutional bodies?,संघीय तथा प्रदेश सरकारी कार्यालय र संवैधानिक निकायहरूको लेखा कसले परीक्षण गर्छ?,""Auditor General.,महालेखा परीक्षक।,Article 241(1) assigns these audits to the Auditor General.,Art. 241(1),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

AG020,Constitution & Law,Auditor General Functions,Multi-hop Factual,Hard,""Besides the offices listed in Article 241(1), who may require audits of other offices or bodies by the Auditor General?"",धारा २४१(१) मा उल्लिखित कार्यालय बाहेक अन्य कार्यालय वा निकायको लेखापरीक्षण कसले आवश्यक बनाउन सक्छ?,""Federal law.,संघीय कानुन।,Article 241(5) allows Federal law to require audits of other offices or bodies.,Art. 241(5),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

PSC001,Constitution & Law,Public Service Commission,Entity Identification,Easy,What minimum percentage of Public Service Commission Members must be appointed from persons with twenty or more years of government service experience?,लोक सेवा आयोगका सदस्यहरूमध्ये कम्तीमा कति प्रतिशत सदस्य २० वर्ष वा सोभन्दा बढी सरकारी सेवामा काम गरेका व्यक्तिबाट नियुक्त हुनुपर्छ?,""Fifty percent.,पचास प्रतिशत।,Article 242(3) requires at least fifty percent of Members to be appointed from such persons.,Art. 242(3),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

PSC002,Constitution & Law,Public Service Commission,Fact Retrieval,Easy,How many members, including the Chairperson, constitute the Public Service Commission?,अध्यक्षसहित लोक सेवा आयोगमा कति जना सदस्य हुन्छन्?,""Five members.,पाँच जना सदस्य।,Article 242(1) states that the commission consists of the Chairperson and four other Members.,Art. 242(1),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

PSC003,Constitution & Law,Public Service Commission,Constitutional Provision,Medium,Who appoints the chairperson and members of the Public Service Commission?,लोक सेवा आयोगका अध्यक्ष र सदस्यहरूलाई कसले नियुक्त गर्छ?,""The President.,राष्ट्रपति।,Article 242(2) provides that the President appoints the Chairperson and Members.,Art. 242(2),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

PSC004,Constitution & Law,Public Service Commission,Constitutional Provision,Medium,On whose recommendation are the chairperson and members of the Public Service Commission appointed?,लोक सेवा आयोगका अध्यक्ष र सदस्यहरू कसको सिफारिसमा नियुक्त हुनुपर्छ?,""Constitutional Council.,संवैधानिक परिषद्।,Article 242(2) requires the recommendation of the Constitutional Council.,Art. 242(2),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

PSC005,Constitution & Law,Public Service Commission,Composition,Hard,What minimum percentage of Public Service Commission Members must be appointed from persons with twenty or more years of government service experience?,लोक सेवा आयोगका सदस्यहरूमध्ये कम्तीमा कति प्रतिशत सदस्य २० वर्ष वा सोभन्दा बढी सरकारी सेवामा काम गरेका व्यक्तिबाट नियुक्त हुनुपर्छ?,""Fifty percent.,पचास प्रतिशत।,Article 242(3) requires at least fifty percent of Members to be appointed from such persons.,Art. 242(3),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

PSC006,Constitution & Law,Public Service Commission,Multi-hop Factual,Hard,""Besides the offices listed in Article 241(1), who may require audits of other offices or bodies by the Auditor General?"",धारा २४१(१) मा उल्लिखित कार्यालय बाहेक अन्य सरकारी सेवामा नियुक्त अन्य अधिकारीको लेखापरीक्षण कसले आवश्यक बनाउन सक्छ?,""Federal law.,संघीय कानुन।,Article 241(5) allows Federal law to require audits of other offices or bodies of other officials.,Art. 241(5),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

