LL019,English,When must another Village Assembly or Municipal Assembly be elected after expiration of the current term?,Not later than six months after expiration of the term.,"Article 242(6) of the Constitution of Nepal outlines the process for electing new Village Assemblies and Municipal Assemblies. It states that “If the term of a Village Assembly or Municipal Assembly expires, then a new election must be held within six months.”  Therefore, after the current term ends, another election must occur within six months.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
