LFP008,Nepali,गाउँ कार्यपालिका वा नगर कार्यपालिकाले घाटा बजेट पेश गरेमा के प्रस्ताव गर्नुपर्छ?,घाटा पूर्ति गर्ने स्रोतहरू।,"गाउँ कार्यपालिका वा नगर कार्यपालिकाले घाटा बजेट पेश गर्दा, निम्न कामहरू प्रस्ताव गर्नुपर्छन्:

*   **बजट निर्माण:** गाउँ कार्यपालिकाले आफ्नो बजेट योजना बनाउनुपर्छ। यसमा स्थानीय सरकारको आवश्यकता अनुसार राजस्व स्रोत र खर्चहरूको अनुमान लगाइनु पर्छ।
*   **खर्च व्यवस्थापन:** बजेटमा समावेश गरिने Expenses (खर्च)को सूची तयार गर्नु पर्छ, जस्तै:
    *   **निर्माण कार्य:** roads, bridges, parks, public spaces, infrastructure निर्माणका लागि expenses.
    *   **देखभालकार्य:** सार्वजनिक शौचालय, तिरामा, यातायात, सुरक्षा व्यवस्था, आदि।
    *   **कर्मचारी खर्च:** कर्मचारीहरूको तलब, भत्ते, प्रशिक्षण, र अन्य लाभहरू।
    *   **व्यवस्थापन खर्च:** कार्यालयीन ठाउँको व्यवस्थापन, प्रशासनिक expenses, आदि।
    *   **अन्य Expenses:** स्थानीय कार्यक्रम, festivals, sports events, civic activities, आदि।
*   **बजट स्वीकृतीकरण:** बजेटमा दिए गए रकमलाई सरकारले स्वीकार गर्नुपर्छ।
*   **बजट समीक्षा:** बजेटको व्यवस्थापन कसरी छ, तिस वर्षभित्रसम्मको प्रगति जाँच गरनु पर्छ।
*   **बजट अपडेट:** आवश्यकता अनुसार बजेटलाई अद्यतन (update) गराउनुपर्छ ताकि स्थानीय सरकारले आफ्नो योजनाअनुरुद्ध expenses पूरा गर्न सक्ये।

त्यसैले, गाउँ कार्यपालिकाले घाटा बजेट पेश गर्दा, तिस वर्षभित्रको प्रगतिमा सुधार आउनु पर्छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
FI001,English,To what extent may Federal Law be made applicable according to Article 231?,The whole of Nepal or any part of its territory.,"Article 231 of the Constitution of Nepal outlines the powers and limitations of Federal Law. It states that Federal Law shall not conflict with the provisions of the Constitution, and it shall be interpreted in a manner consistent with the principles of federalism.  Therefore, Federal Law can be made applicable to matters that are within its scope, but it cannot override fundamental constitutional rights or duties.

Here's a breakdown of how this works:

* **Scope of Federal Law:** Federal Law is generally limited to areas specifically defined in the Constitution as being subject to federal jurisdiction.
* **Constitutional Rights and Duties:**  Federal Law cannot interfere with fundamental rights guaranteed by the Constitution, such as the right to life, liberty, equality, and freedom from arbitrary arrest or detention. It also can't diminish the powers of the Federal Government.

**In essence, Federal Law operates within a framework established by the Constitution.**

To provide a more detailed answer, I would need to know *which* specific areas of law are being considered when asking this question.  However, based solely on the text provided, the core principle is that federal law must be consistent with the constitution.",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
FI001,Nepali,धारा २३१ अनुसार संघीय कानून कुन क्षेत्रमा लागू गर्न सकिन्छ?,नेपालको सम्पूर्ण भूभाग वा आवश्यक परे कुनै भागमा।,"धारा २३१ अनुसार संघीय कानून, संघीय सरकारको अधिकारलाई सीमित गर्दछ। यसले संघीय सरकारको कार्यहरूको एक निश्चित सूची प्रदान गर्दछ, जसमध्ये केवल संघीय सरकारले मात्र काम गर्न सक्छन्।",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FI002,English,What is the difference between the applicability of Federal Law and State Law under Article 231?,Federal Law applies to Nepal or any part of Nepal; State Law applies to the whole or any part of that State.,"Under Article 231 of the Constitution of Nepal, Federal Law takes precedence over State Law when there’s a conflict. Here's a breakdown of the key differences:

* **Federal Law Takes Precedence:** If there is a legal dispute or conflict between federal and state laws, the federal law prevails. This means the federal government's interpretation of the Constitution will be applied first.
* **State Law Remains in Effect:** State Law remains in effect until it’s superseded by Federal Law.  This ensures that the fundamental rights and principles enshrined in the Constitution are protected at all times.

**In essence, Article 231 establishes a hierarchy where federal law is supreme when there's a conflict.** It’s designed to safeguard the constitutional framework of Nepal, ensuring both national unity and individual liberties.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FI002,Nepali,धारा २३१ अनुसार संघीय कानून र प्रदेश कानूनको लागू हुने क्षेत्रबीच के फरक छ?,संघीय कानून नेपालभर वा कुनै भागमा लागू हुन्छ; प्रदेश कानून सम्बन्धित प्रदेशभर वा त्यसको कुनै भागमा लागू हुन्छ।,"धारा २३१ अनुसार, संघीय कानून र प्रदेश कानूनको लागू हुने क्षेत्र बीचमा निम्नफरक छ।

*   **संघीय कानून:** संघीय कानूनले सबै राज्यहरूलाई एकजुट बनाउनुको लागि बनाए गए तर यसले स्थानीय सरकारको अधिकारलाई सीमित गर्दछ।
*   **प्रदेश कानून:** प्रदेश कानूनले स्थानीय सरकारको अधिकारलाई थप विस्तार दिन्छ, र यो संघीय कानूनमा पाएको तरथमेली नहुँdV सकेनको अधिकारलाई समावेश गर्छ।

संक्षिप्त रूपमा, संघीय कानूनले सबै राज्यहरूलाई एकजुट बनाउनुको लागि बनाए गए तर यसले स्थानीय सरकारको अधिकारलाई सीमित गर्दछ, जबकि प्रदेश कानूनले स्थानीय सरकारको अधिकारलाई थप विस्तार दिन्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FI003,English,When may the Federal Parliament make laws on matters listed in Schedule-6 for States?,When two or more States request the Government of Nepal to make such laws.,Article 242(3) of the Constitution of Nepal states that the Federal Parliament can make laws on matters listed in Schedule-6 for States.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FI003,Nepali,अनुसूची-६ मा रहेका विषयमा संघीय संसदले कहिले कानून बनाउन सक्छ?,दुई वा दुईभन्दा बढी प्रदेशले नेपाल सरकारलाई कानून बनाउन अनुरोध गरेमा।,अनुसूची-६ मा रहेका विषयमा संघीय संसदले कानून बनाउन सक्नेछन्।,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FI004,English,"What principles form the basis of relations between the Federation, States, and Local levels?","Cooperation, co-existence and coordination.","The Constitution of Nepal outlines a framework that establishes a hierarchical relationship between the Federal Government, State Governments, and Local Authorities. Here’s a breakdown of the key principles underpinning this system:

*   **Federalism:** The Constitution enshrines federalism as the fundamental principle. This means power is divided among three levels – the Federal Government, States, and Local Authorities – each with distinct responsibilities and areas of authority.
*   **Division of Powers:**  The Constitution clearly defines the division of powers between these levels. It establishes a clear hierarchy where the Federal Government has supreme legislative authority, while States have responsibility for local governance, and Local Authorities handle day-to-day administration within their jurisdictions.
*   **Constitutional Guarantee of Rights:** The Constitution guarantees fundamental rights to all citizens across all three levels – federal, state, and local. This includes protection against arbitrary deprivation of life, liberty, security, health, dignity, and/or freedom.
*   **Accountability & Transparency:**  The Constitution emphasizes accountability and transparency in the functioning of each level. The Federal Government is accountable to the people through elections, while States are accountable to the people through their legislatures. Local Authorities are also subject to oversight by the Federal Government.
*   **Mutual Trust & Cooperation:** The Constitution promotes mutual trust and cooperation between the three levels. It emphasizes that all three levels must work together for the common good of Nepal.

In essence, the Constitution establishes a system where power is distributed, rights are protected, and each level has responsibilities to ensure the overall well-being of the nation.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FI004,Nepali,"संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहबीचको सम्बन्ध कुन सिद्धान्तमा आधारित हुन्छ?","सहकार्य, सहअस्तित्व र समन्वय।","संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय तह बीचका सम्बन्ध सिद्धान्त मा आधारित हुन्छ **""संसदीय प्रणाली""**।

यहाँ तरिकाexplained दिइएकी छन्:

*   **संसदीय प्रणाली (Parliamentary System):** भारत, नेपालको अधिकांशै देशहरू सन्दर्भमा संस्कृतिएकी छन् कि संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहले सरकारलाई प्रयोग गर्छन्। यसमा, संसदले स्थानीय तथा संघीय нивоका निर्णयहरूको समीक्षा गर्छ् तर उनलाई कार्यान्वयन गर्न सक्दैन्।
*   **संसदीय प्रणालीको आधार:** भारतमा, संसदले स्थानीय तथा صوبीय स्तरका नीतिहरू तय गर्दछन् र त्यसलाई सरकारी अधिकारीहरू चलाउनु पर्छन्। यसको कारण यो कि संसदले स्थानीय सरकारलाई प्रयोग गर्छ् तर त्यसलाई कार्यान्वयन गर्न सक्दैन्।
*   **स्थानीय तहहरूको भूमिका:** स्थानीय तहहरूले स्थानीय सरकारमा निर्णयहरू बनाउने, 시행 गर्ने र उनका व्यवस्थापन गर्ने जिम्मेवारी दिन्छन्।

त्यसैността, संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय तह बीचका सम्बन्ध सिद्धान्त मा आधारित हुन्छ ""संसदीय प्रणाली"" ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FI005,English,Who may give necessary directions to a State Council of Ministers on matters of national importance?,The Government of Nepal.,"Article 240(7) of the Constitution of Nepal lists the authorities that can provide direction to the State Council of Ministers on matters of national importance. These are:

*   **Federal Law:** Federal law can give directions to the State Council of Ministers on matters of national importance.
*   **Constitutional Council:** The Constitutional Council can give directions to the State Council of Ministers on matters of national importance.
*   **The President:** The President can give directions to the State Council of Ministers on matters of national importance.

Essentially, any authority with constitutional powers can provide direction.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FI005,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय महत्वका विषयमा प्रदेश मन्त्रिपरिषद्लाई आवश्यक निर्देशन कसले दिन सक्छ?,नेपाल सरकारले।,"राष्ट्रिय महत्वका विषयमा प्रदेश मन्त्रिपरिषद्लाई आवश्यक निर्देशन दिन, सरकारले प्रदेश मन्त्रिपरिषद्को कार्यक्षेत्रमा सुधार र व्यवस्थापन गर्न सकसम्म। यसले स्थानीय स्तर पर पहिलेय योजना बनाउन, समस्या समाधान गर्न र विकासलाई प्रोत्साहन गर्न गाहट बन्न दिनेछ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
FI006,English,For how long may the President suspend or dissolve a State Council of Ministers and State Assembly under Article 232(3)?,Not exceeding six months.,Article 232(3) of the Constitution of Nepal states that the President can suspend or dissolve the State Council of Ministers and State Assembly for a period not exceeding three months.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FI006,Nepali,धारा २३२(३) अनुसार राष्ट्रपतिले प्रदेश मन्त्रिपरिषद् र प्रदेश सभा कति समयसम्म निलम्बन वा विघटन गर्न सक्छन्?,छ महिनाभन्दा बढी नहुने गरी।,"Article 232(3) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) allows the President to remove or suspend the Provincial Council and Provincial Assembly for a period of up to six months.

Here's a breakdown of what that means in practical terms:

*   **Removal:** The President can remove the Provincial Council and Provincial Assembly if they are deemed to be obstructing the functioning of the government or not performing their duties effectively.
*   **Suspension:**  The President can suspend the Provincial Council and Provincial Assembly for a period of up to six months without any specific reason.

It's important to note that this is a temporary measure, and the President must have a valid justification for such action.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FI007,English,What majority of the Federal Parliament is required to ratify suspension or dissolution of a State Council of Ministers and State Assembly?,Two-thirds majority of the total number of existing members.,"Article 242, Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that the majority of the Federal Parliament must be required to ratify suspension or dissolution of a State Council of Ministers and State Assembly.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FI007,Nepali,प्रदेश मन्त्रिपरिषद् र प्रदेश सभा निलम्बन वा विघटनको अनुमोदन गर्न संघीय संसदमा कस्तो बहुमत आवश्यक हुन्छ?,तत्काल कायम रहेका सदस्यहरूको दुई तिहाइ बहुमत।,The federal parliament will require a majority of the votes to approve the suspension or dissolution of the provincial council.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
FI008,English,Within how many days must the Federal Parliament ratify a suspension or dissolution made under Article 232(3)?,Within thirty-five days.,Article 232(3) of the Constitution of Nepal outlines the process for suspending or dissolving the Federal Parliament. It states that the Federal Parliament must ratify such a measure within **14 days** after its announcement.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FI008,Nepali,धारा २३२(३) अन्तर्गत गरिएको निलम्बन वा विघटनलाई संघीय संसदले कति दिनभित्र अनुमोदन गर्नुपर्छ?,पैँतीस दिनभित्र।,"The answer is: **Within thirty days**

Article 232(3) of the Constitution of Nepal outlines the process for approving suspension or dissolution of a federal parliament. It states that the Federal Parliament must approve the suspension or dissolution within thirty (30) days of its occurrence.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FI009,English,"If dissolution of a State Assembly is ratified, within what period must an election be held?",Within six months.,"Article 67 of the Constitution of Nepal outlines the timeframe for holding elections after the dissolution of a State Assembly. It states that **within six months** following the dissolution, an election must be held.

Here's a breakdown:

*   **Article 67(1):** ""The President shall hold elections within six months following the dissolution of the State Assembly.""
*   **Article 67(2):** “The President shall hold elections within six months after the dissolution of the State Assembly.”

Therefore, an election must be held within six months.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
FI009,Nepali,प्रदेश सभा विघटन अनुमोदन भएमा कति समयभित्र निर्वाचन गरिनुपर्छ?,छ महिनाभित्र।,Article 242(6) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that the Regional Assembly must be dissolved within six months of the approval of the dissolution decree.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FI010,English,"During Federal rule in a State, which body may make laws on Schedule-6 matters?",The Federal Parliament.,"The answer is the **Federal Council**.

Article 242(3) of the Constitution of Nepal states that “the Federal Council shall make laws on Schedule-6 matters.” This provision grants the Federal Council authority to legislate on specific areas within the state’s framework.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FI010,Nepali,प्रदेशमा संघीय शासन कायम रहेको समयमा अनुसूची-६ का विषयमा कानून कसले बनाउन सक्छ?,संघीय संसदले।,"Article 242(3) of the Constitution of Nepal outlines the requirements for appointing members to the Public Service Commission. It states that the Constitutional Council must appoint at least fifty percent of the Members from persons with twenty or more years of government service experience.  Therefore, the jurisdiction of Article 6 (the subject of the regulation) is limited to the areas where there is a federal system in Nepal.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FI011,English,What must one State do regarding legal provisions or judicial and administrative decisions of another State?,Render assistance in execution.,"Article 242 of the Constitution of Nepal outlines the obligations of a state to provide for the protection of foreign nationals. It states that a state has a duty to ensure the rights and safety of foreign nationals within its territory, including the right to legal assistance and protection against arbitrary actions by other states.

Here's a breakdown of what this entails:

* **Right to Legal Assistance:** A state must provide access to legal counsel for foreign nationals in matters involving their rights and interests.
* **Protection Against Arbitrary Actions:** The state has a responsibility to safeguard the safety and well-being of foreign nationals from arbitrary actions by other states, including those that violate international law or human rights standards.
* **Fair Treatment & Due Process:**  The state must ensure fair treatment and due process for foreign nationals in legal proceedings within its territory. This includes upholding the rule of law and preventing discrimination.

**In essence, Article 242 emphasizes a state's duty to act as a guarantor of international human rights and fundamental freedoms for individuals residing within its borders.**

It’s important to note that this obligation is not absolute; it's balanced against the sovereignty of other states.  The extent of a state's obligations under Article 242 can be determined by international law, treaties, and customary practice.

Do you want me to elaborate on any specific aspect of this? For example, would you like to know more about:

*   Specific mechanisms for providing legal assistance?
*   The role of the International Court of Justice in addressing disputes involving foreign nationals?",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
FI011,Nepali,एउटा प्रदेशले अर्को प्रदेशको कानूनी व्यवस्था वा न्यायिक तथा प्रशासनिक निर्णय सम्बन्धमा के गर्नुपर्छ?,कार्यान्वयनमा सहयोग गर्नुपर्छ।,"Article 242(3) of the Constitution of Nepal states that the Regional Assembly (PA) can order the remaining members of the Public Service Commission to be appointed from persons with twenty or more years of government service experience.

So, a region must appoint the remaining members of the Public Service Commission from people who have worked for 20 years or more in government service.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
FI012,English,Who chairs the Inter-State Council?,The Prime Minister.,"The Constitution of Nepal doesn’t explicitly state who chairs the Inter-State Council. The text focuses on the roles and responsibilities of the Auditor General, which is a separate body with its own chair.",Question repetition / non-answer,Question repetition / non-answer,True
