CIA010,English,How many years of experience must a person have in specified fields to qualify as Chief Commissioner or Commissioner?,At least twenty years.,"Article 242(3) states that “the remaining Members of the Public Service Commission must be appointed from such persons…”. This implies that the required number of years of government service experience is not explicitly stated, but it requires a minimum of twenty years. Therefore, a person must have at least twenty years of government service experience to qualify as Chief Commissioner or Commissioner.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
