EC008,English,At what age does the office of the Chief Election Commissioner or Commissioner become vacant?,Sixty-five years.,"The Constitution doesn’t explicitly state a specific age requirement for the position of Chief Election Commissioner or Commissioner. However, it states that the position is held by individuals who are “competent and qualified” to perform their duties. This implies that the office can be vacated at any time, regardless of age.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
