EC009,English,Which constitutional process can remove the Chief Election Commissioner or Commissioner before completion of tenure?,Impeachment under Article 101.,Article 267(8) of the Constitution of Nepal outlines the procedures for removing a Commissioner from office. It states that “the President may remove the Commissioner before the end of their term.”,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
EC009,Nepali,पदावधि पूरा हुनुअघि प्रमुख निर्वाचन आयुक्त वा निर्वाचन आयुक्तलाई कुन संवैधानिक प्रक्रियाबाट हटाउन सकिन्छ?,धारा १०१ बमोजिम महाभियोग।,"Article 267(8) of the Constitution of Nepal outlines the process for removing the Chief Electoral Commissioner (CEC) or Election Commission Chair (ECCh) from office. Here’s a breakdown of the steps involved:

1. **Notice of Removal:** The CEC/ECCh must formally notify the Supreme Court of their intention to be removed.
2. **Supreme Court Review:** The Supreme Court will review this notification and determine if it is justified. They'll consider whether the removal is necessary for the good of the country.
3. **Court Order:** If the Supreme Court approves the removal, they issue a court order formally removing the CEC/ECCh from office.

**In essence, the process involves a formal legal challenge and approval by the highest judicial body.**",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
