NS006, Constitution & Law,National Security Council Composition,Fact Retrieval,Medium,Who acts as the member secretary of the National Security Council?,Secretary at the Ministry of Defence.,रक्षा मन्त्रालयको सचिव।,Article 266(2) provides that the Secretary at the Ministry of Defence acts as the member secretary.,Art. 266(2),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

NS007, Constitution & Law,National Security Council Reporting,Constitutional Provision,Medium,To whom does the National Security Council submit its annual report?,The President.,राष्ट्रपति।,Article 266(3) states that the Council submits its annual report to the President.,Art. 266(3),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

NS008, Constitution & Law,National Security Council Parliamentary Process,Multi-hop Factual,Hard,How is the annual report of the National Security Council presented before the Federal Parliament?,The President causes it to be laid before the Federal Parliament through the Prime Minister.,राष्ट्रपतिले प्रधानमन्त्रीमार्फत संघीय संसदमा पेश गराउँछन्।,Article 266(3) specifies the reporting process involving the President and Prime Minister.,Art. 266(3),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

NS009, Constitution & Law,National Security Council Fiscal Representation,Fact Retrieval,Medium,Which finance-related government position is included as a member of the National Security Council?,Minister for Finance.,अर्थ मन्त्री।,Article 266(1)(e) lists the Minister for Finance as a member of the Council.,Art. 266(1)(e),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

NS010, Constitution & Law,National Security Council Parliamentary Process,Multi-hop Factual,How is the annual report of the National Security Council presented before the Federal Parliament?,The President causes it to be laid before the Federal Parliament through the Prime Minister.,राष्ट्रपतिले प्रधानमन्त्रीमार्फत संघीय संसदमा पेश गराउँछन्।,Article 266(3) specifies the reporting process involving the President and Prime Minister.,Art. 266(3),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

NS011, Constitution & Law,Nepal Army,Entity Identification,Easy,""What organization shall exist in Nepal for safeguarding independence, sovereignty, territorial integrity, and national unity?"",""नेपालको स्वतन्त्रता, सार्वभौमसत्ता, भौगोलिक अखण्डता र राष्ट्रिय एकताको रक्षा गर्न नेपालमा कुन संगठन रहनेछ?"",Nepal Army.,नेपाली सेना।,Article 267(1) provides for the Nepal Army as an organization committed to safeguarding these national interests.,Art. 267(1),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

NS012, Constitution & Law,Nepal Army Inclusive Representation,Fact Retrieval,Medium,Which groups are specifically mentioned for ensuring inclusive entry into the Nepal Army under the Constitution?,Women, Dalit, आदिवासी, आदिवासी जनजाति, खस आर्य, मधेसी, थारू, पिछडा वर्ग र पिछडिएको क्षेत्रका नागरिक।,Article 267(3) lists these groups for ensuring inclusive entry into the Nepal Army.,Art. 267(3),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

NS013, Constitution & Law,Nepal Army Commander-in-Chief,Fact Retrieval,Medium,Who appoints and removes the Commander-in-chief of the Nepal Army?,The President on the recommendation of the Council of Ministers.,मन्त्रिपरिषद्को सिफारिसमा राष्ट्रपतिले।,Article 267(5) provides this appointment and removal procedure.,Art. 267(5),Constitution ofNepal (2015),,,,,,

NS014, Constitution & Law,Nepal Army Mobilization Procedure,Multi-hop Factual,Hard,What conditions must exist for the mobilization of the Nepal army in cases of grave emergency?,गम्भीर आपतकालीन अवस्थामा नेपाली सेनाको परिचालन गर्न कुन अवस्थाहरू हुनुपर्छ?,""War, external aggression, armed rebellion, or extreme economic disarray affecting sovereignty, territorial integrity, or security."",""युद्ध, बाह्य आक्रमण, सशस्त्र विद्रोह वा चरम आर्थिक विशृंखलताका कारण सार्वभौमसत्ता, भौगोलिक अखण्डता वा सुरक्षामा गम्भीर संकट।,Article 267(6) specifies the circumstances requiring Army mobilization.,Art. 267(6),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,

NS015, Constitution & Law,Nepal Army Commander-in-Chief,Fact Retrieval,Medium,Who appoints and removes the Commander-in-chief of the Nepal Army?,The President on the recommendation of the Council of Ministers.,मन्त्रिपरिषद्को सिफारिसमा राष्ट्रपतिले।,Article 267(5) provides this appointment and removal procedure.,Art. 267(5),Constitution ofNepal (2015),,,,,,

NS016, Constitution & Law,Nepal Army Mobilization Ratification,Numerical Threshold,Hard,Within what period must the declaration of Nepal Army mobilization be ratified by the House of Representatives?,नेपाली सेनाको परिचालन घोषणालाई प्रतिनिधि सभाले कति अवधिभित्र अनुमोदन गर्नुपर्छ?,""War, external aggression, armed rebellion, or extreme economic disarray affecting sovereignty, territorial integrity, or security."",""युद्ध, बाह्य आक्रमण, सशस्त्र विद्रोह वा चरम आर्थिक विशृंखलताका कारण सार्वभौमसत्ता, भौगोलिक अखण्डता वा सुरक्षामा गम्भीर संकट।,Article 267(6) requires ratification by the House of Representatives within one month after declaration.,Art. 267(6),Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,",Correct,Not a strict error,False
NNRFC006,English,To whom must the Chairperson or member submit a written resignation to vacate office?,The President.,"Article 266(3) states that the annual report of the National Security Council is submitted to the President through the Prime Minister. Therefore, the chairperson or member secretary must submit a written resignation to the President.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
NNRFC006,Nepali,पद रिक्त गराउन राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोगका अध्यक्ष वा सदस्यले लिखित राजीनामा कसलाई दिनुपर्छ?,राष्ट्रपति।,The President of the National Natural Resources and Finance Commission shall accept the resignation letter.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
NNRFC007,English,At what age does the office of the Chairperson or member of the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission become vacant?,Sixty-five years.,The Constitution doesn’t specify a specific age for the position of Chairperson or Member of the National Natural Resource and Fiscal Commission. It states that the position becomes vacant upon the resignation of the Prime Minister.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC007,Nepali,कुन उमेर पुगेपछि राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोगका अध्यक्ष वा सदस्यको पद रिक्त हुन्छ?,पैंसठ्ठी वर्ष।,Article 267(8) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that the President of the National Security Council shall be replaced by the Commander-in-Chief of the Nepal Army when they reach the age of 65.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC008,English,Which constitutional process can make the office of the Chairperson or member of the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission vacant before completion of tenure?,Impeachment under Article 101.,"Article 266(1) specifies that the Prime Minister is the chairperson of the National Security Council. Therefore, if the Prime Minister leaves their position, the chairwoman/member of the National Security Council can become vacant.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC008,Nepali,पदावधि पूरा हुनुअघि राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोगका अध्यक्ष वा सदस्यको पद कुन संवैधानिक प्रक्रियाबाट रिक्त हुन सक्छ?,धारा १०१ बमोजिम महाभियोग।,"Article 267(8) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that the President can remove the Commander-in-Chief of the Nepal Army, but only if the House of Representatives approves the removal within one month after the declaration.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC009,English,Who recommends removal of the Chairperson or member of the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission due to physical or mental illness preventing performance of duties?,Constitutional Council.,"Article 266(2) specifies that the Secretary at the Ministry of Defence acts as the member secretary, which implies that if there is a conflict between their duties and health issues, they are responsible for removing them. Therefore, the Chairperson or member of the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission would be removed due to this issue.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC009,Nepali,शारीरिक वा मानसिक रोगका कारण कार्य गर्न असमर्थ भएमा राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोगका अध्यक्ष वा सदस्यलाई हटाउन कसले सिफारिस गर्छ?,संवैधानिक परिषद्।,Article 267(8) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) specifies that the President can recommend the removal of the Chairman or Member of the National Natural Resources and Finance Commission (NRFC) due to physical or mental health conditions.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC010,English,What happens to the office of the Chairperson or member of the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission if the person dies?,The office becomes vacant.,"The Constitution does not specify what happens to the position of Chairperson or Member of the National Natural Resource and Fiscal Commission if the person dies. It states that the Secretary at the Ministry of Defence acts as the member secretary, but there is no mention of succession or replacement procedures in the text.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC010,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोगका अध्यक्ष वा सदस्यको मृत्यु भएमा पदको अवस्था के हुन्छ?,पद रिक्त हुन्छ।,"NS008, Constitution & Law,National Security Council Composition,Fact Retrieval,Easy,If the President of the National Resources and Finance Commission (NRFC) dies, who is appointed as its Chairperson?"",""यदि नेपाली संसाधन तथा वित्त आयोगका प्रधानसेनापतिको मृत्यु भएमा, उनको अध्यक्ष को कति व्यक्तिलाई नियुक्त गरिनेछ?"",The Vice-President of the NRFC.,Vice-प्रिंसिपल र संयुक्त सेनापति।,Article 267(8) states that the Vice-President is appointed by the President.,Art. 267(8), Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
NNRFC011,English,Are the Chairperson and members of the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission eligible for reappointment after completing their term?,"No, they are not eligible for reappointment.","The Constitution does not explicitly state whether the Chairperson and members of the National Resource and Fiscal Commission are eligible for reappointment. However, it states that “the Secretary at the Ministry of Defence acts as the member secretary.” This implies that the position is temporary and subject to change based on the Prime Minister’s discretion.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
NNRFC011,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोगका अध्यक्ष र सदस्यहरू पदावधि पूरा गरेपछि पुनः नियुक्तिका लागि योग्य हुन्छन्?,"होइन, पुनः नियुक्तिका लागि योग्य हुँदैनन्।",The National Natural Resources and Finance Commission (NRFIC) President and Members are appointed and reappointed based on the completion of their tenure.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC012,English,Can a member of the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission be appointed as the Chairperson after serving as a member?,Yes.,"No, according to Article 266(1)(a) of the Constitution of Nepal, the Chairperson of the National Security Council cannot be a member of the Natural Resource and Fiscal Commission. The article states that the Prime Minister is designated as the Chairperson.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC012,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोगको सदस्य पछि अध्यक्ष पदमा नियुक्त हुन सक्छ?,सक्छ।,"उत्तर: हाँ, राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक संसाधन तथा वित्त आयोगको सदस्य पछि अध्यक्ष पदमा नियुक्त हुन सक्छ।

Explanation: Constitution of Nepal (2015) ले स्पष्ट रूप से उल्लेख किया है कि ""राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक संसाधन तथा वित्त आयोग"" (National Natural Resources and Finance Commission) मा सदस्य पछि अध्यक्ष पदमा नियुक्त हुन सक्छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
NNRFC013,English,What educational and professional experience requirement is specified for appointment as Chairperson or member of the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission?,A bachelor's degree in a relevant subject from a recognized university and at least twenty years of expertise in specified fields.,"The Constitution does not specify any specific educational or professional experience requirements for appointments to the National Natural Resource and Fiscal Commission. It states that the Prime Minister is the chairperson, and members are selected from government ministers and military officials.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
NNRFC013,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोगको अध्यक्ष वा सदस्य नियुक्तिका लागि शैक्षिक तथा व्यावसायिक अनुभवसम्बन्धी कस्तो योग्यता आवश्यक छ?,मान्यता प्राप्त विश्वविद्यालयबाट सम्बन्धित विषयमा स्नातक उपाधि र तोकिएका क्षेत्रमा कम्तीमा बीस वर्षको विशेषज्ञता।,"The Constitution of Nepal doesn't explicitly state the required educational and professional experience for the President or Member Secretary of the National Security Council (NSC). However, it does mention that the President is appointed by the Prime Minister.  Therefore, the constitution doesn’t specify any specific qualifications for these positions.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC014,English,"How many years of expertise must a person have in natural resources, fiscal management, economics, law, or management to qualify for appointment?",At least twenty years.,The provided text doesn’t specify the number of years of experience required. It only mentions that the President is responsible for ratifying the declaration of Nepal Army mobilization within one month after the declaration.,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
NNRFC014,Nepali,"राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत, वित्त व्यवस्थापन, अर्थशास्त्र, कानून वा व्यवस्थापन क्षेत्रमा नियुक्तिका लागि कति वर्षको विशेषज्ञता आवश्यक छ?",कम्तीमा बीस वर्ष।,"Answer:
The Constitution of Nepal doesn't specify a specific number of years of expertise required for appointments in the National Security Council or other government positions. However, it does state that the President shall be the supreme commander-in-chief of the Nepal Army. This implies that the President has significant authority and responsibility within these areas, requiring considerable experience and knowledge.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC015,English,Which fields are specifically mentioned for gaining expertise for appointment to the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission?,"Natural resources, fiscal management, economics, law, and management.","The following fields are explicitly mentioned for gaining expertise for appointment to the National Natural Resource and Fiscal Commission:

*   **Natural Resources**
*   **Fiscal Management**",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
NNRFC015,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोगमा नियुक्तिका लागि विशेषज्ञता प्राप्त गर्न कुन-कुन क्षेत्र उल्लेख गरिएको छ?,"प्राकृतिक स्रोत, वित्त व्यवस्थापन, अर्थशास्त्र, कानून र व्यवस्थापन।","The following sectors are mentioned for expert qualifications at the National Natural Resources and Finance Commission (NRFC):

*   **Agriculture**
*   **Forestry**
*   **Mining**
*   **Tourism**
*   **Civil Service**
*   **Social Welfare**",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC016,English,Can a person who is a member of a political party at the time of appointment become Chairperson or member of the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission?,No.,"No, according to the provided text, a person who is a member of a political party at the time of their appointment cannot be the chairperson or member of the National Natural Resource and Fiscal Commission. The text states that ""The Prime Minister is the Chairperson of the National Security Council.""",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
NNRFC016,Nepali,नियुक्तिको समयमा राजनीतिक दलको सदस्य रहेको व्यक्ति राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोगको अध्यक्ष वा सदस्य बन्न सक्छ?,सक्दैन।,"Article 267(8) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that ""The President may appoint a person to be a member of the Natural Resources and Finance Commission.""  Therefore, a political party member can certainly be appointed as a member of this commission.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC017,English,What minimum age is required for appointment as Chairperson or member of the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission?,Forty-five years.,The Constitution does not specify a minimum age requirement for appointments to the National Natural Resource and Fiscal Commission. The text states that “the Prime Minister is the chairperson.”,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
