2),Constitution of Nepal (2015),(NS014,Constitution & Law,National Security Council Composition,Multi-hop Factual,Hard,Which conditions must exist for the mobilization of the Nepal army in cases of grave emergency?—War, external aggression, armed rebellion, or extreme economic disarray affecting sovereignty, territorial integrity, or security.,राष्ट्रिय सुरक्षा परिषद्को परिचालन गर्न कुन अवस्थाहरू हुनुपर्छ?,युद्ध, बाह्य आक्रमण, सशस्त्र विद्रोह वा चरम आर्थिक विशृंखलताका कारण सार्वभौमसत्ता, भौगोलिक अखण्डता वा राष्ट्रिय एकतामा गम्भीर संकट।।,Article 267(5) specifies the circumstances requiring Army mobilization.,Art. 267(5),Constitution of Nepal (2015),(NS015,Constitution & Law,National Security Council Composition,Fact Retrieval,Medium,Who appoints and removes the Commander-in-Chief of the Nepal Army?—The President on the recommendation of the Council of Ministers.,मन्त्रिपरिषद्को सिफारिसमा राष्ट्रपतिले।,Article 267(6) specifies the appointment and removal procedure.,Art. 267(6),Constitution of Nepal (2015),(NS016,Constitution & Law,National Security Council Reporting,Constitutional Provision,Medium,What conditions must exist for the mobilization of the Nepal army in cases of grave emergency?—War, external aggression, armed rebellion, or extreme economic disarray affecting sovereignty, territorial integrity, or security.,राष्ट्रिय सुरक्षा परिषद्को परिचालन गर्न कुन अवस्थाहरू हुनुपर्छ?,युद्ध, बाह्य आक्रमण, सशस्त्र विद्रोह वा चरम आर्थिक विशृंखलताका कारण सार्वभौमसत्ता, भौगोलिक अखण्डता वा राष्ट्रिय एकतामा गम्भीर संकट।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
NNRFC018,English,What moral requirement is required for appointment as Chairperson or member of the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission?,High moral character.,"Article 266(1) of the Constitution of Nepal specifies that the Chairperson of the National Security Council must be the Prime Minister. Therefore, the moral requirement for appointment is that the individual must be the Prime Minister.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC018,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोगको अध्यक्ष वा सदस्य नियुक्तिका लागि कस्तो नैतिक आवश्यकता तोकिएको छ?,उच्च नैतिक चरित्र।,"राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक संसाधन तथा वित्त आयोगको अध्यक्ष वा सदस्य नियुक्तिका लागि, आयोगका सदस्यहरलाई नैतिकताको आधारमा चयन गर्नुपर्छ। यसले निम्न नैतिक आवश्यकताहरू समावेश गर्नेछ:

*   **निष्पक्षता:** सबै кандидатитеबाट निष्पक्ष रूप से मूल्यांकन गरिनेछ ।
*   **समानता:** सबै नागरिकहरूको समान अवसर प्रदान गरिनेछ ।
*   **भूमिकाको अनुरूप नैतिकता:** आयोगका कार्यमा आधारित नैतिकतालाई प्राथमिकता दिनेछ।
*   **कandidat र देखिको क्षमता:** кандидатитеको योग्यता, अनुभव, र क्षमता देखाउनुपर्छ।
*   **सहिष्णुता:** विभिन्न दृष्टिकोणहरूलाई सहुल रूप से हेर्नेछ ।
*   **जहाँसम्म कि छ, त्यस्तै**: आयोगले आफ्नो कार्यमा नैतिकताको पालन गर्न गर्नेछ।

यस बीच, नैतिक मूल्यांकनका लागि, आयोगले एक बोर्ड बनाएर, सबै кандидатитеलाई छानन्ने र त्यसको निर्णय लिनेछ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
NNRFC019,English,Can the remuneration and conditions of service of the Chairperson and members of the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission be altered to their disadvantage while they hold office?,No.,"The Constitution of Nepal does not explicitly grant the government the power to alter the remuneration or conditions of service of individuals holding positions like the Chairperson of the National Security Council (NSC) or members of the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission. The constitution focuses on establishing the roles, responsibilities, and powers of these bodies as defined by Article 266(1), 266(1)(a), 266(1)(b), 266(1)(f), 266(1)(g) and 267(1).

However, the Constitution does allow for changes to be made through legislation. The government can amend laws related to the NSC and National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission through parliamentary procedures (Article 267).  These amendments could potentially impact their roles or responsibilities.

Therefore, while the constitution doesn't explicitly permit alteration of remuneration/conditions, it provides a framework for legislative action that *could* lead to changes if deemed necessary by the government. It’s important to note this is not guaranteed and would require a valid legal basis established through legislation.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
NNRFC019,Nepali,पदमा रहँदा राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोगका अध्यक्ष र सदस्यहरूको पारिश्रमिक तथा सेवाका सर्तहरू प्रतिकूल परिवर्तन गर्न सकिन्छ?,सकिँदैन।,"Article 267(6) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that ""The President on the recommendation of the Council of Ministers shall appoint and remove the Commander-in-Chief of the Nepal Army."" This means the President has the authority to appoint and remove the Chairman of the National Security Council.

However, the Constitution does not explicitly state whether the Chairman can change the composition or services of the National Security Council. It is up to the government to decide if there are any changes needed. 

Therefore, while the Constitution allows for this, it doesn't guarantee that such changes will be implemented.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC020,English,What is the exception to the protection against disadvantageous alteration of remuneration and conditions of service of the Commission members?,A state of emergency declared because of extreme economic disarrays.,Article 267(8) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that “The Commission members shall be protected from any disadvantageous alteration of their remuneration and conditions of service.”,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC020,Nepali,आयोगका अध्यक्ष र सदस्यहरूको सेवाका सर्तहरू प्रतिकूल परिवर्तन गर्न नपाइने व्यवस्थाको अपवाद के हो?,चरम आर्थिक अव्यवस्थाका कारण संकटकाल घोषणा भएको अवस्था।,"Constitution of Nepal (2015) मध्ये, Article 267(8) quyँ establishes a mechanism for the President to change the composition of the National Security Council without the approval of the House of Representatives. This is an exception to the rule that the Council must be ratified by the House of Representatives within one month after the declaration.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC021,English,What is the responsibility of the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission regarding revenue distribution from the Federal Consolidated Fund?,"To determine detailed basis and modality for distribution of revenues between Federal, State and Local Governments.","The National Natural Resource and Fiscal Commission is responsible for distributing revenue generated from natural resources to the Federal Consolidated Fund. It’s a key part of Nepal's fiscal policy, ensuring equitable resource allocation across different regions and sectors. Specifically, it’s tasked with:

*   **Revenue Collection:** Collecting taxes and fees related to natural resources (such as mineral extraction, forestry, fisheries, etc.).
*   **Distribution:** Distributing these revenues to the Federal Consolidated Fund – which includes the government, provinces, municipalities, and other entities.
*   **Fiscal Planning:** Contributing to the overall fiscal planning process of Nepal by analyzing revenue flows and recommending appropriate spending priorities.

Essentially, it’s a crucial mechanism for ensuring that resources are allocated effectively across the country based on its natural wealth.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
NNRFC021,Nepali,संघीय सञ्चित कोषबाट हुने राजस्व वितरण सम्बन्धमा राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोगको जिम्मेवारी के हो?,"संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय सरकारबीच राजस्व वितरणको विस्तृत आधार र ढाँचा निर्धारण गर्नु।","संघीय सञ्चित कोषबाट हुने राजस्व वितरण सम्बन्धमा राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक संसाधन तथा वित्त आयोगको जिम्मेवारी, नेपालका आर्थिक विकास र प्राकृतिक संसाधनोंको व्यवस्थापनलाई निर्देशित गर्नुपर्ने छ। यसले प्राकृतिक स्रोतहरूको संरक्षण, उनका बुद्धिमानीपूर्वक प्रयोग, साथसाथ तरलता (liquidity) सुनिश्चित गर्ने पनि हो।

यहाँ बिरालो बुझ्ने यस्तहरू छन्:

*   **प्राकृतिक संसाधनहरूको पहियान्छन:** आयोगको कार्यमा प्राकृतिक संसाधनोंको पहियान्छनलाई व्यवस्थापन गर्नुपर्ने छ।
*   **प्राकृतिक स्रोतहरूको बुद्धिमानीपूर्वक प्रयोग:** प्राकृतिक स्रोतहरूको बुद्धिमानीपूर्वक प्रयोग सुनिश्चित गर्ने छ, ताकि उनका मूल्य नभएको पनि हो।
*   **तरलता (liquidity) सुनिश्चित गर्दछ:** तरलताको स्तरमा सुधार ल्याउन र आर्थिक स्थिरता बनाएर राख्छ।
*   **प्राकृतिक संसाधनहरूको संरक्षण:** प्राकृतिक संसाधनोंको संरक्षणलाई प्राथमिकता दिनेछ।

यसले नेपालका सबै नागरिकहरू, स्थानीय समुदायहरू, साथसाथ पर्यावरणीय प्रभावहरू देखाउनुपर्ने छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
NNRFC022,English,From which fund does the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission recommend equalization grants to State and Local Governments?,Federal Consolidated Fund.,The National Natural Resource and Fiscal Commission recommends equalization grants to State and Local Governments from the **Revenue**.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
NNRFC022,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोगले प्रदेश र स्थानीय सरकारलाई समानीकरण अनुदान कुन कोषबाट उपलब्ध गराउन सिफारिस गर्छ?,संघीय सञ्चित कोष।,राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक संसाधन तथा वित्त आयोगले प्रदेश र स्थानीय सरकारलाई समानीकरण अनुदानको व्यवस्थापन कोषबाट उपलब्ध गराउन सिफारिस गर्छ।,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
NNRFC023,English,What type of grants does the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission study and prepare parameters for based on national policies and programs?,Conditional grants.,"The National Natural Resource and Fiscal Commission studies and prepares parameters for national policies and programs through a comprehensive analysis of various aspects, including economic development, environmental sustainability, and fiscal responsibility. Specifically, the commission focuses on identifying opportunities to improve resource management, optimize tax collection, and ensure financial stability within Nepal’s framework. They delve into analyzing data, trends, and potential impacts across different sectors to inform strategic decision-making.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC023,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय नीति तथा कार्यक्रमका आधारमा राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोगले कुन प्रकारका अनुदानका लागि मापदण्ड तयार गर्छ?,सशर्त अनुदान।,"To safeguard the natural resources and financial stability of Nepal, the National Natural Resources and Finance Commission prepares guidelines for grants based on various types of funding.

Here's a breakdown of what they typically do:

*   **Resource Assessment:** They conduct assessments to understand the availability and potential value of different natural resources (water, forests, minerals, etc.).
*   **Regional Planning:** The commission considers regional needs and priorities when determining grant allocations.
*   **Financial Stability:**  They ensure that financial resources are allocated in a sustainable manner, promoting long-term economic growth.

Essentially, they work to balance the needs of various sectors (agriculture, forestry, tourism, etc.) with the protection and management of Nepal's natural assets.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC024,English,What is the difference between revenue distribution from the Federal Consolidated Fund and revenue distribution from the State Consolidated Fund under the functions of the Commission?,"Federal Consolidated Fund distribution is between Federal, State and Local Governments, while State Consolidated Fund distribution is between State and Local Governments.","Under the Constitution of Nepal, the Revenue Distribution between the Federal Consolidated Fund and the State Consolidated Fund primarily focuses on the responsibilities and powers of each. Here’s a breakdown of the key differences:

**1. The Federal Consolidated Fund:**

*   **Responsibility:** Primarily responsible for **national economic policy**, including taxation, fiscal management, and macroeconomic stability within Nepal.
*   **Scope:**  It has broader authority to formulate national strategies related to economic development, infrastructure, and overall growth. It’s focused on the nation as a whole.
*   **Authority:** The Federal Consolidated Fund is empowered to make decisions regarding revenue collection and allocation based on its own assessment of Nepal's needs.

**2. The State Consolidated Fund:**

*   **Responsibility:**  Responsible for **specific areas of government**, such as defense, foreign affairs, justice, and administration.
*   **Scope:** It has a narrower focus on the practical management of state functions and ensuring the effective implementation of laws and policies.
*   **Authority:** The State Consolidated Fund is responsible for implementing laws and policies enacted by the Parliament and the Government.

**3. Commission's Role (as defined in Article 266(1)):**

The Constitution outlines the specific powers and responsibilities of the Commission, which is a crucial part of this framework.  It’s established to ensure that revenue distribution between the Federal Consolidated Fund and the State Consolidated Fund is done in a way that aligns with the principles of national unity and the constitutionally defined functions of each entity.

**In essence:** The Constitution establishes a clear division of responsibility, ensuring that the Federal Consolidated Fund handles broader economic policy while the State Consolidated Fund focuses on the practical management of state affairs.  The Commission's role is to ensure this division is maintained and that revenue distribution aligns with constitutional principles.

---

To provide a more precise answer, I would need the full text of Article 266(1) and the context of how the Commission functions within the Constitution. However, based on the provided information, this explanation captures the core difference in their responsibilities.",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
NNRFC024,Nepali,आयोगको कार्यअन्तर्गत संघीय सञ्चित कोष र प्रदेश सञ्चित कोषबाट हुने राजस्व वितरणमा के फरक छ?,"संघीय सञ्चित कोषबाट हुने वितरण संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय सरकारबीच हुन्छ भने प्रदेश सञ्चित कोषबाट हुने वितरण प्रदेश र स्थानीय सरकारबीच हुन्छ।","Federal State Treasury and Regional State Treasury के बीच राजस्व वितरणमा मुख्य भिन्नता, संघीय सञ्चित कोष (FSB) और क्षेत्रीय सञ्चित कोष (RSTC) द्वारा गरिने व्यवस्थामा निम्न समावेशको हुन्छ:

*   **क्षेत्रीय सञ्चित कोष (RSTC):** RSTC ले FSB बाट थप राजस्व प्राप्त गर्छ। यसले स्थानीय सरकारलाई बजेट वितरण गर्न र स्थानीय पूर्वाधारहरूको लागि धन प्रयोग गर्ने अधिकार राख्छ।
*   **संघीय सञ्चित कोष (FSB):** FSB संघीय सरकारको राजस्वबाट बनाइएका रकमहरूलाई विभिन्न उद्देश्यलका लिएर खर्च गरिने व्यवस्था छ।

संक्षिप्तमा, RSTC ले संघीय बजेटको एक महत्त्वपूर्ण हिस्सा प्राप्त गर्दछ तर FSB संघीय सरकारले चलाएका कार्यक्रमहरूको लागि धन प्रयोग गर्छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
NNRFC025,English,What does the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission recommend regarding government expenditures and revenue collection?,"Measures to meet expenditures of Federal, State and Local Governments and reforms in revenue collection.","The text doesn’t explicitly state what the National Natural Resource and Fiscal Commission recommends regarding government expenditures and revenue collection. It focuses on the purpose of the National Security Council (NSC) – to make recommendations on overall national interest, security, and defence policy. The NSC is tasked with mobilizing and controlling the Nepal Army.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
NNRFC025,Nepali,सरकारी खर्च र राजस्व सङ्कलन सम्बन्धमा राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोगले के सिफारिस गर्छ?,"संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय सरकारको खर्च पूरा गर्ने उपाय र राजस्व सङ्कलन सुधारका उपाय।","The National Natural Resources and Finance Commission (NRFCC) is tasked with recommending policies on the utilization of natural resources for revenue generation. Specifically, they are to recommend government expenditure and revenue collection strategies related to these resources.  They will provide recommendations regarding how to manage and utilize natural resources effectively.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC026,English,What does the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission recommend after analyzing macro-economic indicators?,Ceiling of internal loans that governments can borrow.,"The text doesn’t provide a specific answer to this question. The provided text focuses on the constitutional provisions related to the National Security Council, Nepal Army, and the Constitution of Nepal itself. It does not contain any information about recommendations made by the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission.",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
NNRFC026,Nepali,समष्टिगत आर्थिक सूचकहरूको विश्लेषण गरेपछि राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोगले के सिफारिस गर्छ?,सरकारले लिन सक्ने आन्तरिक ऋणको सीमा।,"समष्टिगत आर्थिक सूचकहरू विश्लेषण गरेपछि राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक संसाधन तथा वित्त आयोगले निम्न सिफारিসभ्यन्को सिफारिश गर्छन्:

*   **प्राकृतिक आपूर्तिको वृद्धि:** नेपालमा उत्पादन भएका प्राकृतिक स्रोतहरूको मात्रा बढाउनुपर्छ, विशेष गरी कृषि र वनस्पति क्षेत्र।
*   **पर्यटन विकास:** देशका पर्यटन स्थलहरूलाई सुधार गर्न मद्दत गरिनेछ ताकि उनका आर्थिक मूल्य बढ सके।
*   **उत्पादनको अनुकूलन:** स्थानीय स्तर पर उत्पादनमा आधारित उद्योगहरूलाई प्रोत्साहन दिनेछन्, जसले प्राकृतिक स्रोतहरूको उपयोगलाई अधिकतम बनाउनु हो।
*   **पर्यावरण र वनस्पतिका संरक्षण:** देशका प्राकृतिक संसाधनहरूको रक्षा गर्न मद्दत गरिनेछ ताकि उनका मूल्य सुरक्षित रह सके।
*   **आर्थिक विकासको लागि प्राकृतिक स्रोतको प्रयोगमा वृद्धि:** नेपालका अर्थव्यविकामा प्राकृतिक स्रोतको महत्वपूर्ण भूमिकालाई बुझाउन मद्दत गरिनेछन्।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
NNRFC027,English,What does the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission do regarding the basis of revenue distribution between the Federal and State Governments?,Reviews the basis and recommends revision.,"The National Natural Resource and Fiscal Commission is responsible for recommending a system of revenue distribution between the federal and state governments. It’s tasked with analyzing existing revenue structures, identifying potential imbalances, and proposing adjustments to ensure equitable resource allocation based on national interests and fiscal responsibility. The Constitution outlines this role as part of its purpose.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC027,Nepali,संघ र प्रदेश सरकारबीच राजस्व बाँडफाँडको आधार सम्बन्धमा राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोगले के गर्छ?,आधारको पुनरावलोकन गरी संशोधनको सिफारिस गर्छ।,The National Natural Resources and Finance Commission shall determine the revenue distribution between the federal government and regional governments regarding the basis of natural resources.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC028,English,What does the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission determine regarding investments and returns from natural resource mobilization?,"Bases for determining shares of Federal, State and Local Governments.","The National Natural Resource and Fiscal Commission determines that investments and returns from natural resource mobilization should be directed towards sustainable development, economic growth, and social welfare. It emphasizes prioritizing long-term planning and responsible management of resources to ensure equitable distribution and benefit for all citizens. Specifically, it advocates for diversifying revenue streams through innovative approaches while maintaining environmental protection and safeguarding the nation’s natural heritage.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC028,Nepali,प्राकृतिक स्रोतको परिचालनबाट हुने लगानी र प्रतिफलमा राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोगले के निर्धारण गर्छ?,"संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय सरकारको हिस्साको निर्धारण गर्ने आधार।","National Natural Resources and Finance Commission shall determine the return on investment from natural resources, considering the national interest.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC029,English,What type of disputes does the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission study and research to provide suggestions for coordinated prevention?,"Possible disputes between Federation and States, between States, between State and Local level, and between Local levels.","The National Natural Resource and Fiscal Commission studies and researches disputes related to natural resources, fiscal policy, and economic stability. Specifically, they investigate issues that could lead to conflict or instability in the country’s natural wealth and financial management.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
NNRFC029,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोगले समन्वयात्मक रोकथामका लागि कस्ता विवादमा अध्ययन तथा अनुसन्धान गर्छ?,"संघ र प्रदेशबीच, प्रदेशहरूबीच, प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहबीच तथा स्थानीय तहहरूबीच हुन सक्ने विवाद।","The National Natural Resources and Finance Commission (NRFCC) conducts studies and research on conflict resolution through various means. Here's a breakdown of their approach:

*   **Conflict Analysis:** The NRFCC analyzes the root causes of conflicts, including territorial disputes, resource management issues, and socio-economic factors that contribute to instability.
*   **Mediation & Negotiation:** They facilitate mediation and negotiation processes between parties involved in conflict situations. This involves bringing together stakeholders to discuss potential solutions and reach mutually acceptable agreements.
*   **Expert Consultation:** The Commission consults with experts from various fields – including law, economics, environmental science, and social sciences – to provide insights into the complexities of conflicts. 
*   **Research & Data Collection:** They conduct research on conflict dynamics, trends, and best practices in conflict resolution. This includes collecting data related to resource management, land use, and socio-economic factors that influence conflict.
*   **Policy Recommendations:** Based on their analysis, the NRFCC develops policy recommendations aimed at preventing conflicts and promoting peaceful resolutions. 

In essence, they act as a crucial body for understanding and addressing conflicts through a multi-faceted approach of research, mediation, and strategic planning.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NNRFC030,English,What study must the National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission conduct regarding distribution of natural resources?,Study and research on required environmental impact assessment.,"The Constitution does not explicitly state that the National Natural Resource and Fiscal Commission must conduct a specific study on the distribution of natural resources. However, it does mention that the government should ensure sustainable development and resource management. Therefore, the commission’s role is to advise the government on this matter through research and recommendations.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
NNRFC030,Nepali,प्राकृतिक स्रोतको वितरण सम्बन्धमा राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोगले कस्तो अध्ययन गर्नुपर्छ?,आवश्यक वातावरणीय प्रभाव मूल्याङ्कनसम्बन्धी अध्ययन तथा अनुसन्धान।,"National Security Council for making recommendations on overall national interest, security, and defence policy.Art. 266(1) specifies both purposes of the National Security Council mentioned in the Constitution, which are to recommend policies on overall national interest, security and defense, and to mobilize and control the Nepal Army.

The Natural Resources and Finance Commission (NRFC) should conduct a study on the distribution of natural resources in Nepal. The study should focus on:

1.  **Resource Mapping:** A detailed map of all natural resources across the country, including their quantity, location, and type.
2.  **Distribution Analysis:** An analysis of how these resources are currently distributed – by region, sector (e.g., agriculture, forestry, mining), and other relevant factors.
3.  **Economic Impact Assessment:** A study on the economic impact of natural resource distribution across different regions. This includes examining potential benefits and risks to the economy.
4.  **Sustainability Considerations:** An assessment of whether current resource management practices are sustainable in the long term, considering environmental impacts and future needs.
5.  **Financial Implications:** Analysis of the financial implications of resource allocation, including revenue generation, expenditure, and investment opportunities.
6.  **Policy Recommendations:** Based on the study's findings, the Commission should provide policy recommendations for optimal resource management, ensuring equitable distribution, promoting sustainable development, and maximizing economic benefits while minimizing environmental risks.

The commission’s report should be regularly updated to reflect changes in the natural resources landscape.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC001,English,What constitutional body is established under Article 252 of the Constitution of Nepal?,National Women Commission of Nepal.,The National Security Council.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC001,Nepali,नेपालको संविधानको धारा २५२ अन्तर्गत कुन संवैधानिक निकायको स्थापना गरिएको छ?,नेपालको राष्ट्रिय महिला आयोग।,नेपालको संविधानको धारा २५२ अन्तर्गत राष्ट्रिय सुरक्षा परिषद् (National Security Council) स्थापित भएको छ।,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC002,English,"How many members, including the Chairperson, constitute the National Women Commission?",Five members.,The Constitution does not specify the number of members of the National Women Commission. It only mentions that the Secretary at the Ministry of Defence acts as the member secretary.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC002,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय महिला आयोगमा अध्यक्षसहित कति जना सदस्य हुन्छन्?,पाँच जना सदस्य।,"Article 267(1) specifies that the President of the National Security Council shall be the Chairperson of the National Security Council. Therefore, the President is the chairperson of the National Security Council.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC003,English,Who appoints the Chairperson and members of the National Women Commission?,The President.,The Constitution doesn’t specify who appoints the Chairperson or members of the National Women Commission. It only states that the Prime Minister is the chairperson.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC003,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय महिला आयोगका अध्यक्ष र सदस्यहरूलाई कसले नियुक्त गर्छ?,राष्ट्रपति।,"The National Security Council (NSC) is responsible for making recommendations on overall national interest, security, and defence policy. Therefore, the President of Nepal is appointed as the Chairperson of the National Security Council.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC004,English,On whose recommendation are the Chairperson and members of the National Women Commission appointed?,Constitutional Council.,Article 266(1)(d) states that the Minister for Foreign Affairs acts as the member secretary of the National Security Council.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC004,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय महिला आयोगका अध्यक्ष र सदस्यहरू कसको सिफारिसमा नियुक्त हुन्छन्?,संवैधानिक परिषद्।,The National Women's Commission President and Members are recommended by the National Security Council.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
OC005,English,What is the term of office of the Chairperson and members of the National Women Commission?,Six years from the date of appointment.,The provided text does not contain information about the terms of office of the Chairperson and members of the National Women Commission. It focuses solely on the roles and composition of the National Security Council.,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
OC005,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय महिला आयोगका अध्यक्ष र सदस्यहरूको पदावधि कति हुन्छ?,नियुक्तिको मितिदेखि छ वर्ष।,"Article 267(8) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that the President of the National Security Council shall be appointed for a term of three years. The members of the National Security Council are also appointed for a term of three years.

Therefore, the answer is: **The President and Members of the National Security Council serve for a term of three years.**",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC006,English,Are the Chairperson and members of the National Women Commission eligible for reappointment after completing their term?,"No, they are not eligible for reappointment.",The provided text does not contain information about the eligibility of the Chairperson and members of the National Women’s Commission to re-appointment. It focuses solely on the composition of the National Security Council and its functions.,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
OC006,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय महिला आयोगका अध्यक्ष र सदस्यहरू पदावधि पूरा भएपछि पुनः नियुक्तिका लागि योग्य हुन्छन्?,"होइन, पुनः नियुक्तिका लागि योग्य हुँदैनन्।","The Constitution doesn't explicitly state that the President or members of the National Security Council are automatically reappointed if their term ends. However, it does mention that ""the President may appoint and remove members of the National Security Council."" This suggests a possibility for re-appointment based on performance or other factors.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC007,English,How many years of contribution in the relevant fields are required for a person to qualify for appointment as Chairperson or member of the National Women Commission?,At least ten years.,The provided text doesn’t contain information about the number of years of contribution required for appointments to the National Women Commission. It focuses on the Constitution's provisions regarding the National Security Council and Nepal Army composition.,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
OC007,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय महिला आयोगको अध्यक्ष वा सदस्य बन्न सम्बन्धित क्षेत्रमा कति वर्षको योगदान आवश्यक हुन्छ?,कम्तीमा दस वर्ष।,"The Constitution of Nepal (2015) doesn't explicitly state a specific number of years required for the President of the National Security Council to be appointed from within the Government of Nepal and Nepal Army. However, it does mention that the President is ""the Chairperson of the National Security Council"" and that the Secretary at the Ministry of Defence acts as the member secretary. This implies that the position requires a significant period of service and experience.

While there isn't a precise timeframe provided in the text, it suggests a considerable commitment to serve for the duration of the term.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC008,English,In which fields must a woman have made outstanding contributions to qualify for appointment to the National Women Commission?,"Rights and interests of women, gender justice, women development, human rights, or law.","Article 267(8) of the Constitution of Nepal specifies that women must make outstanding contributions in the following fields to qualify for appointment to the National Women Commission:

*   **Social Welfare:** Contributing significantly to social welfare programs.
*   **Education and Training:** Providing education or training related to women’s empowerment, gender equality, and development.
*   **Women's Rights Advocacy:** Promoting and advocating for women's rights and equal opportunities.
*   **Community Development:** Working in community development projects that benefit women and girls.

Essentially, the Constitution emphasizes contributing to the advancement of women through various avenues.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC008,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय महिला आयोगमा नियुक्तिका लागि महिलाले कुन-कुन क्षेत्रमा उत्कृष्ट योगदान गरेको हुनुपर्छ?,"महिलाको अधिकार तथा हित, लैङ्गिक न्याय, महिला विकास, मानव अधिकार वा कानून।","The answer is: Women have contributed excellent work in various sectors to the National Gender Harmony Commission (NGC). These include promoting gender equality, supporting women's empowerment initiatives, and advocating for policies that address gender-based discrimination.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC009,English,What additional qualification is specifically required for the Chairperson of the National Women Commission compared to other members?,Holding a bachelor's degree from a recognized university.,"The provided text doesn’t explicitly state that there's a specific qualification requirement for the Chairperson of the National Women Commission compared to other members. It focuses on the role and responsibilities of the Council, specifically regarding the Prime Minister as Chairperson.",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
OC009,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय महिला आयोगका अन्य सदस्यको तुलनामा अध्यक्षका लागि थप कुन योग्यता आवश्यक छ?,मान्यता प्राप्त विश्वविद्यालयबाट स्नातक उपाधि।,"The answer is that the President of the National Security Council is the chairperson of the National Women's Commission. The Constitution doesn’t explicitly state a specific qualification for the Chairperson, but it implies that the position requires a high level of leadership and understanding of women's issues.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC010,English,What is the responsibility of the National Women Commission regarding policies and programs related to women's rights and interests?,To formulate policies and programs and submit them to the Government of Nepal for implementation.,"The National Women Commission has a crucial role in shaping policies and programs that promote gender equality, empower women, and address issues affecting their rights and well-being. Specifically, it is responsible for:

*   **Developing Policies:** The commission develops national strategies and policies aimed at advancing women's participation in all sectors of society – including politics, economy, education, healthcare, and culture.
*   **Conducting Research & Analysis:** It conducts research on gender inequality, identifies challenges faced by women, and provides evidence-based recommendations for policy changes.
*   **Promoting Women’s Participation:** The commission actively promotes the participation of women in decision-making processes at all levels – from national government to local communities. This includes supporting their involvement in political institutions, business ventures, and civil society organizations.
*   **Monitoring & Evaluation:** It monitors progress on gender equality initiatives and evaluates the effectiveness of existing programs.
*   **Advocacy & Awareness Raising:** The commission advocates for policies that protect women's rights and raises awareness about issues affecting their lives through public campaigns and educational activities.

In essence, the National Women Commission acts as a vital oversight body ensuring that all government policies and programs are designed to benefit women and promote gender equality in Nepal.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC010,Nepali,महिलाको अधिकार र हितसम्बन्धी नीति तथा कार्यक्रमका सम्बन्धमा राष्ट्रिय महिला आयोगको जिम्मेवारी के हो?,नीति तथा कार्यक्रम तर्जुमा गरी कार्यान्वयनका लागि नेपाल सरकारसमक्ष पेश गर्नु।,The National Women's Commission’s responsibility concerning the policy and program relating to women’s rights and interests is that it is responsible for formulating policies and programs related to women’s rights and interests.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC011,English,How does the National Women Commission monitor Nepal's obligations under international treaties related to women's rights?,By monitoring implementation and suggesting measures for effective compliance to the Government of Nepal.,"The National Women Commission monitors Nepal’s obligations under international treaties related to women’s rights through a multi-faceted approach involving regular consultations, review of treaty provisions, and advocacy. Here’s a breakdown of how it operates:

* **Regular Consultations:** The NC engages in ongoing consultations with international bodies, organizations, and experts on issues concerning women's rights. This ensures the Commission remains informed about evolving legal frameworks and best practices globally.
* **Review of Treaty Provisions:**  The NC meticulously reviews provisions within Nepal’s treaties (particularly those related to human rights, gender equality, and protection of vulnerable groups) to determine their compatibility with international standards. They analyze whether these treaties adequately protect women's rights and promote equal opportunities. 
* **Advocacy & Recommendations:** Based on its review, the NC advocates for amendments or clarifications within Nepali law and policy to strengthen protections for women’s rights as outlined in international agreements. It provides recommendations to government agencies and other stakeholders regarding implementation of these treaties.
* **Capacity Building:** The Commission supports Nepal's capacity building efforts by providing training and technical assistance to relevant ministries, civil society organizations, and legal professionals on gender-sensitive lawmaking and treaty interpretation. 

In essence, the National Women Commission acts as a crucial mechanism for ensuring that Nepali laws and policies align with international commitments towards women’s empowerment and equality.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC011,Nepali,महिलाको अधिकारसम्बन्धी अन्तर्राष्ट्रिय सन्धिअन्तर्गत नेपालको दायित्वलाई राष्ट्रिय महिला आयोगले कसरी अनुगमन गर्छ?,कार्यान्वयनको अनुगमन गरी प्रभावकारी पालना र कार्यान्वयनका उपायसहित नेपाल सरकारलाई सुझाव दिने।,"NS007, Constitution & Law,Nepal Army,Entity Identification,Easy,Which group is specifically mentioned for ensuring inclusive entry into the Nepal Army under the Constitution?,Women, Dalit, indigenous people, indigenous nationalities, Khas Arya, Madhesi, Tharu, Pichada class, and backward region citizens."",""Women, Dalit, आदिवासी, आदिवासी जनजाति, खस आर्य, मधेसी, थारू, पिछडा वर्ग र पिछडिएको क्षेत्रका नागरिक।"",Article 267(3) lists these groups for ensuring inclusive entry into the Nepal Army.,Art. 267(3),Constitution ofNepal (2015),,,,,,",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC012,English,What recommendation can the National Women Commission make when cases need to be filed regarding violence against women or deprivation of women's rights?,Recommendation to concerned bodies to file cases in courts according to law.,"The National Women’s Commission recommends that cases involving violence against women and deprivation of women’s rights be addressed with a focus on prevention, protection, and empowerment. Specifically, they suggest the following actions:

*   **Strengthening Legal Framework:** Advocate for strengthening laws and policies related to gender equality and protecting women's rights.
*   **Promoting Awareness & Education:** Increase awareness among law enforcement officials, judicial personnel, and community members about violence against women and their rights. Implement educational programs on gender-based violence prevention.
*   **Providing Support Services:** Offer accessible and effective support services to victims of violence, including counseling, legal assistance, safe shelters, and rehabilitation programs.
*   **Addressing Root Causes:** Tackle the underlying social norms and attitudes that perpetuate violence against women through community engagement and awareness campaigns.
*   **Empowering Women:** Promote women's leadership and participation in decision-making processes to ensure their voices are heard and their rights are respected.

In essence, the National Women’s Commission emphasizes a holistic approach encompassing prevention, protection, empowerment, and addressing systemic issues that contribute to violence against women.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC012,Nepali,महिला हिंसा वा महिलाको अधिकारबाट वञ्चित गरिएका विषयमा मुद्दा दायर गर्न आवश्यक भए राष्ट्रिय महिला आयोगले के सिफारिस गर्न सक्छ?,कानून बमोजिम सम्बन्धित निकायलाई अदालतमा मुद्दा दायर गर्न सिफारिस।,National Women's Commission may file a case to address issues related to women violence and the rights of women.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
OC013,English,What constitutional body is established under Article 255 of the Constitution of Nepal?,National Dalit Commission of Nepal.,The National Security Council (NSC) is established under Article 255 of the Constitution of Nepal.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC013,Nepali,नेपालको संविधानको धारा २५५ अन्तर्गत कुन संवैधानिक निकायको स्थापना गरिएको छ?,नेपालको राष्ट्रिय दलित आयोग।,"नेपालको संविधानको धारा २५५ अन्तर्गत, नेपाल सरकारले 'राष्ट्रिय सुरक्षा परिषद्' (National Security Council) बनाउने तरतव्य भएको संवैधानिक निकाय हो।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC014,English,"How many members, including the Chairperson, constitute the National Dalit Commission?",Five members.,"The Constitution doesn’t explicitly state the number of members of the National Dalit Commission. However, it states that “the Council shall include representatives from the Dalit community.” This implies there are at least two members – one chairperson and potentially others.  It's not a specific number provided in the text.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC014,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय दलित आयोगमा अध्यक्षसहित कति जना सदस्य हुन्छन्?,पाँच जना सदस्य।,The answer is 3.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
OC015,English,Who appoints the Chairperson and members of the National Dalit Commission?,The President.,The Constitution doesn’t explicitly state who appoints the Chairperson or members of the National Dalit Commission. It only mentions that the Prime Minister is the chairperson. The text says “The Prime Minister is the Chairperson.”,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC015,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय दलित आयोगका अध्यक्ष र सदस्यहरूलाई कसले नियुक्त गर्छ?,राष्ट्रपति।,The National दलित Commission’s President and members are appointed by the government.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
OC016,English,On whose recommendation are the Chairperson and members of the National Dalit Commission appointed?,Constitutional Council.,Article 267(5) specifies that the President on the recommendation of the Council of Ministers appoints the chairperson and members of the National Dalit Commission.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC016,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय दलित आयोगका अध्यक्ष र सदस्यहरू कसको सिफारिसमा नियुक्त हुन्छन्?,संवैधानिक परिषद्।,"The National Dalit Commission is headed by Dr.  Ramesh Kumar and has members like Mr.  Suresh Kumar, Mr.  Rajesh Kumar, Mr.  Vikram Kumar, Mr.  Shyam Kumar, Mr.  Prashant Kumar, Mr.  Subhash Kumar, Mr.  Vijay Kumar, Mr.  Arjun Kumar, Mr.  Ravi Kumar, and Mr.  Manish Kumar.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC017,English,What is the term of office of the Chairperson and members of the National Dalit Commission?,Six years from the date of appointment.,The provided text does not contain information about the term of office of the Chairperson or members of the National Dalit Commission. It focuses solely on the purpose of the National Security Council and its composition.,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
OC017,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय दलित आयोगका अध्यक्ष र सदस्यहरूको पदावधि कति हुन्छ?,नियुक्तिको मितिदेखि छ वर्ष।,"Article 267(8) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) states that the President shall appoint and remove the Commander-in-Chief of the Nepal Army. The Commander-in-chief is appointed by the Council of Ministers, and the term of their appointment is for a maximum of three years.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
