The Constitution mentions that the National Security Council has specified that the Secretary at the Ministry of Defence acts as the member secretary of the National Security Council. This position is specifically for individuals representing Indigenous people.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC020,English,What educational qualification is specifically required for the Chairperson of the National Dalit Commission?,At least a bachelor's degree from a recognized university.,The provided text doesn’t mention any specific educational qualifications for the Chairperson of the National Dalit Commission. It focuses on the roles and responsibilities of the Council members as outlined in the Constitution.,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
OC020,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय दलित आयोगका अध्यक्षका लागि विशेष रूपमा कुन शैक्षिक योग्यता आवश्यक छ?,मान्यता प्राप्त विश्वविद्यालयबाट कम्तीमा स्नातक उपाधि।,"The Constitution doesn't explicitly state the educational qualifications required for the President of the National Security Council. However, it does mention that the Prime Minister is the Chairperson of the National Security Council. Therefore, the answer would be **""The Prime Minister.""**",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC021,English,What is the responsibility of the National Dalit Commission regarding the overall situation of the Dalit community?,"To conduct study and exploration, identify areas for reform, and make recommendations to the Government of Nepal.","The Constitution of Nepal doesn’t explicitly detail a specific “National Dalit Commission” with defined responsibilities. However, it does outline the government's commitment to protecting and promoting the rights and well-being of all citizens, including Dalits (Dalit people).  Therefore, the National Security Council, through its constitutional provisions and subsequent laws, is responsible for ensuring that the rights of marginalized communities are protected.

Here’s a breakdown of how the Constitution implicitly supports this responsibility:

* **Article 267(3):** This article states that the government shall mobilize the Nepal Army to ensure the protection of all citizens, including Dalits.
* **Constitutional Guarantee:** The Constitution guarantees equal rights and opportunities for all citizens regardless of caste or social status.  This includes protecting the rights of marginalized communities like Dalits.

While there isn't a dedicated commission, the emphasis on safeguarding all citizens – particularly those facing discrimination – implies that the National Security Council has a responsibility to address issues affecting Dalit communities through appropriate measures and actions. The focus on mobilization by the Army is a key element in this effort.

**In essence, while not explicitly defined as a separate body, the Constitution’s overarching commitment to equality and protection for all citizens places the responsibility of safeguarding the rights of Dalits upon the National Security Council.**",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC021,Nepali,दलित समुदायको समग्र अवस्थासम्बन्धी राष्ट्रिय दलित आयोगको जिम्मेवारी के हो?,अध्ययन तथा खोज गरी सुधारका क्षेत्र पहिचान गर्ने र नेपाल सरकारलाई सिफारिस गर्ने।,"NS003, Constitution & Law,National Security Council Composition,Fact Retrieval,Easy,Which government minister is included as a member of the National Security Council responsible for defence matters?,Minister for Defence.,Defence Minister.,रक्षा मन्त्री।,Article 266(1)(b) lists the Minister for Defence as a member of the Council.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC022,English,What type of policies and programs does the National Dalit Commission formulate and submit to the Government of Nepal?,National policies and programs for the upliftment and development of Dalit communities and ending caste-based discrimination.,"The National Dalit Commission submits its annual report to the government, outlining policy recommendations for addressing the challenges faced by Dalits. It focuses on promoting their rights, ensuring equal opportunities, and combating discrimination across various sectors. The report details specific initiatives aimed at empowering marginalized communities and fostering social justice.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC022,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय दलित आयोगले कस्ता नीति तथा कार्यक्रम तर्जुमा गरी नेपाल सरकारलाई पेश गर्छ?,दलित समुदायको उत्थान तथा विकास र जातीय भेदभाव अन्त्य गर्न राष्ट्रिय नीति तथा कार्यक्रम।,"The National दलित Commission shall present its recommendations to the government of Nepal in the form of policies and programs through the following channels.

*   **Formal Presentation:** The Commission will formally present its recommendations to the government through official channels, including meetings with officials and submission of documents.
*   **Public Consultation:**  It will engage in public consultation processes, holding hearings, workshops, and discussions with stakeholders across various sectors.
*   **Policy Briefs & Reports:** It will produce policy briefs and reports detailing its recommendations for specific areas.
*   **Stakeholder Engagement:** The Commission will actively collaborate with relevant government agencies, civil society organizations, and community groups to ensure the implementation of its recommendations.

The goal is to foster a collaborative approach towards addressing issues related to the Dalit community in Nepal.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC023,English,What does the National Dalit Commission monitor regarding laws and special provisions for the Dalit community?,Whether they have been effectively implemented.,"The National Dalit Commission monitors laws and special provisions related to the rights, welfare, and protection of Dalits within Nepal. Specifically, it focuses on ensuring that these communities are not marginalized or discriminated against under existing legal frameworks. It works towards promoting their social, economic, and political inclusion and empowerment.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC023,Nepali,दलित समुदायसम्बन्धी कानून र विशेष व्यवस्थाका सम्बन्धमा राष्ट्रिय दलित आयोगले के अनुगमन गर्छ?,ती प्रभावकारी रूपमा कार्यान्वयन भएका छन् वा छैनन्।,"National Commission for the Protection of Minorities (NCMP) is responsible for following these actions:

*   **Investigation:** NCMP investigates complaints against individuals or organizations that violate the rights of minorities.
*   **Reporting:** It reports its findings to the government and other relevant authorities.
*   **Recommendations:** NCMP makes recommendations to address discrimination and promote equality among minority communities.
*   **Monitoring:** The commission monitors laws and policies related to minority protection.
*   **Advocacy:** NCMP advocates for legislation that protects the rights of minorities.

In essence, NCMP acts as a watchdog and advocate for the rights of marginalized groups in Nepal.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC025,English,What constitutional body is established under Article 258 of the Constitution of Nepal?,National Inclusion Commission of Nepal.,The National Security Council (NSC) is established under Article 258 of the Constitution of Nepal.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC025,Nepali,नेपालको संविधानको धारा २५८ अन्तर्गत कुन संवैधानिक निकायको स्थापना गरिएको छ?,नेपालको राष्ट्रिय समावेशी आयोग।,नेपालको संविधानको धारा २५८ अन्तर्गत नेपाल सरकारको 'राष्ट्रिय सुरक्षा परिषद्' (National Security Council) स्थापित भएको छ।,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC026,English,"How many members, including the Chairperson, constitute the National Inclusion Commission?",Five members.,The Constitution doesn’t explicitly state the number of members of the National Inclusion Commission. It only mentions that it is composed of “the Secretary at the Ministry of Defence and the Commander-in-Chief of Nepal Army.”,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC026,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय समावेशी आयोगमा अध्यक्षसहित कति जना सदस्य हुन्छन्?,पाँच जना सदस्य।,"The Constitution of Nepal (2015) specifies that the National Security Council has two main purposes: to recommend policies on national interest, security and defence, and to mobilize and control the Nepal Army. Therefore, the National Security Council has two major purposes:

1.  To recommend policies on overall national interest, security, and defence
2.  To mobilize and control the Nepal Army.

Therefore, the answer is **two**.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC027,English,Which groups and communities are included within the scope of study and research of the National Inclusion Commission?,"Khas Arya, Pichhada class, persons with disabilities, senior citizens, labourers, peasants, minorities, marginalized communities, backward classes, people of Karnali and indigent classes.","The National Inclusion Commission is expected to examine and analyze various groups and communities, including but not limited to:

*   **Women:** Recognizing their rights and ensuring equal participation in all aspects of society.
*   **Dalit Communities:** Addressing historical injustices and promoting social equity for marginalized groups.
*   **Indigenous Peoples:** Protecting cultural heritage and traditional practices.
*   **Khas Arya:** Ensuring their representation and well-being within the national framework.
*   **Mitharu, Tharu, Pichhada class:** Recognizing their specific needs and ensuring inclusive policies.
*   **Backward Region Citizens:** Addressing inequalities in access to opportunities across different regions.

The Commission will likely consider factors like discrimination, social exclusion, and promoting inclusivity for all citizens.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC027,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय समावेशी आयोगको अध्ययन तथा अनुसन्धानको दायरामा कुन-कुन समुदाय र वर्ग पर्छन्?,"खस आर्य, पिछडा वर्ग, अपाङ्गता भएका व्यक्ति, ज्येष्ठ नागरिक, श्रमिक, किसान, अल्पसंख्यक, सीमान्तकृत समुदाय, पिछडा वर्ग, कर्णालीका जनता र विपन्न वर्ग।","The National Inclusive Commission’s study and research scope should encompass the following communities and classes:

*   **Women:** The commission must consider women's rights, perspectives, and challenges in Nepal.
*   **Dalit Communities:** It needs to address the specific issues faced by Dalit communities, including discrimination, marginalization, and social justice.
*   **Indigenous Peoples:** The study should focus on the cultural heritage, traditions, and well-being of indigenous communities across Nepal.
*   **Khas Arya:**  The commission must analyze the situation of Khas Arya communities, considering their rights, challenges, and potential for development.
*   **Tharu Communities:** It needs to examine the experiences and concerns of Tharu people, including issues related to language, culture, and social inclusion.
*   **Mithali Class:** The study should address the unique situation of Mithali communities, considering their socio-economic status and potential for empowerment.
*   **Backward Region Citizens:**  The commission must consider the needs and challenges faced by citizens residing in backward regions of Nepal.

It's important to note that this is a general overview; the specific focus of the study will depend on the commission’s objectives and priorities.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC028,English,What does the National Inclusion Commission study regarding government policies and laws for inclusion?,The status of implementation and makes suggestions for reforms.,The National Inclusion Commission studies government policies and laws for inclusion to ensure that all groups are represented in government.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
OC028,Nepali,समावेशीकरणका लागि नेपाल सरकारले अपनाएका नीति तथा कानून सम्बन्धमा राष्ट्रिय समावेशी आयोगले के अध्ययन गर्छ?,कार्यान्वयनको अवस्था अध्ययन गरी सुधारका लागि सुझाव दिन्छ।,"The answer is: **The National Inclusive Commission studies the government's policies and laws related to national inclusion, focusing on promoting social justice, equality, and participation of marginalized groups.**

Here’s a breakdown of what this implies based on the provided text:

*   **""The National Inclusive Commission studies...""**: This indicates that the commission is actively involved in analyzing and understanding the government's approach to inclusivity.
*   **""...the policies and laws related to national inclusion...""**:  This highlights their focus on the legal framework and strategic plans for promoting diversity and equity within Nepal.
*   **""...promoting social justice, equality, and participation of marginalized groups.""**: This is a key objective of the commission – it’s designed to ensure that all segments of society are valued and have equal opportunities.",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
OC029,English,"What does the National Inclusion Commission study regarding representation of specified communities, classes, and regions in State organs?",Whether there has been appropriate representation and recommends review of special provisions.,"The National Inclusion Commission studies the representation of specific communities, classes, and regions within state organs.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
OC029,Nepali,"तोकिएका समुदाय, वर्ग र क्षेत्रको राज्यका अंगहरूमा प्रतिनिधित्व सम्बन्धमा राष्ट्रिय समावेशी आयोगले के अध्ययन गर्छ?",उचित प्रतिनिधित्व भएको छ वा छैन अध्ययन गरी विशेष व्यवस्थाको पुनरावलोकन गर्न सिफारिस गर्छ।,"The National Inclusive Commission studies the representation of communities, classes, and regions in the state's organs to represent the country’s constitutionally enshrined values. It aims to ensure that all groups are adequately represented in government institutions and decision-making processes.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC030,English,What does the National Inclusion Commission recommend regarding the development and prosperity of Karnali and backward regions?,Policies and programs to be pursued for their development and prosperity.,"The National Security Council recommends that the government should focus on developing and promoting the prosperity of Karnali and backward regions through strategic investments, infrastructure projects, and economic initiatives. Specifically, they suggest prioritizing sustainable agriculture, tourism, and industrial development in these areas to create employment opportunities and improve livelihoods. The council also emphasizes strengthening local governance structures and fostering community participation to ensure equitable distribution of benefits.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC030,Nepali,कर्णाली र पिछडिएका क्षेत्रको विकास र समृद्धिका सम्बन्धमा राष्ट्रिय समावेशी आयोगले के सिफारिस गर्छ?,तिनको विकास र समृद्धिका लागि अवलम्बन गरिने नीति तथा कार्यक्रम।,"कर्णाली र पिछडिएका क्षेत्रको विकास र समृद्धिका सम्बन्धमा राष्ट्रिय समावेशी आयोगले निम्न सिफारिस गर्छ:

*   **स्थानीय अर्थ प्रणालीलाई प्रोत्साहन:** स्थानीय अर्थव्यवस्थालाई बलस्तै बनाउनु, जसको उद्देश्य स्थानीय उत्पादन, उद्योग, सेवाहरू, तरलता र लगानीलाई बुझाएर आर्थिक विकासलाई चलाइय बनाइनु हो।
*   **रोजगार निर्माण:** स्थानीय स्तर पर रोजगार निर्माणमा ध्यान केन्द्रित गर्नुहोस्, विशेष रूपकर उनका क्षेत्रमा आगरको कुरा छ।
*   **सकल पूर्वापनाको सुधार:** सामाजिक सुरक्षा प्रणालीलाई बलस्तै बनाउनु र सबै नागरिकहरूको लागि सुरक्षित भविष्य सुनिश्चित गर्नु हो।
*   **पर्यावरण संरक्षण:** प्राकृतिक वातावरणको रक्षा गरिने तर स्थानीय समुदायहरूले आफ्नो जीवनशैलीलाई बदल्न नदिनु हो।
*   **शिक्षामा सुधार:** स्थानीय विद्यालयलगाइको गुणस्तरीय शिक्षा प्रदान गर्नु हो, ताकि सबै नागरिक आगरको कुरा छ।
*   **सुलभताको सुधार:** क्षेत्रका जनताको लागि सामाजिक र आर्थिक पहुँचलाई बुझाउनु हो।
*   **प्रगतिशील पर्यटन:** प्राकृतिक सौदेको संरक्षणमा ध्यान केन्द्रित गर्नुहोस्, जसले स्थानीय अर्थव्यवस्थालाई बलस्तै बनाइय।

यो सिफारिस राष्ट्रिय समावेशी आयोगले कणाली र पिछडिएका क्षेत्रको विकास र समृद्धिका सम्बन्धमा धेरै महत्त्वपूर्ण तरुआतहरू प्रदान गर्छन्।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC031,English,On what basis does the National Inclusion Commission monitor the implementation of rights and interests of minority and marginalized communities and recommend revisions?,Periodic national census and human development index.,"The Constitution of Nepal doesn’t explicitly detail a specific “National Inclusion Commission” solely for monitoring rights and interests of minority and marginalized communities. However, it outlines the responsibilities of the Council of Ministers (which includes the Prime Minister) to consider these concerns in their policy-making processes. The Constitution emphasizes that the government should ""consider"" the needs of all groups, including minorities and marginalized communities, when formulating policies.

Therefore, while there isn’t a dedicated commission named “National Inclusion Commission,” the constitutional framework suggests that the Council of Ministers is obligated to actively engage with and consider these groups' interests through its policy-making process.  The emphasis on ""considering"" their needs implies a monitoring mechanism exists within the government structure.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC031,Nepali,अल्पसंख्यक तथा सीमान्तकृत समुदायको अधिकार र हितको कार्यान्वयन अनुगमन गर्दा राष्ट्रिय समावेशी आयोगले कुन आधार प्रयोग गर्छ?,आवधिक राष्ट्रिय जनगणना र मानव विकास सूचकांक।,"National Inclusive Commission will use the following basis for implementation monitoring of the rights and interests of marginalized and minority communities.

Here's a breakdown of the basis they’ll likely utilize:

*   **Constitutional Provisions:** The National Inclusive Commission will refer to relevant provisions of the Constitution, particularly those related to fundamental freedoms, equality, and protection of minorities.
*   **Legal Framework:** It will draw upon existing laws and regulations that address the rights and interests of marginalized communities.
*   **Data Collection & Analysis:** The commission will collect data on the situation of various groups, including their socio-economic status, access to services, participation in decision-making processes, and any specific challenges they face.
*   **Expert Consultation:** It will consult with experts from diverse fields (social sciences, law, human rights) to provide insights into the complexities of marginalized communities' situations.
*   **Community Participation:** The commission will actively engage with representatives from various groups – including those from marginalized communities themselves – to understand their perspectives and needs.

Essentially, it’s a multi-faceted approach that combines legal frameworks, data analysis, expert knowledge, and community involvement to ensure equitable implementation of policies and programs aimed at protecting the rights and interests of all citizens.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC032,English,"What is the maximum number of members in the Indigenous Nationalities Commission, including the Chairperson?",Five members.,"The Constitution doesn’t explicitly state a maximum number of members for the Indigenous Nationalities Commission. However, it states that “the Council shall include representatives from the indigenous nationalities.” This implies there is no specific limit to the number of members within this commission.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC032,Nepali,आदिवासी जनजाति आयोगमा अध्यक्षसहित अधिकतम कति जना सदस्य हुन्छन्?,पाँच जना सदस्य।,"NS008, Constitution & Law,Nepal Army,Composition,Fact Retrieval,Medium,Which positions from the Government of Nepal and Nepal Army are included as members of the National Security Council besides ministers?,मन्त्रीहरू बाहेक नेपाल सरकार र नेपाली सेनाका कुन पदहरू राष्ट्रिय सुरक्षा परिषद्को सदस्य हुन्छन्?,""The Chief Secretary of Government of Nepal and Commander-in-Chief of Nepal Army.,Minister for Defence."",""नेपाल सरकारका मुख्य सचिव र नेपाली सेनाका प्रधानसेनापति।,Article 266(1)(f) and 266(1)(g) include these two positions as members.,""Art. 266(1)(f), Art. 266(1)(g)""Constitution of Nepal (2015),,,,,,",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC033,English,Who appoints the Chairperson and members of the Madhesi Commission?,The President on the recommendation of the Constitutional Council.,The article states that the Chairman of the National Security Council is the Prime Minister.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC033,Nepali,मधेसी आयोगका अध्यक्ष र सदस्यहरूलाई कसले नियुक्त गर्छ?,संवैधानिक परिषद्को सिफारिसमा राष्ट्रपतिले।,मधेसी आयोगका अध्यक्ष र सदस्यहरूलाई राष्ट्रपति द्वारा नियुक्त गर्छ।,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC034,English,What common constitutional feature is shared by the Tharu Commission and Muslim Commission regarding their composition?,Each consists of a Chairperson and a maximum of four other members.,"The Tharu Commission and Muslim Commission are both included as members of the National Security Council, despite having different ethnic backgrounds.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
OC034,Nepali,थारू आयोग र मुस्लिम आयोगको संरचनासम्बन्धी साझा संवैधानिक व्यवस्था के हो?,दुवैमा अध्यक्ष र अधिकतम चार अन्य सदस्य हुन्छन्।,"थारू आयोग र मुस्लिम आयोगको संरचनासम्बन्धी साझा संवैधानिक व्यवस्था, नेपालका संविधानले थारू आयोग र मुस्लिम आयोगलाई एक संयुक्त संस्थागतमा जोदिएको है। संविधानले यसलाई 'संस्थागत सहकार्यको समिति' (Institutional Cooperation Committee) के रूपীত गरेको छ ।

यहाँ स्पष्टीकरण दिइएको छ:

*   **संस्थागत सहकार्यको समिति:** यो समिति थारू आयोग र मुस्लिम आयोग बीचको सहकार्यलाई प्रोत्साहन गर्छ, तर यसमा धेरै अधिकार र प्रयोगको व्यवस्था छैन।
*   **संसदीय स्वीकृति:** नेपालका संसदले थारू आयोग र मुस्लिम आयोगको संरचनाको स्वीकृतीकरण गर्नुपर्नेछ ।
*   **संस्थागत सहमति:** नेपाली सरकार र थारू आयोग र मुस्लिम आयोगले आपसी सहमतिको माध्यमबाट सहकार्यमा आएनन्।

थारू आयोगलाई मुख्य रूप से न्यायपालिका (न्यायपालिका) द्वारा निर्णयित विषयहरू पर फैसला गर्ने अधिकार दिइएको छ, तर यसका प्रयोग सीमित भित्र्याएको छ । मुस्लिम आयोगलाई पनि न्यायपालिका द्वारा निर्णयित विषय पर फैसला गर्ने अधिकार दिइएको छ, तर यसमा धेरै प्रयोगको व्यवस्था छैन।

संक्षेप में, थारू आयोग र मुस्लिम आयोगले सहकार्यमा आएनन्, तर आपसी सहमतिबाट सहकार्यमा आएनन्।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
OC035,English,After how many years from the commencement of the Constitution must the Federal Parliament review the commissions formed under Part 27?,Ten years.,Article 267(8) of the Constitution of Nepal states that the Federal Parliament shall review the commissions formed under Part 27 within **six months** after the completion of the work.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
OC035,Nepali,संविधान प्रारम्भ भएको कति वर्षपछि संघीय संसदले भाग २७ अन्तर्गत गठन भएका आयोगहरूको पुनरावलोकन गर्नुपर्छ?,दस वर्ष।,"संविधान २०१९ अनुसार, संघीय संसदले भाग २७ अन्तर्गत गठन भएका आयोगहरूलाई पुनरावलोकन गर्नुपर्छ ७ वर्षदेखील следващата годинаमा।",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
NS001,English,"What constitutional body is established for making recommendations on Nepal's overall national interest, security, and defence policy?",National Security Council.,The National Security Council (NSC) is established.,Correct,Not a strict error,False
NS001,Nepali,"नेपालको समग्र राष्ट्रिय हित, सुरक्षा र रक्षा नीतिसम्बन्धी सिफारिस गर्न कुन संवैधानिक निकायको स्थापना गरिएको छ?",राष्ट्रिय सुरक्षा परिषद्।,"Article 266(1) of the Constitution of Nepal (2015) specifies both purposes of the National Security Council – overall national interest, security, and defence, and to mobilize and control the Nepal Army. Therefore, the National Security Council is established by the Constitution.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NS002,English,What are the two major purposes of the National Security Council mentioned in the Constitution?,"To recommend policies on overall national interest, security and defence, and to mobilize and control the Nepal Army.","The two main purposes of the National Security Council, as stated in the Constitution, are to recommend policies on overall national interest, security, and defence, and to mobilize and control the Nepal Army.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
NS002,Nepali,संविधानमा उल्लेख भएअनुसार राष्ट्रिय सुरक्षा परिषद्का दुई प्रमुख उद्देश्य के हुन्?,"समग्र राष्ट्रिय हित, सुरक्षा र रक्षा नीतिका लागि सिफारिस गर्नु तथा नेपाली सेनाको परिचालन र नियन्त्रण गर्नु।",राष्ट्रिय सुरक्षा परिषद्का दुई मुख्य उद्देश्यहरू बुझाउनु र नेपाली सेनाको परिचालन र नियन्त्रण गर्नु हो।,Correct,Not a strict error,False
