NS018,English,"Which police organizations and investigation body shall exist under the Federation, and what police organization shall each State have?","Federation shall have Nepal Police, Armed Police Force, Nepal and National Investigation Department; each State shall have a State police organization.","According to Article 302(2) of the Constitution, the following police organizations will exist under the Federal Government:

*   **Police Headquarters:** The Police Headquarters will be established.
*   **Regional Police Departments:** Each state will have regional police departments.

Here’s a breakdown by state:

*   **Federal Level:** The Police Headquarters will be established.
*   **State Levels:** Each State will have Regional Police Departments.

Article 303(1) ensures continuity of existing Local Bodies during the transition to the constitutional Local level structure.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
NS018,Nepali,"संघअन्तर्गत कुन-कुन प्रहरी संगठन र अनुसन्धान निकाय रहनेछन्, र प्रत्येक प्रदेशमा कुन प्रहरी संगठन रहनेछ?","संघमा नेपाल प्रहरी, सशस्त्र प्रहरी बल, नेपाल र राष्ट्रिय अनुसन्धान विभाग रहनेछन्; प्रत्येक प्रदेशमा प्रदेश प्रहरी संगठन रहनेछ।","संविधान अनुसार, संघले निम्न जाँचकर्ता संस्थाहरूलाई प्रहरीको रूपमा बनाएका छन्:

*   **Inspector General of Police (IGP):** IGP नेपालPolice Force (NPF) को नेतृत्व गर्दछ र पुलिसिङ्ग शक्तिको व्यवस्थापनमा महत्वपूर्ण भूमिका खेलेछ।
*   **Directorate general of Crime Investigation (DGCI):** DGCI अपराध जाँचको लागि जिम्मेवार छ र अपराधीहरूलाई पकड गर्न मद्दत गर्दछ।
*   **National Accountability Bureau (NAB):** NAB जाँचकर्ताहरूको समूह हो जसले भ्रष्टाचार, अनियमितता, वा अन्य मुद्दाहरूमा छान्याव गर्छन्।
*   **Regional Investigation Wings:** प्रत्येक प्रदेशका लागि पाँच क्षेत्रीयInvestigation Wings बनाएको छ, र तिसको जाँचकर्ताहरूलाई जाँच गर्न मद्दत गर्दछ।

प्रत्येक प्रदेशमा प्रहरी संगठनहरूको व्यवस्था निम्न अनुसार छ:

*   **Province Police Headquarters:** प्रत्येक صوبिको पुलिसिङ्ग शक्तिका लिएर ५ Provincial Police Headquarters बनाएको छ।
*   **Regional Police Officers:** प्रत्येक صوبिको पुलिसिङ्ग शक्तिका लिएर पाँच Regional Police Officers बनाएको छ।
*   **Special Task Forces:** प्रत्येक صوبिको जाँचकर्ताहरूलाई जाँच गर्न मद्दत गर्दछ।

यो व्यवस्थाले नेपालमा भ्रष्टाचार, अनियमितता, वा अन्य मुद्दाहरूको जाँचलाई बलस्त बनाउँछ र जनताका सुरक्षा सुनिश्चित्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
PP001,English,Who may form and operate political parties according to the Constitution?,"Persons committed to common political ideology, philosophy and program.","Article 304(1) of the Constitution states that “the President, on the recommendation of the Government of Nepal, Council of Ministers, and other relevant authorities, may form and operate political parties.”",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
PP001,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार कसले राजनीतिक दल गठन र सञ्चालन गर्न सक्छन्?,"साझा राजनीतिक विचारधारा, दर्शन र कार्यक्रमप्रति प्रतिबद्ध व्यक्तिहरू।","संविधान अनुसार, राजनीतिक दलहरूलाई सरकारमा सहभागी गराउनका लागि संविधानले विशेष तरियता प्रदान गर्दछ।

Here's a breakdown of how the constitution allows political parties to participate in government:

*   **Article 304:** This article grants political parties the right to form and operate within Nepal.
*   **Section 304(1):** It states that political parties are allowed to be formed and operated under the Constitution.
*   **Section 304(2):** It provides continuity and legal recognition for existing political parties, ensuring their continued operation until elections take place.

Essentially, the constitution establishes a framework where political parties can participate in government through formation, operation, and election processes as defined by the law.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
PP002,English,What must persons share in order to form and operate a political party under Article 269?,"Common political ideology, philosophy and program.","Article 269 of the Constitution states that “Political parties are formed and operated by individuals, groups, or organizations.” Therefore, persons must share in this process to form and operate a political party. This includes contributing financially, providing expertise, and participating in organizational activities.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
PP002,Nepali,धारा २६९ अनुसार राजनीतिक दल गठन र सञ्चालन गर्न व्यक्तिहरूबीच के समान हुनुपर्छ?,"साझा राजनीतिक विचारधारा, दर्शन र कार्यक्रम।","धारा २६९ अनुसार, राजनीतिक दल गठन र सञ्चालन गर्न व्यक्तिहरूबीच समान हुनुपर्छ, अर्थात्, एक अर्Personको साथमा सहकार्य गर्दा, आपसी सहमतिले बनाइएका नियमहरूको अनुसरण गर्दा, धेरै व्यक्तिहरू बीच सहकार्य गरिनु पर्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
PP003,English,Which constitutional body must a political party register with after being formed?,Election Commission.,Article 304(1) of the Constitution states that political parties must register with the Election Commission of Nepal (ECN) after they are formed.,Correct,Not a strict error,False
PP003,Nepali,गठन भएपछि राजनीतिक दलले कुन संवैधानिक निकायमा दर्ता हुनुपर्छ?,निर्वाचन आयोग।,"Article 302(2) permits employee adjustment among the three levels of government to support service delivery. It states that employees serving in government services at the commencement of the Constitution among the Federal, State and Local levels in accordance with law. Therefore, political parties must register with the relevant government bodies (like the Ministry of Government Services or similar agencies) before they can provide services at the state and local levels.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
PP004,English,Which documents must accompany an application for registration of a political party?,"The party constitution, manifesto, and other documents required by Federal law.","According to the text, the following documents must accompany an application for registration of a political party:

*   **A copy of the applicant’s identification document.**
*   **A copy of the applicant's voter card.**
*   **A copy of the applicant’s birth certificate.**
*   **A copy of the applicant’s address proof.**
*   **A copy of the applicant’s registration with the local election authority (if applicable).**

The text emphasizes that these documents are required to demonstrate the applicant's identity and eligibility for political party registration.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
PP004,Nepali,राजनीतिक दल दर्ताको निवेदनसँग कुन-कुन कागजात संलग्न गर्नुपर्छ?,"दलको विधान, घोषणापत्र र संघीय कानूनले माग गरेका अन्य कागजातहरू।","Political party registration demands various documents, including:

*   **Registration Form:** This is the primary document. It contains details about the party's name, address, and other relevant information.
*   **Identification Documents:** These are essential for verifying the identity of the party members. Examples include:
    *   Passport or National Identity Card
    *   Driving License
    *   Nepali Citizenship Certificate (if applicable)
*   **Membership Certificates:** If the party has existing members, their certificates may be required.
*   **Organizational Documents:** These documents demonstrate the party's structure and activities. Examples include:
    *   Constitution or Bylaw
    *   Financial Statements
    *   Minutes of Meetings
    *   Records of Donations (if applicable)
*   **Other Supporting Documents:** Depending on the specific requirements, other documents might be needed, such as proof of address or a statement of purpose.

It's important to consult the official guidelines and regulations issued by the Nepal Election Commission for the most up-to-date list of required documents.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
PP005,English,What type of constitution and rules must a political party have to qualify for registration?,Democratic.,"According to the provided text, a political party must meet certain requirements to qualify for registration in Nepal. The text states that they must be registered under the Constitution. However, it doesn’t specify *what* those requirements are – it just says they need to be registered as per the Constitution.",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
PP005,Nepali,दर्ताका लागि राजनीतिक दलको विधान र नियम कस्तो हुनुपर्छ?,लोकतान्त्रिक।,"त035,Transitional Provisions,Government Services,Factual,Medium,How may the Government of Nepal arrange for the delivery of services at the State and Local levels during the transition?,संक्रमणकालमा प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहमा सेवा प्रवाहको व्यवस्था नेपाल सरकारले कसरी गर्न सक्छ?,""By adjusting employees serving in government services at the commencement of the Constitution among the Federal, State and Local levels in accordance with law."",""संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदाका सरकारी सेवामा कार्यरत कर्मचारीहरूलाई कानूनबमोजिम संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहमा समायोजन गरेर।"",Article 302(2) permits employee adjustment among the three levels of government to support service delivery.,Art. 302(2),Formation and operation of government services at State and Local levels,,,,,,
TP036,Transitional Provisions,Local Bodies,Factual,Easy,How long do the Local Bodies existing at the commencement of the Constitution continue to exist?,संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदा विद्यमान स्थानीय निकायहरू कति समयसम्म कायम रहन्छन्?,Until the number and areas of the Local level are determined in accordance with the Constitution.,संविधानबमोजिम स्थानीय तहको संख्या र क्षेत्र निर्धारण नभएसम्म।,Article 303(1) ensures continuity of existing Local Bodies during the transition to the constitutional Local level structure.,Art. 303(1),Provisions relating to Local Bodies,,,,,,
TP037,Transitional Provisions,Local Bodies,Factual,Easy,How are elections to officials of the existing Local Bodies conducted during the transitional period?,संक्रमणकालमा विद्यमान स्थानीय निकायका पदाधिकारीहरूको निर्वाचन कसरी गरिन्छ?,In accordance with law.,कानूनबमोजिम।,Article 303(2) provides that elections to officials of existing Local Bodies shall be held according to law.,Art. 303(2),Provisions relating to Local Bodies,,,,,,
TP038,Transitional Provisions,Local Bodies,Factual,Medium,Until when do officials elected to the existing Local Bodies continue to hold office?,विद्यमान स्थानीय निकायमा निर्वाचित पदाधिकारीहरू कहिलेसम्म पदमा कायम रहन्छन्?,Until elections to the Local level are held in accordance with the Constitution.,संविधानबमोजिम स्थानीय तहको निर्वाचन नभएसम्म।,Article 303(3) provides continuity for elected local officials until the new Local Level elections take place.,Art. 303(3),Provisions relating to Local Bodies,,,,,,
TP039,Transitional Provisions,Existing Laws,Factual,Easy,What is the general rule regarding Nepalese laws in force when the Constitution commences?,संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदा प्रचलित नेपालका कानूनहरूबारे सामान्य व्यवस्था के हो?,They continue to remain in force until repealed or amended.,खारेज वा संशोधन नभएसम्म ती कानूनहरू कायम रहन्छन्।,Article 304(1) preserves existing laws to avoid a legal vacuum during constitutional transition.,Art. 304(1),Existing laws to remain in force,,,,,,
TP040,Transitional Provisions,Existing Laws,Factual,Medium,What happens to an existing law that is inconsistent with the Constitution after the specified transitional period?,धारा ३०४(१) अन्तर्गत संविधानसँग बाझिएको कानूनको तोकिएको संक्रमणकालीन अवधिपछि के हुन्छ?,""It becomes invalid to the extent of its inconsistency."",""जति हदसम्म संविधानसँग बाझिन्छ, त्यति हदसम्म अमान्य हुन्छ।"",The Constitution provides a transitional period before inconsistent pre-existing laws automatically become invalid to the extent of inconsistency.,Art. 304(1),Existing laws to remain in force,,,,,,
TP041,Transitional Provisions,Existing Laws,Factual,Hard,After what event and period does the inconsistency rule for existing laws take effect under Article 304(1)?,धारा ३०४(१) अन्तर्गत व्यवस्थाको कुन घटनाले असंगतिलाई प्रभावित गर्छ?,""After one year from the date on which the first session of the Federal Parliament is held, an inconsistent law becomes invalid to the extent of its inconsistency."",""संघीय संसद्को पहिलो अधिवेशन बसेको मितिले एक वर्षपछि संविधानसँग बाझिएको कानून जति हदसम्म बाझिन्छ, त्यति हदसम्म अमान्य हुन्छ।"",The Constitution provides a transitional period before inconsistent pre-existing laws automatically become invalid to the extent of inconsistency.,Art. 304(1),Existing laws to remain in force,,,,,,
TP042,Transitional Provisions,Peace Process,Factual,Medium,""How are Acts relating to the peace process under the Interim Constitution of Nepal, 2007 treated under the Constitution?"",""नेपालको अन्तरिम संविधान, २०६३ अन्तर्गत शान्ति प्रक्रियासम्बन्धी कार्यहरूलाई संविधानअन्तर्गत कसरी मानिन्छ?"",They are deemed to have been done under the Constitution.,संविधानअन्तर्गत गरिएको मानिन्छ।,Article 304(2) provides continuity and legal recognition for peace-process-related acts carried out under the Interim Constitution.,Art. 304(2),Existing laws to remain in force,,,,,,
DF001,Definitions and Interpretations,Minorities,Definition,Easy,What does the term “minority” refer to under Article 306 of the Constitution?,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “अल्पसंख्यक” भन्नाले के जनाउँछ?,""Minorities are ethnic, linguistic, and religious groups whose population is below the percentage specified by Federal law, including groups with distinct ethnic, religious, or linguistic characteristics and aspirations to protect them that have been subjected to discrimination and oppression."",""संघीय कानूनले तोकेको प्रतिशतभन्दा कम जनसंख्या भएका जातीय, भाषिक र धार्मिक समूहहरू, साथै आफ्ना विशिष्ट जातीय, धार्मिक वा भाषिक विशेषता संरक्षण गर्ने आकांक्षा भएका र विभेद तथा उत्पीडनमा परेका समूहहरूलाई अल्पसंख्यक भनिन्छ।"",The definition includes both population-based criteria and groups with distinct characteristics that have faced discrimination or oppression.,Art. 306(1)(e),Definitions and interpretations,,,,,,
DF002,Definitions and Interpretations,Law,Definition,Easy,What does the term “law” refer to under Article 306 of the Constitution?,संविधानको धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “कानून” भन्नाले के बुझिन्छ?,""“Law” means Federal law, State law, and Local law."",""कानुन भन्नाले संघीय कानून, प्रदेश कानून र स्थानीय कानून बुझिन्छ।"",The constitutional definition recognizes laws made at all three levels of the federal structure.,Art. 306(1)(c),Definitions and interpretations,,,,,,
DF003,Definitions and Interpretations,Article,Definition,Easy,What does the term “Article” refer to under Article 306 of the Constitution?,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “धारा” भन्नाले के जनाउँछ?,""It means an Article of the Constitution.,संविधानको कुनै धारा"",The term ""Article"" is specifically defined as a provision of the Constitution itself."",Art. 306(1)(d),Definitions and interpretations,,,,,,
DF004,Definitions and Interpretations,Citizen,Definition,Easy,Who is considered a “citizen” under Article 306?,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “नागरिक” भन्नाले कसलाई जनाउँछ?,""A citizen means a citizen of Nepal.,“नागरিক” भन्नाले नेपालको नागरिकलाई जनाउँछ।,The constitutional definition limits the term to a citizen of Nepal.,Art. 306(1)(e),Definitions and interpretations,,,,,,
DF005,Definitions and Interpretations,Municipality,Definition,Medium,What entities are included within the constitutional definition of “Municipality”?,संवैधानिक रूपमा “नगरपालिका” को परिभाषाभित्र कुन निकायहरू पर्छन्?,A Municipality includes a Municipal Corporation and a Sub-municipal Corporation.,नगरपालिका भन्नाले महानगरपालिका र उपमहानगरपालिका समेत जनाउँछ।,The definition gives “Municipalty” a broader meaning by expressly including Municipal Corporations and Sub-municipal Corporations."",Art. 306(1)(d),Definitions and Interpretations,,,,,,
TP043,Transitional Provisions,Existing Laws,Factual,Hard,After what event and period does the inconsistency rule for existing laws take effect under Article 304(1)?,धारा ३०४(१) अन्तर्गत व्यवस्थाको कुन घटनाले असंगतिलाई प्रभावित गर्छ?,""After one year from the date on which the first session of the Federal Parliament is held, an inconsistent law becomes invalid to the extent of its inconsistency."",""संघीय संसद्को पहिलो अधिवेशन बसेको मितिले एक वर्षपछि संविधानसँग बाझिएको कानून जति हदसम्म बाझिन्छ, त्यति हदसम्म अमान्य हुन्छ।"",The Constitution provides a transitional period before inconsistent pre-existing laws automatically become invalid to the extent inconsistency.,Art. 304(1),Existing laws to remain in force,,,,,,
TP044,Transitional Provisions,Existing Laws,Factual,Medium,What happens to an order issued to remove difficulties under Article 305?,धारा ३०५ अन्तर्गत कठिनाइ हटाउन जारी गरिएको आदेशको कुन परिणाम हुन्छ?,""It must be submitted for approval to the Legislature-Parliament or Federal Parliament that is held immediately after the order is issued.,आदेश जारी भएपछि तुरुन्त बस्ने व्यवस्थापिका–संसद् वा संघीय संसद्समक्ष अनुमोदनका लागि पेश गर्नुपर्छ।,The power to remove difficulties is temporary and subject to legislative oversight through subsequent approval."",जति हदसम्म संविधान",Correct,Not a strict error,False
PP006,English,How often must a political party's office-bearers at Federal and State levels be elected according to its constitution?,At least once every five years.,"According to Article 303(1) of the Constitution, political parties’ office-bearer elections must be held until the number and areas of the Local level are determined in accordance with the Constitution. Therefore, they must be elected **until the number and areas of the Local level are determined in accordance with the Constitution.**",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
PP006,Nepali,राजनीतिक दलको संघीय र प्रदेश तहका पदाधिकारीहरू कति अवधिमा एक पटक निर्वाचित हुनुपर्ने व्यवस्था हुनुपर्छ?,कम्तीमा प्रत्येक पाँच वर्षमा एक पटक।,Article 304 of the Constitution states that political party officials in both the federal and regional levels must be elected at least once during the transitional period.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
PP007,English,What is the maximum additional period allowed for holding office-bearer elections if a political party fails to do so within five years due to a special circumstance?,Within six months.,"Article 304(2) of the Constitution states that “if a political party fails to hold election of officials of the existing Local Bodies within five years due to a special circumstance, the period of holding office-bearer elections shall be extended by an additional period of up to three months.”",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
PP007,Nepali,विशेष परिस्थितिका कारण पाँच वर्षभित्र पदाधिकारी निर्वाचन हुन नसकेमा थप कति अवधिभित्र निर्वाचन गर्न सकिन्छ?,छ महिनाभित्र।,"Article 304(1) of the Constitution of Nepal provides continuity for elected local officials until the elections to the Local Level are held. Therefore, five years from the date of the first session of the Federal Parliament, elected officials of the existing Local Bodies can continue holding office.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
PP008,English,What type of representation must a political party provide in its executive committees at various levels?,Inclusive representation reflecting Nepal's diversity.,"According to Article 306 of the Constitution, political parties must provide representation in their executive committees at all three levels (Federal, State, and Local) based on their size. The specific number of representatives required depends on the party’s size. Here's a breakdown:

*   **Federal Level:** Parties with more than 100 members must provide one representative.
*   **State Level:** Parties with more than 50 members must provide one representative.
*   **Local Level:** Parties with more than 20 members must provide one representative.

Essentially, the Constitution mandates that political parties maintain a proportional representation of their size across all levels of government.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
PP008,Nepali,राजनीतिक दलका विभिन्न तहका कार्यकारी समितिमा कस्तो प्रतिनिधित्वको व्यवस्था हुनुपर्छ?,नेपालको विविधता प्रतिबिम्बित गर्ने समावेशी प्रतिनिधित्व।,"संविधान २०६५ अनुसार, राजनीतिक दलोंका विभिन्न तहका कार्यकारी समितियाँ ३०% प्रतिनिधित्व मा आधारित होनी चाहिए। यहाँ विस्तृत विवरण दिया गया है:

*   **स्थानीय स्तर (Local Level):** प्रत्येक स्थानीय सरकार में एक प्रतिनिधि होने के लिए, पार्टी का एक सदस्य होना चाहिए जो उस क्षेत्र से जुड़ा हो।
*   **प्रांतीय स्तर (Regional Level):** प्रांतीय स्तर पर, पार्टी का एक प्रतिनिधि होने के लिए, प्रांत में काम करने वाले लोगों को चुना जाना चाहिए।
*   **राष्ट्रीय स्तर (National Level):** राष्ट्रीय स्तर पर, पार्टी का एक प्रतिनिधि होने के लिए, देश भर में काम करने वाले लोगों को चुना जाना चाहिए।

यह व्यवस्था सुनिश्चित करती है कि विभिन्न राजनीतिक दलों की आवाजें सभी स्तरों तक पहुंच सकें और सरकार द्वारा निर्णय लेने में शामिल हों।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
PP009,English,Under what circumstances shall a political party not be registered?,"If its name, objective, insignia or flag jeopardizes religious and communal unity or fragments the country.","Article 304(2) of the Constitution states that a political party cannot be registered if it violates the principles of democracy, pluralism, and the rule of law. It further stipulates that registration should not hinder the functioning of democratic processes.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
PP009,Nepali,कुन अवस्थामा राजनीतिक दल दर्ता गरिने छैन?,"यदि यसको नाम, उद्देश्य, चिन्ह वा झण्डाले धार्मिक तथा साम्प्रदायिक एकता खल्बल्याउँछ वा देश विखण्डन गर्छ भने।",Political parties are not registered under Article 306 of the Constitution of Nepal.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
PP010,English,"A political party has a democratic constitution, holds elections every five years, and has inclusive representation. Which constitutional requirement does this satisfy?",Conditions required for political party registration under Article 269(4).,"The constitutional requirement that satisfies this is the **inclusive representation** enshrined in Article 306 of the Constitution. This article states that “Municipality” includes a Municipal Corporation and Sub-municipal Corporation.  This ensures that all communities, regardless of their size or location, are represented within local governance structures.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
PP010,Nepali,"लोकतान्त्रिक विधान भएको, प्रत्येक पाँच वर्षमा निर्वाचन गर्ने र समावेशी प्रतिनिधित्व भएको राजनीतिक दलले कुन संवैधानिक आवश्यकता पूरा गर्छ?",धारा २६९(४) अन्तर्गत राजनीतिक दल दर्ताका लागि आवश्यक शर्तहरू।,"लोकतान्त्रिक विधानको लागि, एक राजनीतिक दलले निम्न संवैधानिक आवश्यकता पूर्ण रूपमा पूरा गर्नुपर्छ:

*   **प्रतिनिधित्व:** पार्टीले आफ्नो सदस्यको संख्या सरकारमा समावेशय र संसदमा प्रतिनिधित्वको पर्याप्त मात्रामा राख्नुपर्छ।
*   **संसद्:** पार्टीले आफ्नो सदस्यताको लागि उचित व्यवस्था सुनिश्चित गर्नुपर्छ, जसलाई संविधानले स्पष्ट रूपमा परिभाषित गर्दछ।
*   **सहिष्णुता:** राजनीतिक दलले अन्य राजनीतिक दलहरूको सदस्यताको सहिष्णुता बनाएर र स्वीकार गरउनुपर्छ।
*   **समानता:** पार्टीले सबै राजनीतिक दलहरू बीच समानता सुनिश्चित गर्नुपर्छ, ताकि कुनै पनि दललाई दबाब नहुँस्।
*   **सहिष्णुता:** पार्टीले अन्य राजनीतिक दलहरूको सदस्यताको सहिष्णुता बनाएर र स्वीकार गरउनुपर्छ।

यो पूर्ण रूपमा संवैधानिक आवश्यकता हो।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
PP011,English,"What happens to any law, arrangement, or decision that restricts the formation and operation of political parties contrary to Article 269?",It is inconsistent with the Constitution and void.,"Article 269 of the Constitution states that the government shall not restrict the formation and operation of political parties. Therefore, any law, arrangement, or decision that restricts the formation and operation of political parties contrary to this article will be invalid under Article 269.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
PP011,Nepali,"धारा २६९ विपरीत राजनीतिक दलको गठन र सञ्चालनमा प्रतिबन्ध लगाउने कानून, व्यवस्था वा निर्णयको अवस्था के हुन्छ?",त्यो संविधानसँग बाझिने र स्वतः अमान्य हुन्छ।,"धारा २६९ अनुसार, यदि एक पार्टीलेOpposition (प्रतिबन्ध) पक्ष बनाउँछ तर प्रयोग गर्दछ, तर सरकारले त्यसलाई हटाउन्छ।

Explanation:
The law states that if a party establishes an opposition party and operates it, the government will remove it.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
PP012,English,What type of political system participation restriction is prohibited by Article 270?,,"Article 270 prohibits restrictions on political participation, specifically limiting the right to vote and participate in government affairs. It states that “the right to vote and participate in government affairs shall not be restricted.”",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
PP012,Nepali,धारा २७० अनुसार कस्तो राजनीतिक प्रणाली सहभाग,,"धारा २७० अनुसार, सहभागितात्मक (participatory) राजनीतिक प्रणालीको व्यवस्थापनमा नेपाल सरकारले निम्न कार्यहरू गर्नुपर्छ:

*   **स्थानीय स्तर पर नागरिकहरूको आवाजलाई बुझिन्छ:** स्थानीय स्तर पर नागरिकहरूको आवाजलाई बुझिदिन र उनका सुझावहरूलाई ध्यानपूर्वक सुनिन।
*   **संसद्वाचक会合को आयोजन:** संसद्वाचक会合को आयोजन गर्यैँ, जहाँ नागरिकहरूले आफ्नो意見 व्यक्त गर्न सक्छन्।
*   **राजनीतिकमा सहभागीथकानी:** राजनीतिकमा सहभागीथकानीलाई प्रोत्साहन दिइँ, ताकि नागरिकहरूले राजनीतिमा सक्रिय रूपमा भाग लिन्छन।
*   **संसद्वाचक会合को резултаतका पर निर्णय लिएर:** संसद्वाचक会合को परिणामका पर निर्णय लिएर, स्थानीय स्तर पर नीतिहरूको निर्माण गर्यैँ।

यो तरिकाले नेपाल सरकारले सहभागितात्मक राजनीतिक प्रणालीलाई चलाउन र नागरिकहरूलाई राजनीतिमा सहभागीथकानी प्रोत्साहित गर्न सक्छन्।",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
PP013,English,What type of political party participation or involvement arrangement is declared void by Article 270?,"An arrangement allowing only a single political party or persons with similar ideology, philosophy, or program to participate in elections or governance.","Article 270 declares void any political party’s participation or involvement arrangements during the transition period. It states that such arrangements are deemed invalid to prevent potential conflicts and ensure a smooth transition of power. The text doesn't provide specific details about *how* this is determined, but it highlights the need for careful consideration of these arrangements.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
PP013,Nepali,धारा २७० अनुसार कस्तो राजनीतिक दलको सहभागिता वा संलग्नताको व्यवस्था अमान्य हुन्छ?,"केवल एक राजनीतिक दल वा समान विचारधारा, दर्शन वा कार्यक्रम भएका व्यक्तिलाई मात्र निर्वाचन वा शासन प्रणालीमा सहभागी हुन दिने व्यवस्था।","धारा २७० अनुसार, यदि कुनै राजनीतिक दलले संविधानमा उल्लिखित तरतव्यहरूलाई उल्लंघन गर्छ भने, त्यसको सहभागिता वा संलग्नता अमान्य हुन्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
PP014,English,Why is a law allowing only one political party to participate in elections considered invalid under the Constitution?,"Because it restricts participation to only a single political party or similar ideology, philosophy, or program.","Under Article 304(1) of the Constitution, existing laws that are inconsistent with the Constitution become invalid to the extent of their inconsistency. This means that if a law allows only one political party to compete in elections, it becomes invalid because it violates the principle of pluralism and representation within the electoral system.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
PP014,Nepali,निर्वाचनमा केवल एउटा राजनीतिक दललाई मात्र सहभागी हुन दिने कानून किन संविधानविपरीत मानिन्छ?,"किनकि यसले केवल एउटा राजनीतिक दल वा समान विचारधारा, दर्शन वा कार्यक्रम भएका व्यक्तिको मात्र सहभागिता सुनिश्चित गर्छ।","Article 304 of the Constitution states that elections to officials of existing Local Bodies shall be held according to law. If only one political party is allowed to participate in elections, it becomes inconsistent with the principles of democracy and representation.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
PP015,English,What must a registered political party do to obtain recognition from the Election Commission for contesting elections?,Register with the Election Commission according to procedures set by Federal law.,"To obtain recognition from the Election Commission for contesting elections, a registered political party must fulfill several requirements outlined in Article 306 of the Constitution of Nepal. Here’s a breakdown of what they need to do:

1.  **Submit an Application:** The party needs to submit a formal application to the Election Commission outlining their intentions and qualifications for election. This application should include details about their organization, leadership, and proposed electoral program.

2.  **Demonstrate Legal Compliance:** The party must demonstrate that they comply with all relevant laws and regulations related to political parties, including those outlined in the Constitution and other applicable legislation.

3.  **Meet Eligibility Criteria:** The party needs to meet specific eligibility criteria as defined by law, such as having a minimum number of registered members, being organized according to established rules, and adhering to ethical standards.

4. **Provide Information about Leadership & Structure**: The application must include details about the leadership structure of the party, including names and qualifications of key figures. 

5.  **Adhere to Election Guidelines:** The party must follow all guidelines and procedures set forth by the Election Commission during the election process. This includes adhering to timelines for registration, campaign activities, and other relevant requirements.

6. **Compliance with Constitution**: The political party must comply with the provisions of the Constitution regarding political parties. 


**Important Note:**  The exact details and specific requirements can be subject to change by law. It's crucial that political parties stay informed about any updates or revisions to these regulations through official sources like the Election Commission website.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
PP015,Nepali,निर्वाचनमा प्रतिस्पर्धा गर्न निर्वाचन आयोगबाट मान्यता प्राप्त गर्न दर्ता भएको राजनीतिक दलले के गर्नुपर्छ?,संघीय कानूनले तोकेको प्रक्रिया पूरा गरी निर्वाचन आयोगमा दर्ता हुनुपर्छ।,"Political parties registered with the Election Commission of Nepal must perform several key actions to be recognized for election purposes. Here's a breakdown of what they need to do:

*   **Submit Required Documents:** The political party needs to submit all necessary documents to the Election Commission, including registration certificates, financial statements, and other required forms.
*   **Comply with Election Rules:** They must adhere strictly to all rules and regulations set by the Election Commission regarding campaign activities, voter eligibility, and election procedures.
*   **Obtain Approval for Campaign Activities:** The party needs to obtain approval from the Election Commission before launching any significant political campaigns or activities. This includes ensuring that campaigns are conducted in accordance with ethical standards and do not violate electoral laws.
*   **Maintain Transparency:** Political parties must maintain transparency in their operations, including disclosing financial information and campaign spending.
*   **Ensure Voter Registration Compliance:** The party needs to ensure that all registered voters are properly registered for elections.

In essence, the political party is responsible for complying with all legal requirements and ethical guidelines to be recognized as a legitimate political entity capable of participating in election processes.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
PP016,English,What is the difference between registration under Article 269 and recognition for election purposes under Article 271?,"Article 269 concerns party registration after formation, while Article 271 concerns recognition for contesting elections.","Under Article 269, the government of Nepal registers individuals or entities who are eligible to hold positions in various sectors. It’s a formal process designed to ensure accountability and transparency. Under Article 271, the government recognizes existing officials and bodies that have been established under the Constitution. This is primarily for election purposes, allowing for the smooth functioning of elections.

Here's a breakdown of the key differences:

*   **Article 269:** Focuses on *registration* – formally listing individuals or entities who are qualified to hold specific roles and responsibilities within government agencies. It’s about establishing eligibility based on qualifications and experience.
*   **Article 271:** Primarily focuses on *recognition* - confirming that existing officials and bodies have the legal authority and legitimacy to continue their functions, particularly during elections.  It's a mechanism for validating established structures.

Essentially, Article 269 is about *who* is qualified; Article 271 is about *what* is recognized as valid.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
PP016,Nepali,धारा २६९ अन्तर्गतको दर्ता र धारा २७१ अन्तर्गत निर्वाचन प्रयोजनको मान्यताबीच के फरक छ?,धारा २६९ गठनपछि दल दर्तासँग सम्बन्धित छ भने धारा २७१ निर्वाचनमा भाग लिन मान्यतासँग सम्बन्धित छ।,"धारा २६९ अन्तर्गतको दर्ता (Registration) और धारा २७१ अन्तर्गत निर्वाचन प्रयोजनको मान्यता (Purpose of Electoral Recognition) बीच मुख्यतе निम्नफरन्सीहरू छन्:

*   **दर्ताको प्रकार:** दर्ताले स्थानीय सरकारका सदस्यहरूको सूची बनाउँछ, तर निर्वाचनमा सहभागी हुन आएर उनका पदमाथप्नको लागि आवश्यक पर्ने व्यक्तिलाई समावेश गर्दैन। जबकि निर्वाचन प्रयोजनको मान्यताले मतदाताहरूलाई मतदान गर्ने अधिकार दिन्छ र निर्वाचनको उद्देश्यको स्पष्टीकरण प्रदान गर्दछ।

*   **निर्वाचित कार्य:** दर्ताका रूपमा, स्थानीय सरकारका सदस्यहरूको प्रतिनिधित्व गराउँछ तर निर्वाचनमा सहभागी हुन आएर उनका पदमाथप्नको लागि आवश्यक पर्ने व्यक्तिलाई समावेश गर्न नसकिन्छ। जबकि निर्वाचन प्रयोजनको मान्यताले मतदाताहरूलाई मतदान गर्ने अधिकार दिन्छ र निर्वाचनको उद्देश्यको स्पष्टीकरण प्रदान गर्दछ।

*   **संसद्वाचक:** दर्ताले स्थानीय सरकारका सदस्यहरूको प्रतिनिधित्व गराउँछ, तर निर्वाचनमा सहभागी हुन आएर उनका पदमाथप्नको लागि आवश्यक पर्ने व्यक्तिलाई समावेश गर्न नसकिन्छ। जबकि निर्वाचन प्रयोजनको मान्यताले मतदाताहरूलाई मतदान गर्ने अधिकार दिन्छ र निर्वाचनको उद्देश्यको स्पष्टीकरण प्रदान गर्दछ।

संक्षेप में, दर्ताले स्थानीय सरकारका सदस्यहरूको प्रतिनिधित्व गराउँछ तर निर्वाचनमा सहभागी हुन आएर उनका पदमाथप्नको लागि आवश्यक पर्ने व्यक्तिलाई समावेश गर्न नसकिन्छ। जबकि निर्वाचन प्रयोजनको मान्यताले मतदाताहरूलाई मतदान गर्ने अधिकार दिन्छ र निर्वाचनको उद्देश्यको स्पष्टीकरण प्रदान गर्दछ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
PP017,English,What additional report must a political party submit along with an application for election recognition?,Yearly audit report.,"According to the provided text, a political party must submit an additional report along with an application for election recognition if they are seeking to be recognized as a candidate in any election. The text states: “Article 305 grants this transitional power to the President, subject to a recommendation from the Council of Ministers.”",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
PP017,Nepali,निर्वाचन प्रयोजनको मान्यताका लागि आवेदन दिँदा राजनीतिक दलले थप कुन प्रतिवेदन बुझाउनुपर्छ?,वार्षिक लेखापरीक्षण प्रतिवेदन।,Article 304 of the Constitution states that political parties must provide the government with a report on the number of candidates elected to local bodies during the transitional period.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
PP018,English,"Besides submitting a yearly audit report, which other constitutional requirements must a political party fulfill to obtain election recognition?",The requirements under Article 269(3) and Article 269(4).,"According to Article 304 of the Constitution of Nepal, a political party must fulfill several constitutional requirements before obtaining election recognition. Here’s a breakdown of those requirements:

*   **Registration with Election Commission:** The political party must register its name and address with the Election Commission of Nepal (ECN). This registration process is crucial for establishing legal identity and ensuring compliance with electoral laws.
*   **Submission of Annual Audit Report:** A yearly audit report detailing financial transactions and assets is mandatory. This report demonstrates accountability and transparency to the public.
*   **Compliance with Electoral Laws:** The party must adhere strictly to all relevant electoral laws, regulations, and guidelines issued by the ECN. These laws cover everything from campaign finance rules to voter registration procedures.
*   **Meeting Requirements for Representation:**  The political party needs to meet specific requirements related to representation in the National Assembly (Parliament) or local councils. This often involves demonstrating a certain level of support within the community and meeting other criteria outlined by the ECN.

In essence, it's not just about registration; it’s a comprehensive process that ensures the political party is legally compliant and capable of participating in elections.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
PP018,Nepali,वार्षिक लेखापरीक्षण प्रतिवेदन बाहेक निर्वाचन मान्यता प्राप्त गर्न राजनीतिक दलले अन्य कुन संवैधानिक शर्त पूरा गर्नुपर्छ?,धारा २६९(३) र धारा २६९(४) का आवश्यकताहरू।,"Political parties must fulfill other constitutional conditions to obtain the annual audit report, considering the election recognition. Here’s a breakdown of those conditions:

*   **Election Recognition:** The political party must have successfully completed the electoral process in accordance with the Constitution. This includes registering voters, conducting elections, and ensuring fair and transparent voting procedures.
*   **Representation in Parliament:** The political party must maintain a minimum representation percentage in the parliament (Federal Parliament or Regional Assemblies). This is determined by the Federal Law.
*   **Political Stability:** There should be a degree of political stability within the country to ensure continuity of governance.
*   **Public Trust:** Political parties need to demonstrate public trust and confidence, which can be assessed through various mechanisms like voter surveys and public opinion polls.

In essence, the constitutional requirements for obtaining an audit report are tied directly to the electoral process and the overall political landscape within Nepal.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
PP019,English,"A political party submits its constitution, manifesto, yearly audit report, and proves democratic internal rules. Which constitutional processes is it satisfying?",Party registration and election recognition requirements.,"Article 304 of the Constitution ensures continuity of existing Local Bodies during the transitional period to the new Local Level structure. It provides for elections to officials of existing Local Bodies to be held according to law, ensuring their continued operation until the new Local level is determined in accordance with the Constitution.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
PP019,Nepali,"राजनीतिक दलले आफ्नो विधान, घोषणापत्र, वार्षिक लेखापरीक्षण प्रतिवेदन बुझाई लोकतान्त्रिक आन्तरिक नियम प्रमाणित गरेमा कुन संवैधानिक प्रक्रियाहरू पूरा गरिरहेको हुन्छ?",दल दर्ता र निर्वाचन मान्यता सम्बन्धी आवश्यकताहरू।,"Political parties must complete several constitutional processes when they certify their annual financial statements and legislative proceedings by adhering to the law. These include:

*   **Accountability:** Political parties are accountable to the public for their finances, ensuring transparency in their operations.
*   **Compliance with Laws:** They must comply with all relevant laws and regulations related to finance and governance.
*   **Legal Requirements:** The certification process is governed by specific legal requirements outlined in the Constitution and other legislation.
*   **Public Trust:**  The process demonstrates that political parties are operating within the bounds of the law, fostering public trust and confidence.

In essence, it's a formal verification of their financial practices and governance structure as mandated by the Constitution.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
PP020,English,"Which law provides detailed provisions regarding formation, registration, operation, facilities, and other matters of political parties?",Federal law.,"Article 304 of the Constitution of Nepal outlines the rules concerning political parties. It details the process for establishing, registering, operating, and managing these organizations. The text states that elections to officials of existing Local Bodies shall be held according to law. This establishes a framework for the establishment and operation of political parties within the context of local governance.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
PP020,Nepali,"राजनीतिक दलको गठन, दर्ता, सञ्चालन, सुविधा तथा अन्य विषयसम्बन्धी विस्तृत व्यवस्था कुन कानूनले गर्छ?",संघीय कानून।,"संविधान २०६५ अनुसार राजनीतिक दलहरूको गठन, सदस्यता, संचालन, सुવિધाहरू र अन्य सहभागिताहरूलाई व्यवस्थित गर्नको लागि नियम बनाएको कानून हो - **Political Parties Act (PAA)**।

यस कानूनले निम्न कार्यहरू गर्दछ:

*   **राजनीतिक दलहरूको निर्माण:** नयाँ राजनीतिक दलहरू बनाउनकाै लिएनको নিয়মलाई स्पष्ट पार्छ।
*   **सदस्यता प्रक्रिया:** राजनीतिक दलहरू सदस्यता प्राप्त गर्नको लागि नियमहरू प्रदान गर्दछ।
*   **संचालनमा आवश्यकताहरू:** राजनीतिक दलहरूले आफ्नो संचालनको लागि आवश्यक तरतव्यहरू बुझिन्छ।
*   **सुविधाहरू:** राजनीतिक दलहरूको लागि सुવિધाहरूको व्यवस्थापनलाई सुनिश्चित गर्दछ।
*   **अन्य सहभागिताहरू:** राजनीतिक दलहरूको अन्य सहभागिताहरूलाई स्पष्ट पार्छ।

संविधान २०६५मा,Political Parties Act (PAA)ले राजनीतिक दलहरूको निर्माण, सदस्यता, संचालन, सुવિધाहरू र अन्य सहभागिताहरूलाई व्यवस्थित गर्नको लागि नियम बनाएको कानून हो।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
EP001,English,Who has the authority to declare or order a state of emergency under Article 273?,The President.,Article 273 of the Constitution grants the President the power to declare a state of emergency.,Correct,Not a strict error,False
EP001,Nepali,धारा २७३ अनुसार संकटकाल घोषणा वा आदेश गर्ने अधिकार कसलाई हुन्छ?,राष्ट्रपति।,"धारा २७३ अनुसार, संकटकाल घोषणा वा आदेश गर्ने अधिकार, सरकारको संसदमा एक प्रस्तावनामा प्रस्तुत गरेर, संविधानको प्रावधानहरूलाई स्पष्ट बनाउनु र त्यसका पालन नहुँदाले जनतालाई सुरक्षित राख्नु पर्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP002,English,What situations may lead to the declaration of a state of emergency under the Constitution?,"War, external aggression, armed rebellion, extreme economic disarray, natural calamity, or epidemic.","According to Article 305 of the Constitution, the following situations can lead to the declaration of a state of emergency:

*   **Threats to national security:** This includes threats to the stability and integrity of Nepal.
*   **Serious threat to public order:**  This refers to a situation that disrupts public order and safety.
*   **Serious threat to public health:** This involves a significant risk to public health, such as an outbreak of disease or a danger to public welfare.
*   **Serious threat to the peaceful enjoyment of life by citizens:** This means a situation that undermines the fundamental rights and freedoms of citizens.

Essentially, any situation that poses a serious and immediate danger to the well-being of the nation is considered a potential trigger for declaring a state of emergency.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
EP002,Nepali,संविधानअनुसार कुन-कुन अवस्थामा संकटकाल घोषणा गर्न सकिन्छ?,"युद्ध, बाह्य आक्रमण, सशस्त्र विद्रोह, चरम आर्थिक विशृंखलता, प्राकृतिक विपद् वा महामारी।","संविधानअनुसार, संकटकाल घोषणा गर्न सकिन्छ जब तक कि संविधानको लेखहरूलाई कसरी बुझिन्छ भन्ने माथि जाँच गर्ने समय आए हो।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP003,English,"Can a state of emergency be declared only for the whole country, or can it apply to a specific part of Nepal?",It may apply to the whole of Nepal or any specified part thereof.,"The Constitution does not explicitly define whether an Emergency State can be declared solely for the entire country or for a specific part of Nepal. However, the text suggests that the declaration is contingent on the number and areas determined in accordance with the Constitution. It implies that the emergency state will be triggered when the constitutionally defined boundaries of the country are established.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP003,Nepali,संकटकाल केवल सम्पूर्ण नेपालमा मात्र लागू हुन्छ वा नेपालको कुनै निश्चित भागमा पनि लागू हुन सक्छ?,सम्पूर्ण नेपाल वा नेपालको कुनै निश्चित भागमा लागू हुन सक्छ।,"संक्रमणकालले सबै नेपाली राष्ट्रियता र भाषा भएको क्षेत्रमा लागू हुनेछ।"",""संकक्रमणकालले सबै नेपाली राष्ट्रियता र भाषा भएको क्षेत्रमा लागू हुनेछ।""",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP004,English,In what situation may a State Government request the Government of Nepal to declare a state of emergency?,When a grave emergency arises in a State due to natural calamity or epidemic.,"Article 305,Powers and Responsibilities of the Government of Nepal, Section 305, states that the President can issue orders to remove difficulties in implementing the Constitution before the first session of the Federal Parliament. This is done under the recommendation of the Council of Ministers. Therefore, a State Government might request this action if it believes implementation is severely hampered and requires urgent intervention.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
EP004,Nepali,कुन अवस्थामा प्रदेश सरकारले नेपाल सरकारलाई संकटकाल घोषणा गर्न अनुरोध गर्न सक्छ?,प्राकृतिक विपद् वा महामारीका कारण प्रदेशमा गम्भीर आपतकालीन अवस्था उत्पन्न हुँदा।,"संविधान अनुसार, प्रदेश सरकारले नेपाल सरकारलाई संकटकालीन स्थिति घोषणा गर्नको लागि अनुरोध गर्न सकिन्छ। संविधानले विशेष रूप देखेर, स्थानीय तहहरूलाई तत्काल समयमा आлото अवस्थामा जान्ने र राज्यको व्यवस्थापनमा बिगासिने अवस्था देखाउँदै, स्थानीय तहहरूको सुरक्षा सुनिश्चित गर्नका लागि निवेदन गर्न सक्ने जनाउँछ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP005,English,Within what period must an emergency declaration be presented before both Houses of the Federal Parliament for approval?,Within one month after the date of issuance.,"Article 305 grants the President the power to issue orders to remove difficulties under Article 305. The President, on the recommendation of the Government of Nepal, Council of Ministers, must submit an order for approval before the first session of the Federal Parliament.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
EP005,Nepali,संकटकाल घोषणालाई संघीय संसदका दुवै सदनमा अनुमोदनका लागि कति अवधिभित्र पेश गर्नुपर्छ?,जारी भएको मितिले एक महिनाभित्र।,"संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदाका सरकारी सेवामा कार्यरत कर्मचारीहरूलाई कानूनबमोजिम संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहमा समायोजन गरेर।"",""By adjusting employees serving in government services at the commencement of the Constitution among the Federal, State and Local levels in accordance with law.""",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP006,English,Which legislative bodies must approve a declaration or order of emergency?,Both Houses of the Federal Parliament.,"Article 305 of the Constitution grants this power to the President, subject to the recommendation of the Council of Ministers.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
EP006,Nepali,संकटकाल घोषणा वा आदेशलाई कुन-कुन व्यवस्थापिकाले अनुमोदन गर्नुपर्छ?,संघीय संसदका दुवै सदन।,"संविधानको धारा ३०४(१) अनुसार, संकटकाल घोषणा वा आदेशलाई संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहमा पहली व्यवस्थापिकाले अनुमोदन गर्नुपर्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP007,English,What majority is required in both Houses of the Federal Parliament to approve a state of emergency declaration?,At least two-thirds majority of the total number of then members of both Houses.,Article 305 of the Constitution of Nepal states that “the majority required for declaring a State of Emergency shall be two-thirds (two-fifths) of the members of both Houses of the Federal Parliament.”,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP007,Nepali,संकटकाल घोषणा अनुमोदन गर्न संघीय संसदका दुवै सदनमा कस्तो बहुमत आवश्यक हुन्छ?,तत्काल कायम रहेका दुवै सदनका कुल सदस्य संख्याको कम्तीमा दुई तिहाइ बहुमत।,"संविधानको धारा ३०५ अनुसार, संघीय संसदका दुई सदनमा शान्ति प्रक्रियासम्बन्धी कार्यहरूलाई कार्यान्वयनमा आएSebelum के बहुमत आवश्यक हुन्छ?
সংবিধানकोधारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत, संघीय संसदका दुवै सदनमा शान्ति प्रक्रियासम्बन्धी कार्यहरूलाई कार्यान्वयनमा आएSebelum के बहुमत आवश्यक हुन्छ?
The majority of the two houses of parliament must be more than 50% in number.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP008,English,For how long does an approved state of emergency declaration remain in force from the date of issuance?,Three months.,Until the number and areas of the Local level are determined in accordance with the Constitution.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
EP008,Nepali,अनुमोदन भएको संकटकाल घोषणा जारी भएको मितिबाट कति समयसम्म कायम रहन्छ?,तीन महिना।,"अनुमोदन भएको संकटकाल घोषणा जारी भएको मितिले एक वर्षपछि संविधानसँग बाझिएको कानून जति हदसम्म अमान्य हुन्छ।"",After one year from the date on which the first session of the Federal Parliament is held, an inconsistent law becomes invalid to the extent of its inconsistency."",After one year from the date on which the first session of the Federal Parliament is held, an inconsistent law becomes invalid to the extent of its inconsistency.""",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP009,English,What happens if a state of emergency declaration is not approved according to the constitutional requirement?,It becomes inoperative automatically.,"According to Article 305 of the Constitution, if a state of emergency declaration is not approved according to the constitutional requirement, it becomes invalid to the extent of its inconsistency.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP009,Nepali,संवैधानिक आवश्यकता अनुसार संकटकाल घोषणा अनुमोदन नभएमा के हुन्छ?,त्यो स्वतः निष्क्रिय हुन्छ।,"Article 304(1) of the Constitution states that an inconsistent law becomes invalid to the extent of its inconsistency. Therefore, if a law is not enacted under the Constitution during the transitional period, it remains in force until it is repealed or amended by the Legislature.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
EP010,English,A state of emergency is declared and presented to both Houses within one month. What additional condition is required for it to continue in force?,Approval by at least a two-thirds majority of the total number of then members of both Houses.,"Article 305 of the Constitution of Nepal states that “the State of Emergency shall continue until the number and areas of the Local Level are determined in accordance with the Constitution.” Therefore, the additional condition required for it to continue in force is that the **number and areas of the Local Level are determined in accordance with the Constitution.**",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
EP010,Nepali,संकटकाल घोषणा गरी एक महिनाभित्र दुवै सदनमा पेश गरिएपछि कायम रहन थप कुन शर्त आवश्यक हुन्छ?,तत्काल कायम रहेका दुवै सदनका कुल सदस्य संख्याको कम्तीमा दुई तिहाइ बहुमतबाट अनुमोदन।,"संविधान अनुसार, संकटकाल घोषणा गरी एक महिनाभित्र दुवै सदनमा पेश गरिएपछि कायम रहन थप, सरकारले तत्काल व्यवस्थापनको आदेश जारी गर्नुपर्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP011,English,What is the difference between the approval deadline and the validity period of an approved emergency declaration?,"Approval must occur within one month, while an approved declaration remains for three months from issuance.","According to Article 305 of the Constitution, the President can issue an order to remove difficulties under Article 305. This order must be submitted for approval by the Legislature-Parliament or Federal Parliament that is held immediately after the order is issued. The validity period of this approved emergency declaration is limited to one year from the date it was issued.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP011,Nepali,संकटकाल अनुमोदनको समयसीमा र अनुमोदनपछि कायम रहने अवधिबीच के फरक छ?,अनुमोदन एक महिनाभित्र हुनुपर्छ भने अनुमोदन भएको घोषणा जारी भएको मितिबाट तीन महिनासम्म कायम रहन्छ।,"संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदाका सरकारी सेवामा कार्यरत कर्मचारीहरूलाई कानूनबमोजिम समायोजन गरेर, संसद्को पहिलो अधिवेशन बसेको मितिले एक वर्षपछि संविधानसँग बाझिएको कानून जति हदसम्म अमान्य हुन्छ।"",संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदाका सरकारी सेवामा कार्यरत कर्मचारीहरूलाई कानूनबमोजिम समायोजन गरेर, संसद्को पहिलो अधिवेशन बसेको मितिले एक वर्षपछि संविधानसँग बाझिएको कानून जति हदसम्म अमान्य हुन्छ।"",The Constitution provides a transitional period before inconsistent pre-existing laws automatically become invalid to the extent of their inconsistency."",""The term ‘अमान्य’ (invalid) means that the law becomes ineffective until it is repealed or amended by the legislature."",Article 304(1) establishes constitutional supremacy over inconsistent existing laws.,Art. 304(1),Existing laws to remain in force,,,,,,",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP012,English,"Before the expiry of an emergency declaration, for how long can a motion be submitted to extend the emergency period?",Another period not exceeding three months.,"Article 305 of the Constitution of Nepal grants the President the power to issue orders to remove difficulties in implementing the Constitution before the first session of the Federal Parliament. This allows for a limited time extension of the emergency period, up to a maximum of six months.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
EP012,Nepali,संकटकालको अवधि समाप्त हुनुअघि कति अवधिसम्म थप गर्न प्रस्ताव पेश गर्न सकिन्छ?,थप तीन महिनाभन्दा बढी नहुने अवधि।,"संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदा विद्यमान स्थानीय निकायहरू कति समयसम्म कायम रहन्छन्?,संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदा विद्यमान स्थानीय तहहरूको कार्यकाल सम्ममा कति समयसम्म कायम रहन्छन्?,Until the number and areas of the Local level are determined in accordance with the Constitution.,संविधानबमोजिम स्थानीय तहको संख्या र क्षेत्र निर्धारण नभएसम्म।,Article 303(1) ensures continuity of existing Local Bodies during the transition to the constitutional Local level structure."",""संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदाका सरकारी सेवामा कार्यरत कर्मचारीहरूलाई कानूनबमोजिम संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहमा समायोजन गरेर।"",कानूनबमोजिम।,Article 303(1),Provisions relating to Local Bodies,,,,,,
TP036,Transitional Provisions,Local Bodies,Factual,Easy,How are elections to officials of the existing Local Bodies conducted during the transitional period?,संक्रमणकालमा विद्यमान स्थानीय निकायका पदाधिकारीहरूको निर्वाचन कसरी गरिन्छ?,In accordance with law.,कानूनबमोजिम।,Article 303(2) provides that elections to officials of existing Local Bodies shall be held according to law."",""संविधानसँग बाझिएको विद्यमान कानूनहरूलाई भழுகுउन, स्थानीय तहका पदाधिकारीहरूको निर्वाचनको तरिका कसरी गरिन्छ?"",The election process is governed by the law.,Art. 303(2),Provisions relating to Local Bodies,,,,,,
TP037,Transitional Provisions,Local Bodies,Factual,Easy,How are elections to officials of the existing Local Bodies continued to exist until the new Local level elections take place?,संक्रमणकालमा विद्यमान स्थानीय निकायका पदाधिकारीहरूको निर्वाचन सम्ममा कति समयसम्म जारी रहन्छ?,Until elections to the Local level are held in accordance with the Constitution.,संविधानबमोजिम स्थानीय तहको निर्वाचन नभएसम्म।,Article 303(3) provides continuity for elected local officials until the new Local level elections take place."",""संविधानसँग बाझिएको विद्यमान स्थानीय तहका निर्वाचन नभएसम्म ती कानूनहरू कायम रहन्छन्।"",The Constitution provides a transitional period before election to the Local Level takes place.,Art. 303(3),Provisions relating to Local Bodies,,,,,,
TP038,Transitional Provisions,Local Bodies,Factual,Medium,Until when do officials elected to the existing Local Bodies continue to hold office?,संक्रमणकालमा विद्यमान स्थानीय निकायमा निर्वाचित पदाधिकारीहरू कहिलेसम्म पदमा कायम रहन्छन्?,Until elections to the Local level are held in accordance with the Constitution.,संविधानबमोजिम स्थानीय तहको निर्वाचन नभएसम्म।,Article 303(3) provides continuity for elected local officials until the new Local Level elections take place."",""संविधानसँग बाझिएको विद्यमान स्थानीय तहका निर्वाचित पदाधिकारीहरू कहिलेसम्म पदमा कायम रहन्छन्?"",The Constitution provides a transitional period before election to the Local level takes place.,Art. 303(3),Provisions relating to Local Bodies,,,,,,
TP039,Transitional Provisions,Existing Laws,Factual,Easy,What is the general rule regarding Nepalese laws in force when the Constitution commences?,संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदा प्रचलित नेपालका कानूनहरूबारे सामान्य व्यवस्था के हो?,They continue to remain in force until repealed or amended.,खारेज वा संशोधन नभएसम्म ती कानूनहरू कायम रहन्छन्।,Article 304(1) preserves existing laws to avoid a legal vacuum during constitutional transition."",""संविधानसँग बाझिएको विद्यमान कानुनहरूलाई अमान्य बनाउन, संवैधानिक परिवर्तनको समयमा एक कानूनी खाली स्थानको सामना गर्दैन।"",The Constitution provides a transitional period before inconsistent pre-existing laws automatically become invalid to the extent of their inconsistency."",Art. 304(1),Existing laws to remain in force,,,,,,
TP040,Transitional Provisions,Existing Laws,Factual,Medium,What happens to an existing law that is inconsistent with the Constitution after the specified transitional period?,संविधानसँग बाझिएको विद्यमान कानूनको तोकिएको संक्रमणकालीन अवधिपछि के हुन्छ?,It becomes invalid to the extent of its inconsistency.,धारा ३०४(१) अन्तर्गत विद्यमान कानुनहरूको अमान्यतालाई भழுகுउन।"""",Article 304(1),Existing laws to remain in force,,,,,,
TP041,Transitional Provisions,Existing Laws,Factual,Hard,After what event and period does the inconsistency rule for existing laws take effect under Article 304(1)?,धारा ३०४(१) अन्तर्गत विद्यमान कानुनहरूको असंगतिसम्बन्धी व्यवस्था कुन घटना र अवधिपछि लागू हुन्छ?,""After one year from the date on which the first session of the Federal Parliament is held, an inconsistent law becomes invalid to the extent of its inconsistency."",""संघीय संसद्को पहिलो अधिवेशन बसेको मितिले एक वर्षपछि संविधानसँग बाझिएको कानून जति हदसम्म बाझिन्छ, त्यति हदसम्म अमान्य हुन्छ।"",The Constitution provides a transitional period before inconsistent pre-existing laws automatically become invalid to the extent of their inconsistency.,Art. 304(1),Existing laws to remain in force,,,,,,
DF001,Definitions and Interpretations,Peace Process,Definition,Easy,Which groups are considered “minorities” under Article 306?,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “अल्पसंख्यक” भन्नाले कुन समूहलाई जनाउँछ?,""Minority is ethnic, linguistic, and religious groups whose population is below the percentage specified by Federal law, including groups with distinct ethnic, religious, or linguistic characteristics and aspirations to protect them that have been subjected to discrimination and oppression."",""संघीय कानूनले तोकेको प्रतिशतभन्दा कम जनसंख्या भएका जातीय, भाषिक र धार्मिक समूहहरूलाई जनाउँछ जसले भेदभावमा परेका हुन् तर बचाउन चाहन्छ भन्ने आकांक्षा राख्ने समूहहरू।"",The definition includes both population-based criteria and groups with distinct characteristics that have faced discrimination or oppression.,Art. 306(1)(a),Definitions and interpretations,,,,,,
DF002,Definitions and Interpretations,Law,Definition,Easy,What does the term “law” refer to under Article 306 of the Constitution?,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “कानून” भन्नाले के बुझिन्छ?,""“Law” means Federal law, State law, and Local law."",""“कानून” भन्नाले संघीय कानून, प्रदेश कानून र स्थानीय कानून जनाउँछ।"",The constitutional definition recognizes laws made at all three levels of the federal structure.,Art. 306(1)(b),Definitions and interpretations,,,,,,
DF003,Definitions and Interpretations,Article,Definition,Easy,What does the term “Article” refer to under Article 306?,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “धारा” भन्नाले के जनाउँछ?,""“Article” means an Article of the Constitution.,संविधानको कुनै धारा।,The term is specifically defined as a provision of the Constitution itself."",""संविधानको कुनै धारालाई लेख्ने शब्दको अर्थ हो।"",Art. 306(1)(c),Definitions and interpretations,,,,,,
DF004,Definitions and Interpretations,Municipality,Definition,Easy,What entities are included within the constitutional definition of “Municipality”?,संवैधानिक रूपमा “नगरपालिका” को परिभाषाभित्र कुन निकायहरू पर्छन्?,""“Municipalty” भन्नाले कसलाई जनाउँछ?"",A Municipality includes a Municipal Corporation and a Sub-municipal Corporation.,नगरपालिका भन्नाले महानगरपालिका र उपमहानगरपालिका समेत जनाउँछ।"",The definition gives “Municipality” a broader meaning by expressly including Municipal Corporations and Sub-municipal Corporations."",""संविधानसँग बाझिएको विद्यमान स्थानीय निकायहरूको परिभाषामा समावेशको नगरपालिका र उपनगरपालिका सहितका रूपमा, नगरपालिकाको अवधारणाको विस्तृत अर्थ हो।"",Article 306(1)(d),Definitions and interpretations,,,,,,
DF005,Definitions and Interpretations,Citizen,Definition,Easy,Who is considered a “citizen” under Article 306?,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “नागरिक” भन्नाले कसलाई जनाउँछ?,""A citizen means a citizen of Nepal.,“नागरिक” भन्नाले नेपालको नागरिकलाई जनाउँछ।"",The constitutional definition limits the term to a citizen of Nepal."",""संविधानसँग बाझिएको विद्यमानCitizen, नेपालका नागरिकलाई जनाउँछ।"",The constitutional definition gives “Citizen” a broader meaning by expressly including Municipal Corporations and Sub-municipal Corporations."",""Article 306(1)(e),Definitions and interpretations,,,,,,",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP013,English,What majority is required for the Federal Parliament to extend the period of a state of emergency?,At least two-thirds majority of the total number of then members of both Houses.,"Article 305 of the Constitution grants this power to the President, subject to recommendation from the Council of Ministers.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
EP013,Nepali,संकटकालको अवधि थप गर्न संघीय संसदमा कस्तो बहुमत आवश्यक हुन्छ?,तत्काल कायम रहेका दुवै सदनका कुल सदस्य संख्याको कम्तीमा दुई तिहाइ बहुमत।,"संविधान अनुसार, संघीय संसदमा एक समूहले बहुमत प्राप्त गर्नुपर्छ। संविधानले स्पष्ट रूपमा बताएको छ कि संघीय संसदमा बहुमत प्राप्त गर्नका लागि, कुनै पनि समूहले बहुमत प्राप्त गर्नुपर्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP014,English,"If the House of Representatives has been dissolved during an emergency, which body exercises the Federal Parliament’s emergency-related powers?",The National Assembly.,The Federal Parliament.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
EP014,Nepali,संकटकाल कायम रहेको अवस्थामा प्रतिनिधि सभा विघटन भए संघीय संसदको संकटकालसम्बन्धी अधिकार कसले प्रयोग गर्छ?,राष्ट्रिय सभा।,"संविधान २०६५ अनुसार, संसद् (Federal Parliament) प्रतिनिधि सभा विघटन गरेपछि संकटकाललाई समाप्त गर्नका लागि संघीय संसदले कति समयभरकर आउने अधिकार प्रयोग गर्दछ। संविधानको धारा ३०३(२) बमुறிয়া, संसद्ले प्रतिनिधित्वा कार्यालयमा रहे electors को कार्यकाल सकिए जाने पर उनको निर्वाचन पदहरू हटाउन पाउँछन्।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP015,English,What authority does the President have after declaring a state of emergency to address emergency situations?,The President may issue necessary orders to meet the exigencies.,Article 305 of the Constitution grants the President the power to issue orders to remove difficulties in implementing the Constitution before the first session of the Federal Parliament. This is done subject to legislative approval through subsequent review and consideration by the Legislature-Parliament.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP015,Nepali,संकटकाल घोषणा भएपछि आपतकालीन अवस्था समाधान गर्न राष्ट्रपतिसँग कस्तो अधिकार हुन्छ?,राष्ट्रपतिले आवश्यक आदेश जारी गर्न सक्छन्।,"संविधान अनुसार, राष्ट्रपतिले संकटकाल घोषणा गरे पश्चात्, तत्कालकालीन सरकारलाई आपतकालीन व्यवस्थापनमा समस्याहरू समाधान गर्न पर्याप्त अधिकार दिन्छ। यसको मुख्य तरिका हो कि राष्ट्रपतिले सरकारी निर्णयहरूको कार्यान्वयनमा आएका अवरोधहरू हटाउन र जनताको सुरक्षा सुनिश्चित गर्न आवश्यक措置 बुदबुदाए।

यहाँ विस्तृत विवरण दिए गए:

*   **आज्ञा:** संविधानले राष्ट्रपतिलाई संकटकाल घोषणा गरे पश्चात्, सरकारलाई तत्कालकालीन व्यवस्थापनमा समस्या समाधान गर्न पर्याप्त अधिकार दिन्छ।
*   **सुरुचिपूर्ण उपायय:** राष्ट्रपतिले संकटकालको समयमा आएका समस्याहरू समाधान गर्न आवश्यक措置 बुदबुदाए।
*   **अधिकार प्रयोग:** राष्ट्रपतिले संविधान अनुसार, संकटकाल घोषणा गरे पश्चात् सरकारलाई तत्कालकालीन व्यवस्थापनमा समस्या समाधान गर्न पर्याप्त अधिकार दिन्छ।

संक्षेप में कहें तो, राष्ट्रपति संकटकाल घोषणा भएपछि आपतकालीन अवस्था समाधान गर्न सक्षम हुन्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP016,English,"During a state of emergency, what is the legal status of orders issued by the President under Article 273(9)?",They apply as law while the state of emergency is in operation.,"Article 273(9) of the Constitution outlines the powers of the President during a State of Emergency. It states that the President has the power to issue orders, decrees, and directives necessary for maintaining public order and security, including the implementation of laws and regulations.

Therefore, during a state of emergency, the President can issue orders to:

*   **Suspend existing laws:** This allows for temporary changes in law to address urgent situations.
*   **Implement policies:** The President can enact policies that are necessary to maintain stability and security.
*   **Direct actions:**  The President can take direct action to protect citizens and ensure public safety.

However, these orders must be consistent with the Constitution and other laws. They also require a legal basis for their issuance.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP016,Nepali,धारा २७३(९) अनुसार राष्ट्रपतिले जारी गरेका आदेशहरूको कानुनी स्थिति के हुन्छ?,संकटकाल कायम रहँदासम्म ती आदेश कानुनसरह लागू हुन्छन्।,धारा २७३(९) अनुसार राष्ट्रपतिले जारी गरेका आदेशहरूलाई कमजोर बनाउनु र हटाउनु पर्छ। यसको कारण यो छ कि संविधानमा स्थानीय सरकारका कार्यहरूको व्यवस्था गर्नका लागि एक स्पष्ट तरिका प्रदान गरिएको है।,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP017,English,Which category of rights may be suspended during a state of emergency?,"Fundamental rights provided in Part-3, subject to constitutional exceptions.","Article 306, Definitions and Interpretations,Citizen,Easy,A citizen means a citizen of Nepal.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
EP017,Nepali,संकटकालको समयमा कुन प्रकारका अधिकार निलम्बन गर्न सकिन्छ?,"भाग–३ मा प्रदान गरिएका मौलिक हकहरू, संविधानमा तोकिएका अपवाद बाहेक।","संविधान अनुसार, संकटकालको समयमा सरकारले निम्न प्रकारका अधिकार निलम्हन गर्न सक्नेछन्:

*   **संसद्वास्तवकहरूको अधिकार:** संविधानलाई रद्द गरे पनि, संसद्वास्तवकहरूले आफ्नो अधिकार राख्न पाउँलान।
*   **स्थानीय तहका अधिकार:** स्थानीय तहको व्यवस्था बनाएर काम जारीमा रोक लगाउन सकिन्छ।
*   **आगतिक अधिकार:** संविधानलाई रद्द भएपछि आगतिक अधिकारहरूलाई सुरक्षित保संरक्षित गर्न सकिन्छ।
*   **संसद्वास्तवकहरूको अधिकार:** संविधानलाई रद्द गरे पनि, संसद्वास्तवकहरूले आफ्नो अधिकार राख्न पाउँलान।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP018,English,Are all fundamental rights suspended during a state of emergency?,"No, specified rights and remedies cannot be suspended.","No, fundamental rights are not suspended during a state of emergency according to Nepali law. The Constitution guarantees certain fundamental rights even in times of crisis. However, the government has the power to impose restrictions on these rights under specific circumstances outlined in Article 302(2) of the Constitution. These restrictions are limited and must be proportionate to the need for security or public order.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP018,Nepali,के संकटकालमा सबै मौलिक हकहरू निलम्बन हुन्छन्?,"होइन, तोकिएका मौलिक हक र उपचारका अधिकार निलम्बन गर्न सकिँदैन।",संक्रमणकालमा सबै मौलिक हकहरू निलम्बन हुन्छन्।,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP019,English,Which constitutional remedy specifically remains protected and cannot be suspended during an emergency?,The remedy of habeas corpus.,Article 304(1) of the Constitution preserves existing laws to avoid a legal vacuum during constitutional transition.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP019,Nepali,संकटकालमा कुन संवैधानिक उपचारको अधिकार निलम्बन गर्न सकिँदैन?,बन्दी प्रत्यक्षीकरणको उपचार।,"संविधानलेCitizenलाईCitizen of Nepal बनाउनबाट, Citizen को अधिकार निलम्बन गर्न सकिँदैन।",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
EP020,English,Can a petition be filed in court to enforce a suspended fundamental right during an emergency?,"No, no petition may lie for enforcement of that suspended right.","Yes, a petition can be filed in court to enforce a suspended fundamental right during an emergency under Article 305 of the Constitution.

Here's why and how it works:

* **Article 305:** This article grants the President the power to suspend laws and other measures that are deemed necessary to maintain public order, stability, and security during a state of exigency (emergency).
* **Petition as Enforcement Mechanism:**  A petition can be filed in court seeking an injunction or relief under Article 305. The petitioner argues that the suspended law is inconsistent with fundamental rights and must be reinstated.

**How it works practically:**

1. **Emergency Situation:** Nepal often faces emergency situations (e.g., natural disasters, political instability) where the government needs to temporarily suspend laws.
2. **Petition Filed:**  A citizen or group can file a petition in court requesting the Court of Justice to review and potentially reinstate the suspended law.
3. **Court Review:** The Court of Justice will examine whether the suspension is justified under Article 305. They'll consider factors like:
   - Whether the suspension is necessary for public order.
   - Whether it’s proportionate to the threat.
4. **Injunction/Restraining Order:** If the court finds that the suspension violates fundamental rights, it can issue an injunction or restraining order compelling the government to reinstate the law.

**Important Note:**  The Court of Justice's role is primarily focused on ensuring constitutional compliance and protecting fundamental rights during emergencies. It doesn’t typically involve a full-blown legal battle like in a regular court case.


Do you want me to elaborate on any specific aspect, such as:

*   Specific types of petitions that can be filed?
*   The process of the Court of Justice reviewing a petition?",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP020,Nepali,संकटकालमा निलम्बित मौलिक हक कार्यान्वयनका लागि अदालतमा निवेदन दिन सकिन्छ?,"सकिँदैन, त्यस्तो निलम्बित हक कार्यान्वयनका लागि निवेदन लाग्दैन।","संक्रमणकालमा निलम्बित मौलिक हक्क कार्यान्वयनका लागि अदालतमा निवेदन दिन सकिन्छ।

यहाँ पर, नेपाल सरकारले निलम्बित मौलिक हक्कानुसारको आदेशलाई लागू गर्न अमेज्ड (vindicated) र अनुपालना गर्नुपर्ने हुन्छ। यसको कारण हो कि निलम्बित हक्कलाई हटाउनुअतिरिक्त, त्यसको कार्यान्वयनका लागि अदालतमा निवेदन दिन सकिन्छ।

यहाँ पर, नेपाल सरकारले निलम्बित मौलिक हक्कको आदेशलाई लागू गर्न अमेज्ड (vindicated) र अनुपालना गर्नुपर्ने हुन्छ। यसको कारण हो कि निलम्बित हक्कलाई हटाउनुअतिरिक्त, त्यसको कार्यान्वयनका लागि अदालतमा निवेदन दिन सकिन्छ।

संविधान अनुसार, निलम्बित मौलिक हक्कको आदेशलाई कार्यान्वयनका लागि अदालतमा निवेदन दिन सकिन्छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
EP021,English,"If a person suffers injury due to an official’s bad faith action during emergency, within what period may compensation be claimed after termination of the emergency?",Within three months from the date of termination.,"Article 306(2) of the Constitution states that “in case of injury caused by the wrongful act of any public officer, the injured party shall have the right to claim compensation within a period of six months from the date of the injury.”",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP021,Nepali,संकटकालमा अधिकारीको बदनियतपूर्ण कार्यबाट क्षति भएमा संकटकाल समाप्त भएपछि कति अवधिभित्र क्षतिपूर्तिको माग गर्न सकिन्छ?,समाप्त भएको मितिले तीन महिनाभित्र।,"संक्रमणकालका बीच, आधिकारिकको बाटोको कारणले आएको क्षतिलाई बुझाउन पर्याप्त समयभरन्न योजनले, क्षतिपूर्तिको माद थप गर्न सकिन्छ।

Explanation:
Article 304(1) of the Constitution states that if a person is injured due to the official's actions during the transition period, they can file a claim for compensation within six months from the date of injury. This provision allows for a reasonable time frame to mitigate the damage caused by the official’s negligence.

Therefore, the answer is: **Six months**.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP022,English,Who may order compensation or punishment when a valid petition is filed for injury caused during an emergency?,The court.,"Article 305,Powers and Responsibilities of the President, Section 305 grants the President the power to issue orders to remove difficulties in implementing the Constitution before the first session of the Federal Parliament. This allows them to address urgent situations that may arise during the transition period.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP022,Nepali,संकटकालको समयमा भएको क्षतिका लागि निवेदन परेमा क्षतिपूर्ति वा सजायको आदेश कसले दिन सक्छ?,अदालतले।,"संविधान अनुसार, सरकारले संकटकालको समयमा भएको क्षतिका लागि निवेदन परेमा क्षतिपूर्ति वा सजायको आदेश दिन्छ। यसलाई ‘आँट्यासन’ (Allocation) भनिएको छ।

यहाँ तरिकाexplained गरिएको विवरण दिएकीं:

*   **आँट्यासन:** संविधानले सरकारलाई संकटकालको समयमा भएको क्षतिका लागि निवेदन परेमा क्षतिपूर्ति वा सजायको आदेश दिन्छ।
*   **संसद्पूर्ण व्यवस्था:** यसले देशको सन्देशिक व्यवस्था बनाएर राख्ने तरละ पर आधारित छ, जसले न्यायको उचित व्यवस्था सुनिश्चित गर्छ।
*   **सरकारी दायित्व:** सरकारले क्षतिका लागि निवेदन परेमा क्षतिपूर्ति वा सजायको आदेश दिन्छ, र यो आदेश सरकारको कर्तव्य हो।

संविधान अनुसार, सरकारले क्षतिका लागि निवेदन परेमा क्षतिपूर्ति वा सजायको आदेश दिन्छ।",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
EP023,English,Who may withdraw a declaration or order of a state of emergency?,The President.,Article 305 of the Constitution grants the President the power to withdraw a declaration or order of a state of emergency.,Correct,Not a strict error,False
EP023,Nepali,संकटकाल घोषणा वा आदेश फिर्ता गर्ने अधिकार कसलाई हुन्छ?,राष्ट्रपति।,"संविधान अनुसार, संकटकाल घोषणा या आदेश फिर्ता गर्ने अधिकार राष्ट्रपतिमा रहेको छ। संविधानले राष्ट्रपतिलाई यसको अधिकार दिन्छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
EP024,English,What is the difference between approval of an emergency declaration and extension of an emergency period?,"Approval requires two-thirds majority after issuance, while extension requires a separate two-thirds majority motion before expiry.","According to Article 305, the President can issue orders to remove difficulties under Article 305. However, this power is temporary and subject to legislative oversight through subsequent approval. Therefore, the difference between issuing an emergency declaration and extending an emergency period lies in the **duration and scope of the authority granted by the Constitution.**

Here’s a breakdown:

*   **Emergency Declaration:** This gives the President broad powers to address urgent situations requiring immediate action. It's a temporary measure with defined limits.
*   **Extension of Emergency Period:**  This extends the existing emergency period, but it is still subject to legislative approval and doesn’t grant unlimited authority. The Constitution provides for this extension through subsequent legislation.

Essentially, Article 305 allows the President to *extend* an emergency, while the constitutional framework establishes a process for *reviewing* and potentially modifying that extension.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
EP024,Nepali,संकटकाल घोषणा अनुमोदन र संकटकाल अवधि थप गर्ने प्रक्रियाबीच के फरक छ?,घोषणा अनुमोदनका लागि जारी भएपछि दुई तिहाइ बहुमत आवश्यक हुन्छ भने अवधि थपका लागि समाप्त हुनुअघि छुट्टै दुई तिहाइ बहुमतको प्रस्ताव आवश्यक हुन्छ।,"संकटकाल घोषणा स्वीकृतीकरण र संकटकालको समयसीमामा प्रक्रिया बीचको मुख्य अन्तर तद्よそ, तर पनि दोसलाई धेरै महत्वपूर्ण अन्तर छ। यहाँ बुझाइयाँ दिइएका छन्:

*   **संकटकाल घोषणा:** संकटकाल घोषणा स्वीकृतीकरणको लागि बनाए गए आधिकारिक घोषणा हो। यसले सरकारलाई संकटकालको अवधि सुरू भएको घोषणा गर्छ र त्यसको नियमनमा जान্বित्छ।
*   **संकटकाल अवधि थपванеली प्रक्रिया:** यह प्रक्रिया संकटकाल घोषणा स्वीकृतीकरणपछि सुरु हुन्छ। यसमा, सरकारले संकटकालको समयसीमा मापन गर्नुपर्ने व्यवस्था छ।

संक्षेप में कहें तो, संकटकाल घोषणा एक आधिकारिक घोषणा हो तर संकटकालको समयसीमा थप्नका लागि जान্বित्ने प्रक्रिया हो।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
EP025,English,Arrange the correct constitutional sequence after a state of emergency is declared by the President.,Declaration → submission to both Houses within one month → approval by two-thirds majority → continuation for specified period.,"Here’s the order of events following a State of Emergency declaration, based on the provided text:

1.  **President declares the State of Emergency:** This initiates the process.
2.  **Government of Nepal arranges for service delivery at the State and Local levels during the transition.** (This is a key action)
3.  **Election to officials of existing Local Bodies are held according to law.** (Ensuring continuity of local governance)
4. **Until elections to the Local level are held in accordance with the Constitution.** (Ensuring the election process aligns with constitutional requirements.)
5. **The President, on the recommendation of the Government of Nepal, Council of Ministers.** (This is a crucial step for implementation)

**Important Note:** The text doesn't explicitly state *when* this sequence begins. It simply describes the actions taken *after* the declaration.",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
EP025,Nepali,राष्ट्रपतिले संकटकाल घोषणा गरेपछि संविधानअनुसार सही प्रक्रिया क्रम मिलाउनुहोस्।,घोषणा → एक महिनाभित्र दुवै सदनमा पेश → दुई तिहाइ बहुमतबाट अनुमोदन → तोकिएको अवधिसम्म कायम।,"संविधानको धारा ३०४(१) अनुसार, राष्ट्रपती संघ, स्थानीय तह र संघीय स्तरमा सेवा प्रवाहलाई व्यवस्थापन गर्नका लागि आवश्यक कदम उठाउनेछ। यसको मतलब, सरकारी सेवाहरूले अवस्था परिवर्तन हुँदादेखिसम्म सही रूपमा चलाइयदै गらが छ भने, उनलाई कानून अनुसार समायोजन गरिनेछन्।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CA001,English,What limitation does the Constitution impose on the amendment of the Constitution?,"An amendment must not prejudice sovereignty, territorial integrity, independence of Nepal, or sovereignty vested in the people.",Article 304 of the Constitution states that “the Constitution shall not be amended except by a constitutional assembly convened in accordance with law.”,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
CA001,Nepali,संविधान संशोधन गर्दा संविधानले कुन सीमाना तोकेको छ?,"संशोधनले नेपालको सार्वभौमसत्ता, भौगोलिक अखण्डता, स्वतन्त्रता वा जनतामा निहित सार्वभौमसत्तामा प्रतिकूल असर पार्नु हुँदैन।","Article 304 of the Constitution of Nepal states that the constitution is subject to amendment, but it does not specify a specific limit or boundary within which amendments can be made. It emphasizes that amendments should be done in accordance with the principles of good governance and transparency.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
CA002,English,Can the Constitution be amended in a manner that affects the sovereignty vested in the people?,No.,"Yes, Article 304 of the Constitution allows for amendments to affect the sovereignty vested in the people. It states that “the Constitution may be amended by Parliament or the Federal Council, subject to the requirements of law.” This means that while the Constitution itself is supreme, it can be modified through legislative processes, provided they adhere to legal procedures and principles.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
CA002,Nepali,के जनतामा निहित सार्वभौमसत्तामा असर पर्ने गरी संविधान संशोधन गर्न सकिन्छ?,सकिँदैन।,"संविधान संशोधन गर्न सकिन्छ, तर यसको प्रक्रिया धेरै जटिल छ। यहाँ पर लेख दिइएका बुलेट मास्टरहरूले बताउँछन् कि जनतामा निहित सार्वभौमसत्ता (Constitutional Sovereignty) वरिनिने गरी संविधान संशोधन गर्न सकिन्छ:

*   **संसद् वा संघीय संसद्समक्षको निर्णय:** संविधान संशोधनलाई सम्बक्न, સંસद्को सदस्यहरूको सहमति आवश्यक छ। संसद्ले यसका लागि निर्णय दिनेछन्।
*   **संविधानमा परिवर्तनको आवश्यकता:** यदि संविधानमा कुनै महत्त्वपूर्ण परिवर्तन हुन्छ भने, ससंद् भोलकानी निर्णय गरेर संशोधन गर्न सकिन्छ।
*   **संसद् वा संघीय संसद्समक्षको आदेश:** संसद्ले संशोधनका लागि आवश्यक आदेश दिनेछन्।

त्यसैले, जनतामा निहित सार्वभौमसत्तालाई ध्यानपूर्वक जाँचेर, संविधानमा परिवर्तनहरू ल्याएर त्यसको अर्थ र प्रभावलाई सुरक्षित保 जाय सकिन्छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
CA003,English,Which body may introduce a bill to amend or repeal any Article of the Constitution?,Either House of the Federal Parliament.,Article 305,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
CA003,Nepali,संविधानको कुनै धारा संशोधन वा खारेज गर्ने विधेयक कुन निकायमा पेश गर्न सकिन्छ?,संघीय संसदको कुनै पनि सदनमा।,Article 305 of the Constitution grants this power to the Legislature-Parliament.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
CA004,English,Which clause of Article 274 itself cannot be amended?,Clause (1).,"Article 274, “Powers and Duties of the Government,” allows for amendments to the Constitution. It does not explicitly state that it can only be amended by the Federal Parliament. Therefore, it is impossible to amend this article.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
CA004,Nepali,धारा २७४ को कुन उपधारा आफैं संशोधन गर्न सकिँदैन?,उपधारा (१)।,"धारा २७४ का उपधारा जो संशोधन न हो सके, ती ३०३ (२) मा थली गई है।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CA005,English,What type of legislative proposal may be introduced under Article 274(2)?,A bill to amend or repeal any Article of the Constitution.,Article 274(2) allows the government to introduce new legislation that addresses issues not covered by existing laws. It’s a mechanism for adapting legal frameworks to evolving societal needs and challenges.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CA005,Nepali,धारा २७४(२) अनुसार कस्तो विधेयक पेश गर्न सकिन्छ?,संविधानको कुनै पनि धारा संशोधन वा खारेज गर्ने विधेयक।,"धारा २७४(२) अनुसार, सरकारले निम्न प्रकारका विधेयक पेश गर्न सक्नेछ:

*   **बदलावको विधेयक:** संविधानमा परिवर्तन ल्याउने तरत बुझाउनुको लागि।
*   **नयाँ विधेयक:** नयाँ कानून जोर्नुको लिएर।
*   **अंतिम विधेयक:** एक नयाँ कानून बनाउनुको लिएर।
*   **संसद्वाचक विधेयक:** सட்டம் enactedकाले आझानванеमा आएको तरत बुझाउनुको लिएर।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CA006,English,Within how many days must an introduced constitutional amendment bill be publicly published for information?,Within thirty days of introduction.,Article 304 of the Constitution of Nepal states that “an introduced constitutional amendment bill shall be publicly published within thirty (30) days after its introduction.”,Correct,Not a strict error,False
CA006,Nepali,पेश गरिएको संविधान संशोधन विधेयक सार्वजनिक जानकारीका लागि कति दिनभित्र प्रकाशित गर्नुपर्छ?,पेश भएको तीस दिनभित्र।,"Article 304 of the Constitution states that a law must be published within 30 days of its enactment. Therefore, the government should publish the proposed constitution amendment bill within 30 days of its enactment.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
CA007,English,What is the purpose of publishing an amendment bill within thirty days?,To provide information to the general public.,The text doesn’t explicitly state the *purpose* of publishing an amendment bill within thirty days. It simply describes that it's a requirement under Article 304 of the Constitution to allow for amendments to the constitution. The purpose is to ensure continuity and stability in the legal framework during the transition period.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
CA007,Nepali,संविधान संशोधन विधेयक तीस दिनभित्र प्रकाशित गर्नुको उद्देश्य के हो?,सर्वसाधारण जनतालाई जानकारी दिनु।,"संविधान संशोधन विधेयक तीस दिनभित्र प्रकाशन गर्न गरिएको मुख्यobjectifले संविधानलाई अद्यतन गराउनुको लागि छ। यसमा, सरकारले संविधानमा परिवर्तनहरू समावेश गर्ने प्रस्तावलाई सार्वजनिक गरेर, जनतालाई अपडेट दिन्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CA008,English,When must an amendment bill be sent to the State Assembly for consent?,When it relates to alteration of State borders or matters in Schedule-6.,Article 304 of the Constitution of Nepal states that any amendment bill submitted to the State Assembly must be sent for consent before it can become law.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
CA008,Nepali,कुन अवस्थामा संविधान संशोधन विधेयक प्रदेश सभाको सहमतिका लागि पठाउनुपर्छ?,प्रदेशको सीमाना परिवर्तन वा अनुसूची–६ का विषयसँग सम्बन्धित भएमा।,"संविधान संशोधन विधेयक प्रदेश सभाको सहमतिका लागि पठाउनुपर्छ, जब तक कि संघीय संसद्समक्षले (Federal Parliament) यसलाई स्वीकृत नगराउँदैन।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CA009,English,Who sends an amendment bill to the State Assembly for consent?,The Speaker or Chairperson of the concerned House.,"Article 305 of the Constitution grants the President the power to issue orders to remove difficulties in implementing the Constitution before the first session of the Federal Parliament. Therefore, the President is responsible for sending amendments bills to the State Assembly for consent.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
CA009,Nepali,संविधान संशोधन विधेयक प्रदेश सभाको सहमतिका लागि कसले पठाउँछ?,सम्बन्धित सदनका सभामुख वा अध्यक्षले।,"Article 302(2) permits employee adjustment among the three levels of government to support service delivery. Therefore, the Government of Nepal may request a vote on a proposed constitutional amendment bill from the Local Bodies.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
CA010,English,Within how many days after introduction in the Federal Parliament must a relevant amendment bill be sent to the State Assembly?,Within thirty days after its introduction.,"Article 305, Power to remove difficulties, Grants this temporary power to the President, subject to a recommendation from the Council of Ministers. It states that an order issued to remove difficulties under Article 305 must be submitted for approval to the Legislature-Parliament or Federal Parliament that is held immediately after the order is issued.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
CA010,Nepali,सम्बन्धित संविधान संशोधन विधेयक संघीय संसदमा पेश भएपछि कति दिनभित्र प्रदेश सभामा पठाउनुपर्छ?,पेश भएको तीस दिनभित्र।,"Article 305 of the Constitution states that the President shall submit the related constitution amendment bill to the Legislature-Parliament immediately after it is presented. Therefore, it must be sent to the Federal Parliament within 7 days of its presentation.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
CA011,English,What majority is required for a State Assembly to accept or reject an amendment bill sent for consent?,Majority of the total number of its then members.,Article 305 of the Constitution of Nepal states that “the majority of the members of the State Assembly shall be sufficient to approve or reject an amendment bill.”,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CA011,Nepali,सहमतिका लागि पठाइएको संशोधन विधेयक स्वीकार वा अस्वीकार गर्न प्रदेश सभामा कस्तो बहुमत आवश्यक हुन्छ?,तत्काल कायम रहेका कुल सदस्य संख्याको बहुमत।,"संविधानको धारा ३०६(२) अनुसार, प्रदेश सभाले संशोधन विधेयकलाई सहमथ्य (affirmative) या अस्वीकार (negative) गर्न आवश्यक बहुमत ७५% हो।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CA012,English,Within what period must the State Assembly provide information about acceptance or rejection of an amendment bill?,Within three months.,Article 305 of the Constitution states that the State Assembly must provide information regarding the acceptance or rejection of amendments to the constitution within **three months** after the bill is presented.,Correct,Not a strict error,False
CA012,Nepali,प्रदेश सभाले संशोधन विधेयक स्वीकार वा अस्वीकार गरेको जानकारी कति अवधिभित्र दिनुपर्छ?,तीन महिनाभित्र।,"संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदाका सरकारी सेवामा कार्यरत कर्मचारीहरूलाई कानूनबमोजिम संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहमा समायोजन गरेर,प्रदेश सभाले संशोधन विधेयक स्वीकार वा अस्वीकार गरेको जानकारी पाँच वर्ष बीचमा दिनुपर्छ।"",""संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदाका सरकारी सेवामा कार्यरत कर्मचारीहरूलाई कानूनबमोजिम संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहमा समायोजन गरेर,प्रदेश सभाले संशोधन विधेयक स्वीकार वा अस्वीकार गरेको जानकारी पाँच वर्ष बीचमा दिनुपर्छ।""",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CA013,English,What happens if a State Assembly does not provide information of acceptance or rejection of an amendment bill within the prescribed period?,The Federal Parliament may proceed with the bill.,"Article 305 of the Constitution of Nepal states that the President, on the recommendation of the Government of Nepal, Council of Ministers, shall notify the Legislature-Parliament of acceptance or rejection of an amendment bill within a specified period. If the State Assembly does not provide information of acceptance or rejection of an amendment bill within this prescribed period, it is considered invalid.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CA013,Nepali,तोकिएको अवधिभित्र प्रदेश सभाले संशोधन विधेयक स्वीकार वा अस्वीकार गरेको जानकारी नदिएमा के हुन्छ?,संघीय संसदले विधेयकमाथि प्रक्रिया अगाडि बढाउन सक्छ।,"संविधानको धारा ३०६(१) अनुसार,प्रदेश सभाले संशोधन विधेयक स्वीकृति वा अस्वीकार गर्न सक्ने तर धेरै वर्ष आएपछि हो भने, त्यसलाई स्वीकार वा अस्वीकार गर्नु पर्दा।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CA014,English,What is the consequence if a State Assembly rejects an amendment bill by majority and informs the Federal Parliament within the required period?,The bill becomes inoperative.,"If a State Assembly rejects an amendment bill by majority, it informs the Federal Parliament within the required period. The Constitution provides for this process to ensure constitutional supremacy.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CA014,Nepali,प्रदेश सभाले बहुमतबाट संशोधन विधेयक अस्वीकार गरी समयभित्र संघीय संसदलाई जानकारी दिएमा के हुन्छ?,विधेयक निष्क्रिय हुन्छ।,"संविधानको धारा ३०६(२) अनुसार, यदि प्रदेश सभा द्वारा एक संशोधन विधेयकमा बहुमतबाट अस्वीકાર गरे तर संघीय संसदलाई जानकारी दिन्छ। यसको अर्थ यो छ कि संघीय संसदले सरकारलाई सूचित गर्दाैँ विधेयकमा परिवर्तन नहोर्न पाए । संविधानले स्पष्ट रूपত बताएकोछाई, संघीय संसदलाई सूचना दिएपछि鏨 विधेयकमा परिवर्तन गर्न पाउँगा र त्यससम्मर रद्द हुन्छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
CA015,English,What majority is required to pass an amendment bill that does not require State Assembly consent?,At least two-thirds majority of the total number of then members of both Houses of the Federal Parliament.,"Article 304(2) of the Constitution states, “The provisions of this Constitution shall be amended by a simple majority in Parliament.” Therefore, a majority of five votes (50%) is required to pass an amendment bill that does not require State Assembly consent.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
CA015,Nepali,प्रदेश सभाको सहमति आवश्यक नपर्ने संशोधन विधेयक पारित गर्न कस्तो बहुमत आवश्यक हुन्छ?,संघीय संसदका दुवै सदनका तत्काल कायम रहेका कुल सदस्य संख्याको कम्तीमा दुई तिहाइ बहुमत।,"प्रदेश सभाको सहमति आवश्यक नपर्ने संशोधन विधेयक पारित गर्न, प्रदेश सभाको बहुमतले आवश्यक हुन्छ।",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
CA016,English,What majority is required to pass an amendment bill that has been accepted by a majority of the State Assembly?,At least two-thirds majority of the total number of then members of both Houses of the Federal Parliament.,"Article 305 of the Constitution of Nepal, 2024, states that an amendment bill must be passed by a majority of the State Assembly.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
CA016,Nepali,प्रदेश सभाको बहुमतबाट स्वीकार गरिएको संशोधन विधेयक पारित गर्न संघीय संसदमा कस्तो बहुमत आवश्यक हुन्छ?,संघीय संसदका दुवै सदनका तत्काल कायम रहेका कुल सदस्य संख्याको कम्तीमा दुई तिहाइ बहुमत।,प्रदेश सभाको बहुमतबाट स्वीकार गरिएको संशोधन विधेयक पारित गर्न संघीय संसदमा ३/५ बहुमत आवश्यक हुन्छ।,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CA017,English,Which amendment bills require State Assembly consent before being passed by the Federal Parliament?,Bills related to State border alteration or matters in Schedule-6.,Article 302(2) permits employee adjustment among the three levels of government to support service delivery. This means that amendments requiring state assembly consent are handled through this process.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
CA017,Nepali,कुन संविधान संशोधन विधेयकलाई संघीय संसदबाट पारित गर्नुअघि प्रदेश सभाको सहमति आवश्यक हुन्छ?,प्रदेशको सीमाना परिवर्तन वा अनुसूची–६ का विषयसँग सम्बन्धित विधेयक।,"संविधान संशोधन विधेयकलाई संघीय संसदबाट पारित गर्दा, प्रदेश सभाको सहमति आवश्यक हुन्छ। Article 305(1) मध्येले यो स्पष्ट रूपमा बताइएको छ कि संविधान संशोधन विधेयकलाई संघीय संसदबाट पारित गर्न, प्रदेश सभाको सहमतिRequired ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CA018,English,"If a State Assembly rejects an amendment bill, can the Federal Parliament continue processing that bill?","No, the bill becomes inoperative.","Yes, the Federal Parliament can continue processing the amendment bill even if it is rejected by the State Assembly. The Constitution provides for this continuity under Article 305.  The Federal Parliament has the power to review and potentially amend a bill passed by the State Legislature, but it retains the authority to override the State Assembly's rejection through its own process.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CA018,Nepali,प्रदेश सभाले संशोधन विधेयक अस्वीकार गरेपछि संघीय संसदले सो विधेयकमाथि प्रक्रिया जारी राख्न सक्छ?,"सक्दैन, विधेयक निष्क्रिय हुन्छ।","संविधानको धारा ३०३(२) बमोजकि प्रावधान अनुसार, यदि संघीय संसद प्रदेश सभाबाट स्वीकृत गरिएको संशोधन विधेयकलाई अस्वीकार गर्छन् भने, वेष्टना सरकारले त्यस विधेयकमाथि प्रक्रिया जारी गर्न सक्ने हो। यसको अर्थ यो हुन्छ कि वेष्टना सरकारले प्रदेश सभालाई हटाएका हुनाले उनको कार्य चलाउन पाउँदा, उनले तसर्थ विधेयकमा परिवर्तनहरू ल्याउने अधिकार राख्न सक्छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
CA019,English,To whom is a constitutional amendment bill passed under Article 274(8) presented for assent?,The President.,"According to Article 274(8) of the Constitution, a constitutional amendment bill is presented for assent to the Parliament, the House of Representatives, and the Federal Council.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CA019,Nepali,धारा २७४(८) अनुसार पारित संशोधन विधेयक स्वीकृतिका लागि कससमक्ष पेश गरिन्छ?,राष्ट्रपति।,"धारा २७४(८) अनुसार,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “कानून” भन्नाले कुन पेश गरिनेछ?,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “कानून” भन्नाले कुन पेश गरिनेछ?,The bill must be submitted to the Legislature-Parliament for approval before it can become law."",""बिललाई संसद र संघीय संसदसमक्षमा अनुमति दिएर कानून बनाइइसकेपछि मात्र देखाउन सकिन्छ।"",The legislative process ensures that laws are enacted according to constitutional principles and legal requirements.,Art. 306(1)(a),Definitions and interpretations,,,,,,",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
CA020,English,Within how many days must the President give assent to a constitutional amendment bill after receiving it?,Within fifteen days.,Article 305 of the Constitution grants the President the power to issue orders to remove difficulties in implementing the Constitution before the first session of the Federal Parliament. This power is temporary and subject to legislative oversight through subsequent approval. The President must give assent within a period of **three days** after receiving the bill.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CA020,Nepali,संविधान संशोधन विधेयक प्राप्त भएपछि राष्ट्रपतिले कति दिनभित्र स्वीकृति दिनुपर्छ?,पन्ध्र दिनभित्र।,Article 305 of the Constitution states that the President shall give their consent to a bill for constitutional amendment within **three days** of receiving it.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
CA021,English,From which date does the Constitution become amended after an amendment bill receives presidential assent?,From the date of assent.,"After one year from the date on which the first session of the Federal Parliament is held, an inconsistent law becomes invalid to the extent of its inconsistency.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
CA021,Nepali,संशोधन विधेयकमा राष्ट्रपतिको स्वीकृति पाएपछि संविधान कुन मितिबाट संशोधन भएको मानिन्छ?,स्वीकृति दिएको मितिबाट।,"संशोधन विधेयकमा राष्ट्रपतिको स्वीकृति पाएपछि संविधान, २०६३ मा २५ месеन्ths बाद संशोधन भएको मानिन्छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
CA022,English,What is the correct sequence for an amendment bill requiring State Assembly consent?,Introduction in Federal Parliament → publication within thirty days → State Assembly consent process → two-thirds approval by both Houses → President’s assent.,"The correct order for an amendment bill requiring State Assembly consent is as follows:

1.  **Drafting:** The amendment bill must be drafted by the government.
2.  **Submission to the State Assembly:** It needs to be submitted to the State Assembly for review and approval.
3.  **State Assembly Debate & Vote:** The State Assembly will debate and vote on the amendment.
4.  **Legislative Approval:** If approved, the amendment passes through the legislative process.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
CA022,Nepali,प्रदेश सभाको सहमति आवश्यक पर्ने संशोधन विधेयकको सही प्रक्रिया क्रम के हो?,संघीय संसदमा पेश → तीस दिनभित्र प्रकाशन → प्रदेश सभाको सहमति प्रक्रिया → दुवै सदनको दुई तिहाइ स्वीकृति → राष्ट्रपतिको स्वीकृति।,"प्रदेश सभाको सहमति आवश्यक पर्ने संशोधन विधेयकको सही प्रक्रिया क्रम निम्न हुन्थ्यो:

1.  **प्रदेश सभामा सहमति:** पहली चरण प्रदेश सभामा संशोधन विधेयकलाई छानन्ने र सहमति तोडनेछ।
2.  **प्रदेश सभाको निर्णय:** यदि प्रदेश सभाले सहमति दिएनन्, तर सरकारले प्रदेश सभाको निर्णयका आधार पर विधेयकलाई संशोधित गर्नेछ।
3.  **स्थानीय तहमा समीक्षा:** स्थानीय तहमा, विधेयकको जाँच गरिनेछ र आवश्यक परिवर्तनहरू yapıl बनाएcektir।
4.  **وزارتको स्वीकृति:** त्यसपछि, सरकारले नेपाल सरकारी विभागको स्वीकृतियाँ पाएगी।
5.  **संसद्को निर्णय:** अन्ततः, संविधान सभाको निर्णयका आधार पर विधेयकलाई पारित गर्नुपर्ने हुन्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CA023,English,"If a State Assembly fails to communicate acceptance or rejection within three months, what constitutional option remains available?",The originating House of the Federal Parliament may proceed with the bill.,"Article 305 of the Constitution grants the Legislature-Parliament the power to take action if the State Assembly fails to communicate acceptance or rejection within three months. This allows for various options to be considered. Here’s a breakdown of those options, based on the provided text and general legal principles:

1.  **Request for Clarification:** The legislature can formally request clarification from the President regarding the meaning of Article 305.
2.  **Amendment:** The legislature can propose an amendment to the Constitution to address the situation. This is a significant step, requiring consensus among all three levels of government.
3.  **Referral to a Judicial Body:** The legislature can refer the matter to a judicial body (like the Supreme Court) for interpretation and guidance. 

Essentially, Article 305 provides a mechanism for addressing a constitutional impasse when the legislative process is stalled.",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
CA023,Nepali,प्रदेश सभाले तीन महिनाभित्र स्वीकार वा अस्वीकारको जानकारी नदिएमा संविधानले के विकल्प दिन्छ?,विधेयक उत्पत्ति भएको संघीय संसदको सदनले प्रक्रिया अगाडि बढाउन सक्छ।,"संविधानले ३ महिने समय दिएर приема वा अस्वीकारको जानकारी नदिएमा, माइनिस्ट्रियल विभागले विकल्प दिन्छ।",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
CA024,English,What is the highest voting requirement specified in Article 274 for passing a constitutional amendment bill?,At least two-thirds majority of the total number of then members of both Houses of the Federal Parliament.,Article 274 states that a constitutional amendment bill must be passed by a majority vote of the members of the Federal Parliament.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
CA024,Nepali,धारा २७४ अनुसार संविधान संशोधन विधेयक पारित गर्न तोकिएको सबैभन्दा उच्च मतदान आवश्यकता के हो?,संघीय संसदका दुवै सदनका तत्काल कायम रहेका कुल सदस्य संख्याको कम्तीमा दुई तिहाइ बहुमत।,"धारा २७४ अनुसार, संविधान संशोधन विधेयक पारित गर्नको लागि सबैभन्दा उच्च मतदान आवश्यकता छ - **२/३rds vote**।",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
MT001,English,What majority of the total number of the then members of the Federal Parliament is required to decide that a referendum is necessary on a matter of national importance?,A two-thirds majority of the total number of the then members of the Federal Parliament is required.,"Article 305 of the Constitution of Nepal states, “The President, on the recommendation of the Government of Nepal, Council of Ministers."",""नेपाल सरकारको सिफारिसमा राष्ट्रपतिले।"",The President must decide that a referendum is necessary on a matter of national importance based on their recommendation from the government.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
MT001,Nepali,राष्ट्रिय महत्वको विषयमा जनमतसंग्रह आवश्यक छ भनी निर्णय गर्न संघीय संसदका तत्काल कायम रहेका सम्पूर्ण सदस्य संख्याको कति बहुमत आवश्यक पर्छ?,संघीय संसदका तत्काल कायम रहेका सम्पूर्ण सदस्य संख्याको दुई तिहाइ बहुमत आवश्यक पर्छ।,"The federal parliament’s majority required to decide on a national issue through a public referendum is currently permanent under the Constitution. To make a decision on this matter, the federal parliament needs a majority of at least 50% of the total number of members.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
MT002,English,On what type of matter may a decision be taken through a referendum under Article 275?,"A matter of national importance, if the Federal Parliament decides by a two-thirds majority that a referendum is necessary.","Under Article 275, a decision can be taken through a referendum on matters that are deemed to be important for the nation’s future and development. These matters include things like:

*   **Changes in the Constitution:** This is perhaps the most significant area where referendums can be held.
*   **Amendments to laws:** Significant changes to existing laws, particularly those affecting fundamental rights or public policy.
*   **Major policies:** Decisions regarding important national policies that have a substantial impact on society.

Essentially, any issue that significantly affects the nation’s direction and well-being can be subject to a referendum under this provision.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
MT002,Nepali,धारा २७५ बमोजिम कुन प्रकारको विषयमा जनमतसंग्रहमार्फत निर्णय लिन सकिन्छ?,संघीय संसदले दुई तिहाइ बहुमतबाट आवश्यक ठहर गरेको राष्ट्रिय महत्वको विषयमा।,"धारा २७५ बमोजिम विषयमा जनमतसंग्रहमार्फत निर्णय लिन सकिन्छ किन्हीं निम्न विषयमा:

*   **अनुच्छेद (Article) र व्यवस्था (Sections) का असంగति:** यदि संविधानको कुनै अनुच्छेद वा व्यवस्था गलत हुर्किन्छ भने, त्यसलाई सही बनाउनु अथवा हटाउनु केही हुन्छ।
*   **संसद्वाचक (Constitutional) नियमहरूको भ्रामक प्रयोग:** यदि कोई व्यक्ति संविधानको नियमहरूमा भ्रामक प्रयोग गर्छ भने, त्यसलाई हटाएर जानिन्छ।
*   **कानूनको व्यवस्था (Law) र संवैधानिक व्यवस्था (Constitution) बीचको असంగति:** यदि कानूनको व्यवस्था संवैधानिक व्यवस्थासँग बाझिएको हो तर यो गलत हुर्किन्छ भने, त्यस्तै त्यसलाई हटाउनु केही हुन्छ।
*   **संसद्वाचक (Constitutional) नियमहरूको कार्यान्वयनमा आएका समस्याहरू:** संविधानको कार्यान्वयनमा आएका कुनै समस्याहरू समाधान गर्न सकिन्छ।
*   **संसद्वाचक (Constitutional) नियमहरूको परिवर्तन:** यदि कोई व्यक्ति संविधानको नियमहरू बदल्छ भने, त्यसलाई हटाएर जानिन्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT003,English,"Who may grant pardons, suspend, commute, or remit sentences under Article 276?",The President may do so in accordance with law.,"Article 276 of the Constitution grants the President the power to grant pardons, suspend, commute, or remit sentences.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
MT003,Nepali,"धारा २७६ बमोजिम कसले माफी दिन, सजाय स्थगन गर्न, घटाउन वा मिनाहा गर्न सक्छ?",राष्ट्रपतिले कानूनबमोजिम त्यस्तो कार्य गर्न सक्छन्।,"धारा २७६ बमोजिममा, यदि कुनै व्यक्तिलाई थप अधिकार दिए गए तर त्यसको प्रयोगमा समस्या आउदाए भने, त्यस्तै माथिल्लको अधिकार तोक्ने र माफी दिने हो।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT004,English,Can the President grant a pardon for a sentence imposed only by a regular court?,"No. The President may grant pardons, suspend, commute, or remit sentences passed by a court, judicial or quasi-judicial body, or administrative authority or body, in accordance with law.","No, the President cannot grant a pardon for a sentence imposed solely by a regular court under Article 305 of the Constitution. The Constitution explicitly states that the President’s power to grant pardons is limited and subject to legislative approval.  Article 305(1)(a) defines the scope of the President's powers regarding pardons, which includes only federal laws and State/Local laws.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
MT004,Nepali,के राष्ट्रपतिले नियमित अदालतले दिएको सजायमा मात्र माफी दिन सक्छन्?,"होइन। राष्ट्रपतिले अदालत, न्यायिक वा अर्धन्यायिक निकाय वा प्रशासनिक अधिकारी वा निकायबाट भएको सजायलाई कानूनबमोजिम माफी, स्थगन, घटाउन वा मिनाहा गर्न सक्छन्।","हाँ, राष्ट्रपतिले नियमित अदालतले दिएको सजायमामात्र माफी दिन सक्छन्। संविधानले राष्ट्रपतिलाई सामान्यतः निर्णयहरूको माथिमा आलिकालमा अधिकार दिन्छ तर यसमा कसैले थप माफी मागने अनुमति छैन।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT005,English,"Who confers titles, honours, and decorations on behalf of the State?",The President.,"Article 305 of the Constitution of Nepal grants the President the power to bestow titles, honours, and decorations on behalf of the state.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
MT005,Nepali,"राज्यको तर्फबाट उपाधि, सम्मान र विभूषण कसले प्रदान गर्छ?",राष्ट्रपति।,"Article 304 of the Constitution of Nepal provides for the provision of titles, honors, and privileges to the President, Government Spokesperson, and other officials of the government. It states that the State shall provide these honors and privileges in accordance with law.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
MT006,English,"May a citizen of Nepal accept a title, honour, or decoration from a foreign government without approval from the Government of Nepal?",No. Approval from the Government of Nepal is required.,"The Constitution does not explicitly prohibit a citizen of Nepal from accepting titles, honours, or decorations from a foreign government. However, it requires that such acceptance be done in accordance with Nepali law and regulations. The constitution states that any title, honour, or decoration must be accepted by the government of Nepal before being accepted by the foreign government.

Here’s a breakdown:

*   **Constitutional Requirement:** Article 304(1) of the Constitution outlines the process for accepting foreign honours. It requires approval from the Government of Nepal.
*   **Practical Considerations:** While not explicitly stated, it is reasonable to assume that acceptance by a foreign government would require consultation and approval with the Nepali authorities.

Therefore, while the constitution doesn't forbid it, a citizen must obtain permission before accepting such titles or honours.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT006,Nepali,"के नेपालका नागरिकले नेपाल सरकारको स्वीकृतिबिना विदेशी सरकारबाट उपाधि, सम्मान वा विभूषण स्वीकार गर्न सक्छ?",होइन। नेपाल सरकारको स्वीकृति आवश्यक हुन्छ।,"Article 304 of the Constitution of Nepal states that “The President, on the recommendation of the Government of Nepal, Council of Ministers, may grant titles, honors, and privileges to citizens.” This means that a citizen can apply for these benefits without prior approval from the government.

Here's a breakdown:

*   **Article 304(1):**  This article explicitly allows the President to grant titles, honors, and privileges to citizens.
*   **Recommendation of the Government:** The process typically involves the government recommending a citizen for these benefits.
*   **President’s Decision:** Ultimately, the President makes the final decision based on the recommendation.

Therefore, while the Constitution provides the framework for this, it's up to the President to grant these honors and privileges.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
MT007,English,Which level of government has the power to make treaties or agreements under Article 278(1)?,The Federation.,"Article 278(1) of the Constitution grants the Legislature, Parliament, and Federal Council the power to make treaties and agreements.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT007,Nepali,धारा २७८(१) बमोजिम सन्धि वा सम्झौता गर्ने अधिकार कुन तहको सरकारसँग हुन्छ?,संघसँग।,"धारा २७८(१) बमोजिम सन्धि वा सम्झौता गर्ने अधिकार संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहका सरकारी अधिकारीहरूलाई सरकारसँग हुन्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT008,English,What must the Government of Nepal do when making a treaty or agreement concerning a matter falling within the list of State powers?,It must consult the concerned State.,The government of Nepal must adjust employees serving in government services at the state and local levels according to law.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT008,Nepali,प्रदेशको अधिकार सूचीमा पर्ने विषयमा सन्धि वा सम्झौता गर्दा नेपाल सरकारले के गर्नुपर्छ?,सम्बन्धित प्रदेशसँग परामर्श गर्नुपर्छ।,"संविधान अनुसार, नेपाल सरकारले प्रदेशको अधिकार सूचीमा पर्ने विषयलाई पहिचान र व्यवस्थापनका लागि जाँच गरिनेछ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT009,English,Under what condition may a State Council of Ministers make contractual agreements on financial and industrial matters?,With the consent of the Government of Nepal.,"Article 305 of the Constitution of Nepal grants the President the power to issue orders to remove difficulties in implementing the Constitution before the first session of the Federal Parliament. This allows the Government of Nepal to enter into contractual agreements on financial and industrial matters, subject to the President’s approval.

Here's a breakdown:

*   **Article 305:** Grants the President the power to issue orders to remove difficulties.
*   **Purpose:** Facilitates implementation of constitutional provisions without disrupting existing arrangements.
*   **Conditions for Agreement:** The President must approve these agreements, ensuring they align with the Constitution and are in the best interest of Nepal.

Essentially, it's a mechanism for the government to make crucial decisions related to economic development and policy while respecting the Constitution’s framework.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
MT009,Nepali,प्रदेश मन्त्रिपरिषद्ले वित्तीय तथा औद्योगिक विषयमा कुन शर्तमा करार सम्झौता गर्न सक्छ?,नेपाल सरकारको सहमतिमा।,"संविधानको धारा ३०६(१) अनुसार, प्रदेश सरकारले वित्तीय तथा industrial विषयमा करतारदारी सम्झौता गर्न सकिन्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT010,English,"Which four categories of treaties or agreements require ratification, accession, acceptance, or approval by a two-thirds majority of the total number of the then members of both Houses of the Federal Parliament?",Peace and friendship; defence and strategic alliance; boundaries of Nepal; and natural resources and the distribution of their uses.,"Article 304(1) of the Constitution of Nepal states that “existing laws remain in force until repealed or amended.” Therefore, four categories of treaties or agreements require ratification, accession, acceptance, or approval by a two-thirds majority of the total number of then members of both Houses of the Federal Parliament.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
MT010,Nepali,"संघीय संसदका दुवै सदनका तत्काल कायम रहेका सम्पूर्ण सदस्य संख्याको दुई तिहाइ बहुमतबाट अनुमोदन, सम्मिलन, स्वीकृति वा समर्थन आवश्यक पर्ने सन्धि वा सम्झौताका चार विषय कुन-कुन हुन्?",शान्ति तथा मैत्री; रक्षा तथा सामरिक गठबन्धन; नेपालको सीमाना; तथा प्राकृतिक स्रोत र त्यसको उपयोगको बाँडफाँड।,"संघीय संसदका दुवै सदनका तत्काल कायम रहेका सम्पूर्ण सदस्य संख्याको दुई तिहाइ बहुमतबाट अनुमोदन, सम्मिलन, स्वीकृति वा समर्थन आवश्यक पर्ने चौबीस विषय निम्न छन्:

