MT011,English,Under what exception may a treaty concerning peace and friendship or natural resources be approved by a simple majority of members present in a meeting of the House of Representatives?,"If the treaty or agreement is of an ordinary nature and does not affect the nation extensively, seriously, or in the long term.","Article 305 of the Constitution of Nepal states that treaties concerning peace and friendship, as well as natural resources, can be approved by a simple majority of members present in a meeting of the House of Representatives.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
MT011,Nepali,शान्ति तथा मैत्री वा प्राकृतिक स्रोतसम्बन्धी सन्धि वा सम्झौता कुन अवस्थामा प्रतिनिधि सभाको बैठकमा उपस्थित सदस्यहरूको साधारण बहुमतबाट अनुमोदन गर्न सकिन्छ?,"त्यस्तो सन्धि वा सम्झौता साधारण प्रकृतिको भई राष्ट्रलाई व्यापक, गम्भीर वा दीर्घकालीन रूपमा असर नगर्ने भएमा।","शान्ति तथा मैत्री वा प्राकृतिक स्रोतसम्बन्धी सन्धि वा सम्झौता प्रतिनिधि सभाको बैठकमा उपस्थित सदस्यहरूको साधारण बहुमतबाट अनुमोदन गर्न सकिन्छ, तर यो केवल तभी हुन्छ जब त्यस्तै अवस्था हो कि सदस्यहरूले आफ्नो पदमा रहे।"",""शान्ति तथा मित्रता वा प्राकृतिक स्रोतसम्बन्धी सन्धि वा सम्झौता प्रतिनिधि सभाको बैठकमा उपस्थित सदस्यहरूको साधारण बहुमतबाट अनुमोदन गर्न सकिन्छ, तर यो केवल तभी हुन्छ जब त्यस्तै अवस्था हो कि सदस्यहरूले आफ्नो पदमा रहे।""",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT012,English,"What is the constitutional consequence if a treaty or agreement is not ratified, acceded to, accepted, or approved according to Article 279?","After the commencement of the Constitution, the treaty or agreement does not apply to Nepal or the Government of Nepal. Additionally, no treaty or agreement may be concluded in a manner detrimental to Nepal's territorial integrity.","According to Article 279 of the Constitution of Nepal, if a treaty or agreement is not ratified, accredited, agreed upon, or approved by the House of Representatives (Federal Parliament), it becomes invalid. This means that the treaty/agreement is no longer legally binding and cannot be enforced in court.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT012,Nepali,"धारा २७९ बमोजिम कुनै सन्धि वा सम्झौता अनुमोदन, सम्मिलन, स्वीकृति वा समर्थन नगरिएमा त्यसको संवैधानिक परिणाम के हुन्छ?",संविधान प्रारम्भ भएपछि त्यस्तो सन्धि वा सम्झौता नेपाल वा नेपाल सरकारमा लागू हुँदैन। साथै नेपालको क्षेत्रीय अखण्डतामा प्रतिकूल हुने गरी कुनै सन्धि वा सम्झौता गर्न सकिँदैन।,"धारा २७९ बमोजिम सन्धि वा सम्झौता अनुमोदन, सम्मिलन, स्वीकृति वा समर्थन नगरिएमा त्यसको संवैधानिक परिणाम हो कि संविधानले त्यस्तै स्वीकृत गर्दा र यसलाई कार्यान्वयनमा ल्याउनुвањеका लागि आवश्यक व्यवस्था बनाउने।"",""धारा २७९ बमोजिम सन्धि वा सम्झौता अनुमोदन, सम्मिलित, स्वीकृति वा समर्थन नगरिएमा त्यसको संवैधानिक परिणाम हो कि संविधानले त्यस्तै स्वीकृत गर्दा र यसलाई कार्यान्वयनमा ल्याउनुвањеका लागि आवश्यक व्यवस्था बनाउने।""

Explanation:
The constitutional outcome when a convention or agreement is ratified, incorporated, accepted, or supported is that the constitution will enact necessary measures to implement it.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT013,English,"If both the offices of the President and Vice-President become vacant, who shall discharge the functions of the President until a new President or Vice-President is elected and assumes office?",The Speaker of the House of Representatives.,The President will discharge the functions of the Presidency until a new President or Vice-President is elected and assumes office.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT013,Nepali,राष्ट्रपति र उपराष्ट्रपति दुवै पद रिक्त भएमा नयाँ राष्ट्रपति वा उपराष्ट्रपति निर्वाचित भई पदभार ग्रहण नगरेसम्म राष्ट्रपतिको कार्य कसले सम्पादन गर्छ?,प्रतिनिधि सभाका सभामुखले।,Presidential and Vice-Presidency positions are held by the President until they become vacant in the new presidential or vice-presidential election.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
MT014,English,How frequently must the Government of Nepal appraise and review the implementation and impacts of the special rights of women and the Dalit community?,"Every ten years, concurrently with the national census.","The text doesn’t explicitly state how often the government must appraise and review the implementation and impact of the special rights of women and the Dalit community. It focuses on the constitutional framework surrounding these rights, particularly Article 306(1)(a) which defines “Law.” The text mentions that the government is obligated to assess and review, but doesn’t provide a specific frequency or timeframe for this assessment.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
MT014,Nepali,महिला र दलित समुदायका विशेष अधिकारको कार्यान्वयन र त्यसको प्रभावको मूल्याङ्कन तथा समीक्षा कति अवधिमा गर्नुपर्छ?,प्रत्येक दस वर्षमा हुने राष्ट्रिय जनगणनासँगै।,"The government of Nepal is obligated to review and update the implementation of laws and policies related to women's and Dalit communities, with a focus on ensuring their rights are effectively protected. This review should be conducted within a timeframe of **three years** from the date of the Constitution’s adoption.

Here’s a breakdown of why this timeline is crucial:

*   **Constitutional Framework:** The Constitution guarantees fundamental rights to women and Dalit communities, necessitating ongoing evaluation to ensure these rights are upheld.
*   **Dynamic Context:**  Social norms, laws, and societal attitudes evolve, requiring periodic reassessment to maintain effectiveness.
*   **Legal Requirements:** Nepal’s legal framework must be reviewed to identify gaps or areas where existing laws need adjustment.

Therefore, a comprehensive review and assessment of the implementation of laws and policies related to women's and Dalit rights should occur within three years of the Constitution's adoption.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
MT015,English,On what principle may the President appoint Nepalese ambassadors and special emissaries?,The principle of inclusion.,Article 305 of the Constitution grants the President the power to appoint Nepalese ambassadors and special emissaries.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT015,Nepali,राष्ट्रपतिले नेपाली राजदूत तथा विशेष दूतहरू कुन सिद्धान्तका आधारमा नियुक्त गर्न सक्छन्?,समावेशी सिद्धान्तका आधारमा।,"President may appoint Nepali Ambassadors and Special Representatives according to the following principles:

*   **Experience:** The President should consider the experience of candidates, prioritizing those with relevant expertise in Nepal's foreign affairs.
*   **Qualifications:** Candidates must possess qualifications that demonstrate their ability to effectively represent Nepal internationally.
*   **Loyalty:**  The appointment process should be based on loyalty and commitment to Nepal’s interests.
*   **Competence:** The President will assess the candidates' competence in handling diplomatic duties and representing Nepal’s interests abroad.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
MT016,English,Who receives letters of credentials from foreign ambassadors and diplomatic representatives?,The President.,"Article 304(1) of the Constitution states that “the President, on the recommendation of the Government of Nepal, Council of Ministers, shall issue orders to remove difficulties in implementing the Constitution before the first session of the Federal Parliament.” This provision allows the government to request letters of credentials from foreign ambassadors and diplomatic representatives.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
MT016,Nepali,विदेशी राजदूत तथा कूटनीतिक प्रतिनिधिहरूको ओहोदाको प्रमाणपत्र कसले ग्रहण गर्छ?,राष्ट्रपतिले।,"विदेशी राजदूत तथा कूटनीतिक प्रतिनिधिहरूको ओहोदाको प्रमाण (Certificate of Residence) नेपाल सरकार द्वारा ग्रहण हुन्छ।"",""Foreign diplomats and representatives receive a certificate from the government for their residence in Nepal.""",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT017,English,"According to Article 283, what principle must be followed when making appointments to Constitutional Organs and Bodies?",The inclusive principle.,"Article 283 states that the Government of Nepal must follow the following principles when appointing members to Constitutional Organs and Bodies:

*   **Eligibility:** Appointments should be based on qualifications and experience relevant to their roles.
*   **Competence:** Individuals should possess the necessary skills, knowledge, and expertise for the positions they hold.
*   **Merit:** Consideration of merit and qualifications is crucial in determining appointments.
*   **Transparency:** The appointment process must be transparent and open to public scrutiny.
*   **Accountability:** Appointments should be accountable to the Constitution and the government.

Essentially, the principle emphasizes that appointments should reflect competence, relevance, fairness, and accountability within the constitutional framework.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT017,Nepali,धारा २८३ बमोजिम संवैधानिक अंग तथा निकायमा नियुक्ति गर्दा कुन सिद्धान्तको पालना गर्नुपर्छ?,समावेशी सिद्धान्त।,"धारा २८३ बमोजिम संवैधानिक अंग तथा निकायमा नियुक्ति गर्दा, नियुक्तिकर्ताले पदकात्मक योग्यता, अनुभव, दक्षता र अन्य आवश्यक मापदंडहरू जाँच्ने हुनुपърछ। संविधानले विशेष रूप से कर्मचारीहरहरूको क्षमता र योग्यताको मूल्यांकन गर्नुपर्छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
MT018,English,Who serves as the Chairperson of the Constitutional Council?,The Prime Minister.,"Article 304(1) provides that the President, on the recommendation of the Government of Nepal, Council of Ministers.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
MT018,Nepali,संवैधानिक परिषद्को अध्यक्ष को हुन्छ?,प्रधानमन्त्री।,Article 305 of the Constitution states: “The President shall be the Head of the Constitutional Council.”,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
MT019,English,Which of the following is NOT a regular member of the Constitutional Council under Article 284(1)? A. Chief Justice B. Speaker of the House of Representatives C. Minister for Law and Justice D. Chairperson of the National Assembly,The Minister for Law and Justice.,C. Minister for Law and Justice,Correct,Not a strict error,False
MT019,Nepali,धारा २८४(१) बमोजिम निम्नमध्ये को संवैधानिक परिषद्को नियमित सदस्य होइन? क. प्रधानन्यायाधीश ख. प्रतिनिधि सभाका सभामुख ग. कानून तथा न्यायमन्त्री घ. राष्ट्रिय सभाका अध्यक्ष,कानून तथा न्यायमन्त्री।,"क. प्रधानन्यायाधीश ख. प्रतिनिधि सभाका सभामुख ग. कानून तथा न्यायमन्त्री घ. राष्ट्रिय सभाका अध्यक्ष

Explanation:

धारा २८४(१) मध्ये, ‘संवेशनीय परिषद्’ (Constitutional Council)को नियमित सदस्य होउनुためには, माइनरिटी (Minority) को सुरक्षा सुनिश्चित गर्न र संविधानको अर्थ स्पष्ट बनाउनमा पर्याप्त क्षमता छ हुनुपर्छ। यसले देखाएर, संविधानको व्याख्यालाई सुरक्षित गराउन र कमजोर समूहहरूको रक्षा गर्नुपर्छ।

*   **क. प्रधानन्यायाधीश:** प्रधानन्यायाधीशहरूConstitutional Councilको सदस्य होलान्छ, तर यो सदस्यता Constitutional Councilको सुरक्षा सुनिश्चित गर्न र संविधानको अर्थ स्पष्ट बनाउनमा पर्याप्त क्षमता छ हुनुपर्छ।
*   **ग. कानून तथा न्यायमन्त्री:** कानून तथा न्यायमन्त्रीConstitutional Councilको सदस्य होलान्छ, तर यो सदस्यता Constitutional Councilको सुरक्षा सुनिश्चित गर्न र संविधानको अर्थ स्पष्ट बनाउनमा पर्याप्त क्षमता छ हुनुपर्छ।
*   **घ. राष्ट्रिय सभाका अध्यक्ष:** राष्ट्रिय सभाका अध्यक्षConstitutional Councilको सदस्य होलान्छ, तर यो सदस्यता Constitutional Councilको सुरक्षा सुनिश्चित गर्न र संविधानको अर्थ स्पष्ट बनाउनमा पर्याप्त क्षमता छ हुनुपर्छ।

त्यसैले, क. प्रधानन्यायाधीश, ग. कानून तथा न्यायमन्त्री, और घ. राष्ट्रिय सभाका अध्यक्ष मध्ये कोणा पनि संवैधानिक परिषद्को सदस्य होइन।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
MT020,English,How far in advance must the Constitutional Council generally make a recommendation for the appointment of a Chief Justice or a chief or official of a Constitutional Body before the office becomes vacant?,At least one month before the office becomes vacant.,Article 304(2) of the Constitution states that the Constitutional Council shall make recommendations for the appointment of a Chief Justice or a chief or official of a Constitutional Body at least six months prior to the date when the office becomes vacant.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT020,Nepali,प्रधानन्यायाधीश वा संवैधानिक निकायका प्रमुख वा पदाधिकारीको पद रिक्त हुनुभन्दा सामान्यतया कति अगाडि संवैधानिक परिषद्ले नियुक्तिको सिफारिस गर्नुपर्छ?,पद रिक्त हुनुभन्दा कम्तीमा एक महिना अगाडि।,"प्रधानन्यायाधीश (Chief Justice) वा संवैधानिक निकायका प्रमुख वा पदाधिकारीको पद रिक्त हुनुदा, साधारणतम्, पाँच वर्ष अगावैं तरिकाले नियुक्तिको सिफारस गर्नुपर्छ।

यहाँ विस्तृत स्पष्टीकरण दिइएको छ:

*   **सिफारिस:** प्रधानन्यायाधीश वा संवैधानिक निकायका प्रमुख वा पदाधिकारीको पद रिक्त भएमा, सरकारले एक पाँचवर्षीय योजना बनाउँदै, नियुक्तिको प्रस्ताव गरिनेछन्।
*   **प्रस्तावना:** यो योजनाले नियुक्तिको सिफारसलाई प्राथमिकता दिन्छ र समयোপযোগী रूपमा नियुक्ति गर्नुपर्छ।
*   **समयसीमा:** ५ वर्ष अगावैं तरिकाले नियुक्तिको सिफारस गर्नुपर्छ, यसले सुनिश्चित गर्दछ कि संवैधानिक निकायले पर्याप्त समय दिएर योग्य व्यक्तिहरूलाई पदमा पुर्‍याउन सक्नेछन्।

यो व्यवस्था Constitutional Council (CC) द्वारा बनाए गए भनीय प्रणालीको हिस्सा हो जसले संविधानको अनुपालनलाई सुरक्षित गराउँदै छ र त्यसका लागि आवश्यक सहकार्य गरिनेछन्।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT021,English,On what basis must positions in the Federal civil service and other Federal government services be filled?,Through competitive examinations based on open and proportional inclusive principles.,"According to Article 304 of the Constitution, positions in the Federal civil service and other Federal government services should be filled based on the following principles:

*   **Legal Procedures:** Positions should be filled according to established legal procedures.
*   **Election Process:** Elections for officials within the Federal Civil Service and other Federal Government Services shall be held according to law.
*   **Appointment by the President:** The President is responsible for appointing officials, subject to recommendations from the Council of Ministers.

Essentially, the Constitution outlines a process for filling positions through established legal channels and with the approval of the President.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT021,Nepali,संघीय निजामती सेवा तथा अन्य संघीय सरकारी सेवाका पदहरू कुन आधारमा पूर्ति गर्नुपर्छ?,खुला तथा समानुपातिक समावेशी सिद्धान्तका आधारमा प्रतिस्पर्धात्मक परीक्षामार्फत।,"संघीय निजामती सेवा तथा अन्य संघीय सरकारी सेवाका पदहरू संविधानको आचारसंहिता (Constitution Code) अनुसार पूर्ति गर्नुपर्छ।"",""संघीय निजामती सेवा तथा अन्य संघीय सरकारी सेवाका पदहरूको पूर्ति संविधानको आचारसंहितामा दिएर गर्नुपर्छ।""",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT022,English,Which of the following is NOT listed as a member of the Election Constituency Delimitation Commission? A. A retired Judge of the Supreme Court B. A geographer C. A sociologist or demographer D. The Chief Election Commissioner,The Chief Election Commissioner.,"C. A sociologist or demographer

**Explanation:**

The text describes the composition of the Election Constituency Delimitation Commission (CCDC) in Nepal, and it lists retired Judges, Geographers, Sociologists, and Demographers as members. The question asks for which one is NOT listed.  Therefore, the correct answer is C.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT022,Nepali,निम्नमध्ये को निर्वाचन क्षेत्र निर्धारण आयोगको सदस्यका रूपमा उल्लेख गरिएको छैन? क. सर्वोच्च अदालतका सेवानिवृत्त न्यायाधीश ख. भूगोलविद् ग. समाजशास्त्री वा जनसांख्यिकीविद् घ. प्रमुख निर्वाचन आयुक्त,प्रमुख निर्वाचन आयुक्त।,क. सर्वोच्च अदालतका सेवानिवृत्त न्यायाधीश (Retired Judge),Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT023,English,"What factors must the Election Constituency Delimitation Commission consider when determining election constituencies, in addition to population and geography?","It must consider, among other things, population density, geographical specificity, administrative and transportation convenience, and the community and cultural aspects of the constituencies.","The Election Constituency Delimitation Commission (Coalition) is tasked with dividing electoral constituencies based on population and geography. In addition to these two factors, it must also consider several other crucial elements. Here’s a breakdown of the key factors they need to assess:

*   **Historical Significance:** The commission needs to analyze the historical significance of each constituency. This includes examining its past role in political representation, community identity, and development. A constituency's history might be more relevant than purely geographical location.
*   **Demographic Diversity & Distribution:**  The Commission must consider how the demographic distribution (age, gender, ethnicity, etc.) within a constituency varies across different regions. Uneven distribution can lead to disproportionate representation and potentially create political imbalances.
*   **Economic Activity & Development:** The commission needs to evaluate the economic activity and development levels in each constituency. A constituency with strong industrial or agricultural sectors might warrant a larger number of constituencies, while areas with limited economic opportunities could require fewer.
*   **Social and Cultural Factors:**  The Commission must consider social and cultural factors that influence community identity and political participation. This includes examining the presence of distinct communities (religious, ethnic, linguistic) within a constituency.
*   **Geographical Features & Connectivity:** The commission needs to assess how geographical features like mountains, rivers, or plains affect the accessibility and representation of different constituencies.  Connectivity between areas is also important for ensuring fair representation.
*   **Political Considerations & Political Stability:** While not always explicitly stated, the Commission must consider potential political implications of constituency boundaries. It aims to create a system that promotes stability and avoids creating new divisions that could lead to conflict.
* **Existing Boundaries:** The commission will take into account existing boundary lines and how they might be affected by changes in population or geography.

In essence, the Election Constituency Delimitation Commission's task is not solely about population and geography; it’s a complex balancing act involving historical context, demographic realities, economic factors, social dynamics, and political considerations to ensure equitable representation across Nepal.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT023,Nepali,निर्वाचन क्षेत्र निर्धारण गर्दा जनसंख्या र भूगोलका अतिरिक्त निर्वाचन क्षेत्र निर्धारण आयोगले कुन-कुन पक्षलाई ध्यान दिनुपर्छ?,"जनघनत्व, भौगोलिक विशिष्टता, प्रशासनिक तथा यातायात सुविधा र निर्वाचन क्षेत्रका सामुदायिक तथा सांस्कृतिक पक्षलगायतका विषयलाई ध्यान दिनुपर्छ।","Election area determination commissions should consider both population and geography, in addition to the number and physical characteristics of the local areas. Here’s a breakdown of what they need to consider:

*   **Population:** The commission needs to understand the demographic makeup of each region – its size, age distribution, ethnic composition, and overall growth rate. This helps determine which areas are likely to have more voters.
*   **Geography/Terrain:**  The terrain (mountains, valleys, rivers, etc.) significantly impacts accessibility and voter turnout. Areas with difficult terrain might see lower participation rates. The commission should consider how the geography influences voting patterns.

Essentially, a holistic approach that combines demographic data with geographic factors is crucial for creating fair and representative electoral boundaries.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
MT024,English,"State three important constitutional requirements relating to the Language Commission's composition, term, and qualifications.","The Commission must have one Chairperson and the required number of members; the term of the Chairperson and members is six years and they cannot be reappointed; and appointees must have a relevant master's degree, at least twenty years of experience in the study, teaching, and research of Nepal's languages, be at least forty-five years old, and possess high moral character.","Here are three important constitutional requirements regarding the language commission’s composition, term, and qualifications as stipulated in Nepal’s Constitution:

1.  **Composition:** The constitution mandates that the language commission must consist of at least five members – two from each level of government (Federal, State, and Local). This ensures representation across different levels of governance to ensure linguistic diversity is reflected in the commission's deliberations.

2.  **Term:** The language commission’s term is defined as “five years” starting from the date of its establishment. This establishes a clear timeframe for the commission’s activities and allows for regular review and adjustments.

3.  **Qualifications:** The constitution specifies that members must possess a recognized degree in linguistics, translation, or related fields. Furthermore, they are expected to have extensive knowledge of Nepali language and culture, as well as experience working with linguistic issues within the government.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT024,Nepali,"भाषा आयोगको गठन, पदावधि र योग्यता सम्बन्धी तीनवटा महत्वपूर्ण संवैधानिक प्रावधान उल्लेख गर्नुहोस्।","आयोगमा एक जना अध्यक्ष र आवश्यक संख्यामा सदस्य हुन्छन्; अध्यक्ष तथा सदस्यको पदावधि छ वर्षको हुन्छ र पुनः नियुक्ति हुन सक्दैन; तथा नियुक्त व्यक्तिसँग सम्बन्धित विषयमा स्नातकोत्तर उपाधि, नेपालको विभिन्न भाषाको अध्ययन, अध्यापन तथा अनुसन्धानमा कम्तीमा बीस वर्षको अनुभव, कम्तीमा पैंतालीस वर्ष उमेर र उच्च नैतिक चरित्र हुनुपर्छ।","यहाँ भाषा आयोगको गठन, पदअवधि र योग्यता सम्बन्धित तीनवटा महत्वपूर्ण संवैधानिक प्रावधानहरू बुझिएका छन्:

**1. प्रावधान - गठन:**

*   संविधानले भाषा आयोगलाई सरकारमा समावेश गर्ने तरतव्य है।
*   भाषा आयोगको गठन संविधान अनुसार हुनेछ हो।
*   भाषा आयोगको गठनमा, नेपाल सरकारले स्थानीय स्तरदेखि संघीय нивоमा भाषाविद्हरूलाई नियुक्त गर्नुपर्नेछ।
*   भाषा आयोगको गठनमा, नेपाली भाषाका जानकार व्यक्तिहरूको समावेशी रूपमा बनाउन सकूनेछ।

**2. प्रावधान - पदअवधि:**

*   भाषा आयोगको कार्यकाल संविधान अनुसार हुनेछ हो।
*   भाषा आयोगको कार्यकालमा, सरकारले भाषालाई सुरक्षित राख्ने उपायहरू 시행 गर्नुपर्नेछ।
*   भाषा आयोगको कार्यकालमा, नेपाली भाषाका जानकार व्यक्तिहरूको सहभागिता सुनिश्चित गरिनेछ।
*   भाषा आयोगको कार्यकालमा, नेपालक भाषाको अध्ययन र प्रचारमा योगदान दिने मान्नेछ।

**3. प्रावधान - योग्यता:**

*   भाषा आयोगले संविधानको अर्थ बुझिन्छ भन्ने कुन तरतव्य है, त्यसलाई स्पष्टीकरण गर्नुपर्नेछ।
*   भाषा आयोगले भाषाका जानकार व्यक्तिहरूको रूपमा बनाउनुपर्नेछ।
*   भाषा आयोगले नेपालक भाषाका जानकार व्यक्तिहरूलाई प्रोत्साहन गर्नुपर्नेछ।

यी तीन प्रावधानहरू संविधानको आधारमा बनाए गएन् जसले भाषा आयोगको गठन, पदअवधि र योग्यता सम्बन्धित नियमहरू तय गर्दछन।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT025,English,Where is the capital of Nepal situated?,Kathmandu.,Kathmandu,Correct,Not a strict error,False
MT025,Nepali,नेपालको राजधानी कहाँ अवस्थित छ?,काठमाडौंमा।,नेपालको राजधानी Kathmandu हुन्छ।,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
MT026,English,By what majority is the capital of a State decided by the concerned State Assembly?,A two-thirds majority of the total number of the then members of the concerned State Assembly.,"According to Article 306(1) of the Constitution, the capital of a State is decided by the concerned State Assembly.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT026,Nepali,सम्बन्धित प्रदेश सभाले प्रदेशको राजधानी कुन बहुमतबाट निर्धारण गर्छ?,सम्बन्धित प्रदेश सभाका तत्काल कायम रहेका सम्पूर्ण सदस्य संख्याको दुई तिहाइ बहुमतबाट।,"संविधान अनुसार, प्रदेशको राजधानी प्रदेश सभा द्वारा निर्धारित बहुमतबाट निर्धारण गर्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT027,English,"Which type of citizenship must a person possess to be eligible for election, nomination, or appointment as President, Vice-President, Prime Minister, Chief Justice, Speaker of the House of Representatives, Chief of State, Chief Minister, Speaker of a State Assembly, or chief of a security body?",Citizenship of Nepal by descent.,"The Constitution does not explicitly define who constitutes a citizen for these positions. However, it states that “a citizen of Nepal” is required to be eligible for election, nomination, or appointment as President, Vice-President, Prime Minister, Chief Justice, Speaker of the House of Representatives, Chief of State, Chief Minister, Speaker of a State Assembly, or chief of a security body.

Therefore, any person who is a citizen of Nepal must meet this requirement to be eligible for these positions.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT027,Nepali,"राष्ट्रपति, उपराष्ट्रपति, प्रधानमन्त्री, प्रधानन्यायाधीश, प्रतिनिधि सभाका सभामुख, प्रदेश प्रमुख, मुख्यमन्त्री, प्रदेश सभाका सभामुख वा सुरक्षा निकायको प्रमुख पदमा निर्वाचित, मनोनीत वा नियुक्त हुन व्यक्तिसँग कस्तो नागरिकता हुनुपर्छ?",वंशजको आधारमा प्राप्त नेपालको नागरिकता।,"संविधान अनुसार, राष्ट्रपति, उपराष्ट्रपति, प्रधानमन्त्री, प्रधानन्यायाधीश, प्रतिनिधि सभाका सभामुख, प्रदेश प्रमुख, मुख्यमन्त्री, प्रदेश सभाका सभामुख वा सुरक्षा निकायको प्रमुख पदमा निर्वाचित हुन व्यक्तिसँग नागरिकता हुनुपर्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT028,English,Under what additional residence conditions may a person with naturalized citizenship or citizenship by birth be qualified for an office of a Constitutional Body other than the offices listed in Article 289(1)?,"A naturalized citizen must have resided in Nepal for at least ten years, while a person who obtained citizenship by birth must have resided in Nepal for at least five years.","Article 306(2) states that “a citizen of Nepal shall be qualified to hold any position under the Constitution, including those of Constitutional Bodies, except as otherwise specified by law.” This means a naturalized or birth-right citizen can serve in any constitutional body. However, it doesn’t specify *additional* residence conditions beyond this general rule.

Therefore, based solely on Article 306(2), there are no additional residence conditions required for a person with naturalized citizenship or citizenship by birth to hold an office of a Constitutional Body other than those listed in Article 289(1). The Constitution allows them to serve in any position under the law.",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
MT028,Nepali,धारा २८९(१) मा उल्लिखित बाहेक अन्य संवैधानिक निकायको पदमा प्राकृतिकीकृत वा जन्मको आधारमा नागरिकता प्राप्त व्यक्तिले कुन अतिरिक्त बसोबाससम्बन्धी शर्त पूरा गर्नुपर्छ?,प्राकृतिकीकृत नागरिकले कम्तीमा दस वर्ष र जन्मको आधारमा नागरिकता प्राप्त व्यक्तिले कम्तीमा पाँच वर्ष नेपालमा बसोबास गरेको हुनुपर्छ।,"धारा २८९(१) मा उल्लिखित अन्य संवैधानिक निकायको पदमा प्राकृतिकीकृत वा जन्मको आधारमा नागरिकता प्राप्त व्यक्तिले, संविधानको तहत, खाली स्थानको लागि कुन अतिरिक्त बसोबाससम्बन्धी शर्त पूरा गर्नुपर्छ?

उत्तर:
धारा २८९(१) मा उल्लिखित अन्य संवैधानिक निकायको पदमा प्राकृतिकीकृत वा जन्मको आधारमा नागरिकता प्राप्त व्यक्तिले, संविधानको तहत, खाली स्थानको लिएर, नेपालका स्थानीय सरकारको व्यवस्थापनमा सहभागितामा कुन अतिरिक्त बसोबाससम्बन्धी शर्त पूरा गर्नुपर्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT029,English,What must the Federal Parliament ensure when making laws concerning the rights of trusts and farmers enjoying possessory rights over trust lands?,The laws must not be prejudicial to the basic norms of the trusts.,"The Federal Parliament must ensure that any law regarding the rights of trusts and farmers enjoying possessory rights over trust land is consistent with the Constitution. Specifically, it needs to ensure that the law does not violate fundamental principles enshrined in the Constitution, particularly those related to individual freedoms, property rights, and the rule of law. It also requires a careful balance between protecting the interests of both trusts and farmers while upholding the overall legal framework of Nepal.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT029,Nepali,गुठीको अधिकार तथा गुठी जग्गामा भोगाधिकार भएका किसानका अधिकारसम्बन्धी कानून बनाउँदा संघीय संसदले के सुनिश्चित गर्नुपर्छ?,त्यस्ता कानून गुठीका आधारभूत मान्यतामा प्रतिकूल नहुने कुरा सुनिश्चित गर्नुपर्छ।,The Federal Parliament must ensure that the rights of marginalized farmers and the right to jurisdiction are protected in the law regarding the establishment of such laws.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
MT030,English,"Can a Nepali citizen holding a foreign permanent residence permit be elected, nominated, or appointed to an office under the Constitution?","No. However, a person who has renounced the permit may become eligible after at least three months have expired from the date of renunciation.","Yes, according to Article 306 of the Constitution, a Nepali citizen holding a foreign permanent residence permit can be elected, nominated, or appointed to an office under the Constitution.

Here’s a breakdown of how it works based on the provided text:

*   **Article 306(1)(d):** “The definition of ‘Municipality’ includes Municipal Corporations and Sub-municipal Corporations.” This means that foreign residents holding permanent residency can be appointed to positions within municipalities.
*   **Article 306(1)(e):** “The constitutional definition limits the term to a citizen of Nepal.”

Therefore, the text explicitly states that a Nepali citizen with a foreign permanent residence permit is eligible for all three types of office positions as defined by the Constitution.",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
MT030,Nepali,"विदेशी स्थायी आवासीय अनुमति लिएको नेपाली नागरिक संविधानबमोजिम निर्वाचित, मनोनीत वा नियुक्त हुने पदमा योग्य हुन्छ?",हुँदैन। तर त्यस्तो अनुमति त्यागेको व्यक्तिले त्यागेको मितिले कम्तीमा तीन महिना पूरा भएपछि योग्य हुन सक्छ।,"संविधान बमोजिम निर्वाचित, मनोनीत वा नियुक्त हुने पदमा योग्य नागरिक नेपाली राज्यको कानूनको अनुसारले तरतव्य हुन्छ।

Explanation:
Article 304 of the Constitution states that “a citizen shall be eligible for foreign residence permits according to law.” This means that any Nepali citizen who is elected, nominated, or appointed in a position under the constitution is entitled to receive a foreign residence permit.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT031,English,For which categories of appointments are parliamentary hearings conducted under Article 292?,"Appointments to the offices of the Chief Justice and Supreme Court Judges, members of the Judicial Council, chiefs and members of Constitutional Bodies appointed on the recommendation of the Constitutional Council, and ambassadors.","Article 292 of the Constitution outlines the procedures for conducting parliamentary hearings regarding appointments. Here’s a breakdown of the categories of appointments covered by this provision:

*   **Appointments to the Federal Council:** This includes all positions on the Federal Council, including the President and Vice-President.
*   **Appointments to the Provincial Councils:** Appointments to provincial councils are also subject to parliamentary hearings.
*   **Appointments to Local Government Bodies:**  This encompasses appointments to local government bodies at the sub-national level (such as municipalities and districts).

Essentially, Article 292 establishes a mechanism for the legislature to scrutinize and review appointments made by the executive branch, ensuring accountability and proper selection processes.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT031,Nepali,धारा २९२ बमोजिम कुन-कुन नियुक्तिका लागि संसदीय सुनुवाइ गरिन्छ?,"प्रधानन्यायाधीश तथा सर्वोच्च अदालतका न्यायाधीश, न्याय परिषद्का सदस्य, संवैधानिक परिषद्को सिफारिसमा नियुक्त हुने संवैधानिक निकायका प्रमुख तथा सदस्य र राजदूतको नियुक्तिमा।","धारा २९२ बमोजिम,  सं संसदीय सुनुवाइ निम्न अनुसार हुन्छ:

*   **संसदीय पदको लिएर, नेपाल सरकारले ३० दिन सकेसम्मबाट, उनलाई सार्वजनिक रूपमा घोषणा गरेन तर, उनको कार्यका लागि संसदीय सुनुवाइ गरिन्छ।**
*   **संसदीय पदको लिएर, नेपाल सरकारले ५ वर्ष सकेसम्मबाट, उनको कार्यका लागि संसदीय सुनुवाइ गरिन्छ।**",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT032,English,How many members are in the joint committee formed for the purpose of parliamentary hearings?,Fifteen members from both Houses of the Federal Parliament.,The text doesn’t specify the number of members in the joint committee. It only mentions that it is a “joint committee” formed for parliamentary hearings.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
MT032,Nepali,संसदीय सुनुवाइका लागि गठन हुने संयुक्त समितिमा कति सदस्य हुन्छन्?,संघीय संसदका दुवै सदनका गरी पन्ध्र जना सदस्य।,"Article 305 of the Constitution of Nepal states that a Joint Committee can be formed within a parliamentary session. It is not specified how many members are required to constitute such a committee. However, it does state that the number of members should be determined by the House of Representatives.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
MT033,English,What professional restriction applies to members of the parliamentary hearing joint committee during that term of the Federal Parliament?,They may not practice law in the Supreme Court.,"Article 305, Definitions and Interpretations, Citizen, Definition, Easy, A citizen means a citizen of Nepal.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
MT033,Nepali,संघीय संसदको उक्त कार्यकालमा संसदीय सुनुवाइ संयुक्त समितिका सदस्यहरूलाई कुन पेशागत प्रतिबन्ध लागू हुन्छ?,उनीहरूले सर्वोच्च अदालतमा कानून व्यवसाय गर्न पाउँदैनन्।,"Article 305 of the Constitution of Nepal grants the President the power to issue orders to remove difficulties in implementing the Constitution before the first session of the Federal Parliament. This power is exercised by the members of the Joint Committee, which are appointed by the President.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
MT034,English,Which Constitutional Body is specifically excluded from monitoring and evaluation by committees of the House of Representatives under Article 293?,The National Human Rights Commission.,Article 293 of the Constitution states that “The House of Representatives shall not be responsible for the monitoring and evaluation of any Committee of the Federal Parliament.”,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
MT034,Nepali,धारा २९३ बमोजिम प्रतिनिधि सभाका समितिहरूले संवैधानिक निकायहरूको कामकारबाही अनुगमन तथा मूल्याङ्कन गर्दा कुन संवैधानिक निकायलाई विशेष रूपमा अपवाद गरिएको छ?,राष्ट्रिय मानव अधिकार आयोग।,"धारा २९३ बमोजिम प्रतिनिधि सभाका समितिहरूले संवैधानिक निकायहरूको कामकारबाही अनुगमन तथा मूल्याङ्कन गर्दा, नेपालको संविधानको व्यवस्था अनुसार, **स्थानीय सरकार (Local Bodies)** को कामकारबाहीलाई विशेष रूपमा अपवाद गरिएको छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT035,English,What is the reporting process for Constitutional Bodies under Article 294?,"Each Constitutional Body submits an annual report of its functioning to the President, who causes it to be laid before the Federal Parliament through the Prime Minister. A Constitutional Body may also prepare a separate report on its functioning in each State and submit it to the Chief of State.","Article 294 outlines the reporting requirements for constitutional bodies, primarily focusing on their financial accountability and transparency. Here’s a breakdown of the key aspects of the reporting process:

**1. Reporting Frequency:**

*   Constitutional bodies (including Parliament, Constitutional Council, Supreme Court, etc.) are required to submit annual reports to the government.
*   These reports must be submitted within 60 days after the end of each fiscal year.

**2. Content of Reports:**

The reports cover several key areas:

*   **Financial Status:** Detailed financial statements outlining income and expenditure. This includes details about revenue sources, expenses, and assets/liabilities.
*   **Operational Activities:**  Reports detailing the activities undertaken by the body, including meetings held, decisions made, and projects completed.
*   **Compliance with Laws & Regulations:** Demonstrating adherence to relevant laws and regulations governing their operations.
*   **Transparency Measures:** Information on measures taken to ensure transparency in governance and decision-making processes.

**3. Reporting Channels:**

*   The government is responsible for disseminating these reports to the public through official channels (e.g., website, publications).
*   There are specific procedures for submitting the reports, including required forms and documentation.

**4.  Specific Requirements for Different Types of Bodies:**

*   **Parliament:** Reports must be submitted in a standardized format with detailed financial statements.
*   **Constitutional Council:** The report will focus on the council's activities and performance.
*   **Supreme Court:** Reports are required to demonstrate compliance with judicial decisions and legal principles.


**5.  Purpose of Reporting:**

The government’s reporting requirements serve several important purposes:

*   **Accountability:** To ensure that constitutional bodies operate efficiently and effectively, demonstrating responsible use of public funds.
*   **Transparency:** To increase public trust in the functioning of the constitution.
*   **Compliance:** To ensure compliance with legal and regulatory frameworks.


**Resources for Further Information:**

*   **Official Government Website:** [https://www.gov.nl/en/](https://www.gov.nl/en/) - Search for ""Constitutional Bodies Reporting"" or similar terms.
*   **Nepali Law & Governance Portal:** [https://www.nepallawgovernance.gov.np/](https://www.nepallawgoverance.gov.np/) – This portal provides detailed information on constitutional bodies and their reporting obligations.

Do you want me to elaborate on any specific aspect of this reporting process, such as the format of reports or the types of data included?",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
MT035,Nepali,धारा २९४ बमोजिम संवैधानिक निकायहरूको वार्षिक प्रतिवेदन पेश गर्ने प्रक्रिया के हो?,प्रत्येक संवैधानिक निकायले आफ्नो कामकारबाहीको वार्षिक प्रतिवेदन राष्ट्रपतिसमक्ष पेश गर्छ र राष्ट्रपतिले प्रधानमन्त्रीमार्फत संघीय संसदसमक्ष पेश गराउँछन्। संवैधानिक निकायले प्रत्येक प्रदेशमा आफ्नो कामकारबाहीसम्बन्धी छुट्टै प्रतिवेदन तयार गरी प्रदेश प्रमुखसमक्ष पेश गर्न पनि सक्छ।,"धारा २९४ बमोजिम संवैधानिक निकायहरूको वार्षिक प्रतिवेदन पेश गर्ने प्रक्रिया, संविधानको अनुच्छेद ३०३(२) अनुसार, संघीय संसदसमेतले व्यवस्थापन गर्छन्।"",""धारा २९४,Constitutional bodies submit annual reports according to the Constitution."",""संविधानको अनुच्छेद ३०३(२) अनुसार,संघीय संसदले संवैधानिक निकायहरूको वार्षिक प्रतिवेदन पेश गर्ने प्रक्रियालाई व्यवस्थापन गर्छ।”",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP001,English,What may the Government of Nepal constitute under Article 295(1) to make suggestions on matters relating to the boundaries of States?,The Government of Nepal may constitute a Federal Commission.,The government of Nepal can constitute recommendations regarding the boundaries of states through Article 295(1). This allows them to propose changes in state borders based on legal and political considerations.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP001,Nepali,धारा २९५(१) बमोजिम प्रदेशको सीमासम्बन्धी विषयमा सुझाव दिन नेपाल सरकारले के गठन गर्न सक्छ?,नेपाल सरकारले संघीय आयोग गठन गर्न सक्छ।,"The Government of Nepal can arrange for the delivery of services at the State and Local levels during the transition by establishing a committee or commission specifically dedicated to addressing the issues related to regional boundaries and delimitation. Here’s a breakdown of how they could approach this, incorporating best practices and considering potential challenges:

**1. Formation of a Regional Boundary Commission (RBC):**

* **Composition:** The government should form a RBC comprising representatives from various levels of local governance – including municipalities, districts, and regional authorities.  It’s crucial to include representatives from the Nepal Geographical Information System (NGIS) and other relevant departments.
* **Mandate:** This commission's primary mandate would be:
    * **Review Existing Boundaries:** Conduct a thorough review of existing boundary lines established under previous laws or agreements, considering historical context, geographical realities, and potential conflicts.
    * **Analyze Current Challenges:** Identify the key challenges related to boundary disputes – including overlapping claims, unclear demarcations, and issues with land ownership.
    * **Develop New Boundaries (if necessary):** Based on a comprehensive analysis, propose new boundaries that are legally sound, politically acceptable, and minimize conflict.  This should involve consultation with stakeholders.
    * **Implement Boundary Adjustments:** Oversee the implementation of boundary adjustments through legal processes, ensuring transparency and fairness.

**2. Collaboration with NGIS (National Geographical Information System):**

* **Data Integration:** The RBC would need to integrate data from the NGS – including land surveys, maps, and other geospatial information – to inform its analysis and recommendations.
* **Geospatial Analysis:** Utilize advanced geospatial technologies like LiDAR scanning and remote sensing to create high-resolution digital terrain models (DTMs) that can be used for boundary demarcation.

**3. Stakeholder Consultation & Engagement:**

* **Local Government Representatives:**  Actively involve local government officials at all levels – including mayors, district administrators, and regional heads – in the consultation process.
* **Community Participation:** Engage with communities to understand their perspectives on boundary issues and ensure that any proposed changes are acceptable. This could include public forums, surveys, and participatory mapping exercises.
* **Landowners & Indigenous Communities:**  Recognize the importance of land rights and indigenous knowledge. Consult with landowners and indigenous communities to address potential conflicts arising from boundary disputes.

**4. Legal Framework & Transparency:**

* **Legal Review:** The RBC’s recommendations should be thoroughly reviewed by legal experts to ensure compliance with constitutional provisions, existing laws, and international standards.
* **Transparency in Process:**  The entire process – from data collection to decision-making – must be transparent and accessible to the public. Public consultations and open access to information are vital.

**5. Addressing Specific Challenges:**

* **Historical Boundary Disputes:** Develop a strategy for addressing historical boundary disputes, potentially through mediation or arbitration.
* **Land Consolidation & Development:**  Consider how new boundaries might impact land consolidation efforts and development plans.


**6. Phased Implementation:**

* **Pilot Projects:** Consider starting with pilot projects in specific regions to test the RBC’s approach before implementing it nationwide.



By establishing a robust Regional Boundary Commission, Nepal can significantly improve its ability to manage boundary issues effectively, reduce conflict, and promote stability across the country.  It's an investment that will pay off in long-term benefits for governance and regional development.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
TP002,English,By what majority must the names of the States be decided by the concerned State Assemblies under Article 295(2)?,A two-thirds majority of the total number of members of the concerned State Assembly is required.,"According to Article 295(2) of the Constitution, the names of the States should be determined by the concerned State Assemblies through a majority vote.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP002,Nepali,धारा २९५(२) बमोजिम सम्बन्धित प्रदेश सभाले प्रदेशको नाम निर्धारण गर्दा कस्तो बहुमत आवश्यक पर्छ?,सम्बन्धित प्रदेश सभाका सम्पूर्ण सदस्य संख्याको दुई तिहाइ बहुमत आवश्यक पर्छ।,"धारा २९५(२) बमोजिम सम्बन्धित प्रदेश सभाले प्रदेशको नाम निर्धारण गर्दा, प्रदेशको नाममा ३०% बहुमत आवश्यक हुन्छ।

Explanation:
Article 295(2) states that the provincial assembly must determine the name of the province in a manner that is consistent with the Constitution. This means that the majority of votes cast by the provincial assembly should be in favor of the proposed name.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP003,English,"What commission was required to be constituted to determine the number and boundaries of Village Bodies, Municipalities, and Special, Protected, or Autonomous Regions?",The Government of Nepal was required to constitute a commission for determining their number and boundaries.,"Article 306(1) of the Constitution states that “the Commission for Determining the Number and Boundaries of Village Bodies, Municipalities, and Special, Protected, or Autonomous Regions shall be constituted.” This commission is required to determine the number and boundaries of these regional units.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP003,Nepali,"गाउँ निकाय, नगरपालिका तथा विशेष, संरक्षित वा स्वायत्त क्षेत्रको संख्या र सीमाना निर्धारण गर्न कुन आयोग गठन गर्नुपर्ने व्यवस्था थियो?",नेपाल सरकारले तिनको संख्या र सीमाना निर्धारण गर्न आयोग गठन गर्नुपर्ने व्यवस्था थियो।,"संविधान २०६५ अनुसार, गाँई निकाय, नगरपालिका तथा विशेष क्षेत्रहरूको संख्या र सीमाना निर्धारण गर्न एक आयोग गठन गर्नुपर्ने व्यवस्था छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
TP004,English,"Within what period after the commencement of the Constitution was the commission under Article 295(3) required to be constituted, and what was its term?","It had to be constituted within six months of the commencement of the Constitution, and its term was one year.",Article 295(3) states that the Commission under Article 295(3) must be constituted within six months after the commencement of the Constitution. The commission’s term is seven years.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP004,Nepali,संविधान प्रारम्भ भएको कति समयभित्र धारा २९५(३) बमोजिमको आयोग गठन गर्नुपर्ने थियो र यसको कार्यकाल कति थियो?,संविधान प्रारम्भ भएको छ महिनाभित्र आयोग गठन गर्नुपर्ने र यसको कार्यकाल एक वर्षको हुने थियो।,Article 305 of the Constitution states that a Commission for the Implementation of the Constitution (CIC) must be formed within 60 days of the constitution's commencement. This commission has been in operation since 1987.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
TP005,English,What happened to the Constituent Assembly existing at the commencement of the Constitution?,It was automatically converted into the Legislature-Parliament.,"Until elections to the Local Level are held in accordance with the Constitution, officials elected to the existing Local Bodies continue to hold office.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
TP005,Nepali,संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदाका बखत विद्यमान संविधान सभाको के भयो?,संविधान सभा स्वतः व्यवस्थापिका–संसदमा परिणत भयो।,"संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदाका बखत विद्यमान संविधान सभा, Constitution Assembly,  आँकियाँ छ। संविधान सभाले सन् १९४८ मा तयारвена गई थी।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP006,English,What happened to Bills under consideration in the Legislature-Parliament when the Constitution commenced?,They were automatically transferred to the Legislature-Parliament formed under Article 296(1).,"After one year from the date on which the first session of the Federal Parliament is held, an inconsistent law becomes invalid to the extent of its inconsistency.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
TP006,Nepali,संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदा व्यवस्थापिका–संसदमा विचाराधीन विधेयकहरूको के भयो?,ती विधेयकहरू धारा २९६(१) बमोजिमको व्यवस्थापिका–संसदमा स्वतः हस्तान्तरण भए।,"संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदा व्यवस्थापिका-संसदमा विचाराधीन विधेयकहरू निम्न छन्:

*   **भेलिग बिल (Bill of Passage):** यसले सरकारलाईislationको अधिकार दिन्छ।
*   **बदलाव बिल (Amendment Bill):** यो संविधानमा परिवर्तनहरूको लागि प्रयोग हुन्छ।
*   **प्रवचन बिल (Election Bill):** यसले निर्वाचन प्रणालीको व्यवस्थापन गर्छ।
*   **संसद् बिल (Constitutional Bill):** यो संविधानमा महत्त्वपूर्ण संशोधनहरू समावेश छ, जसमा सरकारको अधिकार, न्याय, र सामाजिक व्यवस्थाको विषयहरू शामिल छन्।

यो सूची पूर्ण छैन, तर ती विधेयकहरूको मुख्य रूपरेखा प्रस्तुत गरिएको हो।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP007,English,"Until the election to the House of Representatives was held under the Constitution, what functions did the transitional Legislature-Parliament perform?",It performed the business required to be performed by the Federal Parliament under the Constitution.,"The transitional Legislature-Parliament performed several key functions during the transition period until the first session of the Federal Parliament was held. These included:

*   **Reviewing and approving laws:** They were responsible for reviewing and approving new laws enacted under the Interim Constitution.
*   **Making recommendations to the President:** The Council of Ministers, acting on the recommendation of the Legislature-Parliament, presented recommendations to the President regarding issues related to implementation.
*   **Ensuring constitutional supremacy:** They ensured that existing laws remained in force until repealed or amended by the Constitution.
*   **Providing continuity and legal recognition:** They were tasked with maintaining continuity and recognizing existing laws during this transitional period.

Essentially, they acted as a crucial bridge between the old and new legal frameworks of Nepal.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP007,Nepali,संविधानबमोजिम प्रतिनिधि सभाको निर्वाचन नभएसम्म संक्रमणकालीन व्यवस्थापिका–संसदले कुन कार्य सम्पादन गर्थ्यो?,यसले संविधानबमोजिम संघीय संसदले गर्नुपर्ने कार्य सम्पादन गर्थ्यो।,"संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदाका सरकारी सेवामा कार्यरत कर्मचारीहरूलाई कानूनबमोजिम संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहमा समायोजन गरेर।

Here's a breakdown of why this is the correct answer and how it relates to Article 302(2):

* **Article 302(2) specifically states:** ""संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदाका सरकारी सेवामा कार्यरत कर्मचारीहरूलाई कानूनबमोजिम संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहमा समायोजन गरेर।"" (The Government of Nepal shall adjust employees serving in government services at the commencement of the Constitution among the Federal, State and Local levels in accordance with law.)

* **This action is a crucial part of the transitional period:** The transition from federal to local governments involves reorganizing personnel.  Article 302(2) ensures that these individuals are placed into their new roles within the existing framework.

Let me know if you'd like more detail on any specific aspect!",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP008,English,"Until a State Assembly was formed, who exercised the legislative power relating to matters listed in Schedule 6?",The Legislature-Parliament exercised that legislative power.,"According to Article 302(2) of the Constitution, until the Federal Parliament is formed, the following powers were exercised by the Government of Nepal:

*   **Local Bodies:** The government was responsible for overseeing and managing local bodies.
*   **State Governments:** The government was responsible for implementing laws and policies related to state governments.
*   **Federal Government:** The government was responsible for matters relating to the federal structure, including the establishment of the Federal Parliament.

Therefore, until the Federal Parliament was formed, the government exercised legislative power over these areas.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP008,Nepali,प्रदेश सभा गठन नभएसम्म अनुसूची–६ मा उल्लिखित विषयसम्बन्धी प्रदेशको विधायिकी अधिकार कसले प्रयोग गर्थ्यो?,व्यवस्थापिका–संसदले उक्त विधायिकी अधिकार प्रयोग गर्थ्यो।,"The government of Nepal utilized the authority granted to the State and Local governments under Article 302(2) of the Constitution to establish an agenda-six schedule, even before the formation of the Province Assembly. This allows for the consideration of issues related to the existing local bodies.

Here's a breakdown of how this is explained in the text:

*   **Article 302(2):** Grants the government authority to adjust employees serving in government services at the State and Local levels, according to law.
*   **The Transition Period:** The Constitution establishes a transitional period for local bodies until the new Local level structure is determined.
*   **Purpose of Agenda-Six:** This schedule allows for the consideration of issues related to existing local bodies during this transition period.

Therefore, the government used this authority to establish an agenda-six schedule, even before the Province Assembly was formed, to address matters relevant to the existing local bodies.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
TP009,English,Until when did the President and Vice-President existing at the commencement of the Constitution continue to hold office?,They continued to hold office until another President and Vice-President were elected in accordance with Article 297.,"Until elections to the Local level are held in accordance with the Constitution.,संविधानबमोजिम स्थानीय तहको निर्वाचन नभएसम्म,until elections to the Local level are held in accordance with the Constitution.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
TP009,Nepali,संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदाका बखत पदमा रहेका राष्ट्रपति र उपराष्ट्रपति कहिलेसम्म पदमा कायम रहने व्यवस्था थियो?,धारा २९७ बमोजिम अर्को राष्ट्रपति र उपराष्ट्रपति निर्वाचित नभएसम्म उनीहरू पदमा कायम रहने व्यवस्था थियो।,"Article 304 of the Constitution states that “the President and Vice-President shall hold office until the number and areas of the Local level are determined in accordance with the Constitution.” This provision establishes a continuity of office for these officials until the new Local Level structure is established. Therefore, they continue to hold their positions until the constitutionally mandated election process concludes.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
TP010,English,"If the Legislature-Parliament failed to reach a political understanding for electing the President and Vice-President, how were they to be elected?",They were to be elected by a majority of all the then members of the Legislature-Parliament.,"According to Article 305 of the Constitution, the election of the President and Vice-President is determined by the Legislature-Parliament. It states that “the President and Vice-President shall be elected by the Legislature-Parliament.”",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP010,Nepali,राष्ट्रपति र उपराष्ट्रपति निर्वाचित गर्न व्यवस्थापिका–संसदमा राजनीतिक सहमति हुन नसकेमा उनीहरू कसरी निर्वाचित हुने थिए?,व्यवस्थापिका–संसदका तत्काल कायम रहेका सम्पूर्ण सदस्यको बहुमतबाट निर्वाचित हुने थिए।,"Article 305 of the Constitution of Nepal states that the President and Vice-President are elected by the Federal Parliament through a political majority vote. However, there is no mechanism for them to be elected without the consent of the Legislature-Parliament. The Constitution provides for their election based on the will of the people, but it does not outline any specific process or procedure for their selection.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
TP011,English,What minimum proportion of the total number of then members of the Legislature-Parliament could move an impeachment motion against the transitional President or Vice-President for serious violation of the Constitution and law?,At least one-fourth of the total number of the then members of the Legislature-Parliament.,"Article 305, Section 1(a) of the Constitution states that “the Legislature-Parliament may move an impeachment motion against the transitional President or Vice-President for serious violations of the Constitution and law.” This provision grants the legislature the power to investigate and remove these officials if they are found to be acting in violation of the constitution.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
TP011,Nepali,संविधान र कानूनको गम्भीर उल्लङ्घन गरेको आधारमा संक्रमणकालीन राष्ट्रपति वा उपराष्ट्रपतिविरुद्ध महाभियोग प्रस्ताव ल्याउन व्यवस्थापिका–संसदका तत्काल कायम रहेका कुल सदस्य संख्याको कम्तीमा कति भाग आवश्यक पर्थ्यो?,व्यवस्थापिका–संसदका तत्काल कायम रहेका कुल सदस्य संख्याको कम्तीमा एक चौथाइ।,संविधान र कानूनको गम्भीर उल्लङ्घन गरिएको आधारमा संक्रमणकालीन राष्ट्रपति वा उपराष्ट्रपतिविरुद्ध महाभियोग प्रस्ताव ल्याउन व्यवस्थापिका–संसदका तत्काल कायम रहेका कुल सदस्य संख्याको कम्तीमा ३४ भाग आवश्यक पर्थ्यो।,Correct,Not a strict error,False
TP012,English,What majority was required for an impeachment motion against the transitional President or Vice-President to remove them from office?,A two-thirds majority of the total number of the then members of the Legislature-Parliament was required.,"Article 305 of the Constitution of Nepal, Section 305, states that “the majority required for impeachment motion against the transitional President or Vice-President is two-thirds (2/3) of the members of the House of Representatives.”",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP012,Nepali,संक्रमणकालीन राष्ट्रपति वा उपराष्ट्रपतिलाई पदबाट हटाउन महाभियोग प्रस्ताव पारित गर्न कस्तो बहुमत आवश्यक पर्थ्यो?,व्यवस्थापिका–संसदका तत्काल कायम रहेका कुल सदस्य संख्याको दुई तिहाइ बहुमत आवश्यक पर्थ्यो।,"संविधानको धारा ३०३(१) अनुसार, यदि कुनै व्यक्तिले संविधानमा नमूदको रूपमाspecifiedका समूहहरूलाई (जैसे कि अल्पसंख्यक) कमजोर बनाउनु हो भने, तर उनको पदमा रहे, महाभियोग प्रस्ताव पारित गर्न ७५% बहुमत आवश्यक पर्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP013,English,What happened to the Council of Ministers existing at the commencement of the Constitution?,It continued to exist until the Council of Ministers under Article 298(2) was formed.,"Until elections to the Local level are held in accordance with the Constitution, officials elected to the existing Local Bodies continue to hold office.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
TP013,Nepali,संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदाका बखत विद्यमान मन्त्रिपरिषद्को के भयो?,धारा २९८(२) बमोजिमको मन्त्रिपरिषद् गठन नभएसम्म विद्यमान मन्त्रिपरिषद् कायम रह्यो।,"संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदाका बखत विद्यमान मन्त्रिपरिषद्को नाम “Minister of Government” हुन्छ।"",""Constitution Established Until the Date, Minister of Government was established.""",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP014,English,Within what period was the Prime Minister required to be elected after the commencement of the Constitution when the Legislature-Parliament was not in recess?,The Prime Minister had to be elected no later than seven days after the commencement of the Constitution.,"Article 305, Definitions and Interpretations, Law, Definition, Easy, What does the term “Law” mean under Article 306 of the Constitution?,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “कानून” भन्नाले के जनाउँछ?,It means Federal law, State law, and Local law."",""“कानून” भन्नाले संघीय कानून, प्रदेश कानून र स्थानीय कानुन बुझिन्छ।"",The constitutional definition recognizes laws made at all three levels of the federal structure.,Art. 306(1)(c),Definitions and interpretations,,,,,,",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
TP014,Nepali,व्यवस्थापिका–संसद अधिवेशनमा नरहेको अवस्थामा संविधान प्रारम्भ भएपछि कति समयभित्र प्रधानमन्त्री निर्वाचित गर्नुपर्ने थियो?,संविधान प्रारम्भ भएको सात दिनभित्र प्रधानमन्त्री निर्वाचित गर्नुपर्ने थियो।,"संविधान अनुसार, व्यवस्थापिका–संसद अधिवेशनमा नरहेको अवस्थामा प्रधानमन्त्री निर्वाचित गर्नुपर्ने समय २० वर्षभित्रै थ हुन्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP015,English,"If political understanding could not be reached for electing the Prime Minister, how was the Prime Minister elected?",The Prime Minister was elected by a majority of all the then members of the Legislature-Parliament.,"According to Article 305 of the Constitution, the Prime Minister is elected through a parliamentary vote of confidence. This means that if there’s no consensus among the members of Parliament (the House of Representatives), they must pass a motion for a new election.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP015,Nepali,प्रधानमन्त्री निर्वाचित गर्न राजनीतिक सहमति हुन नसकेमा प्रधानमन्त्री कसरी निर्वाचित हुने व्यवस्था थियो?,व्यवस्थापिका–संसदका तत्काल कायम रहेका सम्पूर्ण सदस्यको बहुमतबाट प्रधानमन्त्री निर्वाचित हुने व्यवस्था थियो।,"संविधान २०६५ अनुसार, प्रधानमन्त्रीलाई राजनीतिक सहमतिले निर्णय नहुँदा निर्वाचित गर्नुपर्ने व्यवस्था थियो। संविधानको धारा ३०३(१) बमोजिम, प्रधानमन्त्रीलाई सरकारका नेतृत्वमा राख्ने व्यवस्था छ, तर त्यसलाई निर्वाचित गर्नुपर्ने सम्भावना छैन।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP016,English,What minimum composition of the Council of Ministers was expressly provided under Article 298?,"It consisted of the Prime Minister, a Deputy Prime Minister, and other Ministers as required.",Article 298 of the Constitution of Nepal states that the Council of Ministers shall be composed of at least **three** members.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
TP016,Nepali,धारा २९८ बमोजिम गठन हुने मन्त्रिपरिषद्को न्यूनतम संरचनामा को–को रहने व्यवस्था थियो?,"प्रधानमन्त्री, एक उपप्रधानमन्त्री तथा आवश्यकताअनुसार अन्य मन्त्रीहरू रहने व्यवस्था थियो।","धारा २९८ बमोजिम गठन हुने मन्त्रिपरिषद्को न्यूनतम संरचनामा, माइनर (Minor) र सिएन (Sen) सदस्यहरू रहलान्छन्।",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
TP017,English,From whom did the Prime Minister appoint Ministers under the transitional arrangement?,Ministers were appointed from among the members of the Legislature-Parliament on the recommendation of the concerned party.,"Article 305 grants this temporary power to the President, subject to a recommendation from the Council of Ministers.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP017,Nepali,संक्रमणकालीन व्यवस्थाअन्तर्गत प्रधानमन्त्रीले मन्त्रीहरू कसबाट नियुक्त गर्थे?,सम्बन्धित दलको सिफारिसमा व्यवस्थापिका–संसदका सदस्यहरूमध्येबाट मन्त्री नियुक्त गरिन्थ्यो।,"Article 302(2) permits employee adjustment among the three levels of government to support service delivery. This means that the Government of Nepal can appoint ministers and other officials to various positions within the government, including those involved in providing services at the state and local levels during the transition period. The process is governed by law and involves adjusting employees serving in government services at the commencement of the Constitution among the Federal, State and Local levels in accordance with law.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
TP018,English,What minimum proportion of the then members of the Legislature-Parliament could table a written motion of no-confidence against the transitional Prime Minister?,At least one-fourth of the total number of the then members of the Legislature-Parliament.,"Article 305 of the Constitution of Nepal, 2007 states that “The Legislature-Parliament may table a written motion of no-confidence against the transitional Prime Minister not less than 2/3 (two-thirds) of the then members of the Legislature-Parliament.”",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP018,Nepali,संक्रमणकालीन प्रधानमन्त्रीविरुद्ध लिखित अविश्वास प्रस्ताव ल्याउन व्यवस्थापिका–संसदका तत्काल कायम रहेका सदस्य संख्याको कम्तीमा कति भाग आवश्यक पर्थ्यो?,व्यवस्थापिका–संसदका तत्काल कायम रहेका कुल सदस्य संख्याको कम्तीमा एक चौथाइ।,"Article 305 of the Constitution of Nepal, 2006, states that if a member of Parliament (Parliament) submits an objection to the implementation of the constitution, it must be supported by at least the number of members required by law. The number of members required by law is determined by the Federal Parliament.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
TP019,English,Within what period were the Speaker and Deputy Speaker required to be elected after the commencement of the Constitution when the Legislature-Parliament was not in recess?,They had to be elected no later than twenty days after the commencement of the Constitution.,"Article 303(1) ensures continuity of existing Local Bodies during the transition to the constitutional Local level structure. It states that elections to officials of existing Local Bodies shall be held according to law. Therefore, until elections are held according to the Constitution, officials elected to the existing Local Bodies continue to hold office.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP019,Nepali,व्यवस्थापिका–संसद अधिवेशनमा नरहेको अवस्थामा संविधान प्रारम्भ भएपछि सभामुख र उपसभामुख कति समयभित्र निर्वाचित गर्नुपर्ने थियो?,संविधान प्रारम्भ भएको बीस दिनभित्र सभामुख र उपसभामुख निर्वाचित गर्नुपर्ने थियो।,"संविधान अनुसार, व्यवस्थापक (Chief) र उपव्यवस्थापक (Vice-President) को कार्यकाल सकभर पाँच वर्ष हुन्छ। यसको कारण हो कि संविधानले व्यवस्थापक र उपव्यवस्थापकलाई सरकारमा सहभागिता दिन्छ तर आफ्नो अधिकार सीमित गर्दछ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP020,English,What requirement applied to the political-party representation of the Speaker and Deputy Speaker elected under Article 299?,They had to be members representing different political parties in the Legislature-Parliament.,"Article 299 states that the Political-Party Representation of the Speaker and Deputy Speaker must be based on the number of seats allocated to each party in the National Assembly. Therefore, the requirement is that the political-party representation should reflect the proportion of seats allocated to each party within the National Assembly.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP020,Nepali,धारा २९९ बमोजिम निर्वाचित सभामुख र उपसभामुखको राजनीतिक दलसम्बन्धी प्रतिनिधित्वमा के व्यवस्था थियो?,उनीहरू व्यवस्थापिका–संसदमा प्रतिनिधित्व गर्ने फरक–फरक राजनीतिक दलका सदस्य हुनुपर्ने थियो।,"धारा २९९ बमोजिम निर्वाचित सभामुख र उपसभामुखको राजनीतिक दलसम्बन्धी प्रतिनिधित्वमा नेपालका संविधानले निम्न व्यवस्था दिन्छ।

*   **राजनीतिक दलहरूको संख्या:** प्रत्येक राजनीतिक दललाई सरकारमा प्रतिनिधित्व गर्न पाउँदा, त्यसको संख्या ५ प्रतिशत अधिकतम हुन्छ।
*   **दलहरूको सहभागिता:** पाँचतम दलहरूलाई सरकारमा सहभागी दिन मिल्नेछन्।
*   **सभामुखको अधिकार:** उपसभामुखको पनि अधिकार हुन्छ।

संक्षेप में, संविधानले राजनीतिक दलहरूको प्रतिनिधित्वका लागि एक प्रणाली प्रदान गर्दछ जसले उनका संख्या अनुसार सरकारमा भाग लिन्छ र उपसभामुखको अधिकार दिन्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP021,English,How were the Speaker and Deputy Speaker required to perform their functions under Article 299?,They had to perform their functions as neutral persons without standing for or against any political party.,"According to Article 299, the Speaker and Deputy Speaker are required to perform the following functions:

*   **To oversee the work of the House:** They are responsible for overseeing the overall operation and management of the House.
*   **To ensure the smooth functioning of the House:** This includes maintaining order, facilitating debates, and ensuring that all proceedings take place according to the rules of law.
*   **To represent the House:** They must act as representatives of the House in all matters related to its governance.

In essence, they are crucial for the effective operation and administration of the legislative body.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP021,Nepali,धारा २९९ बमोजिम सभामुख र उपसभामुखले आफ्नो कार्य कसरी सम्पादन गर्नुपर्ने थियो?,कुनै पनि राजनीतिक दलको पक्ष वा विपक्षमा नउभिई तटस्थ व्यक्तिको रूपमा कार्य सम्पादन गर्नुपर्ने थियो।,"धारा २९९ बमोजिम सभामुख र उपसभामुखले आफ्नो कार्य संविधानको अनुसार, स्थानीय तहमा सेवा प्रवाहलाई व्यवस्थित गराउनुको लागि सँधित तरतव्यको व्यवस्थापन गर्नुपर्ने थियो।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP022,English,What majority was required for a resolution declaring that the conduct of the Speaker or Deputy Speaker was incompatible with the office?,A majority of at least two-thirds of the total number of members of the Legislature-Parliament was required.,"Article 305 of the Constitution of Nepal, Section 305, states that “the President, on the recommendation of the Government of Nepal, Council of Ministers, may issue an order to declare that the conduct of the Speaker or Deputy Speaker was incompatible with the office.”

Therefore, a majority of 2/3 (60%) of the members of the House of Representatives (Federal Parliament) were required for this resolution to be valid.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP022,Nepali,सभामुख वा उपसभामुखको आचरण निजको पदसँग अनुकूल नभएको घोषणा गर्ने प्रस्ताव पारित गर्न कस्तो बहुमत आवश्यक पर्थ्यो?,व्यवस्थापिका–संसदका कुल सदस्य संख्याको कम्तीमा दुई तिहाइ बहुमत आवश्यक पर्थ्यो।,"अनुच्छेद ३०६(२) अनुसार, सभामुख वा उपसभामुखको आचरण निजको पदसँग अनुकूल नभएको घोषणा गर्ने प्रस्ताव पारित गर्नमा न्यूनतम बहुमत आवश्यक पर्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP023,English,Which existing courts continued to exist until the judicial structure provided for in the Constitution was established?,"The Supreme Court, Constituent Assembly Court, Appellate Courts, and District Courts continued to exist.",Article 303(1) ensures continuity of existing Local Bodies during the transition to the constitutional Local level structure.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
TP023,Nepali,संविधानमा व्यवस्था गरिएको न्यायपालिकाको संरचना स्थापना नभएसम्म कुन–कुन विद्यमान अदालतहरू कायम रहने व्यवस्था थियो?,"सर्वोच्च अदालत, संविधान सभा अदालत, पुनरावेदन अदालत र जिल्ला अदालतहरू कायम रहने व्यवस्था थियो।",Article 303 of the Constitution ensures continuity of existing Local Bodies during the transitional period. The Constitution provides for the continued existence of these bodies until elections to the Local level are held in accordance with the Constitution.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
TP024,English,What happened to cases pending in the Appellate Courts after the establishment of the High Courts?,They were transferred to the High Courts specified by the Government of Nepal in consultation with the Judicial Council.,"After the establishment of the High Courts, existing cases pending in the Appellate courts were transferred to them. The Constitution provides for this transfer as part of the transition process. Specifically, Article 305 states that “cases pending in the appellate courts shall be transferred to the high courts.” This ensures a smooth and orderly transition of judicial matters within Nepal’s legal system.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP024,Nepali,उच्च अदालत स्थापना भएपछि पुनरावेदन अदालतमा विचाराधीन मुद्दाहरूको के हुने व्यवस्था थियो?,न्याय परिषद्सँग परामर्श गरी नेपाल सरकारले तोकेका उच्च अदालतहरूमा ती मुद्दाहरू हस्तान्तरण गरिने व्यवस्था थियो।,"उच्च अदालत स्थापना भएपछि पुनरावेदन अदालतमा विचाराधीन मुद्दाहरूलाई निम्न प्रकारको श्रेणीतर्फ धेरै समस्याहरू आउन सक्ने व्यवस्था थियो। यहाँ तरिकाexplained गरिएको छ:

*   **अधिकारिक जाँच:** उच्च अदालतले पहिलेचाहि मुद्दाहरूको समीक्षा गर्नुपर्ने व्यवस्था हो, जसले मुद्दाको आधारमा न्यायको निर्णय सकेन मापन गर्छ।
*   **सुरुचिपूर्ण जाँच:** यदि मुद्दालाई उच्च अदालतमा दाखिन्छ भने, यसले मुद्दाको विषयवस्तु, मुद्दामा जोडने पक्षका 주장, मुद्दामा आधारित दास्तानहरू, र मुद्दाको उद्देश्यको बारेमा जाँच गरिने व्यवस्था हो।
*   **अधिकारिक निर्णय:** यदि उच्च अदालतले फैसलामा सहमति गर्छ भने, तर मुद्दालाई पुनरावेदन अदालतमा दाखिन्छ भने, यसले मुद्दाको विषयवस्तु, मुद्दामा जोडने पक्षका 주장, मुद्दामा आधारित दास्तानहरू, र मुद्दाको उद्देश्यको बारेमा जाँच गरिने व्यवस्था हो।
*   **सुरुचिपूर्ण जाँच:** उच्च अदालतले मुद्दाको समीक्षा गर्छ तर फैसलामा सहमति गर्दैनथै, मुद्दालाई पुनरावेदन अदालतमा दाखिन्छ भने, यसले मुद्दाको विषयवस्तु, मुद्दामा जोडने पक्षका 주장, मुद्दामा आधारित दास्तानहरू, र मुद्दाको उद्देश्यको बारेमा जाँच गरिने व्यवस्था हो।
*   **सुरुचिपूर्ण निर्णय:** उच्च अदालतले फैसलामा सहमति गर्छ तर फैसलामा मद्दूलन गर्दैनथै, मुद्दालाई पुनरावेदन अदालतमा दाखिन्छ भने, यसले मुद्दाको विषयवस्तु, मुद्दामा जोडने पक्षका 주장, मुद्दामा आधारित दास्तानहरू, र मुद्दाको उद्देश्यको बारेमा जाँच गरिने व्यवस्था हो।
*   **अधिकारिक निर्णय:** उच्च अदालतले फैसलामा सहमति गर्छ तर फैसलामा मद्दूलन गर्दैनथै, मुद्दालाई पुनरावेदन अदालतमा दाखिन्छ भने, यसले मुद्दाको विषयवस्तु, मुद्दामा जोडने पक्षका 주장, मुद्दामा आधारित दास्तानहरू, र मुद्दाको उद्देश्यको बारे मापन गरिने व्यवस्था हो।

त्यसैले, उच्च अदालतले मुद्दाहरूको समीक्षा गर्नुपर्ने व्यवस्था हो, तर मुद्दालाई पुनरावेदन अदालतमा दाखिन्छ भने, यसले न्यायको निर्णय सकेन मापन गर्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP029,English,How are Constitutional Bodies existing at the commencement of the Constitution treated under Article 301?,They are deemed to have been formed under the Constitution.,"Article 301 states that “the constitutional bodies shall continue to exist until the number and areas of the Local level are determined in accordance with the Constitution.” Therefore, constitutional bodies – including local councils – will remain existing until the constitution establishes their structure and scope.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP029,Nepali,संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदा विद्यमान संवैधानिक निकायहरूलाई धारा ३०१ अन्तर्गत कसरी मानिन्छ?,संविधानअन्तर्गत गठन भएको मानिन्छ।,Article 301 states that existing constitutional bodies shall be treated as existing under the Constitution until they are repealed or amended.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
TP030,English,What happens to matters under consideration by existing Constitutional Bodies when the Constitution commences?,They may continue to be settled subject to the Constitution.,"After one year from the date on which the first session of the Federal Parliament is held, an inconsistent law becomes invalid to the extent of its inconsistency.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
TP030,Nepali,संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदा विद्यमान संवैधानिक निकायहरूमा विचाराधीन विषयहरूको के हुन्छ?,संविधानको अधीनमा रही तिनको निरूपण जारी रहन सक्छ।,"संविधानको सुरुदेखि, नेपालका विभिन्न संवैधानिक निकायहरूमा अनेकत्र विचाराधीन विषयहरू छन्। यी विषयहरूलाई मुख्यतया तीन समूहमध्ये एकर फरक-फरक देखाउन सकिएछन्। यहाँ ती विषयहरूको बुझानो बताइएको छ:

*   **स्थानीय तहको व्यवस्था:** स्थानीय तहको संरचना, कार्यकाल, र प्रशासनको बारेमा प्रश्नहरू उठउन्।
*   **संसद् वा संघीय संसदको भूमिका:** ससंद् भन्नको कार्यको अर्थ, तरिका, र प्रभावलाई जाँच गर्न सकिएछन्।
*   **कानूनको कार्यान्वयन:** कानूनको 시행को प्रक्रियामा आएका समस्याहरूको समाधान खोज्न सकिएछन्।

त्यसैले, संविधानको सुरुदेखि, नेपालका विभिन्न संवैधानिक निकायहरूमा अनेकत्र प्रश्नहरू उठउन्।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP031,English,How are chiefs and officials of Constitutional Bodies holding office at the commencement of the Constitution treated?,They are deemed to have been appointed under the Constitution.,"According to Article 305 of the Constitution, chiefs and officials of constitutional bodies (Federal Parliament, State Parliament, and Local Councils) continue to hold their positions until elections to the local level are held in accordance with the Constitution.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP031,Nepali,संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदा पदमा रहेका संवैधानिक निकायका प्रमुख तथा पदाधिकारीहरूलाई कसरी मानिन्छ?,संविधानअन्तर्गत नियुक्त भएको मानिन्छ।,"Article 305 of the Constitution states that “the President, on the recommendation of the Government of Nepal, Council of Ministers.” This means that the President, along with the Council of Ministers, is responsible for appointing and overseeing the key officials within the government institutions, including those involved in the administration of justice and ensuring compliance with the constitution.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
TP032,English,Under what conditions may existing chiefs and officials of Constitutional Bodies continue in office?,They continue subject to the conditions of service applicable at the time of their appointment.,Article 303(3) of the Constitution provides continuity for elected local officials until elections to the Local Level are held. This means that officials currently holding positions within their respective Local Bodies will remain in office as long as the election process is completed according to the Constitution.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
TP032,Nepali,विद्यमान संवैधानिक निकायका प्रमुख तथा पदाधिकारीहरू कुन शर्तमा पदमा कायम रहन सक्छन्?,नियुक्तिको समयमा लागू रहेका सेवाका शर्तहरूको अधीनमा रही।,"Article 302(2) permits employee adjustment among the three levels of government to support service delivery. This means that the key conditions for continued employment are:

*   **They are serving in government services at the State and Local levels.** This is the core requirement – they must be working within these governmental entities.
*   **They are under the law.** The adjustment must comply with existing laws and regulations governing their roles.

Essentially, it's a temporary arrangement based on existing legal frameworks.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
TP033,English,What special provision applies to officials of the Commission for the Investigation of Abuse of Authority and the Public Service Commission who exceed the number specified in the Constitution?,They may continue to hold office subject to the conditions of service applicable at the time of their appointment.,Article 304(2) of the Constitution states that elections to officials of existing Local Bodies shall be held according to law. This provision applies specifically to officials of the Commission for the Investigation of Abuse of Authority and the Public Service Commission who exceed the number specified in the Constitution.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
TP033,Nepali,संविधानमा तोकिएको संख्याभन्दा बढी रहेका अख्तियार दुरुपयोग अनुसन्धान आयोग र लोक सेवा आयोगका पदाधिकारीसम्बन्धी विशेष व्यवस्था के हो?,उनीहरू नियुक्तिको समयमा लागू रहेका सेवाका शर्तहरूको अधीनमा रही पदमा कायम रहन सक्छन्।,"Article 304 of the Constitution outlines the specific measures taken to ensure continuity of power and prevent abuse of authority during the transitional period. Here’s a breakdown of what it specifies:

*   **Appointment of Commissioners:** The constitution mandates that the President appoints the Commissioner of the Council of Ministers (Government) and the Chief Investigator of the Anti-Corruption Commission (Anti-Corruption Commission).
*   **Specific Powers for Commissioners:** These commissioners have specific powers to investigate allegations of misuse of power, conduct inquiries, and recommend actions.
*   **Independent Oversight:** The Constitution establishes a system of independent oversight – the Council of Ministers and the Anti-Corruption Commission – to review these appointments and ensure accountability.

Essentially, the Constitution creates a framework for ensuring that those in charge of government affairs are accountable and cannot abuse their power during this crucial transition period.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
TP034,English,Who is responsible for making necessary provisions for the delivery of services at the State and Local levels?,The Government of Nepal.,"Article 302(2) permits employee adjustment among the three levels of government to support service delivery. Therefore, the Government of Nepal is responsible for making necessary provisions for the delivery of services at the State and Local levels.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
TP034,Nepali,प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहमा सेवा प्रवाहका लागि आवश्यक व्यवस्था गर्ने जिम्मेवारी कसको हो?,नेपाल सरकारको।,"संविधान अनुसार, प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहमा सेवा प्रवाहका लागि आवश्यक व्यवस्था गर्ने जिम्मेवारी नेपाल सरकारको हुन्छ। संविधानले सरकारी अधिकारीलाई प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहमा सेवा प्रवाह सुनिश्चित गर्न दिन्छ तर त्यसको कार्यान्वयनमा सरकारले प्रयोग गर्छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
TP035,English,How may the Government of Nepal arrange for the delivery of services at the State and Local levels during the transition?,"By adjusting employees serving in government services at the commencement of the Constitution among the Federal, State and Local levels in accordance with law.","The government of Nepal can arrange for the delivery of services at the state and local level during the transitional period through several mechanisms, primarily focusing on adjusting employee roles and responsibilities. Here’s a breakdown of how they plan to do this, based on the provided text:

*   **Adjusting Employee Roles:** The core mechanism is to adjust employees serving in government services at the commencement of the Constitution among the Federal, State and Local levels in accordance with law. This involves restructuring existing teams and assigning responsibilities accordingly.
*   **Article 302(2):** This article permits employee adjustment among the three levels of government to support service delivery.
*   **Transition Period Management:** The government will continue to manage these services until the number and areas of local level are determined in accordance with the Constitution.
*   **Ongoing Review & Adjustment:**  The government intends to review and adjust existing laws, particularly those related to Local Bodies, as the transition progresses.

Essentially, it’s a phased approach involving adjustments based on the constitutional framework and ongoing monitoring of the transition period.",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
TP035,Nepali,संक्रमणकालमा प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहमा सेवा प्रवाहको व्यवस्था नेपाल सरकारले कसरी गर्न सक्छ?,"संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदाका सरकारी सेवामा कार्यरत कर्मचारीहरूलाई कानूनबमोजिम संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहमा समायोजन गरेर।","By adjusting employees serving in government services at the commencement of the Constitution among the Federal, State and Local levels in accordance with law."",""संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदाका सरकारी सेवामा कार्यरत कर्मचारीहरूलाई कानूनबमोजिम संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहमा समायोजन गरेर।"",कानूनबमोजिम,"",""संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदाका सरकारी सेवामा कार्यरत कर्मचारीहरूलाई कानूनबमोजिम संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहमा समायोजन गरेर।"",Article 302(2) permits employee adjustment among the three levels of government to support service delivery.,Art. 302(2),Formation and operation of government services at State and Local levels,,,,,,
TP036,Transitional Provisions,Local Bodies,Factual,Easy,How may the Government of Nepal arrange for the delivery of services at the State and Local levels during the transition?,संक्रमणकालमा प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहमा सेवा प्रवाहको व्यवस्था नेपाल सरकारले कसरी गर्न सक्छ?"",संक्रमणकालमा प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहमा सेवा प्रवाहको व्यवस्था नेपाल सरकारले कसरी गर्न सक्छ?"",In accordance with law.,कानूनबमोजिम।,Article 302(2) permits employee adjustment among the three levels of government to support service delivery.,Art. 302(2),Formation and operation of government services at State and Local levels,,,,,,
TP037,Transitional Provisions,Local Bodies,Factual,Easy,How are elections to officials of the existing Local Bodies conducted during the transitional period?,संक्रमणकालमा विद्यमान स्थानीय निकायका पदाधिकारीहरूको निर्वाचन कसरी गरिन्छ?,In accordance with law.,कानूनबमोजिम।,Article 303(1) ensures continuity of existing Local Bodies during the transition to the constitutional Local level structure."",""संविधानबमोजिम स्थानीय तहको निर्वाचन नभएसम्म"",संविधानसँग बाझिएको विद्यमान कानूनहरूबारे सामान्य व्यवस्था के हो?,संविधानले तरिका बनाएर स्थानीय निकायमा निर्वाचित पदाधिकारीहरू कहिलेसम्म पदमा कायम रहन्छन्?"",संविधानले तरिका बनाएर स्थानीय निकायमा निर्वाचित पदाधिकारीहरू कहिलेसम्म पदमा कायम रहन्छन्?"",संविधानको धारा ३०३(१) अन्तर्गत, Elected local officials को निर्वाचन कसरी गरिन्छ?,The Constitution provides a transitional period before inconsistent pre-existing laws automatically become invalid to the extent of their inconsistency."",""संविधानले तरिका बनाएर स्थानीय निकायमा निर्वाचित पदाधिकारीहरू कहिलेसम्म पदमा कायम रहन्छन्?"",The Constitution provides a transitional period before inconsistent pre-existing laws automatically become invalid to the extent of their inconsistency."",Article 304(1) preserves existing laws to avoid a legal vacuum during constitutional transition.,Art. 304(1),Existing laws to remain in force,,,,,,
TP038,Transitional Provisions,Existing Laws,Factual,Medium,Until when do officials elected to the existing Local Bodies continue to hold office?,संक्रमणकालमा निर्वाचित स्थानीय निकायमा पदाधिकारीहरू कहिलेसम्म पदमा कायम रहन्छन्?,""Until elections to the Local level are held in accordance with the Constitution.,संविधानबमोजिम स्थानीय तहको निर्वाचन नभएसम्म"",The election to the Local level must occur before the first session of the Federal Parliament is held, according to the Constitution."",Article 303(3) provides continuity for elected local officials until the new Local level elections take place."",""Until elections to the Local level are held in accordance with the Constitution.,The Constitution provides a transitional period before inconsistent pre-existing laws automatically become invalid to the extent of their inconsistency."",The Constitution provides a transitional period before inconsistent pre-existing laws automatically become invalid to the extent of their inconsistency."",Art. 304(1),Existing laws to remain in force,,,,,,
TP039,Transitional Provisions,Existing Laws,Factual,Hard,What is the general rule regarding Nepalese laws in force when the Constitution commences?,संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदा प्रचलित नेपालका कानूनहरूबारे सामान्य व्यवस्था के हो?,They continue to remain in force until repealed or amended.,खारेज वा संशोधन नभएसम्म ती कानूनहरू कायम रहन्छन्।,Article 304(2) provides continuity and legal recognition for peace-process-related acts carried out under the Interim Constitution.,Art. 304(2),Existing laws to remain in force,,,,,,
TP040,Transitional Provisions,Existing Laws,Factual,After what event and period does the inconsistency rule for existing laws take effect under Article 304(1)?,धारा ३०४(१) अन्तर्गत विद्यमान कानूनको असंगतिसम्बन्धी व्यवस्था कुन घटना र अवधिपछि लागू हुन्छ?,""After one year from the date on which the first session of the Federal Parliament is held, an inconsistent law becomes invalid to the extent of its inconsistency."",आदेश जारी भएपछि तुरुन्त बस्ने व्यवस्थापिका–संसद् वा संघीय संसद्समक्ष अनुमोदनका लागि पेश गर्नुपर्छ।,The power to remove difficulties is temporary and subject to legislative oversight through subsequent approval.,Art. 304(1),Existing laws to remain in force,,,,,,
DF001,Definitions and Interpretations,Peace Process,Definition,Easy,Which groups are considered “peace process” under Article 306?,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “शान्ति प्रक्रिया” भन्नाले के जनाउँछ?,A peace process includes ethnic, linguistic, and religious groups whose population is below the percentage specified by Federal law, including groups with distinct ethnic, religious, or linguistic characteristics and aspirations to protect them that have been subjected to discrimination and oppression."",""संघीय कानूनले तोकेको प्रतिशतभन्दा कम जनसंख्या भएका जातीय, भाषिक र धार्मिक समूहहरू, साथै आफ्ना विशिष्ट जातीय, धार्मिक वा भाषिक विशेषता संरक्षण गर्ने आकांक्षा भएका र विभेद तथा उत्पीडनमा परेका समूहहरूलाई अल्पसंख्यक भनिन्छ।"",The constitutional definition limits the term to a citizen of Nepal.,Art. 306(1)(c),Definitions and interpretations,,,,,,
DF002,Definitions and Interpretations,Law,Definition,Easy,What does the term “law” refer to under Article 306?,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “कानून” भन्नाले के बुझिन्छ?,""“Law” means Federal law, State law, and Local law."",""“कानून” भन्नाले संघीय कानून, प्रदेश कानून र स्थानीय कानून बुझिन्छ।"",The constitutional definition recognizes laws made at all three levels of the federal structure.,Art. 306(1)(d),Definitions and interpretations,,,,,,
DF003,Definitions and Interpretations,Article,Definition,Easy,What does the term “Article” refer to under Article 306?,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “धारा” भन्नाले के जनाउँछ?,""“Article” means an Article of the Constitution.,संविधानको धारा।,The term is specifically defined as a provision of the Constitution itself.,Art. 306(1)(e),Definitions and interpretations,,,,,,
DF004,Definitions and Interpretations,Municipality,Definition,Easy,What entities are included within the constitutional definition of “Municipality”?,संवैधानिक रूपमा “नगरपालिका” को परिभाषाभित्र कुन निकायहरू पर्छन्?,""नगरपालिका भन्नाले महानगरपालिका र उपमहानगरपालिका समेत जनाउँछ."",A Municipality includes a Municipal Corporation and a Sub-municipal Corporation.,The definition gives “Municipality” a broader meaning by expressly including Municipal Corporations and Sub-municipal Corporations."",Art. 306(1)(d),Definitions and Interpretations,,,,,,
DF005,Definitions and Interpretions,Citizen,Definition,Easy,Who is considered a “citizen” under Article 306?,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “नागरिक” भन्नाले कसलाई जनाउँछ?,""A citizen means a citizen of Nepal.,“नागरিক” भन्नाले नेपालको नागरिकलाई जनाउँछ।,The constitutional definition limits the term to a citizen of Nepal.,Art. 306(1)(e),Definitions and Interpretations,,,,,,",Question repetition / non-answer,Question repetition / non-answer,True
TP036,English,How long do the Local Bodies existing at the commencement of the Constitution continue to exist?,Until the number and areas of the Local level are determined in accordance with the Constitution.,"Until the number and areas of the Local level are determined in accordance with the Constitution.,संविधानबमोजिम स्थानीय तहको संख्या र क्षेत्र निर्धारण नभएसम्म।,Until the number and areas of the Local level are determined in accordance with the Constitution,",Correct,Not a strict error,False
TP036,Nepali,संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदा विद्यमान स्थानीय निकायहरू कति समयसम्म कायम रहन्छन्?,संविधानबमोजिम स्थानीय तहको संख्या र क्षेत्र निर्धारण नभएसम्म।,"संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदा विद्यमान स्थानीय निकायहरू कति समयसम्म कायम रहन्छन्, तक संविधानसँग बाझिएको विद्यमान कानूनहरूबारे सामान्य व्यवस्था के हो?,संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदा प्रचलित नेपालका कानूनहरूबारे सामान्य व्यवस्था के हो?,They continue to remain in force until repealed or amended."",""संविधान भित्रैले कानून परिवर्तन गर्नबाट सुरक्षित हुन्छ।"",The Constitution provides a transitional period before inconsistent pre-existing laws automatically become invalid to the extent of their inconsistency.""",Question repetition / non-answer,Question repetition / non-answer,True
TP037,English,How are elections to officials of the existing Local Bodies conducted during the transitional period?,In accordance with law.,"In accordance with law.,कानूनबमोजिम।,Article 303(1) ensures continuity of existing Local Body members during the transition to the new structure."",""संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदाका सरकारी सेवामा कार्यरत कर्मचारीहरूलाई कानूनबमोजिम संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहमा समायोजन गरेर।"",By adjusting employees serving in government services at the commencement of the Constitution among the Federal, State and Local levels in accordance with law."",""संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदाका सरकारी सेवामा कार्यरत कर्मचारीहरूलाई कानूनबमोजिम संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय तहमा समायोजन गरेर。"",Article 303(1) ensures continuity of existing Local Body members during the transition to the constitutional Local level structure.,Art. 303(1),Provisions relating to Local Bodies,,,,,,",Correct,Not a strict error,False
TP037,Nepali,संक्रमणकालमा विद्यमान स्थानीय निकायका पदाधिकारीहरूको निर्वाचन कसरी गरिन्छ?,कानूनबमोजिम।,"In accordance with law.,कानूनबमोजिम।,Article 303(2) ensures continuity of existing Local Bodies during the transition to the constitutional Local level structure.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
TP038,English,Until when do officials elected to the existing Local Bodies continue to hold office?,Until elections to the Local level are held in accordance with the Constitution.,"Until elections to the Local level are held in accordance with the Constitution.,संविधानबमोजिम स्थानीय तहको निर्वाचन नभएसम्म,until elections to the Local level are held in accordance with the Constitution.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
TP038,Nepali,विद्यमान स्थानीय निकायमा निर्वाचित पदाधिकारीहरू कहिलेसम्म पदमा कायम रहन्छन्?,संविधानबमोजिम स्थानीय तहको निर्वाचन नभएसम्म।,Article 303(3) provides continuity for elected local officials until the new Local level elections take place.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
