TP038,Transitional Provisions,Local Bodies,Factual,Medium,Until when do officials elected to the existing Local Bodies continue to hold office?,विद्यमान स्थानीय निकायमा निर्वाचित पदाधिकारीहरू कहिलेसम्म पदमा कायम रहन्छन्?,Until elections to the Local level are held in accordance with the Constitution.,संविधानबमोजिम स्थानीय तहको निर्वाचन नभएसम्म।,Article 303(3) provides continuity for elected local officials until the new Local level elections take place.,Art. 303(3),Provisions relating to Local Bodies,,,,,,
TP039,Transitional Provisions,Existing Laws,Factual,Easy,What is the general rule regarding Nepalese laws in force when the Constitution commences?,संविधान प्रारम्भ हुँदा प्रचलित नेपालका कानूनहरूबारे सामान्य व्यवस्था के हो?,They continue to remain in force until repealed or amended."",""खारेज वा संशोधन नभएसम्म ती कानूनहरू कायम रहन्छन्।"",The Constitution provides a transitional period before inconsistent pre-existing laws automatically become invalid to the extent of their inconsistency."",Art. 304(1) preserves existing laws to avoid a legal vacuum during constitutional transition.,Art. 304(1),Existing laws to remain in force,,,,,,
TP040,Transitional Provisions,Existing Laws,Factual,Medium,What happens to an existing law that is inconsistent with the Constitution after the specified transitional period?,संविधानसँग बाझिएको विद्यमान कानूनको तोकिएको संक्रमणकालीन अवधिपछि के हुन्छ?,""जति हदसम्म संविधानसँग बाझिन्छ, त्यति हदसम्म अमान्य हुन्छ।"",Article 304(1) establishes constitutional supremacy over inconsistent existing laws.,Art. 304(1),Existing laws to remain in force,,,,,,
TP041,Transitional Provisions,Peace Process,Factual,Hard,How are Acts relating to the peace process under the Interim Constitution of Nepal, 2007 treated under the Constitution?,नेपालको अन्तरिम संविधान, २०६३ अन्तर्गत शान्ति प्रक्रियासम्बन्धी कार्यहरूलाई संविधानअन्तर्गत कसरी मानिन्छ?"",They are deemed to have been done under the Constitution.,संविधानअन्तर्गत गरिएको मानिन्छ।,Article 304(2) provides continuity and legal recognition for peace-process-related acts carried out under the Interim Constitution.,Art. 304(2),Existing laws to remain in force,,,,,,
DF002,Definitions and Interpretations,Law,Definition,Easy,What does the term “law” refer to under Article 306 of the Constitution?,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “कानून” भन्नाले के जनाउँछ?,""“Law” means Federal law, State law, and Local law."",""“कानून” भन्नाले संघीय कानून, प्रदेश कानुन र स्थानीय कानन बुझिन्छ।"",The constitutional definition limits the term to a citizen of Nepal.,Art. 306(1)(c),Definitions and interpretations,,,,,,
DF003,Definitions and Interpretations,Article,Definition,Easy,What does the term “Article” refer to under Article 306 of the Constitution?,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “धारा” भन्नाले के जनाउँछ?,""It means an Article of the Constitution."",""संविधानको कुनै धारा।,The term “Article” is specifically defined as a provision of the Constitution itself.,Art. 306(1)(e),Definitions and interpretations,,,,,,
DF004,Definitions and Interpretations,Municipality,Definition,Easy,What entities are included within the constitutional definition of “Municipality”?,संवैधानिक रूपमा “नगरपालिका” को परिभाषाभित्र कुन निकायहरू पर्छन्?,A Municipality includes a Municipal Corporation and a Sub-municipal Corporation.,नगरपालिका भन्नाले महानगरपालिका र उपमहानगरपालिका समेत जनाउँछ।,The definition gives “Municipalty” a broader meaning by expressly including Municipal Corporations and Sub-Municipal Corporations."",Art. 306(1)(d),Definitions and interpretations,,,,,,
DF005,Definitions and Interpretations,Citizen,Definition,Easy,Who is considered a “citizen” under Article 306?,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “नागरिक” भन्नाले कसलाई जनाउँछ?,""A citizen means a citizen of Nepal."",""“नागरिक” भन्नाले नेपालको नागरिकलाई जनाउँछ।,The constitutional definition limits the term to a citizen of Nepal.,Art. 306(1)(e),Definitions and interpretations,,,,,,",Question repetition / non-answer,Question repetition / non-answer,True
TP040,English,What happens to an existing law that is inconsistent with the Constitution after the specified transitional period?,It becomes invalid to the extent of its inconsistency.,"It becomes invalid to the extent of its inconsistency.""",Correct,Not a strict error,False
TP040,Nepali,संविधानसँग बाझिएको विद्यमान कानूनको तोकिएको संक्रमणकालीन अवधिपछि के हुन्छ?,"जति हदसम्म संविधानसँग बाझिन्छ, त्यति हदसम्म अमान्य हुन्छ।","संविधानसँग बाझिएको विद्यमान कानूनको तोकिएको संक्रमणकालीन अवधिपछि, त्यस्तै वेष्टन रहन्छ। संविधानले विद्यमान कानुनहरूलाई कायम राख्ने व्यवस्था गर्छ, तर यो व्यवस्था परिवर्तनमा आएपछि आउन सक्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP041,English,After what event and period does the inconsistency rule for existing laws take effect under Article 304(1)?,"After one year from the date on which the first session of the Federal Parliament is held, an inconsistent law becomes invalid to the extent of its inconsistency.","After one year from the date on which the first session of the Federal Parliament is held, an inconsistent law becomes invalid to the extent of its inconsistency.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
TP041,Nepali,धारा ३०४(१) अन्तर्गत विद्यमान कानूनको असंगतिसम्बन्धी व्यवस्था कुन घटना र अवधिपछि लागू हुन्छ?,"संघीय संसद्को पहिलो अधिवेशन बसेको मितिले एक वर्षपछि संविधानसँग बाझिएको कानून जति हदसम्म बाझिन्छ, त्यति हदसम्म अमान्य हुन्छ।","धारा ३००४(१) अन्तर्गत विद्यमान कानूनोंको असंगतिसम्बन्धी व्यवस्था, संघीय संसद्को पहिलो अधिवेशन बसेको मितिदेखि एक वर्षभित्रै लागू हुन्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
TP042,English,"How are Acts relating to the peace process under the Interim Constitution of Nepal, 2007 treated under the Constitution?",They are deemed to have been done under the Constitution.,They are deemed to have been done under the Constitution.,Correct,Not a strict error,False
TP042,Nepali,"नेपालको अन्तरिम संविधान, २०६३ अन्तर्गत शान्ति प्रक्रियासम्बन्धी कार्यहरूलाई संविधानअन्तर्गत कसरी मानिन्छ?",संविधानअन्तर्गत गरिएको मानिन्छ।,"नेपालको अन्तरिम संविधान, २०६३ अन्तर्गत शान्ति प्रक्रियासम्बन्धी कार्यहरूलाई संविधानअन्तर्गत कसरी मानिन्छ?

उत्तर:
नेपालको अन्तरिम संविधान, २०६३ अन्तर्गत शान्ति प्रक्रियासम्बन्धी कार्यहरूलाई संविधानअन्तर्गत एक प्रकारका कामहरू मानिन्छ। यसले शान्तीमा आधारित मुद्दाहरूको समाधान गर्न मद्दत गर्दछ तर यो युद्धको विषयवस्तुबाट अलग हुन्छ।",Question repetition / non-answer,Question repetition / non-answer,True
TP043,English,Who may issue necessary orders to remove difficulties in implementing the Constitution before the first session of the Federal Parliament?,"The President, on the recommendation of the Government of Nepal, Council of Ministers.","The President, on the recommendation of the Government of Nepal, Council of Ministers.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
TP043,Nepali,संघीय संसद्को पहिलो अधिवेशनअघि संविधान कार्यान्वयनमा उत्पन्न कठिनाइ हटाउन आवश्यक आदेश कसले जारी गर्न सक्छ?,"नेपाल सरकार, मन्त्रिपरिषद्को सिफारिसमा राष्ट्रपतिले।","The President, on the recommendation of the Government of Nepal, Council of Ministers.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
TP044,English,What must happen to an order issued to remove difficulties under Article 305?,It must be submitted for approval to the Legislature-Parliament or Federal Parliament that is held immediately after the order is issued.,It must be submitted for approval to the Legislature-Parliament or Federal Parliament that is held immediately after the order is issued.,Correct,Not a strict error,False
TP044,Nepali,धारा ३०५ अन्तर्गत कठिनाइ हटाउन जारी गरिएको आदेशको के गर्नुपर्छ?,आदेश जारी भएपछि तुरुन्त बस्ने व्यवस्थापिका–संसद् वा संघीय संसद्समक्ष अनुमोदनका लागि पेश गर्नुपर्छ।,It must be submitted for approval to the Legislature-Parliament or Federal Parliament that is held immediately after the order is issued.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DF001,English,"Under Article 306, which groups are considered “minorities”?","Minorities are ethnic, linguistic, and religious groups whose population is below the percentage specified by Federal law, including groups with distinct ethnic, religious, or linguistic characteristics and aspirations to protect them that have been subjected to discrimination and oppression.","Minority are ethnic, linguistic, and religious groups whose population is below the percentage specified by Federal law, including groups with distinct ethnic, religious, or linguistic characteristics and aspirations to protect them that have been subjected to discrimination and oppression.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
DF001,Nepali,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “अल्पसंख्यक” भन्नाले कुन समूहलाई जनाउँछ?,"संघीय कानूनले तोकेको प्रतिशतभन्दा कम जनसंख्या भएका जातीय, भाषिक र धार्मिक समूहहरू, साथै आफ्ना विशिष्ट जातीय, धार्मिक वा भाषिक विशेषता संरक्षण गर्ने आकांक्षा भएका र विभेद तथा उत्पीडनमा परेका समूहहरूलाई अल्पसंख्यक भनिन्छ।","संघीय कानूनले तोकेको प्रतिशतभन्दा कम जनसंख्या भएका जातीय, भाषिक र धार्मिक समूहहरू।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
DF002,English,What does the term “law” mean under Article 306 of the Constitution?,"“Law” means Federal law, State law, and Local law.","It means Federal law, State Law, and Local Law.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
DF002,Nepali,संविधानको धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “कानून” भन्नाले के बुझिन्छ?,"“कानून” भन्नाले संघीय कानून, प्रदेश कानून र स्थानीय कानून बुझिन्छ।","It means Federal law, State Law, and Local Law.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DF003,English,What does the term “Article” refer to under Article 306?,It means an Article of the Constitution.,It means an Article of the Constitution itself.,Correct,Not a strict error,False
DF003,Nepali,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “धारा” भन्नाले के जनाउँछ?,संविधानको कुनै धारा।,It means a Municipality includes a Municipal Corporation and a Sub-municipal Corporation.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DF004,English,What entities are included within the constitutional definition of “Municipality”?,A Municipality includes a Municipal Corporation and a Sub-municipal Corporation.,A Municipality includes a Municipal Corporation and a Sub-municipal Corporation.,Correct,Not a strict error,False
DF004,Nepali,संवैधानिक रूपमा “नगरपालिका” को परिभाषाभित्र कुन निकायहरू पर्छन्?,नगरपालिका भन्नाले महानगरपालिका र उपमहानगरपालिका समेत जनाउँछ।,A Municipality includes a Municipal Corporation and a Sub-municipal Corporation.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DF005,English,Who is considered a “citizen” under Article 306?,A citizen means a citizen of Nepal.,A citizen means a citizen of Nepal.,Correct,Not a strict error,False
DF005,Nepali,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “नागरिक” भन्नाले कसलाई जनाउँछ?,“नागरिक” भन्नाले नेपालको नागरिकलाई जनाउँछ।,A citizen of Nepal.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DF006,English,How does Article 306 define the term “State”?,“State” means the area and form of a federal unit of Nepal divided into federal units in accordance with the Constitution.,"Article 306 defines ""State"" as a political entity that has the power to make laws and administer justice. It’s essentially the highest level of government in a country, encompassing all governmental bodies.  It's defined as a political entity with the authority to enact laws and exercise judicial functions.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DF006,Nepali,धारा ३०६ ले “प्रदेश” शब्दलाई कसरी परिभाषित गरेको छ?,“प्रदेश” भन्नाले संविधानबमोजिम संघीय इकाइहरूमा विभाजित नेपालको संघीय इकाइको क्षेत्र र स्वरूपलाई जनाउँछ।,"धारा ३०६ ले ""प्रदेश"" शब्दलाई एक विशिष्ट भौगोलिक क्षेत्रको रूपमा व्याख्या गरिएको हो, जसले राज्यको सीमावर्ती भागहरू समावेश गर्दछ। यसले सरकारले धर्वायुक्त (autonomous) स्थानीय स्वायत्तता प्रदान गर्ने अधिकार दिन्छ तर त्यसका प्रयोगमा देशको मुख्य प्रशासनिक आधारस्तंभको हदसम्म सीमित गर्दैन।

यहाँ विस्तृत विवरण दिए गए हैं:
*   **स्थानीय स्वायत्तता:**धारा ३०६ ले स्थानीय सरकारलाई राज्यको सीमावर्ती भागहरूमा धर्वायुक्त स्वायत्तता प्रदान गर्न अनुमति दिन्छ, तर यसले राज्यको सबैभन्दा महत्वपूर्ण प्रशासनिक आधारस्तंभको हदसम्म सीमित गर्दैन।
*   **प्रदेशको अर्थ:** ""प्रदेश"" शब्द प्रयोग गर्दा, यो एक भौगोलिक क्षेत्रको प्रतिनिधित्व हो जसले स्थानीय सरकारलाई राज्यको सीमावर्ती भागहरूमा धर्वायुक्त स्वायत्तता प्रदान गर्ने अधिकार दिन्छ।
*   **राज्यको मुख्य आधारस्तंभको हदसम्म सीमित नहोर्नुहोस्:** तर, धारा ३०६ ले राज्यको सबैभन्दा महत्वपूर्ण प्रशासनिक आधारस्तंभको हदसम्म सीमित गर्दैन भन्ने मोज हो।

संक्षेप में कहें तो, ""प्रदेश"" शब्द प्रयोग गर्दा सरकारले स्थानीय सरकारलाई धर्वायुक्त स्वायत्तता प्रदान गर्ने अधिकार दिन्छ, तर यसले राज्यको सबैभन्दा महत्त्वपूर्ण प्रशासनिक आधारस्तंभको हदसम्म सीमित गर्दैन।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DF007,English,What does “remuneration” include under Article 306?,"It includes salary, allowance, pension, and any other form of emolument and facility.","Under Article 306 of the Right to Information Act, 2064 (2007), remuneration includes all forms of compensation or benefit that a person receives in exchange for providing information. This encompasses monetary payments, benefits, and other rewards offered as incentive for disclosure. It also covers any financial or non-financial incentives provided by the public body.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DF007,Nepali,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “पारिश्रमिक” मा के–के समावेश हुन्छ?,"यसमा तलब, भत्ता, निवृत्तिभरण तथा अन्य कुनै पनि प्रकारको पारिश्रमिक र सुविधा समावेश हुन्छ।","धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “पारिश्रमिक”मा सूचना जारी गर्न सकिन्छ, तर जानकारीलाई अस्वीकार गर्ने वा लुकाउने कार्यको लागि थप जरिवाना हुन सक्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DF008,English,What powers are included within the meaning of “state power”?,"State power includes executive, legislative, and judicial powers of the State, as well as residual power.",The answer is: The right to information under Section 31(2) allows the concerned Public Body to complain to the Commission against a person who misuses information in violation of Section 31(1). This implies that the Commission has the authority to investigate and take action against individuals or entities who misuse information.,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
DF008,Nepali,“राज्य शक्ति” भन्नाले कुन–कुन शक्ति समावेश भएको बुझिन्छ?,"राज्य शक्तिमा प्रदेशको कार्यपालिका, व्यवस्थापिका र न्यायपालिकासम्बन्धी शक्ति तथा अवशिष्ट शक्ति समावेश हुन्छ।","राज्य शक्ति विभिन्न प्रकारका शक्तिहरूमा विभाजित हुन्छ। यहाँ तीमध्ये केही मुख्य शक्तियाँ छन्:

*   **कार्यकारी शक्ति:** सरकारले धर्मी कार्य गर्नुपर्ने अधिकार, जस्तै नीति निर्माण गर्ने, कानून बनाएर施行 गर्ने, र राज्यको व्यवस्थापन गर्ने क्षमता हो।
*   **स phápिक शक्ति:** स pháp (law) बनाउनु, स phápलाई लागू செய்த हुनु, र स phápको व्याख्या गर्यने क्षमता हो।
*   **आर्थिक शक्ति:** राज्यले आर्थिक विकासका लागि बजेट चलाउने, उद्योगलाई प्रोत्साहन दिने, र वित्तीय स्रोत व्यवस्थापन गर्ने क्षमता हो।
*   **राजनीतिक शक्ति:** सरकारमा नेतृत्व गर्नु, राजनीतिक मुद्दाहरू तय गर्नु, र जनताको निर्णयलाई प्रभावित गराउनुको अधिकार हो।
*   **सामाजिक शक्ति:** राज्यले सामाजिक समस्याहरूको समाधान गर्यने, मानsिहरुको कल्याण सुनिश्चित गर्ने, र समाज चलाउने क्षमता हो।

त्यसैले, राज्यमा धेरै प्रकारका शक्तियाँ हुन्छन्, जसले राज्यको निर्णयहरूलाई विभिन्न क्षेत्रहरूमा प्रभाव पार्न सक्दछें।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
DF009,English,What does the term “Bill” mean under Article 306?,It means a draft of an amendment to the Constitution or of an Act introduced in the Federal Parliament or a State Assembly.,"The term ""Bill"" in Article 306 refers to a proposed law or legislative measure that is being considered by Parliament. It’s essentially an idea or proposal for a new piece of legislation.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DF009,Nepali,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “विधेयक” भन्नाले के बुझिन्छ?,संघीय संसद् वा प्रदेश सभामा पेश गरिएको संविधान संशोधन वा ऐनको मस्यौदालाई विधेयक भनिन्छ।,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “विधेयक” म्हणजे सार्वजनिक निकाय द्वारा एक विशिष्ट व्यक्ती किंवा संस्थेविरुद्ध कार्यवाही करण्यासाठी तयार केलेले पत्र किंवा कागदपत्र.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DF010,English,What is meant by “Federation” and “Federal Units” under Article 306?,"“Federation” means the federal level, which is the apex unit of the federal structure. “Federal Units” means the Federation, State, and Local levels.","According to the text provided, ""Federation"" and ""Federal Units"" refer to a system of government where power is divided between a central authority (the federal unit) and regional units. It’s used in the context of the Right to Information Act, specifically related to the distribution of information across different regions or states within a country.

Here's a breakdown of what it implies:

*   **Federation:** This refers to a system where multiple entities (states, provinces, etc.) have some degree of autonomy and power, but are bound by a central authority with defined powers.
*   **Federal Units:** These are specific regions or areas within the federation that have their own legal frameworks, laws, and administrative structures.

The text highlights this concept as being relevant to the Right to Information Act because it deals with how information is distributed across different jurisdictions. The act aims to ensure that citizens can access information from all parts of the country, recognizing that each region has its own specific needs and concerns.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DF010,Nepali,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “संघ” र “संघीय इकाइ” भन्नाले के बुझिन्छ?,"“संघ” भन्नाले संघीय संरचनाको सर्वोच्च इकाइ अर्थात् संघीय तह बुझिन्छ। “संघीय इकाइ” भन्नाले संघ, प्रदेश र स्थानीय तह बुझिन्छ।","धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत ‘संघ’ (Union) और ‘संघीय इकाई’ (Federated Units) बीच मुख्य रूप से निम्न बातें बुझिन्छन्:

*   **संघीय इकाईंची स्वायत्तता (Federation units autonomy):** धारा ३०६ मध्ये, संघीय इकाइयाँ स्वतःच्या निर्णयनीति आणि धोरणांसाठी पूर्णपणे स्वतंत्र असतात.
*   **संघीय सरकारची भूमिका (Role of the Federal Government):**  संघीय सरकार फक्त ‘संघ’चा भाग आहे आणि संघीय युनिट्सना त्यांच्या अधिकार मर्यादित आहेत.
*   **संघीय संस्थांची जबाबदारी (Responsibilities of Federal Entities):** धारा ३०६ मध्ये, संघीय संस्थांना केवळ विशिष्ट कार्ये पार पाडण्यासाठी किंवा कायद्याचे पालन करण्यासाठी नियुक्त केले जाते.

संक्षेपामध्ये, ‘संघ’ म्हणजे एक व्यापक आणि स्वतंत्र संस्था, तर ‘संघीय इकाई’ म्हणजे संघात सहभागी असलेल्या स्थानिक भागांतील भाग आहेत.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DF011,English,Which institutions are included within the definition of “Constitutional Bodies” under Article 306?,"They include the Commission for the Investigation of Abuse of Authority, Auditor General, Public Service Commission, Election Commission, National Human Rights Commission, National Natural Resources and Fiscal Commission, National Women Commission, National Dalit Commission, National Inclusion Commission, Indigenous Nationalities Commission, Madhesi Commission, Tharu Commission, and Muslim Commission.","According to the text provided, the following institutions are included within the definition of “Constitutional Bodies” under Article 306:

*   The concerned Public Body
*   The related public body
*   The Republic of India",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DF011,Nepali,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “संवैधानिक निकाय” को परिभाषाभित्र कुन–कुन निकायहरू पर्छन्?,"अख्तियार दुरुपयोग अनुसन्धान आयोग, महालेखा परीक्षक, लोक सेवा आयोग, निर्वाचन आयोग, राष्ट्रिय मानव अधिकार आयोग, राष्ट्रिय प्राकृतिक स्रोत तथा वित्त आयोग, राष्ट्रिय महिला आयोग, राष्ट्रिय दलित आयोग, राष्ट्रिय समावेशी आयोग, आदिवासी जनजाति आयोग, मधेसी आयोग, थारू आयोग र मुस्लिम आयोग संवैधानिक निकायमा पर्छन्।","धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत ""संवૈतिक सार्वजनिक निकाय"" म्हणजे वेळेस, स्थान यामा किंवा डेटाच्या व्यवस्थापनात (data management) एक महत्त्वपूर्ण भूमिका बजावणारे कोणतेही संगठन. यात खालील संस्थांचा समावेश होतो:

*   **न्यायालय:** न्यायव्यवस्था आणि कायद्याचे संरक्षण करण्यासाठी हे संस्थेची जबाबदारी आहे.
*   **सरकारी अधिकारी:** सरकारी सेवा पुरवण्यासाठी, नियम लागू करण्यासाठी आणि नागरिकांच्या हक्कांचे रक्षण करण्यासाठी हे संस्थेची भूमिका असते.
*   **सार्वजनिक संस्था:** शिक्षण, आरोग्य, पर्यावरण यांसारख्या क्षेत्रांमध्ये काम करणाऱ्या संस्था.
*   **अदालत:** कायद्याचे पालन सुनिश्चित करणे आणि न्याय वितरीत करणे.
*   **न्यायालयीन विभाग:** न्यायालयीन प्रक्रिया व्यवस्थित पार पाडणे.
*   **पोलिस:** शहराची सुरक्षा राखण्यासाठी आणि गुन्हेगारी रोखण्यासाठी हे संस्थेची जबाबदारी आहे.
*   **सार्वजनिक आरोग्य संस्था:** लोकांच्या आरोग्याचे रक्षण करण्यासाठी आणि सार्वजनिक आरोग्य सेवा पुरवण्यासाठी हे संस्थेचे कार्य महत्त्वाचे आहे.

याव्यतिरिक्त, काही विशिष्ट क्षेत्रातील संस्थांना देखील ""संवૈतिक सार्वजनिक निकाय"" म्हटले जाते, ज्या त्यांच्या कामामुळे समाजावर महत्त्वपूर्ण परिणाम करतात.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DF012,English,Who are considered “marginalized” communities under Article 306?,"They are communities made politically, economically, and socially backward; unable to enjoy services and facilities because of discrimination, oppression, or geographical remoteness; or deprived of them; and having a status below the human development standards specified by Federal law. The definition also includes highly marginalized groups and groups on the verge of extinction.","According to the provided text, marginalized communities are defined as those who have been subjected to ""unauthorized use and disclosure of personal information"" by a Public Body. This includes individuals whose rights to privacy are violated due to misuse of information. The text doesn’t explicitly list specific marginalized groups but it highlights that this violation can occur regardless of the community's identity.",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
DF012,Nepali,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “सीमान्तीकृत” समुदाय भन्नाले कुन समुदायलाई जनाउँछ?,"राजनीतिक, आर्थिक र सामाजिक रूपमा पछाडि पारिएका; विभेद, उत्पीडन वा भौगोलिक विकटताका कारण सेवा तथा सुविधाको उपभोग गर्न नसकेका वा त्यस्ता सेवाबाट वञ्चित भएका; तथा संघीय कानूनमा उल्लिखित मानव विकासको मापदण्डभन्दा न्यून अवस्थामा रहेका समुदायलाई सीमान्तीकृत समुदाय भनिन्छ। यसमा अति सीमान्तीकृत र लोपोन्मुख समूहहरू समेत पर्छन्।","धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत ""सीमान्तीकृत"" समुदाय ती नागरिकहरू हुन् जसले सार्वजनिक निकायको जानकारी प्रयोग गर्दा, निजी डेटा प्राप्त गरेर, वा सार्वजनिक निकायको माहितीमा परिवर्तन ल्याएर, त्यसका उद्देश्यबाट सूचना प्राप्त गर्दछन्।",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DF013,English,What entities are included within the term “Local level” under Article 306?,"It means Village Bodies, Municipalities, and District Assemblies established in accordance with the Constitution.",The answer is: The Local Level.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DF013,Nepali,धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत “स्थानीय तह” भन्नाले कुन निकायहरूलाई जनाउँछ?,"संविधानबमोजिम स्थापना हुने गाउँ निकाय, नगरपालिका र जिल्ला सभालाई स्थानीय तह भनिन्छ।","धारा ३०६ अन्तर्गत ""स्थानीय तह"" मध्ये स्थानीय सरकारको संस्थाहरू समावेश छन्। यसमा विभिन्न प्रकारका सरकारी ادارے, नगरपालिका र अन्य स्थानीय अधिकारीहरूが含まれる होलान् ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DF014,English,How are legal provisions relating to the interpretation of laws applied when interpreting the Constitution?,"Subject to the provisions of the Constitution, the legal provisions relating to the interpretation of laws apply to the interpretation of the Constitution in the same manner as they apply to the interpretation of Nepalese laws.","The provided text doesn’t directly address how legal provisions related to interpretations of laws are applied under the Constitution. It focuses on the rights and responsibilities of a Public Body regarding information misuse, specifically concerning Section 31(2) and 31(3).  It discusses the potential for violations based on misusing information and the consequences that can be imposed by the Commission.

To answer your question about how legal provisions are applied when interpreting laws, we'd need to refer to constitutional principles related to interpretation, such as:

*   **The principle of legality:** Laws must be consistent with fundamental rights and constitutional principles.
*   **Interpretation vs. Application:** Interpretation is the process of understanding a law; application is the actual use of that law.
*   **Constitutional Review:** The judiciary's role in reviewing laws to ensure they comply with the Constitution.

Would you like me to provide more information on any specific aspect of constitutional interpretation?",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
DF014,Nepali,संविधानको व्याख्या गर्दा कानूनको व्याख्यासम्बन्धी कानूनी व्यवस्थाहरू कसरी लागू हुन्छन्?,संविधानका प्रावधानहरूको अधीनमा रही कानूनको व्याख्यासम्बन्धी कानूनी व्यवस्था नेपालको कानूनको व्याख्या गर्दा लागू हुने समान तरिकाले संविधानको व्याख्यामा लागू हुन्छ।,"संविधान एक सरकारी आदेश हो जसले देशको व्यवस्थापनलाई निर्देशित गर्दछ। यसमा नियमहरू समावेश छन्, तर यी नियमहरूको अर्थ र कार्यान्वयन कानून द्वारा तय हुन्छ। यहाँ प्रश्नको उत्तर दिइएका हुन्:

**उत्तर:**
संविधानले कानूनको व्याख्यासम्बन्धी कानूनी व्यवस्थाहरू कसरी लागू हुन्छन्?

संविधानले कानूनलाई एक विशिष्ट मार्गनिर्देशन प्रदान गर्दछ जसले देशको व्यवस्थापनमा नियमहरूलाई स्पष्ट पार्छ। संविधानले कानूनको अर्थ र कार्यान्वयनलाई निर्देशित गर्दछ, तर यसले कानूनको पूर्ण व्याख्या नदिन्छ। संवैधानिक अदालतले कानूनको व्याख्यासम्बन्धी निर्णय दिन्छ, यी निर्णयले कानूनको अर्थ र कार्यान्वयनलाई तय गर्छन।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
DF015,English,"What is the short title of the Constitution, when did it commence, and which previous Constitution did it repeal?","It may be cited as the “Constitution of Nepal”; it commenced on 20 September 2015 (3 Ashwin 2072 Bikram Sambat); and it repealed the Interim Constitution of Nepal, 2007 (2063).","The short title of the Constitution is “Constitution & Law”. It commenced on January 9, 1950, and it repealed the previous Constitution, which was the Constitution of 1942.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
DF015,Nepali,"संविधानको छोटो नाम के हो, यो कहिले प्रारम्भ भयो र यसले कुन अघिल्लो संविधान खारेज गर्‍यो?","यसको छोटो नाम “नेपालको संविधान” हो; यो २० सेप्टेम्बर २०१५ (वि.सं. २०७२ असोज ३ गते) प्रारम्भ भयो; र यसले नेपालको अन्तरिम संविधान, २०६३ खारेज गर्‍यो।",संविधानको छोटो नाम 'सम्बन्धित सार्वजनिक निकाय' (Related Public Body) हो। यसलाई 1964 को 'Art. 31(2)' अनुसार सहीले थोरानी कय संविधान खारेज गर्यो?,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI001,English,What is the short title of the Act?,"Right to Information Act, 2064 B.S. (2007 A.D.).",RI130,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
RI001,Nepali,यस ऐनको छोटो नाम के हो?,"सूचनाको हक सम्बन्धी ऐन, २०६४ (सन् २००७)।","The short name of this law is Right to Information Act, 2064 (2007).",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
RI002,English,"On what day after certification does the Right to Information Act, 2064 come into force?",The 30th day after certification.,"The answer is: **Three months**

Here's why:

*   **Section 32(3) of the Right to Information Act, 2064 states:** “It must notify the Commission of the departmental action taken.” This means that after a Public Body takes departmental action following a recommendation from the Commission, it must inform the Commission within three months.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI002,Nepali,"सूचनाको हक सम्बन्धी ऐन, २०६४ प्रमाणीकरण भएको कति दिनपछि लागू हुन्छ?",प्रमाणीकरण भएको ३०औँ दिन।,"सूचनाको हक सम्बन्धी ऐन, २०६४ प्रमाणीकरण भएको ३ महिनाभित्र लागू हुन्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI003,English,"Under the Act, what is meant by a “Public Body”?",Any body or institution included in the categories listed in Section 2(a).,"The text doesn’t explicitly define ""Public Body"" in detail. However, it refers to “the concerned Public Body” and mentions that it can be a “Person who misuses information.” Therefore, based on the context of misuse of information, it likely means an organization or entity that holds public records or data.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI003,Nepali,ऐनअनुसार “सार्वजनिक निकाय” भन्नाले के बुझिन्छ?,दफा २(क) मा उल्लिखित वर्गमा पर्ने कुनै निकाय वा संस्था।,"सार्वजनिक निकाय भन्नाले बुझिन्छ कि सार्वजनिक संस्थाहरू जसले सरकारको नीतिमा सहभागी हुन्छन् वा राज्यको हितलाई प्राथमिकता दिन्छ। यसमा समावेश छ: सरकारी ادارے, स्थानीय स्वैચ्यपालिका, नगरपालिका, र अन्य सबै संस्थाहरू जो जनताका लागि काम गर्छन्।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI004,English,Which type of body is included as a Public Body because it is established under the Constitution?,A body under the Constitution.,The answer is “Public Bodies”. The text explicitly states that the Right to Information Act applies to “Public Bodies” in Section 31.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
RI004,Nepali,संविधानअन्तर्गत स्थापित कुन प्रकारको निकाय सार्वजनिक निकायमा पर्छ?,संविधानअन्तर्गतको निकाय।,Public Body,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
RI005,English,Is a body established by an Act included within the definition of a Public Body?,Yes.,"Yes, a body established by an Act is considered part of the definition of a Public Body under Section 31(2) of the Right to Information Act, 2064 (2007). The text explicitly states that ""Art. 31(2)"" allows the concerned Public Body to complain to the Commission against a person who misuses information in violation of Section 31(1).""",Correct,Not a strict error,False
RI005,Nepali,ऐनद्वारा स्थापित निकाय सार्वजनिक निकायको परिभाषाभित्र पर्छ कि पर्दैन?,पर्छ।,"हाँ, एन् द्वारा स्थापित निकाय सार्वजनिक निकायको परिभाषा अन्तर्गत हुन्छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
RI006,English,What type of body formed by the Government of Nepal is included as a Public Body?,A body formed by the Government of Nepal.,The answer is “Public Authority”.,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
RI006,Nepali,नेपाल सरकारद्वारा गठन गरिएको कुन प्रकारको निकाय सार्वजनिक निकायमा पर्छ?,नेपाल सरकारद्वारा गठन गरिएको निकाय।,नेपाल सरकार द्वारा गठन गरिएको 'सूचना संरक्षण आयोग' (Information Protection Commission) हो।,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI007,English,"What is the distinction between the first three categories of Public Body under Section 2(a): a body under the Constitution, a body established by an Act, and a body formed by the Government of Nepal?","They are respectively a body under the Constitution, a body established by an Act, and a body formed by the Government of Nepal.","The distinctions are as follows:

*   **Body Under the Constitution:** This is the most fundamental category. It’s defined by the Constitution of Nepal itself and has inherent rights and responsibilities under Article 14, which guarantees certain freedoms and protections. These bodies have a special status and are subject to constitutional limitations.
*   **Body Established by an Act:** This refers to bodies created through legislation (Acts) passed by Parliament or equivalent legislative body. They operate within the framework of existing laws and regulations established by the legislature.
*   **Body Formed by the Government of Nepal:** This category encompasses all other bodies that are not defined under the Constitution or established by an Act. These bodies are formed by the government, typically through administrative processes like appointments, delegation of powers, or creation of new departments.

In essence: The Constitution defines the *fundamental* nature of a body; Acts define its *operational* nature; and the Government of Nepal defines all other bodies.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
RI007,Nepali,दफा २(क) अन्तर्गत सार्वजनिक निकायका पहिलो तीन वर्गबीच के भिन्नता छ?,"ती क्रमशः संविधानअन्तर्गतको निकाय, ऐनद्वारा स्थापित निकाय र नेपाल सरकारद्वारा गठन गरिएको निकाय हुन्।","दफा २(क) अन्तर्गत सार्वजनिक निकायका पहिलो तीन वर्गबीच के भिन्नता छ।

*   **व्यक्तिगत जानकारी:** व्यक्तिगत जानकारीको लागि, निजी व्यक्तिले सूचना प्राप्त गर्नुपर्छ तर त्यसलाई हटाउनुपर्छ र यसमा सहमति गर्नुपर्छ।
*   **सنسोरियल जानकारी:** सنسोरियल जानकारीको लागि, सार्वजनिक निकायले सूचना प्राप्त गर्नुपर्छ तर त्यसलाई हटाउनुपर्छ र यसमा सहमति गर्नुपर्छ।
*   **सामग्रीगत जानकारी:** सामग्रीगत जानकारीको लागि, सार्वजनिक निकायले सूचना प्राप्त गर्नुपर्छ तर त्यसलाई हटाउनुपर्छ र यसमा सहमति गर्नुपर्छ।",Question repetition / non-answer,Question repetition / non-answer,True
RI008,English,Does the definition of Public Body include an institution or foundation established by law for public service?,Yes.,"Yes, according to Section 31(2) of the Right to Information Act, 2064 (2007), a “Public Body” is defined as any organization established by law for the purpose of serving the public interest. Therefore, institutions or foundations established by law are included within the definition of Public Body.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
RI008,Nepali,सार्वजनिक सेवाका लागि कानूनद्वारा स्थापित संस्था वा प्रतिष्ठान सार्वजनिक निकायको परिभाषामा पर्छ?,पर्छ।,हाँ। सार्वजनिक सेवाका लागि कानूनद्वारा स्थापित संस्था वा प्रतिष्ठान सार्वजनिक निकायको परिभाषामा पर्छ।,Correct,Not a strict error,False
RI009,English,Which political organizations are included within the definition of a Public Body under the Act?,Political parties or organizations registered under the relevant law.,"The text doesn’t explicitly list specific political organizations. It focuses on the definition of “Public Body” as established by Section 31(2) and 31(3). However, it does mention that the ""concerned Public Body"" is a body that can complain to the Commission.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
RI009,Nepali,ऐनअनुसार कुन राजनीतिक संगठनहरू सार्वजनिक निकायको परिभाषाभित्र पर्छन्?,सम्बन्धित कानूनअन्तर्गत दर्ता भएका राजनीतिक दल वा संगठनहरू।,"RI130, Constitution & Law, Personal Information and Misuse, Comparison, Hard, How does the protection of personal information under Section 29 differ from the prohibition on misuse of information under Section 31?,Section 29 restricts unauthorized use and disclosure of personal information, while Section 31 restricts a recipient’s misuse of information or use for a purpose different from the purpose for which it was obtained.?

The answer is: **Both Section 29 and Section 31 protect personal information.**

