RI014,Nepali,दफा २(क) मा स्पष्ट रूपमा उल्लिखित वर्गबाहेक नेपाल सरकारले थप कुनै निकाय वा संस्थालाई कसरी सार्वजनिक निकाय तोक्न सक्छ?,राजपत्रमा सूचना प्रकाशित गरेर।,"दफा २(क) मा स्पष्ट रूपमा उल्लिखित वर्गबाहेक नेपाल सरकारले थप निकाय वा संस्थालाई निम्न तरिकाले सार्वजनिक निकाय तोक्न सक्छ:

*   **प्रतिक्रिया (Feedback):** सार्वजनिक निकायको काममा आए અંગે, गलत सूचना या समस्याहरूको लागि प्रतिक्रिया माग गर्न।
*   **समाशिड (Audit):** सार्वजनिक निकायको कार्यको निगरानीका लिए समाशिड चलाउन।
*   **अनुदान (Funding):** सार्वजनिक निकायलाई थप बजेट प्रदान गर्नुहोस् ताकि आफ्नो कामलाई जारी रा सकेनन्।
*   **संस्थागत रूपमा सहयोग (Institutional Support):** सार्वजनिक निकायको लागि आवश्यक सहकार्य गर्न, जति चाल्छ तर तिनी हुन्छ त्यतिके माध्यमले सहयोग गर्न।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI015,English,A body does not fall within any of the first eight listed categories of Public Body. Under what condition can it still be treated as a Public Body under the Act?,If the Government of Nepal prescribes it as a Public Body by publishing a notice in the Gazette.,"The answer is that the body can still be treated as a Public Body if it has been established by law or regulation, and its functions are defined in legislation. It doesn’t necessarily need to have a specific relationship with another public body for this classification. The key here is that it's being governed by laws and regulations rather than simply being a result of an informal agreement between entities.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI015,Nepali,कुनै निकाय सार्वजनिक निकायका पहिलो आठ वर्गमध्ये कुनैमा पर्दैन भने कुन अवस्थामा त्यसलाई ऐनअनुसार सार्वजनिक निकाय मान्न सकिन्छ?,नेपाल सरकारले राजपत्रमा सूचना प्रकाशित गरी त्यसलाई सार्वजनिक निकायका रूपमा तोकेमा।,"If the concerned Public Body does not fall into any of the eight categories mentioned in Section 31, then what situation can be considered to designate it as a public body according to law?

The answer is: **Section 31(2) allows the concerned Public Body to complain to the Commission against a person who misuses information in violation of Section 31.**",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
RI016,English,"Under the Act, what does “Information” mean?","Any written document, material, or information related to the functions, proceedings, or decisions of public importance made by a Public Body.","The text doesn’t define ‘information’ in detail. It simply states that it refers to information misused in violation of Section 31. To understand its meaning, you would need to consult the full text of the law.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
RI016,Nepali,ऐनअनुसार “सूचना” भन्नाले के बुझिन्छ?,"सार्वजनिक निकायका कार्य, कार्यवाही वा सार्वजनिक महत्वका निर्णयसँग सम्बन्धित कुनै लिखित दस्तावेज, सामग्री वा सूचना।",सूचना काउन्सरी (Information Counsellor),Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
RI017,English,What does “Public Importance” mean under the Act?,A subject directly or indirectly related to the interest of citizens.,"The text doesn’t explicitly define ""Public Importance"" in detail. However, it mentions that information held by a Public Body is subject to misuse and requires protection under Section 31. Therefore, public importance refers to information that is crucial for maintaining public trust, safety, or the well-being of citizens. It suggests that information held by a Public Body should be safeguarded from unauthorized use or misapplication.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI017,Nepali,ऐनअनुसार “सार्वजनिक महत्व” भन्नाले के बुझिन्छ?,नागरिकको हितसँग प्रत्यक्ष वा अप्रत्यक्ष रूपमा सम्बन्धित विषय।,"Public importance refers to the public interest and the potential impact of a decision on society. It encompasses matters that are vital for maintaining democratic principles, protecting fundamental rights, ensuring national security, promoting social welfare, and upholding the rule of law.  Essentially, it’s about decisions with significant consequences for citizens and the nation as a whole.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
RI018,English,What types of materials are included within the definition of a “Document”?,"Any kind of written document, including audiovisual material collected and updated through mechanical means or material that can be printed or retrieved.","The answer is: **Information that is communicated or produced in relation to a public body.**

Here's why:

*   **Definition of ""Document""**: The definition of ""document"" under Section 31(1) broadly encompasses any material that relates to a public body. This includes written, printed, electronic, audio, visual, and other forms of information.
*   **Scope**: It covers a wide range of materials – from official reports and records to personal communications, data sets, etc.

Let me know if you'd like more detail!",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI018,Nepali,“दस्तावेज” को परिभाषाभित्र कस्ता सामग्रीहरू समावेश हुन्छन्?,जुनसुकै प्रकारको लिखित दस्तावेज तथा यान्त्रिक माध्यमबाट संकलन र अद्यावधिक गरिएको वा छाप्न वा पुनःप्राप्त गर्न सकिने श्रव्यदृश्य सामग्री।,"""दस्तावेज"" शब्दको श्रेणीमा निम्न प्रकारका सामग्रीहरू समावेश हुन्छन्:

*   **प्रमाण:** यो कुनै पनि प्रमाण हो जसले तथ्यलाई प्रमाणित गर्दछ। यसमा लेख, फोटो, भिडथवा, नक्शा, वा अन्य रूपमा जोडिन्छ् मानिसले बनाएका कुरा छ ।
*   **सूचना:** जानकारीको स्रोतको बारेमा सूचनाहरू समावेश हुन्छन्, जस्तै लेख, रिपोर्ट, सम्बक्नुвање, वा तथ्यात्मक डेटा।
*   **प्रतिक्रिया:** कुनै व्यक्तिले सार्वजनिक रूपमा जारी गरिएको प्रतिक्रिया समावेश हुन्छ।
*   **भूमिकाको कागजात:** मानिसले आफ्नो कार्यको लागि बनाएको कागदपत्रहरू, जस्तै प्रतिपूर्ति, र अन्य फाइलहरू समावेश हुन्छन्।
*   **अन्य सामग्री:** यो धेरै प्रकारका सामग्री हुन सक्छ, तर यसमा तथ्यात्मक जानकारी, सूचना, वा प्रतिक्रिया समावेश हुन्छन्।

थप स्पष्टीकरण केही नहोर्नुहोस्!",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI019,English,How does the Act distinguish “Information” from a “Document”?,"Information concerns material related to the functions, proceedings, or decisions of public importance of a Public Body, while a Document refers to written or specified audiovisual or mechanically stored or retrievable material.","The Right to Information Act distinguishes between ""information"" and ""documents"" based on their nature. Section 31(1) prohibits misuse of information, while Section 31(2) authorizes the Commission to complain against a person who misuses information. The act focuses on the *use* of information rather than its physical form.  It’s about the *purpose* of the information and whether it's being used for a different purpose than what was originally obtained.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
RI019,Nepali,ऐनले “सूचना” र “दस्तावेज” बीच कसरी भिन्नता गर्छ?,"सूचना सार्वजनिक निकायका कार्य, कार्यवाही वा सार्वजनिक महत्वका निर्णयसँग सम्बन्धित सामग्री हो भने दस्तावेज लिखित वा निर्दिष्ट श्रव्यदृश्य वा यान्त्रिक रूपमा संकलित, छाप्न वा पुनःप्राप्त गर्न सकिने सामग्री हो।","RI130, Constitution & Law,Information Protection,Multi-hop Factual,Hard,""The Right to Information Act, 2064 (2007) distinguishes between ‘information’ and ‘documents’ based on their nature. 'Information' refers to data that can be readily accessed and used, while 'documents' are tangible records of events or transactions. The Act grants the public access to documents, but it does not automatically grant access to information.  The focus is on providing access to information, rather than the physical existence of documents.""",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
RI020,English,What is the basic right included within the definition of “Right to Information”?,The right to ask for and obtain information of public importance held by Public Bodies.,The basic right included within the definition of “Right to Information” is the right to access information held by public authorities.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI020,Nepali,“सूचनाको हक” को परिभाषामा समावेश मूलभूत हक के हो?,सार्वजनिक निकायमा रहेको सार्वजनिक महत्वको सूचना माग्ने र प्राप्त गर्ने हक।,"सूचनाको हकको परिभाषामा समावेश मूलभूत हकहरू हुन्:

*   **सूचना प्राप्त गर्ने अधिकार:** कुनै पनि व्यक्तिलाई जानकारी प्राप्त गर्न पाउँदा, त्यसको बारेमा जान्ने र प्रयोग गर्ने अधिकार।
*   **सूचना सार्वजनिक गराउने अधिकार:**  किसी भी व्यक्तिले सूचना सार्वजनिक गरने अधिकार।
*   **सूचना प्रयोगका अधिकार:** सूचना प्रयोग गर्न पाउँदा, त्यसको उद्देश्य अनुसार प्रयोग गर्ने अधिकार।
*   **सूचनालाई गोप्य राख्ने अधिकार:** जानकारीलाई निजी र सुरक्षित राख्ने अधिकार।
*   **सूचना लुकाए जाने या तिराएर नजाने कानुनी उपाय नदिने अधिकार:**  जानकारीलाई लुकाई वा तिराएर नदिने कानुनी उपाय नदिने अधिकार।

यो सबै कुयाँ सार्वजनिकको हकको आधारमा आधारित हुन्, जसले गर्दा जनतालाई जानकारी प्रयोग गर्न पाउँदा, त्यसको बारेमा जान्ने र प्रयोग गर्ने अधिकार हुन्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI021,English,"Besides asking for and obtaining information, what right concerning written documents or materials held by a Public Body is included in the Right to Information?",The right to study or observe them.,"The answer is: **The Right to Information Act, 2064 (2007)**. The text explicitly states that Section 31(2) allows the concerned public body to complain to the Commission against a person who misuses information in violation of Section 31(1). This implies that the right to access and utilize written documents held by the Public Body is covered under this section.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI021,Nepali,सूचना माग्ने र प्राप्त गर्ने अधिकारबाहेक सार्वजनिक निकायमा रहेका लिखित दस्तावेज वा सामग्रीसम्बन्धी कुन अधिकार सूचनाको हकमा समावेश हुन्छ?,तिनको अध्ययन वा अवलोकन गर्ने हक।,"सूचना माग्ने र प्राप्त गर्ने अधिकारबाहेक सार्वजनिक निकायमा रहेका लिखित दस्तावेज वा सामग्रीसम्बन्धी, जानकारीको हकमा समावेश हुने अधिकार, सूचनालाई स्रोतबाट प्राप्त गर्न पाउँदा, ती कागजातहरूलाई सार्वजनिक निकायले हटाउनुपर्ने अधिकार हुन्छ।

यहाँ स्पष्टीकरण दिइएલું છે:
*   **सूचनाको हकमा समावेश:** सूचनालाई स्रोतबाट प्राप्त गर्न पाउँदा, ती कागजातहरूलाई सार्वजनिक निकायले हटाउनुपर्ने अधिकार हुन्छ।
*   **जानकारीको हकमा समावेश:** जानकारीको हकमा समावेश हुने अधिकार, सूचनालाई स्रोतबाट प्राप्त गर्न पाउँदा, ती कागजातहरूलाई सार्वजनिक निकायले हटाउनुपर्ने अधिकार हुन्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI022,English,What may a person obtain regarding a document under the Right to Information?,A verified copy of the document.,The answer is: A person can obtain a copy of a document.,Correct,Not a strict error,False
RI022,Nepali,सूचनाको हकअन्तर्गत कुनै दस्तावेजका सम्बन्धमा के प्राप्त गर्न सकिन्छ?,प्रमाणित प्रतिलिपि।,"सूचनाको हकअन्तर्गत कुनै दस्तावेजका सम्बन्धमा, जनताले सार्वजनिक निकायबाट प्राप्त गर्न सकिలువको कागदपत्रलाई 'जानकारी पत्र' भनिन्छ। यसलाई ‘जानकारी पत्र’ भनिने कागदपत्रलाई ‘प्रसहर’ पनि भन्ने गर्छन्।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI023,English,What access does the Right to Information provide concerning a place where construction of public importance is taking place?,The right to visit or observe the place.,"The right to information provides access to information regarding construction projects that are taking place in areas considered important for public benefit. It allows individuals and entities to monitor developments, assess potential impacts on communities, and ensure transparency in the process.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI023,Nepali,सार्वजनिक महत्वको निर्माण कार्य भइरहेको स्थानका सम्बन्धमा सूचनाको हकले कस्तो पहुँच प्रदान गर्छ?,त्यस्तो स्थानमा भ्रमण वा अवलोकन गर्ने हक।,"Section 31(1) मध्ये व्यक्तिगत जानकारीको अधिकार सुरक्षित र दफा ३१(2) मध्ये सूचना प्रयोगको अनुमति दिइएको है। सार्वजनिक महत्वको निर्माण कार्यमा, निजी माहितीको अधिकार सुरक्षित保्छ तर सूचना प्रयोगको अनुमति दिइएको है।",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
RI024,English,What may be obtained as evidence or information about materials used in construction of public importance under the Right to Information?,A verified sample of the material.,"The right to information can provide evidence and information regarding materials used in the construction of public importance. This includes documents, records, reports, plans, specifications, and any other relevant data related to the construction process.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
RI024,Nepali,सार्वजनिक महत्वको निर्माणमा प्रयोग भएका सामग्रीका सम्बन्धमा सूचनाको हकअन्तर्गत के प्राप्त गर्न सकिन्छ?,सामग्रीको प्रमाणित नमुना।,"Section 29 अन्तर्गत व्यक्तिगत जानकारीको संरक्षण र Section 31 अन्तर्गत सूचनाको दुरुपयोग निषेध बीच का फरक छ। Section 29 पर ध्यान केन्द्रित गर्छ कि व्यक्तिले अनधिकृत प्रयोग वा प्रकाशनलाई सीमित गर्छ, तर Section 31 पर ध्यान केन्द्रित गर्छ कि प्राप्तकर्ताले सूचनाको उपयोगमा अलग उद्देश्यको लागि प्रयोग गर्ने कार्यलाई रोक लगाउँछ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI025,English,What additional access does the Right to Information provide to information held in any type of machine?,The right to obtain the information through that machine.,"The right to information provides access to information held in any type of machine. It allows individuals to request and obtain information stored within machines, including computers, servers, and other digital devices.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI025,Nepali,कुनै पनि प्रकारको यन्त्रमा रहेको सूचनाका सम्बन्धमा सूचनाको हकले कस्तो पहुँच प्रदान गर्छ?,त्यस्तो यन्त्रमार्फत सूचना प्राप्त गर्ने हक।,"कुनै पनि प्रकारको यन्त्रमा रहेको सूचनाका सम्बन्धमा सूचनाको हकले,सूचना प्रयोगकर्तालाई जानकारीको स्रोत, उद्देश्य, र उपयोग बारेमा विस्तृत जानकारी दिने पहुँच प्रदान गर्दछ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI026,English,"Which of the following forms of access are expressly included in the statutory definition of the Right to Information: studying or observing documents, obtaining a verified copy, observing public-interest construction, obtaining a verified material sample, or obtaining machine-held information through the machine?",All of them.,"The statutory definition of the Right to Information includes all listed options: studying or observing documents, obtaining a verified copy, observing public-interest construction, obtaining a verified material sample, and obtaining machine-held information through the machine.

Therefore, the answer is **all of these**.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI026,Nepali,"निम्नमध्ये कुन-कुन पहुँचका स्वरूपहरू सूचनाको हकको वैधानिक परिभाषामा स्पष्ट रूपमा समावेश छन्: दस्तावेज अध्ययन वा अवलोकन गर्नु, प्रमाणित प्रतिलिपि प्राप्त गर्नु, सार्वजनिक महत्वको निर्माण अवलोकन गर्नु, प्रमाणित सामग्रीको नमुना प्राप्त गर्नु, वा यन्त्रमा रहेको सूचना सोही यन्त्रमार्फत प्राप्त गर्नु?",यी सबै।,यहाँ दिए गए प्रश्नका उत्तरहरू बुझिएका छन्। कृपया ध्यानपूर्वक जाँच गर्नुहोस् र यदि तपाईंले कुनै विशेष उत्तर खोज्नुभएको छ भने बताउनुहोस्।,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI027,English,Who is an “Information Authority” under the Act?,A person appointed pursuant to Section 6.,"According to Section 31(2) of the Right to Information Act, 2064 (2007), the ""Information Authority"" is defined as a person who misuses information in violation of Section 31. This implies someone who deliberately or carelessly uses information for purposes different from what was originally obtained.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI027,Nepali,ऐनअनुसार “सूचना अधिकारी” को हो?,दफा ६ बमोजिम नियुक्त व्यक्ति।,"""सूचना अधिकारी"" (Information Officer) का शब्द प्रयोग किया गया है। यह एक विशिष्ट पद या भूमिका के लिए इस्तेमाल होता है, जो कि ""Right to Information Act, 2064 (2007)"" में वर्णित सार्वजनिक निकाय की संरचना और कार्यप्रणाली से संबंधित है।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI028,English,Who is referred to as the “Chief” under the Act?,The Chief of a Public Body.,The Chief of a Public Body or Information Officer,Correct,Not a strict error,False
RI028,Nepali,ऐनअनुसार “प्रमुख” भन्नाले कसलाई जनाउँछ?,सार्वजनिक निकायको प्रमुख।,मुख्य अधिकारी।,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
RI029,English,What does the term “Commission” refer to under the Act?,The National Information Commission constituted pursuant to Section 11.,"The term ""Commission"" refers to the concerned Public Body.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI029,Nepali,ऐनअनुसार “आयोग” भन्नाले के जनाउँछ?,दफा ११ बमोजिम गठन भएको राष्ट्रिय सूचना आयोग।,आयोगमा सार्वजनिक निकायको प्रतिनिधित्वका व्यक्तिहरू समावेश हुन्छन्।,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
RI030,English,What is the distinction between the Chief Information Commissioner and an Information Commissioner under the Act?,"Both are persons appointed pursuant to Section 11, but they are separately identified as the Chief Information Commissioner and Information Commissioner.","The difference lies in their authority and scope of responsibility. The Chief Information Commissioner has a broader mandate, focusing on overseeing the entire process of information access and ensuring compliance with the law. They are responsible for overall policy and strategic direction related to information rights.  An Information Commissioner focuses specifically on investigating complaints about information misuse and ensures that appropriate action is taken against those who violate the rules.

Here's a breakdown:

*   **Chief Information Commissioner:** Primarily concerned with establishing policies, providing guidance, and ensuring consistent application of the law across all levels of government. They are responsible for overseeing the entire process of information access and redress.
*   **Information Commissioner:**  Focused on investigating individual complaints related to misuse or improper handling of information. Their primary role is to determine whether a violation has occurred and take appropriate action, such as issuing fines or imposing other penalties.

In essence, the Chief Information Commissioner sets the framework while the Information Commissioner enforces it through investigation and redress.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI030,Nepali,ऐनअनुसार मुख्य सूचना आयुक्त र सूचना आयुक्तबीच के भिन्नता छ?,"दुवै दफा ११ बमोजिम नियुक्त व्यक्ति हुन्, तर उनीहरूलाई क्रमशः मुख्य सूचना आयुक्त र सूचना आयुक्तका रूपम","RI130, Constitution & Law, Personal Information and Misuse, Comparison, Hard, How does the protection of personal information under Section 29 differ from the prohibition on misuse of information under Section 31?,Section 29 restricts unauthorized use and disclosure of personal information, while Section 31 restricts a recipient’s misuse of information or use for a purpose different from the purpose for which it was obtained.?

The answer is: **Section 29 focuses on protecting personal information and consent-based use, while Section 31 focuses on the subsequent use and misuse of information obtained from a Public Body.**",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
RI031,English,"Who has the right to information under the Act, subject to the provisions of the Act?",Every citizen.,"The Right to Information Act, 2064 (2007) grants the concerned Public Body the right to information from a person lawfully obtaining information from a Public Body. This includes individuals who have obtained information through legal means and are now using it for a different purpose than what they originally obtained it for.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
RI031,Nepali,यस ऐनका प्रावधानहरूको अधीनमा रही सूचनाको हक कसलाई हुन्छ?,प्रत्येक नागरिकलाई।,"RI135,Punishment and Penalties,Fact Retrieval,Easy,What is the fine for unjustified delay in providing information that was required to be provided within the prescribed time?,निर्धारित समयमा उपलब्ध गराउनुपर्ने सूचना बिना कारण ढिला गरी उपलब्ध गराएमा दैनिक कति जरिवाना लाग्छ?,""The daily fine may be NPR 200 per day of delay.,The daily fine may be NPR 200 per day of delay.""",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI032,English,What information shall every citizen have access to under the Act?,Information held by Public Bodies.,"RI131, Constitution & Law,Information Protection,Multi-hop Factual,Hard，“If a person lawfully obtains information from a Public Body but later uses it for a different purpose from the purpose for which it was obtained, which provision is potentially violated and who may complain?”

The right to Information Act, 2064 (2007) protects individuals’ lawful access to information. If someone obtains information from a public body but then uses it for a different purpose, this could be considered misuse of information. The concerned Public Body may complain about this situation.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI032,Nepali,ऐनअनुसार प्रत्येक नागरिकलाई कुन सूचनामा पहुँच हुन्छ?,सार्वजनिक निकायमा रहेको सूचना।,"The answer is ""right to information"".",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
RI033,English,"What types of information concerning Nepal's sovereignty, integrity, national security, public peace, stability, and international relations shall not be disseminated?",Information that seriously jeopardizes any of those interests.,"The answer is:

**Information that could undermine Nepal’s sovereignty, integrity, national security, public peace, stability, or international relations.**

Here’s a breakdown of why this response aligns with the provided text:

*   **Section 31(2) and 31(3):** These sections specifically address misuse of information. The answer directly reflects this by prohibiting dissemination of information that could threaten Nepal's core values.
*   **Article 31(2):** This article focuses on the recipient’s misuse of information, which is a key concern in relation to sovereignty and national security.

Let me know if you would like more detail or clarification!",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
RI033,Nepali,"नेपालको सार्वभौमसत्ता, अखण्डता, राष्ट्रिय सुरक्षा, सार्वजनिक शान्ति, स्थिरता र अन्तर्राष्ट्रिय सम्बन्धका सम्बन्धमा कस्तो सूचना प्रसार गर्न हुँदैन?",तीमध्ये कुनै पनि हितमा गम्भीर रूपमा प्रतिकूल असर पार्ने सूचना।,"नेपालले आफ्नो सार्वभौमसत्ता, अखण्डता, राष्ट्रिय सुरक्षा, सार्वजनिक शान्ती, स्थिरता र आंतरराष्ट्रीय सम्बन्धका सम्बन्धमा निम्न प्रकारको जानकारीलाई बचाउनुपर्छ। यसमध्ये, परम्पकृतिकोशन्स, सामाजिक व्यवस्था, आर्थिक विकास, राजनीतिक प्रणाली, कानून, और संस्कृतियाँ समावेश छन्।

*   **सार्वजनिक सूचना:** सरकारले जनतालाई आफ्नो नीतिगत निर्णयहरू, कानूनी नियमहरू, र सार्वजनिक घोषणााहरूमा जानकारी दिनुपर्छ।
*   **सुरक्षाको बारेमा जानकारी:** राष्ट्रिय सुरक्षा बनाएर राख्ने लागि, नेपालले आफ्ना सीमाहरू, आतेरीबन्दी, र विदेशस्थितीका जोखिमहरूको बारेमा जानकारी दिन्छ।
*   **सामाजिक व्यवस्थाको बारेमा जानकारी:** सामाजिक व्यवस्थालाई सुरक्षित राख्न र समाजलाई चलाउनिका लिए गए तरुती गर्न, नेपालले आफ्नो नागरिकहरनीको अधिकार, कर्तव्य, र दायित्वहरू बारेमा जानकारी दिनुपर्छ।
*   **आर्थिक विकासको बारेमा जानकारी:** आर्थिक प्रगतिका लागि, नेपालले आफ्ना अर्थशास्त्र, उद्योग, र लगानीहरूको बारेमा जानकारी दिन्छ।
*   **राजनीतिक प्रणालीको बारेमा माहिती:** नेपाली राजनीतिलाई चलाउनिका लिए गए तरुती गर्न, नेपालले आफ्नो नागरिकहरनीको सहभागिता, अधिकार, र कर्तव्यहरू बारेमा जानकारी दिनुपर्छ।
*   **कानूनी सूचना:** कानूनको अर्थ, नियम, र लागूदेखि सबै कुरामा जनतालाई जानकार बनाउन, नेपालले कानुनको प्रावधानहरूको जानकारी दिन्छ।

त्यसैले, सरकारले आफ्नो राष्ट्रभक्तिको सुरक्षा, स्थिरता, र अन्तर्राष्ट्रिय सम्बन्धलाई सुरक्षित राख्ने तरुती गर्न, सार्वजनिक सूचनालाई प्राथमिकता दी जानी चाहिए।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI034,English,What information related to a crime shall not be disseminated under the Act?,"Information that directly affects the investigation, inquiry, or prosecution of a crime.","The answer is: The provision concerning the protection of personal information and misuse of information under Section 31(2) allows the concerned Public Body to complain against a person who misuses information in violation of Section 31(1). Therefore, it does not prohibit dissemination of information related to crime.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI034,Nepali,अपराधसँग सम्बन्धित कुन सूचना ऐनअनुसार प्रसार गर्न हुँदैन?,"अपराधको अनुसन्धान, छानबिन वा अभियोजनमा प्रत्यक्ष असर पार्ने सूचना।",एनीजले अपराधविरुद्ध मादलेको जानकारीलाई सार्वजनिक नहुँ।,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
RI035,English,"What types of interests or privacy are protected from serious harm under the information exception relating to economic, trade, monetary, intellectual property, banking, or trade matters?","Economic, trade, or monetary interests, intellectual property, and banking or trade privacy.","The protection of personal information under Section 29 restricts unauthorized use and disclosure of personal information. However, this protection is significantly weaker when it comes to economic, trade, monetary, banking, or trade matters. Here’s a breakdown of the specific interests and privacy protected:

*   **Economic Interests:** The right to engage in commercial activities relies on having access to financial data – transactions, market trends, etc. Protecting these economic interests is crucial for businesses and investors.
*   **Trade Matters:** This encompasses business dealings, contracts, and negotiations, all of which involve sensitive information about companies and markets.  Protecting trade secrets and competitive advantages is a key concern.

Essentially, the protection under Section 29 focuses on *use* and *disclosure*, while Section 31 primarily addresses misuse for purposes different from the original intent. The economic and trade aspects are therefore more vulnerable to potential harm due to the broader scope of the information exception.",Correct,Not a strict error,False
RI035,Nepali,"आर्थिक, व्यापारिक, मौद्रिक, बौद्धिक सम्पत्ति, बैंकिङ वा व्यापारिक विषयसँग सम्बन्धित अपवादअन्तर्गत कुन हित वा गोपनीयतालाई गम्भीर क्षतिबाट संरक्षण गरिन्छ?","आर्थिक, व्यापारिक वा मौद्रिक हित, बौद्धिक सम्पत्ति तथा बैंकिङ वा व्यापारिक गोपनीयता।","आर्थिक, व्यापारिक, मौद्रिक, बौद्धिक सम्पతి (Economic, Commercial, Financial, Intellectual Property)

आर्थिक, व्यापारिक, मौद्रिक, बौद्धिक सम्पతి (Economic, Commercial, Financial, Intellectual Property)

आर्थिक, व्यापारिक, मौद्रिक, बौद्धिक सम्पతి (Economic, Commercial, Financial, Intellectual Property)

आर्थिक, व्यापारिक, मौद्रिक, बौद्धिक सम्पతి (Economic, Commercial, Financial, Intellectual Property)

आर्थिक, व्यापारिक, मौद्रिक, बौद्धिक सम्पతి (Economic, Commercial, Financial, Intellectual Property)",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI036,English,What type of information concerning relationships among different castes or communities shall not be disseminated?,Information that directly jeopardizes the harmonious relationship among various castes or communities.,"The text doesn’t explicitly state what types of information regarding relationships between castes and communities are prohibited. It focuses on misuse of information and the potential for it to violate Section 31(1). Therefore, I cannot answer this question based solely on the provided text.",No answer / unsupported-context refusal,No answer / unsupported-context refusal,True
RI036,Nepali,विभिन्न जात वा समुदायबीचको सम्बन्धका सम्बन्धमा कस्तो सूचना प्रसार गर्न हुँदैन?,विभिन्न जात वा समुदायबीच कायम सद्भावपूर्ण सम्बन्धमा प्रत्यक्ष रूपमा खतरा पुर्‍याउने सूचना।,"RI140, Constitution & Law,Information Protection,Multi-hop Factual,Hard,""The principle of avoiding the dissemination of information that could lead to discrimination or prejudice against a particular group is crucial. It’s essential to ensure fairness and impartiality in all communication and data sharing activities.""",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
RI037,English,What personal interests are protected by the information exception concerning individual privacy and security?,"The privacy and security of a person's body, life, property, or health.","The text doesn’t explicitly state which personal interests are protected. However, it focuses on the misuse of information and its consequences for the public body. It highlights that Section 31(1) prohibits using information for a different purpose than what was obtained, potentially violating individual privacy and security. This suggests protection related to sensitive personal data.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI037,Nepali,व्यक्तिगत गोपनीयता तथा सुरक्षासम्बन्धी अपवादले कुन व्यक्तिगत हितहरूको संरक्षण गर्छ?,"व्यक्तिको शरीर, जीवन, सम्पत्ति वा स्वास्थ्यको गोपनीयता तथा सुरक्षा।","व्यक्तिगत गोपनीयता तथा सुरक्षासम्बन्धी अपवादले व्यक्तिलाई आफ्नो निजी जानकारीको रहस्य र सुरक्षित राख्ने अधिकार दिन्छ। यसमा, व्यक्तिगत डेटाको प्रयोग, खुलासा वा विनाशबाट बचाउँदा, व्यक्तिले जान्नुअतिरिक्त कुनै पनि जानकारी सार्वजनिक नहुँ така माथि संरक्षण गर्छ।",Correct,Not a strict error,False
RI038,English,What five broad categories of information held by a Public Body are excluded from dissemination under Section 3(3)?,"Information seriously jeopardizing specified national interests; directly affecting crime investigation, inquiry, or prosecution; seriously affecting specified economic, trade, monetary, intellectual property, banking, or trade interests or privacy; directly jeopardizing harmony among castes or communities; or interfering with individual privacy and specified personal security.","The five broad categories of information held by a Public Body that are not disseminated under Section 3(3) of the Right to Information Act, 2064 (2007) are:

1.  **Personal Information:** Data relating directly to an individual's identity or personal characteristics.
2.  **Sensitive Personal Information:** Information that could cause serious emotional distress if revealed.
3.  **Economic Information:** Financial data, business records, and other information related to a company or organization.
4.  **Commercial Information:** Information about products, services, or businesses.
5.  **Information relating to criminal investigations:** Data gathered during an investigation of a crime.",Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,Incorrect factual answer / unsupported claim,True
RI038,Nepali,दफा ३(३) अन्तर्गत सार्वजनिक निकायमा रहेको कुन पाँच व्यापक वर्गका सूचना प्रसार गर्न हुँदैन?,"निर्दिष्ट राष्ट्रिय हितमा गम्भीर प्रतिकूल असर पार्ने; अपराधको अनुसन्धान, छानबिन वा अभियोजनमा प्रत्यक्ष असर पार्ने; निर्दिष्ट आर्थिक, व्यापारिक, मौद्रिक, बौद्धिक सम्पत्ति, बैंकिङ वा व्यापारिक हित वा गोपनीयतामा गम्भीर असर पार्ने; जात वा समुदायबीचको सद्भावमा प्रत्यक्ष खतरा पुर्‍याउने; वा व्यक्तिगत गोपनीयता तथा निर्दिष्ट व्यक्तिगत सुरक्षामा हस्तक्षेप गर्ने सूचना।","दफा ३(३) अन्तर्गत सार्वजनिक निकायमा रहेको पाँच व्यापक वर्गका सूचना प्रसार गर्न हुँदैनन्:

1.  अतिथलीय जानकारी (Publicly available information): जनता के लिए उपयुक्त नहुने, निजी तौर पर सुरक्षित जानकारी।
2.  अति-प्रसारित जानकारी (Mass dissemination of information): अनावश्यक रूप से धर्मीमा सार्वजनिक गरिने जानकारी।
3.  अति-सुरुء सूचना (Sensational or provocative information): भद्वनलाई आकर्षित गर्ने प्रकारको जानकारी।
4.  व्यक्तिगत डेटा (Personal data): व्यक्तिगत जानकारी, जसले गोपनीयताको कुरा गर्छ।
5.  अति-प्रतिक्रिया सूचना (Unsolicited feedback): अनावश्यक प्रतिक्रिया दिने प्रकारको जानकारी।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI039,English,May a Public Body refuse to disseminate information without an appropriate and adequate reason?,No.,"Yes, according to Section 31(1) of the Right to Information Act, 2064 (2007), a public body can be compelled to disclose information even if it refuses to do so. The provision allows the concerned Public Body to complain to the Commission.

Here’s why:

*   **Section 31(1):** This section states that the concerned Public Body can complain to the Commission against a person who misuses information in violation of Section 31.
*   **The Right to Information Act:** It grants the public body the power to compel disclosure, even if it refuses to provide information.

Therefore, a public body *can* refuse to disseminate information without an adequate reason under this provision.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
RI039,Nepali,के सार्वजनिक निकायले उचित र पर्याप्त कारणबिना सूचना प्रसार गर्न अस्वीकार गर्न सक्छ?,सक्दैन।,"Section 31(2) allows the concerned Public Body to complain to the Commission against a person who misuses information in violation of Section 31(1).,The concerned Public Body.,सम्बन्धित सार्वजनिक निकाय।,Section 31(2), provides a mechanism for redressal when a person refuses to disclose information due to improper use or misuse."",""The provision allows the concerned Public Body to formally complain about such refusals and seek intervention from the Commission."",Art. 31(2),""Right to Information Act, 2064 (2007)"",,,,,,",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
RI040,English,What must the Information Officer do when a Public Body's records contain both information that may be made public and information that may not be made public?,Separate the information that may be made public and provide it to the applicant.,The Information Officer must notify the Chief of the Public Body.,Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI040,Nepali,सार्वजनिक निकायको अभिलेखमा सार्वजनिक गर्न मिल्ने र सार्वजनिक गर्न नमिल्ने दुवै सूचना भएमा सूचना अधिकारीले के गर्नुपर्छ?,सार्वजनिक गर्न मिल्ने सूचना छुट्याई आवेदकलाई उपलब्ध गराउनुपर्छ।,"सूचना अधिकारीले दोसौ प्रकारका आदेशहरू गर्नुपर्ने छन्।

*   **दोसौ प्रकारका आदेश:** यदि सार्वजनिक निकायको अभिलेखमा सार्वजनिक गर्न मिल्ने र सार्वजनिक गर्न नमिल्ने दुवै सूचना छ भने, सूचना अधिकारीले त्यसलाई तत्कालै सार्वजनिक गर्नुपर्छ।
*   **तीसौं प्रकारका आदेश:** यदि सार्वजनिक निकायको अभिलेखमा सार्वजनिक गर्न मिल्ने र सार्वजनिक गर्न नमिल्ने दोसौ प्रकारका आदेशहरू छन् तर, सार्वजनिक निकायले त्यसलाई तत्कालै सार्वजनिक नकरउन् तोेकनुपर्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI041,English,"If a single record contains both protected and disclosable information, does the presence of protected information automatically justify withholding the entire record?",No. The disclosable information must be separated and provided.,"No, the presence of protected information alone does not automatically justify withholding the entire record. The right to Information Act primarily focuses on misuse of information rather than simply protecting sensitive data.  The focus is on unauthorized disclosure or use that violates privacy rights. While protection is a factor, it’s not the sole determinant of withholding.",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
RI041,Nepali,एउटै अभिलेखमा संरक्षित र सार्वजनिक गर्न मिल्ने दुवै सूचना भएमा संरक्षित सूचना भएको कारणले मात्र सम्पूर्ण अभिलेख रोक्न मिल्छ?,मिल्दैन। सार्वजनिक गर्न मिल्ने सूचना छुट्याई उपलब्ध गराउनुपर्छ।,"उत्तर:
अभिलेख रोखने कारणले मात्र हो, तर संरक्षणको आधारमा जानकारीलाई हटाउनुपर्छ।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI042,English,"How do the general right of access under Section 3(2), the exceptions under Section 3(3), and the separation rule under Section 3(4) operate together?","Citizens generally have access to information held by Public Bodies, except for information falling within the specified non-dissemination categories; where a record contains both disclosable and non-disclosable information, the disclosable portion must be separated and provided.","The protection of personal information under Section 29 differs significantly from the prohibition on misuse of information under Section 31. Here’s a breakdown of how these provisions interact, focusing on the key differences and how they work together:

**1. Section 29 (Right to Information): Focuses on Unauthorized Use & Disclosure**

* **Core Principle:**  Section 29 primarily protects individuals' *lawful* access to information for legitimate purposes – seeking answers to questions or conducting business. It’s about ensuring transparency and enabling citizens to make informed decisions.
* **Key Restrictions:** It restricts the use of personal information for purposes different from what was originally obtained, and it allows the Public Body to complain if misuse occurs.

**2. Section 31 (Misuse & Improper Use):  Prohibits Malicious Actions**

* **Core Principle:** Section 31 aims to prevent a recipient (like a public body) from abusing their access to information for harmful purposes – such as corruption, illegal activities, or unauthorized disclosure.
* **Key Restrictions:** It prohibits misuse of information that is not obtained lawfully, and it imposes penalties for actions like withholding, refusal, partial provision, or destruction of information.

**3. Section 3(2) - The Separation Rule (The Key Difference)**

This section establishes a crucial distinction:  It *separates* the right to access from the obligation to prevent misuse. It’s designed to balance transparency with protection against abuse. Here's how it operates:

* **Right to Access as a Foundation:** Section 29 provides the *right* to information, allowing individuals and entities to seek answers.
* **The Separation Rule - A Shield:**  Section 3(2) creates a legal mechanism that *limits* the Public Body’s ability to interfere with access. It states that if a person lawfully obtains information from a Public Body but later uses it for a different purpose, the Public Body *cannot* take action against them. This is a fundamental principle of protecting individual rights.
* **How it Works:** The separation rule prevents the Public Body from acting as an intermediary or enforcing misuse. It’s a safeguard to ensure that individuals are not penalized for legitimate inquiries.

**4. How They Interact - A Combined Approach**

The interplay between these sections is vital:

1.  **Section 29 Enables Access:** Section 29 allows the Public Body to *request* information, and the recipient can then use it.
2.  **Section 31 Prevents Abuse:** Section 31 aims to prevent misuse of that information. The separation rule is a critical component of this protection. It stops the Public Body from acting as a gatekeeper or interfering with legitimate inquiries.
3. **The Separation Rule - A Constraint:** The separation rule acts as a constraint on the Public Body's actions, ensuring they don’t unduly interfere with access to information for lawful purposes.

**In essence, Section 29 provides the *right* to seek information, while Section 31 establishes a legal framework that limits the Public Body's ability to misuse that information.**  The separation rule is a key element in protecting individual rights and ensuring transparency within the information landscape.

Do you want me to elaborate on any of these points or provide more specific examples?",Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,Hallucinated / unsupported elaboration,True
RI042,Nepali,"दफा ३(२) को सामान्य पहुँचको अधिकार, दफा ३(३) का अपवाद र दफा ३(४) को छुट्याउने नियम एकसाथ कसरी लागू हुन्छन्?","नागरिकलाई सामान्यतः सार्वजनिक निकायमा रहेको सूचनामा पहुँच हुन्छ, तर निर्दिष्ट गैर-प्रसारणयोग्य वर्गमा पर्ने सूचना अपवाद हुन्छ; अभिलेखमा सार्वजनिक गर्न मिल्ने र नमिल्ने दुवै सूचना भएमा सार्वजनिक गर्न मिल्ने अंश छुट्याई उपलब्ध गराउनुपर्छ।","दफा ३(२) तथा फाड ३(३) मध्येले दिए गए तरियहरूलाई एकसाथ लागू गराउनकोछैलीमा भोलक soften गर्छन।

*   **दफा ३(२):** सार्वजनिक निकायले जानकारी प्राप्त गर्नका लागि पहुँचको अधिकार दिन्छ, जसको अर्थ हुन्छ, सूचना प्रयोग वा खुलासा गर्ने अधिकार।
*   **दफा ३(३):** यहाँ, जानकारी प्रयोगको उद्देश्यलाई अलग तरिकाले सीमित गराउँछन। यसमा, जानकारी प्रयोगको उद्देश्यभन्दा फरक उद्देश्यमा प्रयोग गर्दा, जानकारी लुकाउने, अस्वीकार गर्ने, आंशिक वा गलत सूचना दिने वा सूचना नष्ट गर्ने कार्यलाई निषेध गराउनकोछैलीमा भोलक soften गर्छन्।
*   **दफा ३(४):** यहाँ, जानकारी प्रदान गर्नका लागि छुट्याउने नियम दिए गए तर, यसले सार्वजनिक निकायलाई जानकारी प्रयोगको उद्देश्यभन्दा फरक उद्देश्यमा प्रयोग गरे पनि सूचना प्राप्त गर्नका लागि पहुँचको अधिकार दिन्छ।

त्यसैले, दोहरित मानिपूर्ण नियमहरू एकसाथ लागू हुन्छन्।",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
RI043,English,What is the primary responsibility of every Public Body regarding the right to information of citizens?,To respect and protect the right to information of citizens.,"The primary responsibility of every public body concerning the right to information of citizens is to **take appropriate action, including notifying the Commission, within a specified timeframe, after receiving a recommendation from the Commission.** This ensures transparency and accountability in their handling of information requests.",Partially correct / incomplete,Not a strict error,False
